    </node>
    <node id="Authorised Representative">
      <data key="d0">Authorised Representative</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">An Authorised Representative is an individual or entity in the Union appointed by an AI system provider to act on their behalf and ensure compliance with regulatory obligations under relevant legislation. This representative is particularly vital for providers not established within the Union, as they facilitate communication and compliance with regulatory authorities. The Authorised Representative is tasked with fulfilling specific responsibilities related to the compliance of AI systems, including adherence to registration requirements and addressing compliance issues with the AI Office and other relevant authorities. Through their appointment, the Authorised Representative ensures that the providers meet all regulatory commitments associated with the AI model within the Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7d62750f1113d24ac155fcd2b2ef02c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fc29985a43f3bd521b3a1c9eb9ba756&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f77911358a1d821f6b1731fac6d2dbd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b567607dbb431b0d294cd02679760039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-873c3732f26f3ace86c77cfec67991ee</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_82.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_49.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859881</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers">
      <data key="d0">Providers</data>
      <data key="d1">AIProvider</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers are entities or individuals involved in the development, deployment, and support of AI systems, particularly those originating from third countries. They hold the primary responsibility for ensuring compliance with European Union regulations, which includes adhering to legal requirements and maintaining high standards of safety and documentation throughout the AI system lifecycle. This encompasses proper data registration, risk management, and meticulous documentation, especially in financial operations.

Providers are a diverse range of organizations dedicated to creating and maintaining high-risk AI systems. They are tasked with implementing necessary mitigation measures and ensuring their designs and deployments comply with pertinent regulations and standards. As part of their obligations, Providers participate in the AI regulatory sandbox, where they seek guidance on compliance requirements and obligations.

Overall, Providers play a crucial role in the AI landscape by focusing on the development, delivery, and regulatory compliance of AI systems and applications. They are also subject to compliance verifications and must manage risks associated with the outputs of the AI systems they develop or deploy.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers refer to organizations or individuals responsible for supplying AI systems and ensuring that performance information is conveyed effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers are entities responsible for ensuring comprehensive and accessible documentation regarding the AI system, including its intended and precluded uses.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers are responsible for ensuring that AI systems are accompanied by comprehensive and accessible documentation for deployers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-07e8d113bd66975dbb8053a37cc427fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a65ec6b0fbd17afe47587686523a725&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af24a9a67de887431d611cc88e6df8c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70337c5367702b9a8ef4dd8a241aa46d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d08b537f9a5bb2b4f4bbdf442ba39bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2298fd83910d35175065de74977bd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20ac675fffdeba0fbc242b392d3af8da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1d974005cd87fc21678c732472ee11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bccefc944ad0794c75bc69b977c88a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eae051373e28d701c4893438950556b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de3f18a6d766d2baa57ae891b9da7741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a67563c32c3414ab14ce22666bed23dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f77911358a1d821f6b1731fac6d2dbd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0bef2c1dcc3d7b428c7611732f7ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e4ea35b819263359794e3a968f44ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fc29985a43f3bd521b3a1c9eb9ba756&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21acb22d994b8f65ea3709a99eb85032&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7570653f66cb58454b80be2046705a29</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_82.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_34.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_93.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_64.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_85.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_158.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_93.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_120.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_20.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_178.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_71.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_68.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863464</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union">
      <data key="d0">Union</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">The Union is a collective entity that plays multiple roles, primarily focusing on compliance with standards and regulations related to the rights of persons with disabilities as well as fostering collaboration among member states in political and economic matters. It is recognized as a political and economic union of European countries that unites them in efforts to ensure consistent practices, especially in the context of artificial intelligence (AI) systems. 

This collaboration involves the implementation and enforcement of regulations aimed at protecting the rights and safety of citizens, while also promoting responsible usage of AI technologies. The member states are engaged in law enforcement and judicial cooperation, developing a centralized framework to guide AI model providers. Through collective agreements and regulations, the Union seeks to guarantee compliance with established standards, aiming to create a secure and ethical environment for AI development and deployment.

Furthermore, the Union emphasizes shared values such as democracy and the rule of law, ensuring uniformity in the protection of rights and freedoms concerning AI technologies. The Union's collective governance includes a dedicated AI Office that oversees the development of AI capabilities among its member states. Overall, the Union represents the collaborative effort of its member states to establish a cohesive approach to governance, rights protection, and technological innovation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Union refers to the collective entity of Member States, which governs the regulatory framework for AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Union refers to a collective body of Member States working together to establish common policies and regulations regarding AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Union refers to the collective body of member countries in the EU that share regulatory powers and responsibilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9c76dd7edbc6dcf218d6558d18116d52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21da71f798625922669f14e575cb5dcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea1514e01d99729cb280141a24250142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af991f85166d6ddfbbf84e4a73207d3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa9e2916955e882c73231ed69851f6ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33366c5df404f37775ccbf3ec455b578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca7de1b4c82ecd24e2aef654437bd0e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a90a47461f525bba18d74c42ea04f88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f892644f7a3eab6b024d8a386777f23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fc29985a43f3bd521b3a1c9eb9ba756&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41cdee30f8345bc3690d876d77e6845c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0455405f9e173535e78c4ea589745cf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-714d9f621f6eee9273625419653b083c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_82.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_39.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_80.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_64.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_88.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_58.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_21.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_152.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_162.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_176.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863540</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-Risk AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">High-Risk AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">AISystem</data>
      <data key="d2">High-Risk AI Systems are advanced artificial intelligence applications identified by the European Commission as posing significant risks in various critical areas, including democracy, individual rights, legal processes, public health, and safety. These systems raise particular concerns in sensitive domains such as migration, asylum, and border control, where they are related to public authorities that can greatly influence access to essential resources and opportunities.

To address the potential challenges associated with High-Risk AI Systems, the European Union has implemented a comprehensive regulatory framework that ensures stringent oversight, registration, and ongoing performance monitoring. Compliance with Union Financial Services Law is obligatory, prioritizing traceability and safety through the logging of operational events across the lifecycle of these systems. Additionally, acquiring a CE marking is necessary for market entry within the EU, signifying adherence to relevant standards.

The design and development of High-Risk AI Systems must guarantee effective human oversight and compliance with established cybersecurity regulations set by the European Parliament and Council, with an emphasis on safety and transparency. These systems are required to meet specific standards related to risk management and accuracy, given their significant role in safety-critical infrastructure that impacts lives and health.

The regulatory process for High-Risk AI Systems entails rigorous scrutiny, comprehensive testing, and conformity assessments prior to market deployment, aimed at protecting public interests and upholding high management standards. These systems can substantially influence electoral processes, potentially affecting voting outcomes, and significantly impact educational contexts, shaping individuals' educational and professional paths.

In summary, High-Risk AI Systems are characterized by their considerable societal impact and the essential need for stringent oversight and compliance with established regulations and standards. This ensures their safety and reliability across various critical sectors, including law enforcement and decision-making processes involving personal data, reflecting their wide-ranging implications for rights and freedoms within society. They are categorized under specific regulatory requirements that necessitate additional evaluations and adherence to codes of conduct, ensuring increased scrutiny and accountability throughout their deployment and operation.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems are artificial intelligence systems that require strict adherence to safety measures due to their potential for causing harm or negative outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0639a0bd62e8b0bbe41bc1bee4a3098&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf8a675497acfbeb420b95621b7cb31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-727225adfedcad573a12c2ed92e8ee1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-671e76af4a78aebc96c988f0504bfa99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83f37d4143e19486af167d7acee5bee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a1d78baf29c07c65edc311f0ca04126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f56b40e98f8949a37c3ab283b01f7050&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4d62babb1c5a144faeae6ac2f13628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bf82c08e44c3a6e12c9472e052df840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3e6894a9009f1db207c0ec639d8a39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f6e14583352886a741ac1d51eada03a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eae051373e28d701c4893438950556b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de3f18a6d766d2baa57ae891b9da7741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb43ec5a01dc502046ab6ffbe3a25504&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29241e99bddf5af77eca441d2d8dbc1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4518ca313d8493e277775e1a9267b84d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f79a9fca1518856b24fdcb7e59f040&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711f6ce0c9e8f119b1813ffe001673da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fc29985a43f3bd521b3a1c9eb9ba756&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ded1c99cfd152513a4ef07b96a9c5de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-543cc911c9d837b54a06d5f6ca958b34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb0291da832d9defa94aaf2262ad3761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-166a35f517674f4ceba2754c65f88c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37d88f95110db00bbf8230a2632a2035&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b7fd511ed97ef1a87c9783c3425b7d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c4d127e5313d415dd94f6b6761da956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31c82fb046f107cbfab945a92431bbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c1d05b847c03fe702172f787883fc33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43942ba7283893ebf128acb858a20c58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-759ef1bca08a56dec0192e47771d9820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82b1b08be1175d2e6d49ab5a294ef86a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b754e2170dea6f93253ec4fd1fa88d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44eafa4c222bb60e722eca942751cf7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff61ec794793cf787d4a0473487a06f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d44e4d07784e334a8ded2c1da49b969e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e5d20a8e9427a4698b84f758676994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff0d16c0510c298943e3daa75fd581b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07ee6b3452d7