    <node id="Public Assistance Benefits">
      <data key="d0">Public Assistance Benefits</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Public assistance benefits are essential services provided by authorities to help individuals in need, including healthcare, social security, and housing assistance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b31c82fb046f107cbfab945a92431bbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_58.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857235</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Natural Persons">
      <data key="d0">Natural Persons</data>
      <data key="d1">DataSubject</data>
      <data key="d2">Natural Persons are individual human beings whose biometric data may be captured and utilized by artificial intelligence (AI) systems for identification purposes. They are key stakeholders in the ecosystem of AI technologies and have a significant interest in numerous aspects of these systems, particularly concerning transparency and the right to clear information about AI-generated content and processing activities. This interest is especially pronounced as Natural Persons often apply for or receive vital services and benefits from public authorities, highlighting their essential connection to the deployment and management of AI systems.

In overseeing high-risk AI systems, Natural Persons bear the responsibility of ensuring compliance with safety regulations and ethical standards. They must possess the necessary competence, training, and authority to assess and verify AI system identifications, underscoring their critical role in the governance of these technologies. Within the European Union, evaluations involving Natural Persons are based on actual behaviors rather than AI-generated predictions, which emphasizes the necessity for fairness and mitigates the risk of bias in AI assessments.

Natural Persons may be subject to practices such as emotion recognition, which raises ethical concerns related to privacy and autonomy, as these systems aim to identify or infer their emotions or intents. The deployment of high-risk AI systems significantly impacts the health, safety, and fundamental rights of Natural Persons, particularly in decision-making processes that critically affect their lives. Therefore, discussions surrounding data protection laws and the ethical implementation of AI must prioritize the rights and protections of Natural Persons, ensuring they remain fully informed about their interactions with AI systems.

Additionally, Natural Persons have the right to seek legal remedies if their rights and freedoms are infringed upon by AI systems. Their interests and rights must be taken into account during assessments related to the impact of AI technologies, especially when such systems involve biometric data collection and remote identification without their active consent. Overall, Natural Persons are individuals affected by decisions made by AI systems, particularly in high-risk scenarios, and they must be informed about such usage, especially as they may face challenges in contesting the results produced by these systems in a legal context.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural Persons refer to individuals who are capable of acting and are involved in the operation or use of the system.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural persons are individuals assigned to oversee high-risk AI systems, ensuring operational constraints and informed decision-making.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural Persons are individuals whose rights may be affected by the deployment and operation of AI models and systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-83317eda1161cf5d13ef9aa07297c98b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50cb89ed7d0d818018d373ebefa65267&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c4d127e5313d415dd94f6b6761da956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb040a8b4e6e3fa6f26776f560b6591c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ed67e673a6fe0a3c79a41bb9102d44b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89491b02af0a00cbc13f9e8df827a6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5644d48de211c02e29152f909c69640b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d64a2a65aec35f8304efaaee30e0034d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31c82fb046f107cbfab945a92431bbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c1d05b847c03fe702172f787883fc33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d1a48b7c6d78e001878383cb0acaf58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded7b0ac022304fae10651966b33d18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3070277451614bdc67954ec8735dd80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee04f6104a24650416810ede28f3790b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f62cf38e10f73dd06a997571902c1ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41cdee30f8345bc3690d876d77e6845c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61cbf514bcfe4869e269c00a2dc9e712&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ef0a2a22402771842f4d35bbf4be08d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bccefc944ad0794c75bc69b977c88a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602b68fe088482c0037845fc0b520c30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de3f18a6d766d2baa57ae891b9da7741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb43ec5a01dc502046ab6ffbe3a25504&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4274f38f6b4aeff6dc2959e9e1a87f1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e4ea35b819263359794e3a968f44ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7110d3511298db6faf629e1d559dc5ba</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_18.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_93.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_59.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_141.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_170.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_30.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_58.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_97.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_132.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_42.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_71.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863931</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Healthcare Services">
      <data key="d0">Healthcare Services</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Healthcare services form part of public assistance benefits and are critical for users' well-being and standard of living.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b31c82fb046f107cbfab945a92431bbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_58.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857235</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Social Security Benefits">
      <data key="d0">Social Security Benefits</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Social security benefits support individuals during life events like illness, maternity, or unemployment, and are considered essential public services.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b31c82fb046f107cbfab945a92431bbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_58.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857235</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Credit Score Evaluation AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Credit Score Evaluation AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">AISystem</data>
      <data key="d2">AI systems that evaluate credit scores and creditworthiness of individuals can be classified as high-risk due to their impact on access to financial resources.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b31c82fb046f107cbfab945a92431bbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_58.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857235</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk Assessment AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Risk Assessment AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">AISystem</data>
      <data key="d2">AI systems meant for risk assessment in health and life insurance can have serious implications for individuals' rights and well-being.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b31c82fb046f107cbfab945a92431bbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_58.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857235</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Emergency Response Services">
      <data key="d0">Emergency Response Services</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Emergency response services include police, firefighters, and medical aid that may be prioritized or dispatched by AI systems based on emergency calls.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b31c82fb046f107cbfab945a92431bbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_58.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857235</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Essential Private and Public Services">
      <data key="d0">Essential Private and Public Services</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Essential private and public services are services necessary for individuals to fully participate in society and improve their standard of living.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b31c82fb046f107cbfab945a92431bbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_58.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857235</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Social Services">
      <data key="d0">Social Services</data>
      <data key="d1">AreaOfImpact</data>
      <data key="d2">Social services include benefits provided to vulnerable individuals in circumstances such as maternity, illness, or loss of employment.&lt;SEP&gt;Social services represent a public interest where high-risk AI systems may be utilized to support vulnerable populations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b31c82fb046f107cbfab945a92431bbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a1d78baf29c07c65edc311f0ca04126</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_58.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_96.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Public Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">Public Authorities are governmental entities responsible for implementing and monitoring compliance with quality management regulations for high-risk AI systems. These entities are required to register their use of such AI systems in the EU database before their deployment. Additionally, Public Authorities are tasked with administering essential services and benefits to citizens, managing migration, asylum procedures, and border control, often utilizing AI systems for assessments. As entities that deploy high-risk AI systems, they must adhere to specific legal and regulatory requirements set forth under relevant regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Public Authorities refer to government bodies responsible for enforcing regulations and ensuring compliance with Union law.&lt;SEP&gt;Public authorities are required to register their high-risk AI systems in the EU Database before use, ensuring accountability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b31c82fb046f107cbfab945a92431bbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e853663a3f2d06a9cfea8582e10f089&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44eafa4c222bb60e722eca942751cf7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d44e4d07784e334a8ded2c1da49b969e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2806e288e0b71013209c4ad85ecaa38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bece07e296fce9647a40a0dde904fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b8c1122e1044e4445aa96d7fa6d5b6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_177.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_131.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_58.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_77.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_49.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_81.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863655</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Vulnerable Position">
      <data key="d0">Vulnerable Position</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Individuals receiving public assistance benefits often find themselves in a vulnerable position relative to public authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;Vulnerable position refers to individuals or groups who may be more susceptible to harm from the consequences of an AI system due to their status or circumstances.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b31c82fb046f107cbfab945a92431bbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50beca99a2207706ee9f0ad17a4205ff</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_58.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_7.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863901</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Discrimination">
      <data key="d0">Discrimination</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Discrimination can occur when certain groups are unfairly evaluated or treated differently through processes such as AI assessment.&lt;SEP&gt;Discrimination refers to the unjust treatment of individuals based on their characteristics, which can be perpetuated by biased AI outputs.&lt;SEP&gt;Discrimination may occur when AI systems are not adequately trained or designed, leading to unfair treatment of individuals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bbcf833252ce65fd6a1d8bd1f5a6efc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7eb8204c84c6a7310e75effed716fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31c82fb046f107cbfab945a92431bbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_58.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_59.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_67.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862933</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fundamental Rights">
      <data key="d0">Fundamental Rights</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Fundamental Rights are essential rights that serve to protect individuals and uphold their dignity and freedoms, particularly in the context of rapid advancements in technologies such as artificial intelligence (AI). These rights, which include social protection, non-discrimination, human dignity, the right to privacy, freedom of movement, and the protection of private life, are guaranteed and protected by law. As AI technologies evolve, they pose potential threats to these Fundamental Rights, making it crucial to ensure their preservation.

In particular, the implications of AI in high-risk sectors like finance and insurance necessitate careful evaluation to safeguard individual rights and freedoms. Regulatory frameworks aimed at AI deployment emphasize the need to protect Fundamental Rights to prevent any adverse effects stemming from potentially harmful practices associated with AI technologies.

Fundamental Rights encompass various civil liberties that require protection under specific regulations overseeing the development, deployment, and oversight of AI systems. These rights focus on important concerns such as personal data privacy, freedom of expression, non-discrimination, and the protection of vulnerable groups. Recognized as basic human rights, they demand stringent oversight to prevent infringements that may arise from AI usage.

Ultimately, integrating Fundamental Rights into AI decision-making practices is vital for promoting democratic values and protecting individuals from possible abuses tied to AI technology. Societies must ensure that the incorporation of AI across diverse sectors respects these fundamental legal protections and acknowledges the inherent rights entitled to each individual, reinforcing the imperative to consider these rights in all AI-related obligations and risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Fundamental rights are the basic human rights that can be adversely affected by erroneous or biased outputs from AI systems.</data>
