    <node id="national security purposes">
      <data key="d0">national security purposes</data>
      <data key="d1">Purpose</data>
      <data key="d2">National security purposes pertain to regulations excluding AI systems used specifically for defense or military operations from the broader regulatory scope.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13991bdab077b3114e8913f89a1371e5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857239</data>
    </node>
    <node id="importers and distributors">
      <data key="d0">importers and distributors</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Importers and distributors are entities that play a role in the supply chain of AI systems, ensuring they reach the market in compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13991bdab077b3114e8913f89a1371e5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857239</data>
    </node>
    <node id="product manufacturers">
      <data key="d0">product manufacturers</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Product manufacturers place AI systems on the market, ensuring compliance with regulations under their own brand or trademark.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13991bdab077b3114e8913f89a1371e5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857239</data>
    </node>
    <node id="authorised representatives">
      <data key="d0">authorised representatives</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Authorised representatives act on behalf of providers who are not established in the Union but need to comply with local regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13991bdab077b3114e8913f89a1371e5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857239</data>
    </node>
    <node id="affected persons">
      <data key="d0">affected persons</data>
      <data key="d1">AIUser</data>
      <data key="d2">Affected persons are individuals located within the Union who may be impacted by the use and outputs of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13991bdab077b3114e8913f89a1371e5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857239</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Competences">
      <data key="d0">EU Competences</data>
      <data key="d1">RiskConcept</data>
      <data key="d2">EU competences refer to the authority granted to the European Union regarding legislative matters, including AI system regulations under member states' jurisdiction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13991bdab077b3114e8913f89a1371e5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857239</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Military and Defence Purposes">
      <data key="d0">Military and Defence Purposes</data>
      <data key="d1">Purpose</data>
      <data key="d2">Military and defence purposes refer to the use of AI systems specifically for national security and related operations, which are excluded from the Regulation's provisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3105f8ed20ed5608a4571fe7b1d8f942</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857239</data>
    </node>
    <node id="International Organisations">
      <data key="d0">International Organisations</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">International Organisations are entities that may use AI systems in cooperation with the Union for law enforcement and judicial cooperation, subject to specific conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;International Organisations are entities that operate at a global level and may engage in cooperation for law enforcement with the Union.&lt;SEP&gt;International organisations are entities that work on the regulatory frameworks for AI, ensuring legal certainty and promoting international convergence on AI definitions and practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a90a47461f525bba18d74c42ea04f88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd27f4cf61449e217b2273c0cf67adfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3105f8ed20ed5608a4571fe7b1d8f942</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_12.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858541</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Scientific Research and Development">
      <data key="d0">Scientific Research and Development</data>
      <data key="d1">AreaOfImpact</data>
      <data key="d2">Scientific research and development activities focus on innovations, particularly regarding AI systems and models.&lt;SEP&gt;Scientific research and development pertains to activities involving AI systems or AI models developed solely for research, excluded from the Regulation's scope.&lt;SEP&gt;This represents activities related to the development and testing of AI systems for scientific purposes, which may be exempt from certain regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8833999c9ef9aa31a007f2e77ffea02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ffd8df9d8eb9625dca23bc5f974e025&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3105f8ed20ed5608a4571fe7b1d8f942</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2016/679">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2016/679</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2016/679 is the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) that sets guidelines for the collection and processing of personal data.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2016/679 provides a comprehensive framework for data protection, defining biometric data in Article 4, point (14).&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2016/679, commonly referred to as the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), is a comprehensive legal framework established to govern the processing of personal data and protect individuals' privacy rights within the European Union. Its primary objective is to ensure the safeguarding of natural persons concerning the processing of personal data, thereby facilitating the free movement of such data across member states.

The GDPR imposes stringent conditions on the handling of personal data, including sensitive categories such as biometric data, which is generally prohibited from processing in most cases to enhance privacy protection. The regulation emphasizes the importance of individuals' rights regarding their personal data, ensuring robust privacy and data rights for EU citizens and residents.

Moreover, the GDPR establishes strict rules for compliance with data protection laws, mandates transparency in data handling, and advocates for proper data governance practices. Through these mechanisms, Regulation (EU) 2016/679 represents a significant advancement in data protection standards and influences the management of personal data across various sectors within the EU. It also addresses challenges related to privacy in contexts such as law enforcement and data security, while outlining provisions for personal data protection and implications related to profiling by AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;This regulation sets out the principles of data protection applicable to AI systems handling personal data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-15eee417af0ebe299ed66be76a0b845a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-445327adc051facf545b6358f6f01466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4672fd3df7077626af67d20e46d3fcb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-498834b2d84eaf9afe4e5fb0df15933c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3105f8ed20ed5608a4571fe7b1d8f942&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0373d38f7600f51def3b5e5cb5061d17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77093970e26d1be04734ed16ea88f777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a46250ea72037444e96653239f2893b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1be166c61f466e23c3d8c143f6efd3bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de40ca48bf7dafc1db86f4d8a18d2bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0073df6368131f4f385a66430ef1c4f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602b68fe088482c0037845fc0b520c30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8da189e7622be67a80b2e12945a657cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65e9562dd645622f1390ba1863fee19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4882abf1dd869d3dff00b8d88ee946a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc038db2f25d511bf84cccc9550e10c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e726a1ef8f481d54c995afc6a028f60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8833999c9ef9aa31a007f2e77ffea02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85605aee8aaac2bf4ad29d80d902148f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_140.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_10.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_67.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_39.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_95.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863700</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Security">
      <data key="d0">National Security</data>
      <data key="d1">AreaOfImpact</data>
      <data key="d2">National Security pertains to the protection and safety measures by Member States that do not fall under the Regulation's scope regarding AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;National security encompasses efforts to protect a nation from threats or dangers, including the use of AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5981afe4b9fb547c64f49e76b1d9c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3105f8ed20ed5608a4571fe7b1d8f942</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859786</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Military Purposes">
      <data key="d0">Military Purposes</data>
      <data key="d1">Purpose</data>
      <data key="d2">Military Purposes define the application of AI systems utilized for defense and security functions, exempting these from the Regulation's provisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Military purposes involve using AI systems in contexts related to defense and combat, and these usages are specifically regulated by the mentioned Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Military purposes refer to the application of AI systems in defense and national security contexts, which may not fall under standard regulatory requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ffa7662f1a996e8ed97ec3caf0ae564&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5981afe4b9fb547c64f49e76b1d9c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3105f8ed20ed5608a4571fe7b1d8f942</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859786</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Adequate Safeguards">
      <data key="d0">Adequate Safeguards</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Adequate Safeguards are measures required to protect the fundamental rights of individuals when interactions occur with third countries.&lt;SEP&gt;Adequate Safeguards refer to the measures mandated to protect fundamental rights and freedoms during law enforcement activities and international agreements.&lt;SEP&gt;Adequate Safeguards refer to the necessary measures put in place to ensure the protection of individual rights when AI systems are used in international contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a90a47461f525bba18d74c42ea04f88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3105f8ed20ed5608a4571fe7b1d8f942&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing and Development Activities">
      <data key="d0">Testing and Development Activities</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing and Development Activities involve the assessment and refinement of AI systems or models before they are placed on the market, as stipulated in the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3105f8ed20ed5608a4571fe7b1d8f942</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857239</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2022/2065">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2022/2065</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2022/2065 is a legislative measure developed by the European Parliament and the Council that establishes a comprehensive framework for the management and regulation of artificial intelligence (AI) systems and their intermediary services within the European Union. The regulation imposes specific obligations on AI system providers and deployers, particularly concerning the detection and disclosure of artificially generated or manipulated outputs. Additionally, it addresses the liability of providers of intermediary services relating to AI systems and models, ensuring they adhere to risk-management procedures as part of their operations. Overall, Regulation (EU) 2022/2065 aims to enhance transparency and accountability in the use of AI technologies in the digital services landscape.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74def3a33d9c60f3c11227adf7704a09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cac929d0048fe34377179e8ecde4a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8833999c9ef9aa31a007f2e77ffea02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e1bc352c7c8d3a7ba58b9b1a4f9f37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7570653f66cb58454b80be2046705a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1ab686ea2085e0bf2cc7ea2cb5eb270</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_11.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_136.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_120.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_119.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_118.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2018/1725">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2018/1725</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2018/1725 is a crucial legislative framework that focuses on the protection of personal data managed by EU institutions and bodies. Defined in Article 3, point (18), it outlines biometric data and emphasizes the necessity for adherence to established data protection principles. This regulation enhances the existing frameworks of personal data protection within the European Union by introducing specific rules governing the processing of such data, including the use of biometric information.

The regulation aims to ensure compliance with privacy standards, thereby reinforcing the protection of personal data of natural persons within the EU. It addresses the unique challenges posed by the processing of data in the context of artificial intelligence (AI) systems, offering guidelines for data handling, especially in sandbox environments designed for experimentation and innovation.

Overall, Regulation (EU) 2018/1725 seeks to elevate the standards of data protection across EU institutions and agencies, thereby enhancing the privacy rights of individuals and ensuring a higher level of accountability in data processing activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-15eee417af0ebe299ed66be76a0b845a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc038db2f25d511bf84cccc9550e10c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77093970e26d1be04734ed16ea88f777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e726a1ef8f481d54c995afc6a028f60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602b68fe088482c0037845fc0b520c30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8833999c9ef9aa31a007f2e77ffea02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0373d38f7600f51def3b5e5cb5061d17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-498834b2d84eaf9afe4e5fb0df15933c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85605aee8aaac2bf4ad29d80d902148f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-472b03a027e3fcae21e86e23849e4510&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-800752b66b6fe0cd70bb0290efc2fbbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a46250ea72037444e96653239f2893b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-699b82035d71a633a86a67090e5a61e8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_140.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_10.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_39.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_180.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_59.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863383</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2002/58/EC">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2002/58/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2002/58/EC addresses the protection of privacy in electronic communications and the processing of personal data in that sector.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2002/58/EC safeguards private life and communication confidentiality, regulating the storage and access to personal data.&lt;SEP&gt;This Directive focuses on the protection of privacy in electronic communications, affecting how data can be used.&lt;SEP&gt;This directive focuses on privacy and data protection in the electronic communications sector, establishing rules for processing personal data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-85605aee8aaac2bf4ad29d80d902148f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3cb5eb81289d4fb565bd824bdc63506&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15eee417af0ebe299ed66be76a0b845a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8833999c9ef9aa31a007f2e77ffea02</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_10.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862255</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2016/680">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2016/680</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">This Regulation deals with the protection of individuals concerning the processing of personal data by competent authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;This regulation outlines the rules regarding the processing of personal data, including biometric data, especially in law enforcement contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc038db2f25d511bf84cccc9550e10c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8833999c9ef9aa31a007f2e77ffea02</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_39.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857679</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Personal Data">
      <data key="d0">Personal Data</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Personal Data refers to any information relating to identified or identifiable individuals, which must be handled according to stringent legal standards, particularly during AI testing. This encompasses various types of information, including names and contact details of individuals responsible for registering AI systems within the EU Database. The processing of such data is subject to rigorous regulations, notably the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), which emphasizes the protection of individuals' privacy and rights.

Under Regulation (EU) 2016/679, the significance of safeguarding personal information is underscored, establishing that personal data is necessary for the lawful collection and processing in the context of AI technologies. This data is essential for the registration, development, and deployment of AI systems and must be managed with care to protect individuals' rights.

Additionally, personal data pertains to information that must be protected during the testing of AI systems. This includes consent-related information that must comply with data protection laws, ensuring that any information relating to identified or identifiable individuals collected during these processes is appropriately handled.

Importantly, personal data also includes information that needs to be deleted post-testing, following the principles of minimizing data retention in line with legal requirements. This comprehensive understanding of personal data highlights the need for stringent protocols in its collection, processing, and storage to uphold individual privacy rights across various contexts, including legal proceedings and investigations. Overall, personal data is subject to strict handling and processing regulations to ensure compliance with applicable laws and to protect the rights of individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;Personal data is any data that relates to an identified or identifiable individual, which is subject to specific processing laws and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Personal data refers to any information related to an identifiable individual and must be processed following specific data protection laws.&lt;SEP&gt;Personal data refers to information that relates to an identified or identifiable individual and may be processed in the sandbox under certain conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Personal data includes information that relates to identified or identifiable natural persons, protected under regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad1a115533e7d3b3ced9ea8e2e87b0e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34333cde7ca701413cb4d0a0ef1129e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ef570a9dfbda3c55d0d5bcc36fd77c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-184360d53ae652d7f48a919e168f375a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3cb5eb81289d4fb565bd824bdc63506&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-800752b66b6fe0cd70bb0290efc2fbbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a46250ea72037444e96653239f2893b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4988a00689afb1245e0f0ce4ceef5921&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f6e14583352886a741ac1d51eada03a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eea61d03ab615ac5f518e77cd220c1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4518ca313d8493e277775e1a9267b84d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe76292b9a553c383dab6b0a4a67cee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc038db2f25d511bf84cccc9550e10c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e4ea35b819263359794e3a968f44ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8833999c9ef9aa31a007f2e77ffea02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85605aee8aaac2bf4ad29d80d902148f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2612abd3c26dca69a0acec30add3ef15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-699b82035d71a633a86a67090e5a61e8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_63.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_140.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_10.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_141.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_103.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_39.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_71.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_59.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863405</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Models">
      <data key="d0">AI Models</data>
      <data key="d1">AIModel</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Models are algorithms trained to process data and make predictions or decisions based on that input.&lt;SEP&gt;AI models are algorithms designed for AI systems, with exclusions from the Regulation when used solely for scientific research.&lt;SEP&gt;AI models refer to the specific constructs or algorithms that govern the behaviors and decisions of AI systems, which are also regulated.&lt;SEP&gt;AI models refer to the systems developed based on the ethical guidelines to ensure they align with the established principles.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-256a6003a5841f2764536c55f7086431&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ffd8df9d8eb9625dca23bc5f974e025&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8833999c9ef9aa31a007f2e77ffea02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fe270726065b96afec7d35572470b3c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_27.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_44.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Intermediary Services">
      <data key="d0">Intermediary Services</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Intermediary Services refer to the roles that AI systems can play in facilitating interactions between users and other digital services.&lt;SEP&gt;Intermediary services are platforms or systems that connect users and AI services, with specific liability outlined in the regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Intermediary services refer to online platforms that facilitate interactions between users, which are addressed by the new regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74def3a33d9c60f3c11227adf7704a09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8833999c9ef9aa31a007f2e77ffea02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1ab686ea2085e0bf2cc7ea2cb5eb270</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_11.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_119.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862940</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing in Real World Conditions">
      <data key="d0">Testing in Real World Conditions</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing in Real World Conditions involves assessing artificial intelligence (AI) systems to ensure their functionality, safety, and compliance with relevant regulations. This process entails evaluating these systems under realistic operational scenarios that closely mimic actual use, allowing for the validation of their efficacy and safety. By performing evaluations in practical environments representative of typical usage, Testing in Real World Conditions ensures that high-risk AI systems are thoroughly assessed under actual operating conditions. This method emphasizes the importance of regulatory compliance and oversight, making it a crucial step in the development and deployment of AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4518ca313d8493e277775e1a9267b84d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff61ec794793cf787d4a0473487a06f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8833999c9ef9aa31a007f2e77ffea02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba5a4fee300868ea16940c9ea15f534a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a350089bbf860c041d514aa2041d9455&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1516ad8d48077af0d59fc01578f33</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_61.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_76.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863076</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union legal acts">
      <data key="d0">Union legal acts</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Union legal acts refer to the legislative framework established by the European Union that governs member states in various domains including consumer protection and product safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63ef16386f45c7bc364061cc094254fb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857239</data>
    </node>
    <node id="natural persons">
      <data key="d0">natural persons</data>
      <data key="d1">AISubject</data>
      <data key="d2">Natural persons are individuals who deploy AI systems for personal usage and are exempt from specific regulatory obligations under this Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural persons refer to human individuals who are affected by the decisions made based on AI system outputs and play a role in verifying outputs.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural persons refer to individual human beings who are subject to evaluation by AI systems, particularly in social scoring scenarios.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2118453abd880b63eddb91fa3806c3f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28efea7f8fe5945cce5b7be57e88efe7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63ef16386f45c7bc364061cc094254fb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861584</data>
    </node>
    <node id="collective agreements">
      <data key="d0">collective agreements</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Collective agreements are negotiations that may lead to improved work conditions for employees regarding the deployment of AI systems by employers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63ef16386f45c7bc364061cc094254fb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857239</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 25">
      <data key="d0">Recital 25</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 25 is a specific provision within the Regulation that outlines particular exclusions related to its application.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63ef16386f45c7bc364061cc094254fb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857239</data>
    </node>
    <node id="consumer protection">
      <data key="d0">consumer protection</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Consumer protection refers to the set of laws and regulations designed to ensure the rights of consumers and promote fair trade, competition, and accurate information in the marketplace.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63ef16386f45c7bc364061cc094254fb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857239</data>
    </node>
    <node id="product safety">
      <data key="d0">product safety</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Product safety encompasses the regulations and standards intended to ensure that products are safe for consumers when used as intended.&lt;SEP&gt;Product safety refers to the standards and practices ensuring that AI systems do not pose harm to users or the environment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63ef16386f45c7bc364061cc094254fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a57bbcc3ccf00f26352f12c36036aedf</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_125.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858640</data>
    </node>
    <node id="obligations of deployers">
      <data key="d0">obligations of deployers</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Obligations of deployers refer to the responsibilities and requirements established under the Regulation for those who deploy AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63ef16386f45c7bc364061cc094254fb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857239</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI systems released under free and open-source licences">
      <data key="d0">AI systems released under free and open-source licences</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">AI systems released under free and open-source licenses are applications that can be freely used, modified, and shared, but are subject to specific regulatory scrutiny if categorized as high-risk systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63ef16386f45c7bc364061cc094254fb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857239</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Database">
      <data key="d0">EU Database</data>
      <data key="d1">DataSource</data>
      <data key="d2">The EU Database contains information pertinent to the monitoring and evaluation of AI systems as part of regulatory compliance checks.&lt;SEP&gt;The EU Database is a centralized information system established under regulatory frameworks to ensure the registration and traceability of high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) systems. Maintained by the European Commission, the database is designed to be user-friendly and publicly accessible while adhering to stringent regulatory mandates. This comprehensive repository contains essential personal data necessary for the registration of AI systems, facilitating efficient information processing in line with regulations.

Key features of the EU Database include a specific registry dedicated to biometric identification systems, which documents the use and compliance of these systems with EU laws, reflecting legislative requirements for logging such technologies. Although it is primarily meant for public access to promote transparency, the database also has secure sections that protect sensitive information in compliance with EU regulations.

In addition to its primary function of registration, the EU Database acts as a collection point for serious incidents and regulatory compliance related to AI systems. It enables access to incident reports and maintains records pertinent to AI regulation and evaluation, assisting in compliance verification and legislative tracking. The database is crucial for ensuring that the testing of AI systems is properly registered, further promoting transparency and adherence to established regulations.

Overall, the EU Database plays an essential role in the governance and oversight of high-risk AI systems within the European Union, ensuring that all deployments meet European standards and regulatory requirements while managing access to both public and secure information.&lt;SEP&gt;The EU database stores information relevant to the compliance and evaluation of AI systems under the applicable regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa9e2916955e882c73231ed69851f6ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-166a35f517674f4ceba2754c65f88c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4672fd3df7077626af67d20e46d3fcb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-610573a7c194ad780ed97782200a740c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc59c087d680631c2a594779449f195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb5ca2a2f12bb39286916d398b70ed9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00e7606a0fa9d588f18d67d02cfcf654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77093970e26d1be04734ed16ea88f777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0073df6368131f4f385a66430ef1c4f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2806e288e0b71013209c4ad85ecaa38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f74259ac0ec20e9f3989df868f56b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a64bfb94635a0df2f808b2f8a494bd3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e4ea35b819263359794e3a968f44ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98532c431ec75ae38c76dc0730337a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bece07e296fce9647a40a0dde904fe4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_131.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_80.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_141.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_71.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_49.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_83.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863835</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Commission">
      <data key="d0">Commission</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">The Commission is responsible for adopting delegated acts related to high-risk AI systems and their use cases.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission refers to the governing body empowered to adopt delegated acts pertaining to AI regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission, formally known as the European Commission, is a vital governing body within the European Union, charged with overseeing the regulatory framework concerning artificial intelligence (AI). It is responsible for developing implementing acts that detail the arrangements and conditions for evaluating AI models, particularly those categorized as high-risk. The Commission ensures compliance with regulations by certifying AI systems and monitoring their conformance across various member states.

The Commission collaborates with independent experts and appoints them for the evaluation procedures of AI models. It receives reports from notifying authorities regarding notified bodies and their certificates, ensuring an effective oversight mechanism. Among its many responsibilities, the Commission adopts delegated acts to amend regulations and guidelines concerning conformity declarations and technical documentation for high-risk AI systems.

A key aspect of the Commission's role involves developing common specifications in cooperation with international partners for standardization in AI practices. This includes approving codes of practice and establishing common rules for the implementation of these regulations. The Commission also evaluates the enforcement efficacy of AI-related regulations, ensuring that the necessary post-market monitoring plans are in place, and coordinating investigations into AI technologies that pose systemic risks.

To enhance regulatory compliance, the Commission works alongside market surveillance authorities and Member States, managing the Advisory Forum which aids in regulatory functions and assesses national measures. Furthermore, it has the authority to request documentation from AI model providers for compliance assessments and can impose fines for non-compliance.

The Commission also emphasizes quality management standards relevant to microenterprises and other stakeholders, managing an EU Database containing sensitive information about high-risk AI systems. Additionally, it assesses risks associated with general-purpose AI models and mandates compliance regulations to ensure accountability.

In its commitment to supporting small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs), the Commission evaluates the financial impacts of AI regulations and implements targeted measures to assist these businesses. It provides guidelines for detecting and labeling artificially generated or manipulated content, working towards a balance between fostering innovation and maintaining regulatory oversight.

In summary, the Commission plays a crucial role in shaping and managing AI-related regulations within the EU. Its initiatives are aimed at reinforcing commitments to quality assurance in high-risk AI systems, supporting market surveillance among diverse authorities, and enhancing AI literacy and best practices across Europe.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf8a675497acfbeb420b95621b7cb31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83f37d4143e19486af167d7acee5bee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6fc829d58f1a7bbf3defd5cbe758b8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f56b40e98f8949a37c3ab283b01f7050&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0789803641ff590acdf82b97e7d4afbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c553a0db4b39033e7fcfeddeb912aac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67ecee9ae9852fb675f5c9c9cb2f2de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6ed86abb2e8f0e12897e923d1e9964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36cb0fd5abf1b169a8aa13021f58c7b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e519b84a1d0987cd3b0aab32a476aa33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97182f6b8815d40f51faf3e8eaeb7c7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea6a588c10ad2fe493ec8cc1913f72d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae3ab8a3b5c5d0c61e8b99fa718913b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-762d138929f27b0266d948c0aad50daa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aacbea1ddddc58fbf14c882b36d9a6b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aca56f82b70892874784bcec5c2bb2c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f79a9fca1518856b24fdcb7e59f040&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4c7e75432b8ffa8e0b96687dc4dd380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e4ea35b819263359794e3a968f44ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97ee5867d3c03f24001b650ad752686d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-712b56cbfc73c46eacde9204fa4e5c49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cc9a7191827dda78eda5924876e5f7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f3c3fe390cb5d40b199e1bcc024928f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345a8ba89ed0ea3325462384d5e16aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba662546e18e6e5f82c3cd1c5b4c3b75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de6a0d59bb86cca6093fbb52cf156b4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb0291da832d9defa94aaf2262ad3761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-166a35f517674f4ceba2754c65f88c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37d88f95110db00bbf8230a2632a2035&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b7fd511ed97ef1a87c9783c3425b7d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-140dff8b8263721e25ea86a4104c273d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1ef1c9ca92c002cf6ad36264fe1292c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70555b8168fcbd401cc11093ec15091a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c8a6b92fbe8d93eb878957c5ed60aa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee6d94a5f64203f09d02387acbdb39c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86aff1d72a3f6226d0b5db29d9910a59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e75ee11aa912f1497b2a91ae655e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e37c30ee0e0a87b8ea9630ea20f092fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82b1b08be1175d2e6d49ab5a294ef86a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f94df6da4de89cee24b1bd8f504c377&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9317b056c2a260423c79e368903cde7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c742eff7a2b610bb01c8c0ec233b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff61ec794793cf787d4a0473487a06f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad86065dee426d0a1db7444552c4a385&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ec0d2d3cbe2a53a3bbf6373c775edf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e23bb4c71b510fec0bbe6570de37cd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07ee6b3452d764ccd9733dceadb1ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f76666cf495bb0f0810313fe42e2c882&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98532c431ec75ae38c76dc0730337a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec7c9ce58b650afe456517c2483e56c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cb1edc11e8b8d0e952b15617a80f379&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eab6e21707d57be17832ef8dfd7180a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdd0ab3aadbdd5226fa3661ea9057181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0461b38c664574f634a78148bfce0336&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a69b68c9998277692ac6c6341fcdcac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b341fa074527a308a2434a3c68244d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d42aaf56c15be020feabced14d2409d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d58805118916ede230a82a4ec3f60b3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e4f07f79ad3c90c82b86c0a02d0fae9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2187eb3476528ac7c75b571eb3844f0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4058e2567f154203a2d9dacec4bdf7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b16c22014fb75795531a9a187b8fc81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-785d0dafc3a62a1aee53267d076b7533&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0bef2c1dcc3d7b428c7611732f7ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da5fbf959baa6ee8e86278864a9144cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af991f85166d6ddfbbf84e4a73207d3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50be48c46c67191e901c756873069fcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11bdaa862215570a86eed137e3092ea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-075ecb5835777e6044264a23ca0cb20a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fce1cda52753ec9e5183762f5b2c81b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3034aa8ff1b6d41ac6e0b8ff655b76ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8caee37338a6383c30fe06ea2b3e4761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5abff9e94aff7675c473268fd21bf551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f41337092de45470ab838aff17309ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-699c5fa3a4d8d093e6a599637df82443&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f892644f7a3eab6b024d8a386777f23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fa5