    </node>
    <node id="Market Surveillance Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Market Surveillance Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">AIOperator</data>
      <data key="d2">Market Surveillance Authorities are essential regulatory entities tasked with monitoring market activities to ensure compliance with regulations and the safety of products, with a particular emphasis on high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) systems. Their primary responsibilities encompass overseeing adherence to established safety standards and regulations across various sectors, including financial markets and technological products. 

These authorities play a pivotal role in managing complaints from individuals and organizations, imposing penalties on market operators for any violations. They have specialized access to critical databases, including the EU Database, which enhances their capability to effectively monitor compliance. This access is vital for regulating high-risk AI systems and supports their mission to ensure these technologies operate safely within compliance boundaries.

In addition to compliance monitoring, Market Surveillance Authorities are tasked with overseeing AI model providers to ensure adherence to relevant regulations and standards. They conduct joint investigations related to AI systems across Member States, which bolsters collaborative efforts in maintaining market integrity. Furthermore, they utilize Exit Reports during conformity assessments, particularly in the context of AI sandbox initiatives, and can seek assistance from Union AI testing support structures during real-world testing of AI systems.

Market Surveillance Authorities are also informed about serious incidents concerning AI systems, allowing them to take necessary actions to protect consumer safety and uphold market standards. They are responsible for monitoring compliance with registration requirements and relevant regulations concerning high-risk AI systems at the national level. Additionally, they are designated bodies overseeing compliance with Union harmonization legislation related to specific categories of high-risk AI systems.

Overall, the comprehensive mandate of Market Surveillance Authorities underscores their crucial role in the regulatory landscape as they actively assess compliance for various products and services, guaranteeing market integrity and consumer safety while enforcing compliance and reporting annual findings to the Commission and competition authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;Market surveillance authorities assess compliance and oversee the adherence to safety and regulatory standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8caee37338a6383c30fe06ea2b3e4761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf8a675497acfbeb420b95621b7cb31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e28e08bfb7b1ae3208e2c91ea6f1e4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c27775e23d04f7dd6b8ec477a62efd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-166a35f517674f4ceba2754c65f88c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75ec68339f2da8ef06976767a0d5b494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0fa7bd172fb09094c2d62c87957967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af24a9a67de887431d611cc88e6df8c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0711090702fd9b1787822998d5deac9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34333cde7ca701413cb4d0a0ef1129e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83ca16d466deaa751e3b9dc390e91e2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53fb2685a38836a165fa7637bbbadce2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d08b537f9a5bb2b4f4bbdf442ba39bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1516ad8d48077af0d59fc01578f33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d58805118916ede230a82a4ec3f60b3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82b1b08be1175d2e6d49ab5a294ef86a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a5e7031602556ef7d57e2811f58992&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0dc307b8b7cb1f0e39aa9b4b1839c408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2806e288e0b71013209c4ad85ecaa38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e978e96ac6d99cf448b53260c07dded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4058e2567f154203a2d9dacec4bdf7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f77911358a1d821f6b1731fac6d2dbd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b90abf0636c26d546e9b6724e3224ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea1514e01d99729cb280141a24250142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af991f85166d6ddfbbf84e4a73207d3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe4515f5aa3b0876e436a8a0dffc23e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e4ea35b819263359794e3a968f44ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98532c431ec75ae38c76dc0730337a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f3c3fe390cb5d40b199e1bcc024928f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-878d589bc7b69ae2d9c3a44284a1badc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_75.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_85.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_131.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_149.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_84.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_130.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_78.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_160.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_88.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_158.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_162.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_45.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_68.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_156.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_76.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_20.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_71.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_161.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863789</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Non High-Risk AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Non High-Risk AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">AIModel</data>
      <data key="d2">Non high-risk AI systems are those that do not meet the criteria outlined in Article 6(3) and are also registered in the EU Database.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857242</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Regulation">
      <data key="d0">EU Regulation</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">EU Regulation outlines the legal framework and requirements for high-risk AI systems in the Union market.&lt;SEP&gt;The EU Regulation sets the legal framework governing the registration and monitoring of AI systems within the EU Database.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f77911358a1d821f6b1731fac6d2dbd6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_71.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Listed in Annex VIII">
      <data key="d0">Data Listed in Annex VIII</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Data listed in Annex VIII comprises the specific information required for entry into the EU Database, categorized into Sections A, B, and C.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857242</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Entry">
      <data key="d0">Data Entry</data>
      <data key="d1">Process</data>
      <data key="d2">Data entry refers to the procedure for inputting information into the EU Database as regulated by the Commission and Member States.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857242</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Authorized Representative">
      <data key="d0">Authorized Representative</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">An authorized representative is a designated individual who may enter data into the EU Database on behalf of the provider or deployer.&lt;SEP&gt;The authorized representative is a person or entity appointed to act on behalf of the provider regarding compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;An authorized representative is an individual or entity designated by the provider to act on their behalf regarding compliance and regulatory matters for the AI system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8af2de29a8b78dd2b512b6eb64d912a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_71.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Authority">
      <data key="d0">Public Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">A public authority is responsible for developing AI systems that safeguard public interest in various fields.&lt;SEP&gt;A public authority refers to government bodies that deploy AI systems and are responsible for their registration in the EU Database.&lt;SEP&gt;A public authority refers to governmental bodies that can deploy AI systems under their jurisdiction according to the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b28a4b325cc05a6cc4897f58ccdf00f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-699b82035d71a633a86a67090e5a61e8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_13.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_71.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_59.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863374</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Legal Authority">
      <data key="d0">Legal Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">HumanInvolvement</data>
      <data key="d2">Legal authority refers to individuals within organizations who have the power to register AI systems and represent providers in the EU Database.&lt;SEP&gt;Legal authority refers to the rights and permissions granted to individuals representing a provider or a deployer in the context of registration and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e4ea35b819263359794e3a968f44ad</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857242</data>
    </node>
    <node id="User-Friendly Interface">
      <data key="d0">User-Friendly Interface</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">The user-friendly interface of the EU Database is designed to enhance accessibility and navigation for all stakeholders.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857242</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical and Administrative Support">
      <data key="d0">Technical and Administrative Support</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">The Commission provides technical and administrative support to entities involved in the registration and maintenance of the EU Database.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857242</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Functional Specifications">
      <data key="d0">Functional Specifications</data>
      <data key="d1">Document</data>
      <data key="d2">Functional specifications are detailed descriptions of the operations and requirements needed for the effective development and monitoring of the EU database.&lt;SEP&gt;Functional specifications detail the requirements and functionalities necessary for the establishment and management of the EU Database.&lt;SEP&gt;Functional specifications outline the operational criteria that the EU Database must fulfill to meet regulatory requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-166a35f517674f4ceba2754c65f88c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2806e288e0b71013209c4ad85ecaa38b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_71.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_131.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863659</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 60">
      <data key="d0">Article 60</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 60 outlines specific legal guidelines related to the testing and compliance of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 60 outlines the conditions under which information must be accessible to market surveillance authorities and the Commission.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 60 outlines the requirements for obtaining informed consent from subjects involved in testing in real-world conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-35a30c75209c0fbb0ca1bb4afe44c77d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba5a4fee300868ea16940c9ea15f534a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e4ea35b819263359794e3a968f44ad</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_61.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_9.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863750</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Prospective Providers">
      <data key="d0">Prospective Providers</data>
      <data key="d1">AIUser</data>
      <data key="d2">Prospective providers are individuals or entities considering offering systems under the regulations and requiring guidance through compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Prospective providers in AI regulatory sandboxes include SMEs and start-ups that seek to develop AI applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0271020749ae70ce56cbd607a6f6662a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e4ea35b819263359794e3a968f44ad</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_71.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_58.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862814</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Support">
      <data key="d0">Technical Support</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical Support is assistance provided by the Commission to Member States for the establishment and operation of AI regulatory sandboxes.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical support is assistance provided by the Commission to help providers and prospective providers navigate the requirements of the regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical support refers to assistance provided related to AI components, which can affect their use and monetization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7ef570a9dfbda3c55d0d5bcc36fd77c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475967c83e624bc711a9ff13e8150163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e4ea35b819263359794e3a968f44ad</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_103.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858696</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Administrative Support">
      <data key="d0">Administrative Support</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Administrative support complements technical assistance by facilitating administrative processes for compliance and registration.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18e4ea35b819263359794e3a968f44ad</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857242</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Competent Authorities">
      <data key="d0">National Competent Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">National Competent Authorities (NCAs) are designated government bodies appointed by Member States to supervise and enforce compliance with artificial intelligence (AI) regulations at the national level. They play a crucial role in the management of AI regulatory sandboxes, which are controlled environments that facilitate the testing and development of AI technologies under legal standards. By overseeing these sandboxes, NCAs ensure that organizations adhere to applicable laws and regulations, thereby fostering both innovation and responsible governance in the field of AI.

The responsibilities of NCAs encompass a wide range of supervisory functions. They provide guidance on AI systems in accordance with Union law and conduct evaluations to identify potential infringements of regulations. NCAs receive notifications about possible violations and are empowered to enforce penalties when necessary, thereby maintaining objectivity and integrity in their operations. They are also tasked with monitoring compliance with regulations, overseeing assessments of AI system providers, and evaluating applications from those providers seeking to operate within the regulatory framework.

In addition, NCAs are responsible for supervising the application of AI regulations, enforcing regulations related to AI models and systems, and providing information to the European Commission regarding AI regulation enforcement. Furthermore, they oversee compliance and are obligated to notify the Commission of serious incidents concerning AI systems.

Overall, National Competent Authorities serve as vital regulatory bodies that uphold AI regulations, support innovation, and promote responsible governance within their jurisdictions. Their independent and impartial exercise of authority is essential for ensuring the safe and ethical development and implementation of AI technologies, while also making necessary documentation accessible and ensuring legislative recognition for participation within the regulatory sandboxes they manage.&lt;SEP&gt;National competent authorities are the entities responsible for ensuring compliance with the EU regulations regarding high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;National competent authorities are organizations within Member States responsible for ensuring compliance with AI regulations and monitoring risk associated with AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fe05ef9eea0acc63f05d5b9d6a147298&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e28e08bfb7b1ae3208e2c91ea6f1e4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75ec68339f2da8ef06976767a0d5b494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4672fd3df7077626af67d20e46d3fcb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6adb64ff4e7b459fa1df815eac98b096&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d64a2a65aec35f8304efaaee30e0034d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0711090702fd9b1787822998d5deac9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-873c3732f26f3ace86c77cfec67991ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a69b68c9998277692ac6c6341fcdcac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34333cde7ca701413cb4d0a0ef1129e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85bb41c1db2d2e1883172e505d5f7b71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0779dfb4a5c0f82f05a67985fe0224a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-184360d53ae652d7f48a919e168f375a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d08b537f9a5bb2b4f4bbdf442ba39bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d42aaf56c15be020feabced14d2409d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc97d8ad7f3aa0522d885f92ee323822&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77093970e26d1be04734ed16ea88f777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdf1c7e7ad7fe2c6b1b8f1b0b12db35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0c31436f0e7ce27ce5952aa2bf9ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72cfde8a7c3c94fdf1dc93c4253bec9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f13d730755b7535c59eb130d6f7ac62e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dc89de2edca5d2bfe0d5e9e7c99665b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95424b9dff57302628c496570b4baff4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dbe8a4749b15b91fcb1062fee4fa778&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdf6e3e080867f88ec52fa9fabbeafd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7859a0c655f74761757b416c3b50bf36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aca56f82b70892874784bcec5c2bb2c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97ee5867d3c03f24001b650ad752686d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11bdaa862215570a86eed137e3092ea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_153.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_78.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_138.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_139.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_58.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_47.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_156.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_101.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_126.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_6.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_154.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_53.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863789</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market Surveillance Authority">
      <data key="d0">Market Surveillance Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">The Market Surveillance Authority is a regulatory body established by Member States to ensure compliance with laws and regulations related to high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) systems and biometric identification technologies. This Authority plays a critical role in monitoring compliance, particularly during the testing phases of AI systems in real-world conditions, to ensure safety, accountability, and adherence to established legal standards.

As a central point of contact, the Market Surveillance Authority gathers and analyzes reports on compliance issues, communicating relevant information to governmental bodies and promoting transparency within its operations. It functions as a notified body, focusing on law enforcement and governmental operations, and evaluates the implementation of laws governing biometric identification systems used in public spaces.

The Authority conducts comprehensive surveillance activities to scrutinize AI systems and confirm their compliance with health, safety, and public interest regulations. It is also equipped to handle complaints regarding regulatory infringements, providing a straightforward reporting mechanism for individuals. When instances of non-compliance are identified, the Market Surveillance Authority has the power to mandate corrective actions and may impose restrictive measures as necessary.

Furthermore, it oversees the approval and regulation of testing plans for high-risk AI systems, ensuring that these technologies align with applicable regulations and standards. This regulatory oversight ultimately fosters responsible and accountable deployment of biometric identification and AI technologies within the market. In summary, the Market Surveillance Authority is instrumental in enforcing compliance, assessing risk classifications of AI systems, and protecting public interests while addressing serious incidents and promoting adherence to regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c361162e59f587f531364714bb3e3c4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa9e2916955e882c73231ed69851f6ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c27775e23d04f7dd6b8ec477a62efd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27c28ab4482e4bec149657c656192c46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4ac0ccf9bd954306cee6efbfd342416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad9c740a10a5c1577e578a593bd61fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb040a8b4e6e3fa6f26776f560b6591c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28daf57045ce50f0bd160cddd41ffc14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-610573a7c194ad780ed97782200a740c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee6d94a5f64203f09d02387acbdb39c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb5ca2a2f12bb39286916d398b70ed9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0779dfb4a5c0f82f05a67985fe0224a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb2802f1b508b813d06e58ae27a1f77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee04f6104a24650416810ede28f3790b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4988a00689afb1245e0f0ce4ceef5921&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f6e14583352886a741ac1d51eada03a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0c31436f0e7ce27ce5952aa2bf9ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2187eb3476528ac7c75b571eb3844f0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4249f491e5466803d0f267a67c5cb39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff61ec794793cf787d4a0473487a06f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13bd6c41d609ae7976a7b3ac4ab8e3fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dbe8a4749b15b91fcb1062fee4fa778&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8da189e7622be67a80b2e12945a657cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8af2de29a8b78dd2b512b6eb64d912a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb3519876fdebea487c9995e6d3ae4fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4882abf1dd869d3dff00b8d88ee946a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07ee6b3452d764ccd9733dceadb1ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e853663a3f2d06a9cfea8582e10f089&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a64bfb94635a0df2f808b2f8a494bd3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4518ca313d8493e277775e1a9267b84d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c72b31b17ef0accd3df4ab25a063163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4c7e75432b8ffa8e0b96687dc4dd380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2440fb0070f3198e96bd1ad753ae3e0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78dcdae0f5d22df28405d8ae03e038d0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_75.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_153.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_85.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_141.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_170.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_81.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_82.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_83.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_77.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_80.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_76.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863820</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Single Point of Contact">
      <data key="d0">Single Point of Contact</data>
      <data key="d1">Purpose</data>
      <data key="d2">The Single Point of Contact provides a coordinated interface between the public and Member States for regulatory matters.&lt;SEP&gt;The single point of contact is a designated authority responsible for communication and coordination regarding the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1dbe8a4749b15b91fcb1062fee4fa778&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_153.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862964</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cybersecurity">
      <data key="d0">Cybersecurity</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">Cybersecurity encompasses a range of protective measures implemented by national competent authorities and organizations to ensure the safety and integrity of systems and data against cyber threats and attacks. It is particularly critical for high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) systems, which require robust safeguards to prevent unauthorized access and manipulation. Effective cybersecurity measures not only protect these systems from potential cyber threats but also ensure their safe operation and functionality. Overall, cybersecurity is essential in providing adequate protection and safeguarding against both external attacks and internal vulnerabilities within AI systems and other digital infrastructures.&lt;SEP&gt;Cybersecurity ensures AI systems are resilient against attacks that compromise their use, behavior, performance, or security.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed5ccbca443324af303d8bca3aa31a38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9685a1f72e235a3f5b9ee69878eedb21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2f186d6b95e69680f63fabb65ad924a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d42aaf56c15be020feabced14d2409d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20ac675fffdeba0fbc242b392d3af8da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5765a06abb615496a937c9303e1583cd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_15.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_76.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_13.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_74.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862763</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human Resources">
      <data key="d0">Human Resources</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Human Resources refer to the personnel needed by national authorities to implement the AI regulations effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Human resources refer to the personnel and expertise provided to national competent authorities to fulfill their regulatory tasks effectively.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863443</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Resources">
      <data key="d0">Technical Resources</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical Resources are the assets required by national competent authorities to fulfill their tasks under the Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical resources are the tools and infrastructure required for national competent authorities to perform their functions effectively.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863443</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Technologies">
      <data key="d0">AI Technologies</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Technologies comprise systems and algorithms that simulate human intelligence and are designed to be accessible to all users, including those with disabilities. These technologies encompass a rapidly developing family of applications that utilize artificial intelligence to perform specific tasks and make informed decisions. They require careful oversight and integration, particularly because they include various tools and systems that national competent authorities must comprehend to implement appropriate regulations effectively. Additionally, certain AI Technologies are classified as high-risk AI systems, mandating proportional monitoring and documentation by their providers to ensure safety and compliance. Overall, AI Technologies represent a crucial and evolving sector that necessitates both regulatory understanding and responsible management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-94b20fb25052b5f99e867bd24213f8f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdf1c7e7ad7fe2c6b1b8f1b0b12db35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33366c5df404f37775ccbf3ec455b578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d42aaf56c15be020feabced14d2409d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f56b40e98f8949a37c3ab283b01f7050</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_138.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_80.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_139.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_72.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863212</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Member State">
      <data key="d0">Member State</data>
      <data key="d1">LocalityOfUse</data>
      <data key="d2">A Member State is a government entity within the European Union (EU) that plays a critical role in the governance, regulation, and oversight of artificial intelligence (AI) systems and other advanced technologies. Each Member State designates authorities for market surveillance to ensure compliance with EU regulations and directives, and to enforce corrective actions related to AI systems.

Under a legal framework established by the EU, Member States possess the jurisdiction and authority to create rules concerning administrative fines, legal infringement procedures, and compliance with EU law. They are responsible for authorizing the use of AI systems, including law enforcement applications and biometric identification systems, and for establishing national competent authorities to oversee adherence to defined guidelines. This oversight ensures that biometric systems function in accordance with overarching laws.

Additionally, Member States manage conformity assessment processes, designate notifying authorities, and assume liability for these assessments, ensuring that notified bodies within their jurisdiction comply with EU standards. They are also tasked with maintaining market surveillance authorities to regulate AI systems actively, and they appoint representatives to various oversight boards as part of their commitment to AI governance.

Moreover, each Member State must inform the EU Commission of any actions taken regarding AI systems, thereby ensuring transparency and compliance with regulatory obligations. They are required to identify public authorities responsible for enforcing compliance and make their lists publicly accessible. Each Member State also reflects the linguistic diversity within the Union, with its own official language facilitating effective communication in administrative and regulatory contexts.

In summary, Member States are pivotal to the EU's regulatory landscape for AI, playing essential roles in the testing, regulation, and oversight of high-risk AI systems. They are active participants in conformity assessment processes while bearing obligations to adhere to notification requirements and take corrective actions as necessary.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-07e8d113bd66975dbb8053a37cc427fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa9e2916955e882c73231ed69851f6ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e28e08bfb7b1ae3208e2c91ea6f1e4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27c28ab4482e4bec149657c656192c46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f41337092de45470ab838aff17309ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a65ec6b0fbd17afe47587686523a725&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc59c087d680631c2a594779449f195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee6d94a5f64203f09d02387acbdb39c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb5ca2a2f12bb39286916d398b70ed9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67ecee9ae9852fb675f5c9c9cb2f2de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b341fa074527a308a2434a3c68244d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0db03f57b007cfc458657e88e273ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-397d6e2474c4f45e883f265653f2e715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2e0f993ca9c4e593e5fcbdd8fc03fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4249f491e5466803d0f267a67c5cb39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff61ec794793cf787d4a0473487a06f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0695d12d62d4fd15a528842231db1850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13bd6c41d609ae7976a7b3ac4ab8e3fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c712c6235ebe0b7ee5102919bbe87d08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2b7ae4447e7d43e6030d6793c59ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97182f6b8815d40f51faf3e8eaeb7c7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28717558f1bb8bd2fd8b9542f8e2a99c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8da189e7622be67a80b2e12945a657cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdf6e3e080867f88ec52fa9fabbeafd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07ee6b3452d764ccd9733dceadb1ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e853663a3f2d06a9cfea8582e10f089&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff611ee371ea780574e9c16859c31f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4c7e75432b8ffa8e0b96687dc4dd380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cc9a7191827dda78eda5924876e5f7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46418d497e0c090818a97380d173293d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2440fb0070f3198e96bd1ad753ae3e0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a350089bbf860c041d514aa2041d9455&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345a8ba89ed0ea3325462384d5e16aaf</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_41.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_18.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_81.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_37.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_82.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_44.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_28.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_83.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_35.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_29.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_21.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_77.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_31.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_37.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863797</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Notifying Authority">
      <data key="d0">Notifying Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">The Notifying Authority is a designated national body established by Member States to supervise and enforce the application of regulations regarding artificial intelligence (AI) systems. Its primary responsibilities encompass overseeing conformity assessment procedures, ensuring that AI systems adhere to regulatory requirements. The Notifying Authority is crucial in setting up, carrying out, and monitoring these assessment procedures, particularly focusing on high-risk AI systems.

This authority plays a pivotal role in communicating regulatory compliance to the European Commission and ensuring the involvement of designated notified bodies in the conformity assessment processes. It is also responsible for receiving applications for notification from conformity assessment bodies, as well as designating these bodies based on compliance with established requirements.

Furthermore, the Notifying Authority ensures ongoing monitoring of notified bodies, keeping the Commission and Member States informed about any changes related to these entities and their activities. The authority is tasked with conducting investigations into matters concerning notified bodies to ensure their continued compliance with regulatory standards.

Overall, the Notifying Authority is essential for maintaining regulatory oversight and ensuring the safety, compliance, and effective governance of AI technologies within its jurisdiction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8caee37338a6383c30fe06ea2b3e4761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f55b689ece7aa049c38fdc38018dba8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1d974005cd87fc21678c732472ee11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff611ee371ea780574e9c16859c31f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c712c6235ebe0b7ee5102919bbe87d08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f79a9fca1518856b24fdcb7e59f040&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dbe8a4749b15b91fcb1062fee4fa778&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0461b38c664574f634a78148bfce0336</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_38.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_34.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_153.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_29.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_33.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_28.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863789</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Confidentiality Obligations">
      <data key="d0">Confidentiality Obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">CodeOfConduct</data>
      <data key="d2">Confidentiality Obligations are a set of legal requirements that dictate how sensitive information, such as trade secrets, must be handled by organizations and competent authorities. These obligations require that information obtained during compliance checks be managed securely and treated according to established protocols, specifically as outlined in Article 78. The purpose of these obligations is to ensure that sensitive information is properly protected and handled, maintaining privacy and confidentiality in the operations of national competent authorities. Additionally, they provide guidelines for how data and other relevant information should be managed during regulatory procedures, reinforcing the importance of safeguarding sensitive information within compliance assessments.&lt;SEP&gt;Confidentiality obligations refer to the legal requirements imposed on market surveillance authorities to protect sensitive information obtained during compliance checks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e853663a3f2d06a9cfea8582e10f089&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5abff9e94aff7675c473268fd21bf551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8512760339eb776d946a91a28089b34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2b7ae4447e7d43e6030d6793c59ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c49e78c25e30ed3a2557915010f14f3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fce1cda52753ec9e5183762f5b2c81b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_21.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_77.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_55.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_53.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863707</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Compliance Reporting">
      <data key="d0">Compliance Reporting</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Compliance reporting involves Member States providing information to the Commission regarding the status and performance of national competent authorities as mandated by the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_70.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857244</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AUthentication Measures">
      <data key="d0">AUthentication Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Authentication measures are necessary steps taken by Member States to ensure that their authorities act without bias and in accordance to established regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-22275ba6343521309923fef233affa2a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_70.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857244</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data">
      <data key="d0">Data</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Data refers to information collected and processed by AI systems, particularly that which is transferred between jurisdictions.&lt;SEP&gt;Data refers to information processed and used by AI systems, including personal data and computed data.&lt;SEP&gt;Data refers to information that can be processed or analyzed, utilized in AI components to deliver intelligent functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;Data refers to the large amounts of information that General-Purpose AI Models are trained on, crucial for their development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d42aaf56c15be020feabced14d2409d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ef570a9dfbda3c55d0d5bcc36fd77c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-161f3120961644fbdc17c7b09b46e54b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_97.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_103.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863925</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Health and Safety Risks">
      <data key="d0">Health and Safety Risks</data>
      <data key="d1">Risk</data>
      <data key="d2">Health and Safety Risks encompass the potential negative impacts on well-being that may arise from the use of the high-risk AI system.&lt;SEP&gt;Health and safety risks are potential threats to wellbeing posed by AI technologies and their deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;Health and safety risks relate to potential dangers posed by high-risk AI systems that the conformity assessment seeks to mitigate.&lt;SEP&gt;Health and Safety Risks pertain to the potential dangers AI systems may pose to individuals and society that warrant regulatory scrutiny.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2440fb0070f3198e96bd1ad753ae3e0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d2cf289e7ae9939fc7fe1d189daf51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d42aaf56c15be020feabced14d2409d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4d62babb1c5a144faeae6ac2f13628</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_13.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_82.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861647</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SMEs">
      <data key="d0">SMEs</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs) play a critical role in the artificial intelligence (AI) ecosystem, especially in the context of the Union market. Recognized as important stakeholders, SMEs are actively considered by regulatory bodies, such as the Commission, when developing guidelines and regulations surrounding AI. Their interests are prioritized in policy discussions, which is crucial for their operation and growth.

SMEs are characterized by their commitment to compliance with regulations while simultaneously enhancing their capabilities in AI technologies. As distinct commercial entities, they serve both as providers and deployers of AI systems. These enterprises navigate the complexities associated with regulatory compliance, addressing the costs involved and seeking guidance to implement AI in adherence to established frameworks. The regulatory framework takes into account the economic viability of SMEs, incorporating provisions regarding penalties that are scaled according to the size and turnover of the enterprise. This proportional approach reflects a commitment to support the sustainability and growth of SMEs during regulatory enforcement actions.

Additionally, SMEs are targeted participants in AI regulatory sandboxes designed to reduce barriers to innovation. These sandboxes allow for access to free resources that assist SMEs, including startups, in meeting compliance with AI regulations. Such initiatives facilitate experimentation and development within the AI landscape. Furthermore, SMEs are involved in the development of standards that ensure balanced representation of interests, highlighting their integral role in shaping future AI implementation.

To support their engagement, SMEs are recognized as entities that can provide technical documentation in a simplified manner under specific regulations, ensuring that they can contribute effectively without being overwhelmed by compliance burdens. Streamlined compliance processes are also targeted towards SMEs to encourage the utilization of AI models, reinforcing their pivotal position in the advancement of AI technologies.

In summary, SMEs are vital contributors to the AI ecosystem, with their capacity to make significant contributions hinging on adequate regulatory support and resources that align with their unique needs and challenges.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ba662546e18e6e5f82c3cd1c5b4c3b75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65c79a1c0cb37c10df906970d376029d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f76666cf495bb0f0810313fe42e2c882&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc97d8ad7f3aa0522d885f92ee323822&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95424b9dff57302628c496570b4baff4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-712b56cbfc73c46eacde9204fa4e5c49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-184360d53ae652d7f48a919e168f375a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e76c1f88e5810a7e79cf9527486831e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6ed86abb2e8f0e12897e923d1e9964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-064e3e5273a81cd8d9a47da9a3f51240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d42aaf56c15be020feabced14d2409d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e24261c10195e33e965bd7e966c33337&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36cb0fd5abf1b169a8aa13021f58c7b2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_121.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_62.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_143.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_109.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_11.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_139.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_58.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_95.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_150.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_145.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863776</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Board">
      <data key="d0">Board</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">The Board is a governing body responsible for the oversight and implementation of regulations concerning artificial intelligence (AI) initiatives. It plays a critical role in ensuring compliance with established regulations and their procedural rules while managing the Advisory Forum process. The Board is charged with making recommendations on the implementation of these regulations and collaborates closely with the AI Office to fulfill the objectives set out in the codes of practice. 

In its capacity, the Board monitors participant adherence to standards, oversees activities related to market surveillance, and specifies tasks as dictated by the regulations. Comprising representatives from Member States, the collective governance of the Board significantly enhances the effective management of AI regulations and initiatives.

Furthermore, the Board is involved in the decision-making process by seeking opinions and recommendations from the Advisory Forum, which it oversees. It also has the authority to specify requests for standardized templates and oversee regulatory practices concerning AI. Additionally, the Board provides input and consultation to the Commission on the classification of AI systems under the Regulation. To address specific regulatory issues, the Board may form standing or temporary sub-groups, further emphasizing its adaptive governance structure aimed at addressing the interests of the AI ecosystem.&lt;SEP&gt;The Board provides oversight and consultation to the AI Office regarding evaluations of AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aacbea1ddddc58fbf14c882b36d9a6b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6de18717bcb0167956be85a15dd210f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83ca16d466deaa751e3b9dc390e91e2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ab4f338bfa06297d4c996d7d54dc70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad86065dee426d0a1db7444552c4a385&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f76666cf495bb0f0810313fe42e2c882&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-699c5fa3a4d8d093e6a599637df82443&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3d60cf6cbe0ae91a9793cb5c98a4a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e75ee11aa912f1497b2a91ae655e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4058e2567f154203a2d9dacec4bdf7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d42aaf56c15be020feabced14d2409d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85d8b1632746db5110bcd9632c1ace58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4dc0271c68856282748506ff58069b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6a5cc59273abbe42c743808026477c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_56.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_92.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_149.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_67.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_62.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_148.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_150.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863846</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Competence and Expertise">
      <data key="d0">Competence and Expertise</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Competence and expertise refer to the skills and knowledge required by personnel in national competent authorities for effective AI oversight.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d42aaf56c15be020feabced14d2409d7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_70.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857244</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Resources">
      <data key="d0">Resources</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Resources encompass the personnel and infrastructure required for national competent authorities to perform their regulatory tasks effectively.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d42aaf56c15be020feabced14d2409d7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_70.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857244</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Data Protection Supervisor">
      <data key="d0">European Data Protection Supervisor</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Data Protection Supervisor (EDPS) is a regulatory authority responsible for overseeing the implementation of data protection laws within European Union (EU) institutions. As a designated competent market surveillance authority, the EDPS ensures that these institutions comply with relevant regulations governing data privacy and protection. This role has expanded to include supervision of Union institutions concerning artificial intelligence (AI) systems, addressing the growing significance of AI in relation to data protection.

To enhance its regulatory oversight, the EDPS may establish AI regulatory sandboxes specifically for Union institutions, allowing for controlled testing and innovation within the framework of applicable regulations. The EDPS also exercises roles typically assigned to national competent authorities and actively participates in Board meetings as an observer, offering valuable insights and contributions to ongoing discussions related to data protection.

In terms of enforcement, the EDPS has the authority to impose administrative fines on Union institutions that fail to comply with data protection regulations, including those specifically related to AI practices. The authority is recognized throughout the EU for its critical role in maintaining the integrity of data protection standards and for managing complaints and litigation associated with data protection issues. Overall, the European Data Protection Supervisor plays a vital role in ensuring the adherence to and enforcement of data protection laws across EU institutions.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Data Protection Supervisor is an independent supervisory authority responsible for ensuring compliance with data protection regulation in the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Data Protection Supervisor acts as a market surveillance authority for Union institutions and bodies under this regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1b43f399350f0fc36795c0ce358459d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475967c83e624bc711a9ff13e8150163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-111c71f234a0f2d1b26490907acae6eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72cfde8a7c3c94fdf1dc93c4253bec9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e28e08bfb7b1ae3208e2c91ea6f1e4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5da2f6b1c2fa5619efa26719534e9c35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-828a2d9070cae319b764e3b609bc9b81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc97d8ad7f3aa0522d885f92ee323822&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-472b03a027e3fcae21e86e23849e4510&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0271020749ae70ce56cbd607a6f6662a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0711090702fd9b1787822998d5deac9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb</data>
