      <data key="d5">1750863356</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulated Financial Institutions">
      <data key="d0">Regulated Financial Institutions</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulated Financial Institutions are organizations that use AI systems as part of their financial services offerings, governed by Union Financial Services Law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711f6ce0c9e8f119b1813ffe001673da</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857259</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Competent Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Competent Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Competent Authorities are designated governmental bodies with a critical role in overseeing and enforcing regulations related to artificial intelligence (AI) systems, particularly in accordance with Union Financial Services Law. Their primary responsibilities include the supervision, application, and enforcement of laws pertaining to high-risk AI systems. These authorities are tasked with regulating compliance by assessing and granting permissions for biometric identification systems and imposing administrative fines for noncompliance.

To ensure the integrity and safety of AI applications, Competent Authorities require detailed information to evaluate the conformity of high-risk AI systems. They manage AI regulatory sandboxes—controlled environments that facilitate experimentation with AI applications—allocating resources and providing guidance on regulatory expectations to enhance accountability and efficacy. Additionally, Competent Authorities support compliance with AI regulations by overseeing access to critical data necessary for the development and validation of AI systems.

Their jurisdiction extends beyond the financial sector, encompassing areas such as migration and asylum applications, which demonstrates their broad mandate in governance and regulatory practices. Competent Authorities are also responsible for implementing law enforcement measures and ensuring compliance with data protection regulations and guidelines at both Union and national levels. 

In summary, Competent Authorities serve as pivotal entities in establishing a regulated framework for the development, testing, and implementation of AI technologies across various sectors, ensuring adherence to regulatory standards and safeguarding compliance with laws, including those related to data processing concerning criminal offenses.&lt;SEP&gt;Competent authorities are designated bodies responsible for overseeing compliance and addressing serious incidents in AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Competent authorities are the designated bodies that oversee the investigation and compliance pertaining to serious incidents of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13b35a74627bd926656242d6545e09a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee1f186f5aed070bc8e6e813caed9967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6adb64ff4e7b459fa1df815eac98b096&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85fb9638473c0974347ccab540b99b7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85bb41c1db2d2e1883172e505d5f7b71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c1d05b847c03fe702172f787883fc33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577494efd5ce842563e6974b0da9707b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00e7606a0fa9d588f18d67d02cfcf654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21678b36bef336bf18e091bdfdb68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3cb5eb81289d4fb565bd824bdc63506&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b567607dbb431b0d294cd02679760039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a46250ea72037444e96653239f2893b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475967c83e624bc711a9ff13e8150163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0c31436f0e7ce27ce5952aa2bf9ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d44e4d07784e334a8ded2c1da49b969e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95424b9dff57302628c496570b4baff4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0dc307b8b7cb1f0e39aa9b4b1839c408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eae051373e28d701c4893438950556b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f77911358a1d821f6b1731fac6d2dbd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4882abf1dd869d3dff00b8d88ee946a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50be48c46c67191e901c756873069fcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711f6ce0c9e8f119b1813ffe001673da</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_140.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_10.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_141.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_158.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_139.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_167.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_68.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_38.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Central Bank">
      <data key="d0">European Central Bank</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeveloper</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Central Bank is involved in prudential supervisory tasks and oversees credit institution compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Central Bank is responsible for implementing policies regarding the supervisory framework for credit institutions under the mentioned European regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Central Bank provides oversight and takes interest in market surveillance activities conducted by national authorities, particularly concerning AI systems in credit institutions.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Central Bank is the authority that receives reports from national market surveillance regarding AI systems that may interest prudential supervisory tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Central Bank oversees financial stability and supervises high-risk AI systems relevant to financial services.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f12c01099dadb1fc1008ce18c7d800e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfa4c0995d224333f53196e26a30156b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711f6ce0c9e8f119b1813ffe001673da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8da189e7622be67a80b2e12945a657cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af24a9a67de887431d611cc88e6df8c6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_158.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863698</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2013/36/EU">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2013/36/EU</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2013/36/EU establishes a comprehensive framework for the activities of credit institutions and investment firms within the European Union, emphasizing the importance of prudential supervision. It plays a critical role in regulating these entities and overseeing their operations in the financial sector. The directive outlines the relationship between credit institutions and AI systems, focusing on risk management in compliance with Union Financial Services Law. Furthermore, it governs the access to and supervision of these financial institutions, ensuring they adhere to the regulatory standards set forth. Directive 2013/36/EU is also significant for credit institutions that participate in the Single Supervisory Mechanism, reinforcing its relevance for compliance and operational integrity within the EU financial landscape.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f12c01099dadb1fc1008ce18c7d800e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711f6ce0c9e8f119b1813ffe001673da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b0054dbaea0e7f90c303fe7d7a824d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8da189e7622be67a80b2e12945a657cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af24a9a67de887431d611cc88e6df8c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18f422febe10e4293aaf989ea5e3d3e8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_158.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863700</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market Surveillance Activities">
      <data key="d0">Market Surveillance Activities</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Market Surveillance Activities refer to the actions taken by authorities to monitor the market for AI systems to ensure compliance with relevant regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Market Surveillance Activities refer to the monitoring of AI systems by national authorities to ensure compliance with Union Financial Services Law.&lt;SEP&gt;Market surveillance activities involve monitoring and enforcement processes conducted by authorities to ensure compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Market surveillance activities refer to the actions taken by designated authorities to ensure compliance with regulations, particularly regarding high-risk AI systems, without affecting judicial independence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9c27775e23d04f7dd6b8ec477a62efd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711f6ce0c9e8f119b1813ffe001673da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53fb2685a38836a165fa7637bbbadce2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_158.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_85.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863695</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Internal Governance Rules">
      <data key="d0">Internal Governance Rules</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Internal Governance Rules entail the internal policies and measures that regulated financial institutions must implement as part of their compliance with Union Financial Services Law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711f6ce0c9e8f119b1813ffe001673da</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857259</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk-Management Rules">
      <data key="d0">Risk-Management Rules</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Risk-Management Rules are part of Union Financial Services Law, focusing on the measures that financial institutions need to adopt to manage risks associated with their operations, especially when utilizing AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711f6ce0c9e8f119b1813ffe001673da</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857259</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Post Marketing Monitoring">
      <data key="d0">Post Marketing Monitoring</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Post Marketing Monitoring refers to ongoing evaluations of AI Systems by providers and deployers to ensure compliance with risk management and quality standards under applicable laws.&lt;SEP&gt;Post marketing monitoring refers to the ongoing oversight of financial products after they have been released to the market.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-af24a9a67de887431d611cc88e6df8c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711f6ce0c9e8f119b1813ffe001673da</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857259</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Legal Acts">
      <data key="d0">Legal Acts</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Legal acts are pieces of legislation that outline the requirements and processes for assessing high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Legal acts provide the framework for compliance and control over high-risk AI systems to ensure they meet necessary standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The Legal Acts mentioned provide a framework of regulations to which financial institutions must adhere when operating AI Systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Legal acts refer to the set of laws and regulations that the Commission must adhere to and ensure compliance with in the documentation processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c72b31b17ef0accd3df4ab25a063163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bfb9287798720e37fcd8bae961e88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e5d20a8e9427a4698b84f758676994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711f6ce0c9e8f119b1813ffe001673da</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_11.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863780</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Council Regulation (EU) No 1024/2013">
      <data key="d0">Council Regulation (EU) No 1024/2013</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Council Regulation (EU) No 1024/2013 establishes the Single Supervisory Mechanism for financial institutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Council Regulation (EU) No 1024/2013 pertains to specific tasks assigned to the European Central Bank regarding the prudential supervision of credit institutions.&lt;SEP&gt;This regulation assigns specific responsibilities to the European Central Bank regarding prudential supervision of credit institutions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-af24a9a67de887431d611cc88e6df8c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b0054dbaea0e7f90c303fe7d7a824d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfa4c0995d224333f53196e26a30156b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857264</data>
    </node>
    <node id="insurance and re-insurance undertakings">
      <data key="d0">insurance and re-insurance undertakings</data>
      <data key="d1">AISubject</data>
      <data key="d2">Insurance and re-insurance undertakings are financial institutions subject to specific regulatory requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-af24a9a67de887431d611cc88e6df8c6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857264</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2009/138/EC">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2009/138/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2009/138/EC outlines the requirements for insurance and reinsurance undertakings within the Solvency II framework.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2009/138/EC outlines the requirements for insurance business operations within the European Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-af24a9a67de887431d611cc88e6df8c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18f422febe10e4293aaf989ea5e3d3e8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857264</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive (EU) 2016/97">
      <data key="d0">Directive (EU) 2016/97</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive (EU) 2016/97 regulates insurance distribution in the European Union, ensuring standardization and protection for consumers.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive (EU) 2016/97 regulates the activities of insurance intermediaries, ensuring consistency and compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;This directive governs the distribution of insurance products across the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b0054dbaea0e7f90c303fe7d7a824d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af24a9a67de887431d611cc88e6df8c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18f422febe10e4293aaf989ea5e3d3e8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857264</data>
    </node>
    <node id="financial institutions">
      <data key="d0">financial institutions</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">Financial institutions are governed by various directives and regulations to maintain internal governance and operational standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Financial institutions are organizations that must adhere to specific legal frameworks regarding governance and documentation for operating AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Financial institutions as deployers of AI systems have specific regulations and governance requirements to follow as part of their operational framework.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-af24a9a67de887431d611cc88e6df8c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8c5a915dca180e1c423cefa27ea6cd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46418d497e0c090818a97380d173293d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_158.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_18.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862998</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Credit Institutions">
      <data key="d0">Credit Institutions</data>
      <data key="d1">AISubject</data>
      <data key="d2">Credit institutions are financial organizations that are subject to supervision under Directive 2013/36/EU and related regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Credit institutions are the entities that are subject to prudential supervision as per the European regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-af24a9a67de887431d611cc88e6df8c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfa4c0995d224333f53196e26a30156b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857264</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Insurance and Re-Insurance Undertakings">
      <data key="d0">Insurance and Re-Insurance Undertakings</data>
      <data key="d1">AISubject</data>
      <data key="d2">Insurance and re-insurance undertakings are financial institutions subject to specific regulatory requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-af24a9a67de887431d611cc88e6df8c6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857264</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Procedural Obligations">
      <data key="d0">Procedural Obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Procedural obligations refer to the requirements imposed on financial institutions to ensure proper risk management and documentation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-af24a9a67de887431d611cc88e6df8c6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857264</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Prudential Supervisory Tasks">
      <data key="d0">Prudential Supervisory Tasks</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Prudential supervisory tasks ensure that financial institutions operate safely and soundly in the financial system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-af24a9a67de887431d611cc88e6df8c6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857264</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2008/48/EC">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2008/48/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2008/48/EC lays down the rules for credit agreements targeting consumers and addresses important consumer protections.&lt;SEP&gt;This directive covers consumer credit agreements and was amended by Directive 2014/17/EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b0054dbaea0e7f90c303fe7d7a824d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18f422febe10e4293aaf989ea5e3d3e8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857264</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2014/17/EU">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2014/17/EU</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2014/17/EU deals with credit agreements related to residential real estate and coordinates existing directives for consumer protection and lending.&lt;SEP&gt;This directive pertains to credit agreements for consumers related to residential property in the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b0054dbaea0e7f90c303fe7d7a824d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18f422febe10e4293aaf989ea5e3d3e8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857264</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) No 575/2013">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) No 575/2013</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) No 575/2013 sets prudential requirements for credit institutions and investment firms, contributing to the stability of the financial sector.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18f422febe10e4293aaf989ea5e3d3e8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857264</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2002/87/EC">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2002/87/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2002/87/EC relates to the supplementary supervision of financial conglomerates within the European Union, enhancing oversight and regulatory compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;This directive addresses the financial supervision of financial conglomerates in the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b0054dbaea0e7f90c303fe7d7a824d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18f422febe10e4293aaf989ea5e3d3e8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_158.json</data>
