      <data key="d5">1750863499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Criminal Offense">
      <data key="d0">Criminal Offense</data>
      <data key="d1">RiskConcept</data>
      <data key="d2">A criminal offense is an act that violates the law, resulting in legal prosecution and potential incarceration.&lt;SEP&gt;A criminal offense is an action that violates laws and can be predicted or assessed using AI systems based on a person’s behavior or characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;Any action that constitutes a violation of law and may result in legal prosecution, specifically relevant in the context of AI system deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4988a00689afb1245e0f0ce4ceef5921&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83317eda1161cf5d13ef9aa07297c98b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0073df6368131f4f385a66430ef1c4f4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Facial Images">
      <data key="d0">Facial Images</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Facial images are visual data collected from various sources, which are used to create or expand facial recognition databases in AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Facial images refer to pictures used for various purposes, including identification and analysis within AI systems, often sourced from the internet or CCTV footage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-83317eda1161cf5d13ef9aa07297c98b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1be166c61f466e23c3d8c143f6efd3bb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857268</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CCTV Footage">
      <data key="d0">CCTV Footage</data>
      <data key="d1">DataSource</data>
      <data key="d2">CCTV footage consists of recorded video images captured by surveillance cameras used for security, which may include facial data for AI processing.&lt;SEP&gt;CCTV footage refers to video recordings from surveillance cameras, which may be scraped for facial recognition use in AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;CCTV footage refers to video recordings used for surveillance, which can be utilized in facial recognition systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a46d97529092ce970fc3194f0ff15f99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83317eda1161cf5d13ef9aa07297c98b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1be166c61f466e23c3d8c143f6efd3bb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_43.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857511</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Biometric Data">
      <data key="d0">Biometric Data</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Biometric Data refers to personal information derived from the unique biological characteristics of individuals, utilized primarily for identification and categorization purposes. This encompasses a variety of physical attributes, including but not limited to fingerprints, facial recognition data, iris scans, and various physiological and behavioral features. Such data plays an essential role in identification processes, particularly within advanced technologies like artificial intelligence systems deployed in law enforcement and emotion recognition.

The processing of Biometric Data involves technical means to derive insights about individuals' physical or behavioral traits, which can extend to inferring emotions or intentions. Due to the sensitive nature of this information, Biometric Data is deemed high-risk personal data, given its potential for misuse and the serious implications of privacy violations associated with its handling.

The collection and use of Biometric Data are subject to stringent regulations under data protection laws, particularly those enforced by the European Union. These regulations underscore the necessity of safeguarding sensitive personal information, requiring rigorous monitoring to ensure compliance with privacy standards. Thus, managing Biometric Data involves the protection of individuals' personal identifiers across various applications, highlighting the importance of adhering to ethical standards in its handling.

In summary, Biometric Data is specific to individuals and derived from distinctive biological traits, and it is bound by enhanced regulatory frameworks that aim to ensure the privacy and security of identifiable individuals while addressing the significant privacy concerns associated with its use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-83317eda1161cf5d13ef9aa07297c98b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27c28ab4482e4bec149657c656192c46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee1f186f5aed070bc8e6e813caed9967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-498834b2d84eaf9afe4e5fb0df15933c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ac98f64f8751ad51246ca16d843f030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d1a48b7c6d78e001878383cb0acaf58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3070277451614bdc67954ec8735dd80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-737358b61293029e1a6d7326160654fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dead6db59d178a53a4fc03ed67a92e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f62cf38e10f73dd06a997571902c1ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac04e8bc9dd9ff3998ce3c08f3800f57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61cbf514bcfe4869e269c00a2dc9e712&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1be166c61f466e23c3d8c143f6efd3bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1b92a727425c41637e16da3cb9ac9c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0073df6368131f4f385a66430ef1c4f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb43ec5a01dc502046ab6ffbe3a25504&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65e9562dd645622f1390ba1863fee19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4882abf1dd869d3dff00b8d88ee946a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc038db2f25d511bf84cccc9550e10c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62c8c9618d935cf8910927a7d518c1f2</data>
