    <node id="Publicly Accessible Spaces">
      <data key="d0">Publicly Accessible Spaces</data>
      <data key="d1">LocalityOfUse</data>
      <data key="d2">Publicly Accessible Spaces are environments where AI systems may be employed for biometric identification, impacting privacy and regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Publicly accessible spaces are areas open to the general population where biometric identification systems may be deployed for law enforcement.&lt;SEP&gt;Publicly accessible spaces are locations where the use of the biometric identification system can be implemented, subject to specific authorizations.&lt;SEP&gt;Publicly accessible spaces are areas open to the public, which must not include specific restricted locations like prisons or border control.&lt;SEP&gt;Publicly accessible spaces are locations where AI systems are deployed for the identification of individuals, raising privacy concerns.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1be166c61f466e23c3d8c143f6efd3bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4249f491e5466803d0f267a67c5cb39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4013941d0b165f5643b927164f2ffd1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee1f186f5aed070bc8e6e813caed9967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab148daacc5693b15ec462635a5502a7</data>
