      <data key="d5">1750863281</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human Rights">
      <data key="d0">Human Rights</data>
      <data key="d1">LegalBasis</data>
      <data key="d2">Human rights are fundamental rights that should be respected and upheld in the development and deployment of AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Human rights are the fundamental rights to which all individuals are entitled, directly influenced by the use and regulations of biometric data.&lt;SEP&gt;Human rights encompass the fundamental rights and freedoms that individuals are entitled to, which may be affected by AI use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bbcf833252ce65fd6a1d8bd1f5a6efc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-849f8f0403e6b12fa8a9c24b84c094c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1be166c61f466e23c3d8c143f6efd3bb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_27.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_59.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862933</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fundamental Rights Impact Assessment">
      <data key="d0">Fundamental Rights Impact Assessment</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">A fundamental rights impact assessment evaluates the potential effects of using biometric systems on individuals' rights and freedoms.&lt;SEP&gt;A fundamental rights impact assessment is a process required before deploying biometric systems in order to evaluate their implications on individual freedoms.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fundamental Rights Impact Assessment evaluates the potential impacts of using biometric systems on individuals' rights and freedoms, required before system authorization.&lt;SEP&gt;A fundamental rights impact assessment is a process to identify risks to individuals' rights prior to the deployment of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ffc59c087d680631c2a594779449f195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0073df6368131f4f385a66430ef1c4f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-239d42cf353b4be7fdeade1f3fced85d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a1d78baf29c07c65edc311f0ca04126</data>
