    <node id="Missing Persons Search">
      <data key="d0">Missing Persons Search</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">The search for missing persons is an initiative aimed at locating individuals who have disappeared and may be in danger.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0073df6368131f4f385a66430ef1c4f4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857271</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Imminent Threat">
      <data key="d0">Imminent Threat</data>
      <data key="d1">Risk</data>
      <data key="d2">An imminent threat involves a specific and substantial risk to the life or safety of individuals, prompting the need for urgent action.&lt;SEP&gt;An imminent threat refers to a serious, immediate danger to life or physical safety which may arise from various conditions or events.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0073df6368131f4f385a66430ef1c4f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a23e03a78af2035b69e69bd4fc65a435</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_33.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857807</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Terrorist Attack">
      <data key="d0">Terrorist Attack</data>
      <data key="d1">Risk</data>
      <data key="d2">A terrorist attack is a violent act intended to instill fear and cause harm, recognized as a major threat to public safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0073df6368131f4f385a66430ef1c4f4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857271</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Criminal Investigation">
      <data key="d0">Criminal Investigation</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Criminal investigations are processes undertaken by law enforcement to uncover facts about a crime and identify suspects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0073df6368131f4f385a66430ef1c4f4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857271</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Custodial Sentence">
      <data key="d0">Custodial Sentence</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">A custodial sentence is a legal punishment requiring an offender to be imprisoned for a set duration.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0073df6368131f4f385a66430ef1c4f4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857271</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Real-Time Remote Biometric Identification System">
      <data key="d0">Real-Time Remote Biometric Identification System</data>
      <data key="d1">AISystem</data>
      <data key="d2">The 'real-time' remote biometric identification system is used in publicly accessible spaces for law enforcement purposes and requires prior judicial authorization.&lt;SEP&gt;The Real-Time Remote Biometric Identification System is a technology used in publicly accessible spaces for law enforcement purposes, subject to strict regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Real-Time Remote Biometric Identification System is utilized for law enforcement in publicly accessible spaces, necessitating authorizations and assessments regarding its use.&lt;SEP&gt;This system captures and compares biometric data for identification with minimal delay, facilitating instant identification.&lt;SEP&gt;This system captures, compares, and identifies biometric data without significant delays, enabling instant or nearly instant identification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ffc59c087d680631c2a594779449f195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4249f491e5466803d0f267a67c5cb39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27c28ab4482e4bec149657c656192c46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a94885e0b736d24263914e9a9d565900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e726a1ef8f481d54c995afc6a028f60</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Judicial Authority">
      <data key="d0">Judicial Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">Judicial Authorities are legal bodies that must provide authorization for the use of high-risk AI systems in specific scenarios, ensuring oversight and accountability.&lt;SEP&gt;Judicial authorities are independent bodies that grant authorization for the use of the biometric identification system based on a reasoned request.&lt;SEP&gt;The Judicial Authority is responsible for granting prior authorizations for the use of biometric identification systems in line with national law.&lt;SEP&gt;Judicial authorities that deploy AI systems to aid in decision-making regarding legal matters and administration of justice.&lt;SEP&gt;Judicial authorities are responsible for granting authorization for the use of high-risk AI systems in specific investigations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ffc59c087d680631c2a594779449f195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4988a00689afb1245e0f0ce4ceef5921&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-543cc911c9d837b54a06d5f6ca958b34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4249f491e5466803d0f267a67c5cb39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bece07e296fce9647a40a0dde904fe4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_61.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863013</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Independent Administrative Authority">
      <data key="d0">Independent Administrative Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">Independent Administrative Authorities are designated bodies that have the legal authority to make binding decisions without external influence.&lt;SEP&gt;Independent administrative authorities are entities that can provide binding decisions on the use of biometric identification systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Independent Administrative Authority is tasked with overseeing the authorization of biometric system use, ensuring compliance with legal frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ffc59c087d680631c2a594779449f195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-911571ee28a1070a8fcc503dd5d91e14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4249f491e5466803d0f267a67c5cb39</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857271</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Seriousness">
      <data key="d0">Seriousness</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Seriousness refers to the level of potential harm that a system might cause if not used, relevant for assessing risk in AI applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ffc59c087d680631c2a594779449f195</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857271</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Probability">
      <data key="d0">Probability</data>
      <data key="d1">Metric</data>
      <data key="d2">Probability indicates the likelihood of an event, such as the likelihood of harm occurring during a criminal act.&lt;SEP&gt;Probability measures the likelihood of harm occurring as a result of not using the system, which is critical for evaluating AI risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ffc59c087d680631c2a594779449f195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a23e03a78af2035b69e69bd4fc65a435</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_33.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857807</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Scale of Harm">
      <data key="d0">Scale of Harm</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Scale of Harm represents the extent or magnitude of the harm that could result from the lack of a system's use, important in risk assessments.&lt;SEP&gt;Scale of harm refers to the magnitude of injury or damage that can arise from a particular criminal offense.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ffc59c087d680631c2a594779449f195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a23e03a78af2035b69e69bd4fc65a435</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_33.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857807</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Consequences of Use">
      <data key="d0">Consequences of Use</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Consequences of Use cover the potential impacts on the rights and freedoms of individuals as a result of using the system.&lt;SEP&gt;Consequences of use refer to the potential impacts that the implementation of biometric systems may have on individuals and society as a whole.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ffc59c087d680631c2a594779449f195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-239d42cf353b4be7fdeade1f3fced85d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_34.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863646</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Authorisation">
      <data key="d0">Authorisation</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Authorisation is the formal approval required for the use of biometric identification systems, overseen by judicial or independent authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ffc59c087d680631c2a594779449f195</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857271</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Law">
      <data key="d0">National Law</data>
      <data key="d1">LegalBasis</data>
      <data key="d2">National Law refers to the legal frameworks, principles, and statutes established within individual countries, dictating requirements and regulations across various domains, including the development, testing, and deployment of artificial intelligence (AI) systems and the use of biometric data. It complements Union Law by specifying regulations for processing personal data in relation to AI system development and evaluations. National Law encompasses local statutes that may provide exceptions or restrictions regarding individuals' rights when interacting with AI systems and includes specific guidelines for the use and categorization of biometric systems in member states.

Additionally, National Law governs jurisdiction-specific regulations that impact the testing and deployment of high-risk AI systems, ensuring alignment with Union Law concerning AI regulation and data processing. It also incorporates provisions that safeguard local labor rights, asserting that these should not be undermined by broader regulatory frameworks. Overall, National Law plays a crucial role in governing the deployment and use of AI systems within their respective jurisdictions, necessitating careful consideration of local legal requirements alongside overarching Union directives.&lt;SEP&gt;National Law refers to the legislation of individual countries that can modify or exempt certain aspects of verification requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ffc59c087d680631c2a594779449f195&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13b35a74627bd926656242d6545e09a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eea61d03ab615ac5f518e77cd220c1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a23e03a78af2035b69e69bd4fc65a435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff61ec794793cf787d4a0473487a06f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf8a675497acfbeb420b95621b7cb31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-727225adfedcad573a12c2ed92e8ee1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3070277451614bdc67954ec8735dd80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c664ec81872dda212b64d449aa7a2014&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ed67e673a6fe0a3c79a41bb9102d44b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2612abd3c26dca69a0acec30add3ef15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b474f9815c7033ca1ad8daff4012eff</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_78.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_63.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_33.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_30.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_167.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_171.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_92.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_9.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_59.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863737</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Urgency Cases">
      <data key="d0">Urgency Cases</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Urgency Cases involve situations that allow for the deployment of systems without prior authorisation, focusing on immediate needs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ffc59c087d680631c2a594779449f195</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857271</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Judicial Authority's Decision">
      <data key="d0">Judicial Authority's Decision</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Judicial Authority's Decision must be binding and is necessary for authorising the use of biometric identification systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ffc59c087d680631c2a594779449f195</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857271</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Discarding">
      <data key="d0">Data Discarding</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Discarding refers to the requirement to immediately delete all data and results if authorisation is rejected, ensuring compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ffc59c087d680631c2a594779449f195</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857271</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Clear Indications">
      <data key="d0">Clear Indications</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Clear Indications represent the objective evidence that a Judicial Authority needs to grant authorisation for system use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ffc59c087d680631c2a594779449f195</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857271</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Protection Authority">
      <data key="d0">Data Protection Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeveloper</data>
      <data key="d2">The national data protection authority oversees compliance with data protection regulations when biometric identification systems are used.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4249f491e5466803d0f267a67c5cb39</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857271</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sensitive Operational Data">
      <data key="d0">Sensitive Operational Data</data>
      <data key="d1">SensitiveData</data>
      <data key="d2">Sensitive Operational Data refers to critical and confidential information that must be safeguarded due to its sensitive nature. This type of data encompasses confidential information regarding law enforcement activities, particularly those that are essential for the prevention and investigation of criminal offenses. The disclosure of such data could potentially jeopardize ongoing criminal proceedings and undermine legal processes. Sensitive Operational Data is explicitly protected from being included in public disclosures, such as annual reports, as well as from notifications regarding the use of the system it relates to. In essence, it includes any information that is deemed critical for maintaining the integrity and security of law enforcement operations, thereby governed by strict regulations to prevent unauthorized access or public release.&lt;SEP&gt;Sensitive operational data relates to activities of law enforcement, border control, immigration, or asylum, which are protected from public disclosure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4249f491e5466803d0f267a67c5cb39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e726a1ef8f481d54c995afc6a028f60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50be48c46c67191e901c756873069fcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-911571ee28a1070a8fcc503dd5d91e14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ac98f64f8751ad51246ca16d843f030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2612abd3c26dca69a0acec30add3ef15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07ee6b3452d764ccd9733dceadb1ac7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_59.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863383</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Notification Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Notification Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Notification requirements specify the necessary information that must be provided to authorities when using biometric identification systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4249f491e5466803d0f267a67c5cb39</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857271</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Previous Authorisation">
      <data key="d0">Previous Authorisation</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Previous authorisation refers to the mandatory approval required before implementing the biometric identification system in designated areas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4249f491e5466803d0f267a67c5cb39</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857271</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Urgent Situations">
      <data key="d0">Urgent Situations</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Urgent situations refer to instances where the biometric system may be deployed without prior authorisation but requires subsequent notification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4249f491e5466803d0f267a67c5cb39</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857271</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Objective Evidence">
      <data key="d0">Objective Evidence</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Objective evidence is necessary for judicial authorities to determine the necessity and proportionality of using the biometric system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4249f491e5466803d0f267a67c5cb39</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857271</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Adverse Legal Effect">
      <data key="d0">Adverse Legal Effect</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">An adverse legal effect can arise from decisions made solely on the output of the biometric identification system without additional evidence.&lt;SEP&gt;An adverse legal effect refers to a negative outcome for an individual resulting from decisions based solely on biometric identification system outputs.&lt;SEP&gt;An adverse legal effect is a negative outcome that can arise from decisions influenced solely by the outputs generated by an AI system.&lt;SEP&gt;An adverse legal effect refers to any decision or action that negatively impacts an individual's legal rights, particularly in context of decisions made by law enforcement authorities based solely on AI outputs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-27c28ab4482e4bec149657c656192c46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-071372b252509d0e29e64264c0511359&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4882abf1dd869d3dff00b8d88ee946a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4249f491e5466803d0f267a67c5cb39</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_35.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863020</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Data Protection Authority">
      <data key="d0">National Data Protection Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">National Data Protection Authorities oversee data protection rules, including those applying to biometric identification systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The National Data Protection Authority is responsible for overseeing compliance with data protection laws relating to biometric data use.&lt;SEP&gt;National data protection authorities oversee the adherence to data protection laws and may require reports from AI system deployers.&lt;SEP&gt;The National Data Protection Authority oversees compliance and ensures protection measures related to personal data processing are followed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4988a00689afb1245e0f0ce4ceef5921&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27c28ab4482e4bec149657c656192c46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4882abf1dd869d3dff00b8d88ee946a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2187eb3476528ac7c75b571eb3844f0e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annual Reports">
      <data key="d0">Annual Reports</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Annual Reports are formal documents submitted by national competent authorities to the AI Office and the Commission, serving multiple purposes related to the regulation and oversight of artificial intelligence and biometric systems. These reports detail the activities and findings associated with AI regulatory sandboxes, summarizing their implementation, progress, results, best practices, and recommendations. Additionally, they provide information on the use of biometric systems across Member States, including specific details about remote biometric identification systems used for law enforcement. By aggregating data on these systems, the Annual Reports offer insights into their applications and compliance within the legal and regulatory frameworks established by the authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;Annual reports are documents submitted by deployers of high-risk AI systems to oversight authorities detailing the usage and compliance of such systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Annual reports are required from deployers to summarize the usage of high-risk AI systems, focusing on compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4988a00689afb1245e0f0ce4ceef5921&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85bb41c1db2d2e1883172e505d5f7b71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27c28ab4482e4bec149657c656192c46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50be48c46c67191e901c756873069fcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-184360d53ae652d7f48a919e168f375a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-911571ee28a1070a8fcc503dd5d91e14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6adb64ff4e7b459fa1df815eac98b096&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4882abf1dd869d3dff00b8d88ee946a8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Detailed Rules">
      <data key="d0">Detailed Rules</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Detailed Rules are the necessary regulations imposed by Member States to govern the use and supervision of biometric identification systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-27c28ab4482e4bec149657c656192c46</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857271</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Notification">
      <data key="d0">Notification</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Notification is the procedure through which Member States inform relevant authorities about the use of biometric identification systems in public spaces.&lt;SEP&gt;Notification refers to the communication process between the Market Surveillance Authority and the Commission about the issued authorizations for high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Notification refers to the formal communication that initiates the consultation process concerning AI practices as stipulated in Article 79(5).&lt;SEP&gt;Notification is the process whereby providers inform the Commission about a general-purpose AI model that meets specific conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-27c28ab4482e4bec149657c656192c46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4c7e75432b8ffa8e0b96687dc4dd380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e23bb4c71b510fec0bbe6570de37cd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee6d94a5f64203f09d02387acbdb39c5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_81.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862916</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Rules">
      <data key="d0">National Rules</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">National Rules are guidelines defined by Member States that outline the specifics of using biometric systems for law enforcement.&lt;SEP&gt;National Rules are legislative measures taken by member states to ensure the trustworthy and safe development of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-27c28ab4482e4bec149657c656192c46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae8bdbb57af24d78fe2313201571bea7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863288</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Laws">
      <data key="d0">National Laws</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">National laws dictate the rules and regulations governing the use and supervision of remote biometric identification systems by Member States.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50be48c46c67191e901c756873069fcb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857274</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Criminal Offences">
      <data key="d0">Criminal Offences</data>
      <data key="d1">RiskConcept</data>
      <data key="d2">Criminal offences are acts that are punishable by law, and the processing of personal data must comply with legal standards in this context.&lt;SEP&gt;Criminal offences are types of crimes that may be targeted for law enforcement using biometric identification systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Legal justifications that may exempt the publishing of AI-generated content from disclosure if related to ongoing investigations.&lt;SEP&gt;Criminal offences include various illegal acts listed within the legal framework that may involve identification for law enforcement purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Criminal offenses are illegal acts that AI systems may evaluate risks for, including the likelihood of reoffending or victimization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50cb89ed7d0d818018d373ebefa65267&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a23e03a78af2035b69e69bd4fc65a435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50be48c46c67191e901c756873069fcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ba8e0dd4981bd71dedb04a86b45601&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3cb5eb81289d4fb565bd824bdc63506</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_59.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_10.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_33.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862933</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Judicial Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Judicial Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">AISubject</data>
      <data key="d2">Judicial Authorities are competent bodies that issue binding decisions regarding requests for authorizations under the law.&lt;SEP&gt;Judicial authorities are responsible for binding decisions regarding authorizations for the use of remote biometric identification systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Judicial authorities employ AI systems to assist in law application but must ensure that final decisions are human-driven.&lt;SEP&gt;Judicial authorities operate independently and are not affected by market surveillance activities when performing their judicial duties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-911571ee28a1070a8fcc503dd5d91e14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50be48c46c67191e901c756873069fcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-543cc911c9d837b54a06d5f6ca958b34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8da189e7622be67a80b2e12945a657cb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_61.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863700</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Protection Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Data Protection Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeveloper</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Protection Authorities are national entities responsible for ensuring compliance with data protection laws and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Data protection authorities are specialized entities that ensure compliance with data protection laws and regulations, functioning within the framework of the Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Data Protection Authorities oversee data processing activities to safeguard personal data in the context of AI systems, ensuring compliance with data protection laws.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-184360d53ae652d7f48a919e168f375a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-911571ee28a1070a8fcc503dd5d91e14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2315cd7abb88dee440f081de5430a32f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_157.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858704</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Practice">
      <data key="d0">AI Practice</data>
      <data key="d1">AIModel</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Practice refers to the implementation of AI technologies and methods that must adhere to Union law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-911571ee28a1070a8fcc503dd5d91e14</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857274</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Market Surveillance Authorities">
      <data key="d0">National Market Surveillance Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">AISubject</data>
      <data key="d2">National Market Surveillance Authorities are organizations responsible for monitoring and enforcing compliance with market regulations and standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-911571ee28a1070a8fcc503dd5d91e14</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857274</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Template">
      <data key="d0">Template</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Template refers to a structured format provided to authorities for reporting decisions and results related to authorizations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-911571ee28a1070a8fcc503dd5d91e14</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857274</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Competent Judicial Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Competent Judicial Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">AISubject</data>
      <data key="d2">Competent Judicial Authorities are entities that have the legal power to make binding decisions on requests for authorizations pursuant to regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-911571ee28a1070a8fcc503dd5d91e14</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857274</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Decisions">
      <data key="d0">Decisions</data>
      <data key="d1">Output</data>
      <data key="d2">Decisions encompass the outcomes or judgments made by high-risk AI systems, which must be communicated to affected natural persons.&lt;SEP&gt;Decisions refer to the official rulings or determinations made by judicial and administrative authorities regarding requests and authorizations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-911571ee28a1070a8fcc503dd5d91e14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de3f18a6d766d2baa57ae891b9da7741</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_93.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859412</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Results">
      <data key="d0">Results</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Results refer to the outcomes or findings from the decisions taken by authorities concerning requests for authorizations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-911571ee28a1070a8fcc503dd5d91e14</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857274</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Biometric Identification Systems">
      <data key="d0">Biometric Identification Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">Biometric Identification Systems are advanced technological systems used to identify individuals based on unique biological characteristics in public spaces.&lt;SEP&gt;Biometric identification systems are AI technologies that identify individuals based on biological traits, necessitating stringent oversight due to their impact.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ded7b0ac022304fae10651966b33d18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-911571ee28a1070a8fcc503dd5d91e14</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_5.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863731</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Law Enforcement Purposes">
      <data key="d0">Law Enforcement Purposes</data>
      <data key="d1">Purpose</data>
      <data key="d2">Law Enforcement Purposes refer to the objectives aimed at maintaining public safety and order through the use of technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Law enforcement purposes pertain to the application of high-risk AI systems in policing and related activities, requiring strict regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-911571ee28a1070a8fcc503dd5d91e14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de3f18a6d766d2baa57ae891b9da7741</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_93.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859412</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 5">
      <data key="d0">Article 5</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 5 contains the list of prohibited practices within the AI regulatory framework.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 5 is a key provision of Regulation (EU) 2018/858 that addresses the regulation of Artificial Intelligence (AI) systems. It specifically details the prohibition of certain AI practices deemed unsafe or non-compliant, establishing compliance measures that must be adhered to by AI systems. Article 5 outlines various prohibited practices associated with the operation of AI systems, emphasizing that violations of these prohibitions can lead to administrative fines and penalties for non-compliance. Through these provisions, Article 5 aims to ensure the safety and regulatory adherence of AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 5 outlines specific prohibitions concerning AI practices that can be considered non-compliant under EU regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 5 outlines prohibited AI practices, which the Commission reviews annually for potential amendments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8e23760d52ebfb589b4de63afe8ab83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b71cdb20a8fa5befb7c30c90163cd416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee6d94a5f64203f09d02387acbdb39c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-111c71f234a0f2d1b26490907acae6eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5da2f6b1c2fa5619efa26719534e9c35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345a8ba89ed0ea3325462384d5e16aaf</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_111.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_81.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863422</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex X">
      <data key="d0">Annex X</data>
      <data key="d1">Document</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex X lists specific legal acts related to large-scale IT systems that must comply with certain regulatory requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8e23760d52ebfb589b4de63afe8ab83</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_111.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857278</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Large-Scale IT Systems">
      <data key="d0">Large-Scale IT Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">AISystem</data>
      <data key="d2">Large-scale IT systems are comprehensive systems that integrate AI components and must comply with regulatory standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Large-scale IT systems are infrastructures referenced in the Regulation, which include components such as high-risk AI systems that require compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8e23760d52ebfb589b4de63afe8ab83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b8c1122e1044e4445aa96d7fa6d5b6e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_177.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_111.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858309</data>
    </node>
    <node id="General-Purpose AI Models">
      <data key="d0">General-Purpose AI Models</data>
      <data key="d1">AIModel</data>
      <data key="d2">General-Purpose AI Models are designed to perform a wide range of distinct tasks and are characterized by their capability and generality.&lt;SEP&gt;General-Purpose AI Models are versatile artificial intelligence systems designed for efficiency and adaptability across a multitude of tasks and industries. They are intended for widespread use in various applications and contexts, underscoring their significance in the technology landscape. These models are capable of understanding and generating text based on a diverse array of training data, which includes copyrighted and other protected materials. 

While they offer extensive functionality and potential across different sectors, the deployment of General-Purpose AI Models brings with it systemic risks. Therefore, careful evaluation and oversight are necessary to mitigate these risks. To this end, these models must adhere to established codes of practice and comply with regulatory provisions, particularly those outlined in European Union legislation. High-risk categorizations, in particular, necessitate stringent compliance assessments to ensure that these models meet common specifications and standards.

Oversight is essential for promoting the responsible usage of General-Purpose AI Models, requiring standard evaluations and thorough documentation to maintain accountability and protect the interests of various sectors utilizing these technologies. Many of these models are available under open-source licenses, enhancing transparency by allowing public access to their parameters and usage information.

In summary, General-Purpose AI Models serve as foundational elements within the AI ecosystem, characterized by their wide-ranging applications and governed by a regulatory landscape that mandates diligent oversight. This ensures they fulfill their intended purposes while upholding safety and ethical standards.&lt;SEP&gt;General-purpose AI models have the potential to create significant systemic risks associated with various sectors and societal impacts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f41337092de45470ab838aff17309ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83f37d4143e19486af167d7acee5bee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-161f3120961644fbdc17c7b09b46e54b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b7fd511ed97ef1a87c9783c3425b7d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-769497b509433ed0e4746ff50bbdec69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18d33fd192f06f727ac6bb21becbaa57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bee8a141261944c2193bcb00b304b768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a69b68c9998277692ac6c6341fcdcac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c8a6b92fbe8d93eb878957c5ed60aa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ef570a9dfbda3c55d0d5bcc36fd77c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577494efd5ce842563e6974b0da9707b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-010f171cc1a7f217689efe00fd8cb656&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65c79a1c0cb37c10df906970d376029d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4d08c48923bc3e8bff8968fd67a799&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00e7606a0fa9d588f18d67d02cfcf654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1ae06c8c76fc5976313d75e4ffabdfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a0c1908573a7d6a832a6b35befbd7ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b837dd750c95d041180fa3d735328672&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4dc0271c68856282748506ff58069b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cfbca03bf6afb99c3326dc8b02d083b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa2a9a43bd7a2482ad876b406b9e9c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3f46abe104a1bdb0fae1c25094db36d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6de18717bcb0167956be85a15dd210f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8e23760d52ebfb589b4de63afe8ab83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40a9e2a0fc4601f4b3d4f583384b6a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-212b902a4529db42951674775ac3ec73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0695d12d62d4fd15a528842231db1850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dc89de2edca5d2bfe0d5e9e7c99665b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32556db3a80f72f1db354810bba21be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cc37264ee8f2a814b7b6f98953de48c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6579442a2f027e643cf907006333003a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae3ab8a3b5c5d0c61e8b99fa718913b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fcd3af92cad1d85ebf561f059acb114&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b90abf0636c26d546e9b6724e3224ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-778cb9e68fcb25e3f810e3cea927f7b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3177468233ec37ad2a71dc38caa17377&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af991f85166d6ddfbbf84e4a73207d3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98532c431ec75ae38c76dc0730337a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6570d0db42cf764ebb073d69da0137e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11bdaa862215570a86eed137e3092ea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f3c3fe390cb5d40b199e1bcc024928f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_104.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_164.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_41.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_106.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_163.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_179.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_56.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_114.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_110.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_133.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_162.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_173.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_102.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_117.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_111.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_174.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_68.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_55.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_89.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_108.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_101.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_151.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_40.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_97.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_103.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_89.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_109.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_169.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_161.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_53.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863955</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers and Deployers">
      <data key="d0">Providers and Deployers</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers and deployers are responsible for ensuring that AI systems comply with regulatory requirements before specified dates.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8e23760d52ebfb589b4de63afe8ab83</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_111.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857281</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 113(3)">
      <data key="d0">Article 113(3)</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 113(3) outlines prerequisites and conditions related to the application of the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8e23760d52ebfb589b4de63afe8ab83</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_111.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857281</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers of High-Risk AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Providers of High-Risk AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers of High-Risk AI Systems are entities responsible for the development and deployment of AI systems classified as high-risk due to their potential impact on society, safety, or fundamental rights. These organizations or individuals ensure that their AI systems not only meet regulatory and compliance requirements but also adhere to established compliance frameworks throughout their lifecycle. They are tasked with taking corrective actions when necessary to maintain compliance and are responsible for implementing security measures to safeguard their systems from vulnerabilities and threats. Additionally, Providers of High-Risk AI Systems have the obligation to report incidents related to their systems to market surveillance authorities, thereby playing a critical role in maintaining oversight and accountability in the deployment of high-risk AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8e23760d52ebfb589b4de63afe8ab83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8143bb5053cad47b9eaf4c05c9556429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0dc307b8b7cb1f0e39aa9b4b1839c408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e978e96ac6d99cf448b53260c07dded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2298fd83910d35175065de74977bd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5765a06abb615496a937c9303e1583cd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_111.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_76.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_90.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_64.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_20.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863491</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deployers of High-Risk AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Deployers of High-Risk AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">Deployers are responsible for ensuring that the high-risk AI systems they operate comply with regulatory requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8e23760d52ebfb589b4de63afe8ab83</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_111.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857281</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Obligations">
      <data key="d0">Obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Obligations encompass the actions, responsibilities, and legal requirements that stakeholders must adhere to under various regulations, including Article 20 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020. Specifically, these obligations are vital for providers and deployers of artificial intelligence (AI) systems, particularly in the context of high-risk AI applications. They include a range of duties aimed at ensuring the safe, ethical, and compliant deployment of AI technologies.

Key aspects of these obligations involve mandatory requirements for transparent communication with users about content generated by AI. Additionally, they entail legal responsibilities related to the detection and labeling of manipulated content, ensuring that the management and usage of AI systems align with established standards. Obligations also incorporate adherence to copyright law and other legal standards associated with the deployment of AI.

Providers and their representatives are required to ensure compliance with the regulations governing AI models, emphasizing accountability and the alignment of AI technology deployment with regulatory standards. This is particularly important as obligations extend to General-Purpose AI Models once these models are placed on the market, highlighting the specific responsibilities that AI models and systems must uphold in their operational environments. In summary, these obligations are crucial for safeguarding users and the broader public interest through responsible and compliant AI practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8e23760d52ebfb589b4de63afe8ab83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c8a6b92fbe8d93eb878957c5ed60aa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50cb89ed7d0d818018d373ebefa65267&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07e8d113bd66975dbb8053a37cc427fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af991f85166d6ddfbbf84e4a73207d3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c361162e59f587f531364714bb3e3c4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32556db3a80f72f1db354810bba21be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-161f3120961644fbdc17c7b09b46e54b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1ae06c8c76fc5976313d75e4ffabdfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be61089eed18cfaf2703713378c589a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de3f18a6d766d2baa57ae891b9da7741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89491b02af0a00cbc13f9e8df827a6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7963b30391bfa3d5e28ecd9a95b61010&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40de45b5b0c24b78b7ef2ca4e835c29c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b567607dbb431b0d294cd02679760039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3034aa8ff1b6d41ac6e0b8ff655b76ec</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_86.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_111.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_117.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_97.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_106.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_93.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_88.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_162.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_108.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863931</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Compliance Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Compliance Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Compliance Requirements refer to the legal and regulatory obligations that entities, particularly providers of high-risk AI systems, must adhere to in order to ensure their compliance with established standards and criteria. These requirements dictate the specific standards and conditions necessary for conformity assessment bodies and AI systems to follow. 

Specifically, compliance requirements establish the necessary obligations and legal standards that high-risk AI systems must fulfill, which are part of a broader regulatory framework aimed at ensuring safety and effectiveness before such technologies are deployed. They encompass a range of specific regulations and guidelines that organizations must meet, allowing them to gain the necessary authorization to operate legally. 

The requirements are critical for the responsible development and deployment of AI technologies, ensuring that they meet established safety and legal frameworks. Overall, compliance requirements are integral in specifying the necessary actions that entities must take to ensure that AI systems adhere to relevant laws and guidelines, including those outlined in Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 for safety and legality.&lt;SEP&gt;Compliance requirements are the criteria that AI systems must meet to obtain certification from notified bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;Compliance Requirements refer to the legal standards that high-risk AI systems must meet to ensure safety and ethical deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8e23760d52ebfb589b4de63afe8ab83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b754e2170dea6f93253ec4fd1fa88d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff611ee371ea780574e9c16859c31f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c72b31b17ef0accd3df4ab25a063163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ffa7662f1a996e8ed97ec3caf0ae564&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a30c75209c0fbb0ca1bb4afe44c77d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04f1483cdf6b84729e33ebc4a611375b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb2802f1b508b813d06e58ae27a1f77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b813df34a26015e6e1bf14a7a3d8c705&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85fb9638473c0974347ccab540b99b7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1952e0d35566561db978f8ee1ebdbd3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07ee6b3452d764ccd9733dceadb1ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-397d6e2474c4f45e883f265653f2e715</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_8.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_111.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_29.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_41.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_44.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_71.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_9.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863750</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Compliance Deadlines">
      <data key="d0">Compliance Deadlines</data>
      <data key="d1">Timeframe</data>
      <data key="d2">Compliance deadlines refer to specific dates by which the regulatory requirements must be satisfied by the concerned entities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8e23760d52ebfb589b4de63afe8ab83</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_111.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857281</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2 August 2025">
      <data key="d0">2 August 2025</data>
      <data key="d1">Date</data>
      <data key="d2">2 August 2025 is associated with the deadline for finalizing codes of practice or related actions if deemed inadequate.&lt;SEP&gt;2 August 2025 marks the cut-off date for general-purpose AI models to be placed on the market for compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;The date when obligations for providers and provisions regarding the penalties come into force as part of the Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;The date from which specific sections of the Regulation, including Chapter III Section 4, Chapter V, Chapter VII, and Chapter XII will apply.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-47ce3f90343791af10ffae2a7848f26e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40a9e2a0fc4601f4b3d4f583384b6a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e93fbd1f7fc7cbb860b708f989987b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa2a9a43bd7a2482ad876b406b9e9c3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_56.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_113.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_179.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_111.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859218</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2 August 2027">
      <data key="d0">2 August 2027</data>
      <data key="d1">Date</data>
      <data key="d2">2 August 2027 is the deadline for AI model providers to adhere to regulatory obligations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-47ce3f90343791af10ffae2a7848f26e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_111.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857281</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers of general-purpose AI models">
      <data key="d0">Providers of general-purpose AI models</data>
      <data key="d1">AIProvider</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers of general-purpose AI models are organizations or individuals responsible for developing and distributing AI systems intended for various applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-47ce3f90343791af10ffae2a7848f26e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_111.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857281</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2 August 2030">
      <data key="d0">2 August 2030</data>
      <data key="d1">Deadline</data>
      <data key="d2">2 August 2030 is an important compliance date for operators of high-risk AI systems intended for public use under the Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;2 August 2030 is the date mentioned as a reference point for compliance regulations concerning AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-47ce3f90343791af10ffae2a7848f26e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b8c1122e1044e4445aa96d7fa6d5b6e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_177.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_111.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858309</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Parliament">
      <data key="d0">European Parliament</data>
      <data key="d1">Organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Parliament is a vital legislative institution within the European Union (EU), representing the interests of EU citizens and playing a significant role in the decision-making process across various domains. As a directly elected body, the European Parliament is responsible for debating and passing EU laws, including critical regulations related to artificial intelligence (AI), cybersecurity, digital rights, copyright, and safety components.

The Parliament receives and evaluates reports and findings from the European Commission regarding AI regulations and compliance. It also examines proposals concerning the impact of these regulations. The institution holds considerable authority in its legislative functions, including the power to oppose or revoke authorities delegated to the European Commission, thereby ensuring accountability in the legislative process.

The European Parliament must approve various essential regulations, such as Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, which pertains to cybersecurity, Regulation (EU) 2019/881, and the 2014/32/EU Directive. Additionally, it has enacted Regulation (EU) 2024/900, focusing on electoral integrity and political advertising practices. Through its collaborative work with the Council, the Parliament strives to create and amend laws that reflect the democratic will and ethical considerations relevant to its constituents.

In summary, the European Parliament plays an instrumental role in shaping the legislative frameworks that govern technology, innovation, and the protection of digital rights within the EU, ensuring that such legislation aligns with ethical standards and serves the broader interests of EU citizens. Its collective actions are instrumental in influencing the future of the EU's digital landscape and governance.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Parliament is the legislative body of the European Union, involved in passing regulations and directives, including Directive 2005/29/EC.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-feb00b9eef4af47cdd3264cd99d6b2e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eab6e21707d57be17832ef8dfd7180a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83f37d4143e19486af167d7acee5bee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b7fd511ed97ef1a87c9783c3425b7d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-511a9744e58c5bca320f1c98646693c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5ff05678672211287e9053ebcd9c1c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f182220530b59a4450fc951016283bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17045c951f494f621b2305960aade53f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a48f68b8943ab2f8e6bdbb9ccf3e17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a69b68c9998277692ac6c6341fcdcac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fa5fe9ac042448be58de6c82bb33ea4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119d91aacb77775b61f5eddaf23771be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdc616126c9eed60b2893f6f0c5a24b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2499910b26136c66e6e7a013d8f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6485ea34e7fea16b2f5a59242c8ef2a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b837dd750c95d041180fa3d735328672&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b71cdb20a8fa5befb7c30c90163cd416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bedecbbbba0ded6846e6dc97756b7de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74def3a33d9c60f3c11227adf7704a09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a84d660603389dd91dcd96134d5bb46e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3acb107043f5850a72cf1b047a443296&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4fa1ad79284c6e1a9636113352a8e0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c582b50b1dcae6565f7384ebbe5e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6badc71855b10bbd17a31c7dfef0c442&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ec0d2d3cbe2a53a3bbf6373c775edf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-762d138929f27b0266d948c0aad50daa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da5fbf959baa6ee8e86278864a9144cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b46b9cdd1723562953df9638581250&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8f21b63428a38759e45ffcb10bac3d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbb30099cdacdc2f1eb2ed182c6b4491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_78.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_8.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_104.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_121.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_109.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_106.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_11.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_141.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_62.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_105.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_110.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_173.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_9.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_29.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_172.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_174.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_103.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_175.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_33.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_97.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863949</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Council">
      <data key="d0">Council</data>
      <data key="d1">Organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Council of the European Union is a principal decision-making body that works alongside the European Parliament.&lt;SEP&gt;The Council, officially known as the Council of the European Union, is a crucial decision-making and governing body within the European Union. It represents the governments of EU member states and plays an essential role in the legislative process, particularly in collaboration with the European Parliament to create and influence legislation, including regulations related to artificial intelligence (AI) and political advertising. The Council is responsible for evaluating and assessing AI regulations and their implementation, ensuring that the interests of member states are considered in the governance and legislative framework of the EU.

Additionally, the Council reviews reports submitted by the Commission regarding the impacts and evaluations of these regulations and engages with experts from member states to gather insights. It possesses the authority to revoke the delegation of power and mandates that notifications about delegated acts must be communicated simultaneously with the European Parliament. Overall, the Council serves as a vital component of EU governance, facilitating oversight and decision-making in relation to legislation affecting various sectors, including AI practices.&lt;SEP&gt;The Council refers to the Council of the European Union, which collaborates with the European Parliament in the legislative process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-da5fbf959baa6ee8e86278864a9144cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6001fd4ce94d732804de396c3240c65f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bedecbbbba0ded6846e6dc97756b7de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a84d660603389dd91dcd96134d5bb46e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eab6e21707d57be17832ef8dfd7180a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83f37d4143e19486af167d7acee5bee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdc616126c9eed60b2893f6f0c5a24b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c582b50b1dcae6565f7384ebbe5e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6485ea34e7fea16b2f5a59242c8ef2a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b837dd750c95d041180fa3d735328672&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17045c951f494f621b2305960aade53f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-762d138929f27b0266d948c0aad50daa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a69b68c9998277692ac6c6341fcdcac</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_121.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_103.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_29.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_172.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_62.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_97.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_174.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_110.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_173.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863949</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Delegated Acts">
      <data key="d0">Delegated Acts</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Delegated Acts are legal instruments adopted by the European Commission, designed to supplement or amend non-essential parts of existing legislative acts. They empower the Commission to make targeted changes to regulatory frameworks without engaging in a full legislative process, effectively enabling updates that respond to evolving circumstances, such as technological advancements. These acts are particularly significant in the context of AI systems, as they provide crucial specifications related to safety and implementation.

As secondary legal acts, Delegated Acts serve to establish binding directives that enhance the clarity and effectiveness of overarching regulations. They are developed by Commission expert groups and play a vital role in ensuring that legislation remains relevant and up-to-date. For example, Delegated Acts may incorporate amendments to critical criteria, as seen in updates to Annex XIII. Overall, Delegated Acts are essential for the ongoing adaptation and refinement of regulations, especially concerning emerging technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Delegated Acts are legal modifications initiated by the Commission to amend regulations concerning AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-da5fbf959baa6ee8e86278864a9144cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6001fd4ce94d732804de396c3240c65f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b46b9cdd1723562953df9638581250&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7805654ce0fe0d8d9b6ba008562d2aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4ba1d5ee9be6a9378df917d6a467f31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a84d660603389dd91dcd96134d5bb46e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb0291da832d9defa94aaf2262ad3761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eb5283f4e280f1ec77650d624699286&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1ef1c9ca92c002cf6ad36264fe1292c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d64a2a65aec35f8304efaaee30e0034d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4d62babb1c5a144faeae6ac2f13628</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_103.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_106.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_52.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_97.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_104.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_49.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_6.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_173.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_108.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_7.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863914</data>
