    <node id="Interinstitutional Agreement of 13 April 2016">
      <data key="d0">Interinstitutional Agreement of 13 April 2016</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">This agreement establishes principles for Better Law-Making, guiding the consultation of experts from Member States.&lt;SEP&gt;This agreement establishes principles for better law-making practices within the EU, influencing how regulations are formed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-da5fbf959baa6ee8e86278864a9144cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b7fd511ed97ef1a87c9783c3425b7d4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_173.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_97.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861943</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Official Journal of the European Union">
      <data key="d0">Official Journal of the European Union</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">The Official Journal of the European Union publishes references related to the certification of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Official Journal of the European Union serves as the essential publication for a variety of official acts and decisions within the EU framework. It is where published decisions regarding the revocation of delegated acts take effect and are formally documented. The Journal disseminates information about delegated acts and their revocations, ensuring that these important legal documents are made public. It also publishes references related to the certification of high-risk AI systems in accordance with EU regulations. Furthermore, the Official Journal is the medium through which harmonised standards are referenced and various legal acts, including those pertinent to conformity assessments, are officially published and communicated to the public. Overall, it plays a crucial role in the regulation and governance of EU activities by ensuring transparency and accessibility to legal information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-da5fbf959baa6ee8e86278864a9144cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e93fbd1f7fc7cbb860b708f989987b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9db4c15b43d1b7a1a1138d5a7403b240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0695d12d62d4fd15a528842231db1850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07b79b1855840c81b5d9079a82c7e9fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d423f15a7cbd742a57795f884434b60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-762d138929f27b0266d948c0aad50daa</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_42.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_41.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_97.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_122.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_113.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_32.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863619</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Five-Year Period">
      <data key="d0">Five-Year Period</data>
      <data key="d1">AILifecyclePhase</data>
      <data key="d2">The five-year period indicates the time frame within which the delegation of power can be reviewed and potentially renewed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-da5fbf959baa6ee8e86278864a9144cc</data>
