      <data key="d5">1750857286</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 6(6)">
      <data key="d0">Article 6(6)</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 6(6) is a specific provision that outlines conditions under which certain delegated acts can be adopted by the Commission.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 6(6) outlines the process for the Commission to adopt delegated acts, specifying consultation requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-da5fbf959baa6ee8e86278864a9144cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-762d138929f27b0266d948c0aad50daa</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_97.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857286</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 7(1)">
      <data key="d0">Article 7(1)</data>
      <data key="d1">LegalBasis</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 7(1) is a provision that allows the Commission to adopt delegated acts regarding particular matters as defined by regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 7(1) relates to delegated acts that must be consistent with the overall Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-739e3d9c7841d79a7701d630f8c7fa26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da5fbf959baa6ee8e86278864a9144cc</data>
