      <data key="d0">Interinstitutional Agreement of 13 April 2016 on Better Law-Making</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">This agreement lays down the principles for improving the level of regulation and law-making within the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-762d138929f27b0266d948c0aad50daa</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_97.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857286</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Delegated Act Notification">
      <data key="d0">Delegated Act Notification</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Delegated Act Notification involves the Commission informing the European Parliament and the Council once a delegated act has been adopted.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-762d138929f27b0266d948c0aad50daa</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_97.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857286</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Three-Month Period">
      <data key="d0">Three-Month Period</data>
      <data key="d1">Frequency</data>
      <data key="d2">The Three-Month Period is the time frame in which the European Parliament and the Council can express objections to a delegated act after notification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-762d138929f27b0266d948c0aad50daa</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_97.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857286</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Further Three-Month Period">
      <data key="d0">Further Three-Month Period</data>
      <data key="d1">Frequency</data>
      <data key="d2">The Further Three-Month Period can be initiated by the European Parliament or the Council to extend the objection period for delegated acts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-762d138929f27b0266d948c0aad50daa</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_97.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857286</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Legislative Period">
      <data key="d0">Legislative Period</data>
      <data key="d1">Time Frame</data>
      <data key="d2">The Legislative Period refers to the time frame during which the European Parliament and Council may decide on legislative proposals before expiration.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-eab6e21707d57be17832ef8dfd7180a9</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_97.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857286</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Extension">
      <data key="d0">Extension</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">The Extension refers to the ability for the legislative period to be prolonged by three months when initiated by the European Parliament or the Council.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-eab6e21707d57be17832ef8dfd7180a9</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_97.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857286</data>
    </node>
