      <data key="d0">Experts</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-da5fbf959baa6ee8e86278864a9144cc</data>
      <data key="d2">The Commission consults designated Experts from each Member State before adopting Delegated Acts.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_97.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857286</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Protection Law">
      <data key="d0">Data Protection Law</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Protection Law focuses on the handling and protection of personal data, ensuring individual privacy rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-08ef4cc90d0e3e23ebc122fef44151a4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_45.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857291</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Nondiscrimination Law">
      <data key="d0">Nondiscrimination Law</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Nondiscrimination Law prohibits discrimination based on characteristics such as race, gender, or disability within various contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-08ef4cc90d0e3e23ebc122fef44151a4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_45.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857291</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Consumer Protection Law">
      <data key="d0">Consumer Protection Law</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Consumer Protection Law aims to safeguard buyers from unfair trade practices and ensures their rights are protected.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-08ef4cc90d0e3e23ebc122fef44151a4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_45.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857291</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Competition Law">
      <data key="d0">Competition Law</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Competition Law is designed to promote fair competition and prevent monopolistic practices in the marketplace.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-08ef4cc90d0e3e23ebc122fef44151a4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_45.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857291</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Severity of Possible Harm">
      <data key="d0">Severity of Possible Harm</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">The severity of possible harm is an assessment criterion for determining the risk associated with high-risk AI systems, taking into account the potential outcomes of their use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37d88f95110db00bbf8230a2632a2035</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857313</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Probability of Occurrence">
      <data key="d0">Probability of Occurrence</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">The probability of occurrence evaluates how likely it is that high-risk AI systems will cause harm, influencing their classification as high-risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37d88f95110db00bbf8230a2632a2035</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857313</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Methodology and Criteria">
      <data key="d0">Methodology and Criteria</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">This refers to the established rules and methods used to assess and identify high-risk AI systems, ensuring consistent classification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37d88f95110db00bbf8230a2632a2035</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857313</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Health and Safety">
      <data key="d0">Health and Safety</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Health and Safety represent vital aspects that must be maintained in the deployment of AI systems to protect individuals and society.&lt;SEP&gt;Health and safety pertain to the physical well-being of individuals impacted by high-risk AI systems, a critical consideration in their assessment.&lt;SEP&gt;Health and safety refer to the standards and regulations that ensure the well-being of individuals using or affected by AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Health and safety address the implications of AI systems on individual and public well-being.&lt;SEP&gt;Health and safety refer to the well-being of individuals which may be impacted by the deployment of AI systems, particularly in high-risk contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50beca99a2207706ee9f0ad17a4205ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37d88f95110db00bbf8230a2632a2035&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9685a1f72e235a3f5b9ee69878eedb21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21acb22d994b8f65ea3709a99eb85032&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65f69156748df83d9fa179140a3fe2aa</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_52.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_20.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_7.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863906</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Intended Purpose">
      <data key="d0">Intended Purpose</data>
      <data key="d1">Purpose</data>
      <data key="d2">Intended Purpose refers to the specific aims or functions that high-risk AI systems are designed to achieve. It encompasses the typical usage and application for which these AI systems are developed, significantly influencing their risk classification. This term specifically highlights the goals or applications outlined in the provider's specifications and guidelines. Essentially, Intended Purpose is crucial in determining the appropriate context and scenarios in which high-risk AI systems operate, thereby affecting their overall assessment and categorization based on risk.&lt;SEP&gt;The intended purpose refers to the specific functions and outcomes for which the high-risk AI system was designed and deployed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b5e606b14946a1b388f008868e8e155&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37d88f95110db00bbf8230a2632a2035&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2f186d6b95e69680f63fabb65ad924a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d2cf289e7ae9939fc7fe1d189daf51f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_52.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_13.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_84.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_65.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859149</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Methodology">
      <data key="d0">Methodology</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Methodology outlines the systematic approach for identifying and evaluating high-risk AI systems to ensure consistency and objectivity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37d88f95110db00bbf8230a2632a2035</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857320</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Criteria for Assessment">
      <data key="d0">Criteria for Assessment</data>
      <data key="d1">Metric</data>
      <data key="d2">Criteria for assessment comprise the standards and measures used to determine the risks associated with AI systems, including severity and probability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37d88f95110db00bbf8230a2632a2035</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857320</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technological Development">
      <data key="d0">Technological Development</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Technological development entails the advancements in AI technologies that necessitate a reassessment of high-risk systems and regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37d88f95110db00bbf8230a2632a2035</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857320</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Harm">
      <data key="d0">Harm</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Harm is a potential negative outcome stemming from the use of high-risk AI systems, evaluated in terms of severity and likelihood.&lt;SEP&gt;Harm refers to the negative impacts, both material and immaterial, that may arise from the use of AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37d88f95110db00bbf8230a2632a2035&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7114fa80a4a18326b68b2fd61f65c047</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861087</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Rapid Pace of Technological Development">
      <data key="d0">Rapid Pace of Technological Development</data>
      <data key="d1">Frequency</data>
      <data key="d2">The rapid pace of technological development refers to the speed at which AI technologies evolve, necessitating ongoing updates in risk assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37d88f95110db00bbf8230a2632a2035</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857320</data>
    </node>
    <node id="biometric identification">
      <data key="d0">biometric identification</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Biometric identification refers to the automated recognition of human features for establishing identity by comparing biometric data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62c8c9618d935cf8910927a7d518c1f2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_15.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857323</data>
    </node>
    <node id="physical features">
      <data key="d0">physical features</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Physical features such as face and body shape are key components in biometric identification for establishing identity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62c8c9618d935cf8910927a7d518c1f2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_15.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857323</data>
    </node>
    <node id="physiological features">
      <data key="d0">physiological features</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Physiological features like heart rate and blood pressure are utilized in biometric identification processes for building identity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62c8c9618d935cf8910927a7d518c1f2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_15.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857323</data>
    </node>
    <node id="behavioural features">
      <data key="d0">behavioural features</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Behavioural features including voice and keystroke characteristics are important in biometric identification systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62c8c9618d935cf8910927a7d518c1f2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_15.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857323</data>
    </node>
    <node id="reference database">
      <data key="d0">reference database</data>
      <data key="d1">DataSource</data>
      <data key="d2">A reference database stores biometric data against which individual features are compared for identification purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62c8c9618d935cf8910927a7d518c1f2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_15.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857323</data>
    </node>
    <node id="authentication">
      <data key="d0">authentication</data>
      <data key="d1">Purpose</data>
      <data key="d2">Authentication in this context refers to confirming identity for access to services or premises using biometric data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62c8c9618d935cf8910927a7d518c1f2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_15.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857323</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Physical Features">
      <data key="d0">Physical Features</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Physical features refer to traits such as face, body shape, and other characteristics that can be analyzed in biometric identification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62c8c9618d935cf8910927a7d518c1f2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_15.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857323</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Physiological Features">
      <data key="d0">Physiological Features</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Physiological features include measurable body characteristics such as heart rate and blood pressure that can be used for biometric identification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62c8c9618d935cf8910927a7d518c1f2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_15.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857323</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Behavioral Features">
      <data key="d0">Behavioral Features</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Behavioral features pertain to actions and patterns, including voice, prosody, and keystrokes, that contribute to biometric identification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62c8c9618d935cf8910927a7d518c1f2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_15.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857323</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Reference Database">
      <data key="d0">Reference Database</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">A reference database stores the biometric data against which individuals' current biometric data is compared for identity verification.&lt;SEP&gt;The reference database is a crucial resource against which the input data is validated, ensuring accurate outputs from the system.&lt;SEP&gt;The reference database stores biometric data for comparison purposes in remote identification systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The reference database contains information necessary for the operation of biometric systems, ensuring accurate identity verification for specific use cases.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62c8c9618d935cf8910927a7d518c1f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f62cf38e10f73dd06a997571902c1ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-239d42cf353b4be7fdeade1f3fced85d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff0d16c0510c298943e3daa75fd581b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_15.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_12.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_34.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_17.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863646</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Systems for Biometric Verification">
      <data key="d0">AI Systems for Biometric Verification</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">AI systems designed for biometric verification focus on authenticating the identity of users based on their biometric data.&lt;SEP&gt;AI systems designed for biometric verification processes, including authentication that confirms an individual's identity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62c8c9618d935cf8910927a7d518c1f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b65e9562dd645622f1390ba1863fee19</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_15.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862032</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Authentication">
      <data key="d0">Authentication</data>
      <data key="d1">Purpose</data>
      <data key="d2">Authentication processes confirm someone's identity using biometric data to grant access to services or ensure security.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62c8c9618d935cf8910927a7d518c1f2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_15.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857323</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Consent">
      <data key="d0">Consent</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Consent refers to the approval that individuals may or may not give regarding the use of their biometric data, which can impact the legality of its processing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62c8c9618d935cf8910927a7d518c1f2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_15.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857323</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Identity Establishment">
      <data key="d0">Identity Establishment</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Identity establishment is a measurement of how effectively biometric identification processes confirm a person's identity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62c8c9618d935cf8910927a7d518c1f2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_15.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857323</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Affected Persons">
      <data key="d0">Affected Persons</data>
      <data key="d1">DataSubject</data>
      <data key="d2">Affected Persons are individuals who are impacted by the decisions made with the assistance of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Affected persons are individuals or groups who experience negative outcomes as a result of an infringement of AI regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Affected persons are individuals or groups who experience the impact of AI applications and are considered in the evaluation of codes of practice.&lt;SEP&gt;Affected persons are individuals whose rights are impacted by decisions made based on high-risk AI systems, necessitating explanations for such decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Affected persons refer to individuals who may be impacted by the AI practices or infringements of the Union institutions and can experience damage due to such violations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f6de18717bcb0167956be85a15dd210f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-727225adfedcad573a12c2ed92e8ee1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5da2f6b1c2fa5619efa26719534e9c35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21acb22d994b8f65ea3709a99eb85032</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_56.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_171.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_20.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859954</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Explanation Right">
      <data key="d0">Explanation Right</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">The Explanation Right allows affected persons to obtain meaningful explanations regarding decisions made by AI systems that significantly impact them.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-727225adfedcad573a12c2ed92e8ee1f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_171.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Legal Effects">
      <data key="d0">Legal Effects</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Legal effects refer to the outcomes of decisions made by AI systems that influence the rights or status of affected persons.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-727225adfedcad573a12c2ed92e8ee1f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_171.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Adverse Impact">
      <data key="d0">Adverse Impact</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Adverse impact describes the negative consequences that decisions made by high-risk AI systems may have on individuals' health, safety, or fundamental rights.&lt;SEP&gt;Adverse impact indicates the negative effects that an AI system might have on individuals or groups, particularly concerning health and safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-727225adfedcad573a12c2ed92e8ee1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50beca99a2207706ee9f0ad17a4205ff</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_171.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_7.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863901</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Law Exceptions">
      <data key="d0">Union Law Exceptions</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Union Law Exceptions refer to specific legal provisions that may limit the application of the Explanation Right in certain circumstances.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-727225adfedcad573a12c2ed92e8ee1f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_171.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Declaration of Conformity">
      <data key="d0">EU Declaration of Conformity</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">The EU Declaration of Conformity is a mandatory document that certifies a high-risk AI system's compliance with European regulations. This document serves as a formal statement by the provider or importer, confirming that the AI system meets all necessary regulatory requirements established by the European Union. It is specifically required for high-risk AI systems and demonstrates compliance with the essential requirements set forth in related regulations. The issuance of this declaration underscores the provider's commitment to adhering to the regulatory framework, ensuring that the high-risk AI system is safe and meets the established standards within the European market.&lt;SEP&gt;The EU declaration of conformity is a document that states a product's compliance with EU legislation and standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The EU declaration of conformity is a document certifying that a product meets the applicable EU regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The EU Declaration of Conformity is a mandatory document that certifies that a high-risk AI system complies with relevant EU legislation and requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;The EU declaration of conformity is a mandatory document that ensures compliance with EU standards and is to be kept up-to-date.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb5ca2a2f12bb39286916d398b70ed9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f13d730755b7535c59eb130d6f7ac62e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b7fd511ed97ef1a87c9783c3425b7d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6370e960da03a6bbdee69f64993cdae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdd0ab3aadbdd5226fa3661ea9057181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f77911358a1d821f6b1731fac6d2dbd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85fb9638473c0974347ccab540b99b7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73fd7e801c2d8d41361f6b16b45c6ed0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_47.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_173.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_77.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_83.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_16.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863624</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Documentation">
      <data key="d0">Technical Documentation</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical Documentation refers to a comprehensive set of records essential for ensuring transparency and compliance with regulations relating to the operation of AI systems. It encompasses detailed descriptions of various aspects such as the design, intended use, and safety measures of both products and high-risk AI systems. This documentation must be meticulously prepared by the provider and maintained to meet regulatory standards before an AI model can be marketed.

Key components of Technical Documentation include extensive records on the training and testing processes of AI models, evaluation results, and compliance mechanisms. It is crucial that this documentation specifies any modifications and new training data sources to ensure that the AI systems adhere to relevant regulations, particularly those outlined in Article 11 and Annex IV. The documentation serves not only to demonstrate compliance but also as a resource for showcasing the capabilities and characteristics of the AI system.

Moreover, Technical Documentation plays a vital role in the conformity assessment process, providing necessary information on performance and safety. It facilitates effective regulatory review and supports ongoing modifications and compliance of AI systems, while also ensuring proper usage and transparency for general-purpose AI models utilized by downstream providers. Overall, maintaining comprehensive Technical Documentation is critical for the ethical and responsible operation of AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical documentation includes the rationale, testing, and validation results of the AI system, detailed in Annex IV.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical documentation refers to the complete and detailed description of AI processes, including training, testing, and validation results.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical documentation includes all the necessary information providing compliance assessments under specified legal acts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fdf8a675497acfbeb420b95621b7cb31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75ec68339f2da8ef06976767a0d5b494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85fb9638473c0974347ccab540b99b7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-873c3732f26f3ace86c77cfec67991ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4d62babb1c5a144faeae6ac2f13628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c28a81721b7de3ef4442495cc499b1cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65c79a1c0cb37c10df906970d376029d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb5ca2a2f12bb39286916d398b70ed9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bfb9287798720e37fcd8bae961e88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-800752b66b6fe0cd70bb0290efc2fbbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b754e2170dea6f93253ec4fd1fa88d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dc89de2edca5d2bfe0d5e9e7c99665b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e5d20a8e9427a4698b84f758676994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9685a1f72e235a3f5b9ee69878eedb21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f77911358a1d821f6b1731fac6d2dbd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11bdaa862215570a86eed137e3092ea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2612abd3c26dca69a0acec30add3ef15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b474f9815c7033ca1ad8daff4012eff</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_101.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_78.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_109.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_11.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_83.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_71.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_9.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_59.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863780</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Registration Obligations">
      <data key="d0">Registration Obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Registration obligations are the requirements set forth for high-risk AI systems to be documented within the EU database, ensuring accountability and traceability.&lt;SEP&gt;Registration obligations require that providers ensure their information is accurate for high-risk AI systems compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f77911358a1d821f6b1731fac6d2dbd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-166a35f517674f4ceba2754c65f88c5f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_131.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863659</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conformity Assessment Procedure">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Assessment Procedure</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">The Conformity Assessment Procedure is a comprehensive regulatory process that ensures artificial intelligence (AI) systems, particularly those classified as high-risk, comply with specific legal requirements and standards prior to their marketing or operational deployment. This procedure incorporates a series of evaluations aimed at verifying compliance with relevant regulations, especially pertaining to cybersecurity, health, and safety.

Functioning as a formal mechanism, the Conformity Assessment Procedure assesses whether AI systems adhere to prescribed standards, thereby facilitating their safe implementation across various applications. It is conducted by an independent third-party body to ensure that the technologies meet the required safety standards.

This procedure is pivotal in the rigorous evaluation and approval process for AI technologies, ensuring their reliability and safety for end-users before they can enter the market. By assessing compliance with established requirements, it plays a crucial role in safeguarding public interest and enhancing the integrity of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7859a0c655f74761757b416c3b50bf36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44eafa4c222bb60e722eca942751cf7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c72b31b17ef0accd3df4ab25a063163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e5d20a8e9427a4698b84f758676994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95424b9dff57302628c496570b4baff4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b7fd511ed97ef1a87c9783c3425b7d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60a12c037b4dee54159c11f348ff3f11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ab1f3b6cbb052c58ff3b9fc75a6d7a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f77911358a1d821f6b1731fac6d2dbd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4d62babb1c5a144faeae6ac2f13628</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_78.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_139.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_173.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_81.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_16.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863962</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Logs">
      <data key="d0">Logs</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Logs are automatically generated records from high-risk AI systems that provide a comprehensive account of events, transactions, or processes occurring within the system. These records are essential for monitoring system behavior, demonstrating compliance with regulatory standards, and aiding in auditing and troubleshooting efforts. Logs serve as critical data for authorities who may inspect them to verify adherence to compliance requirements. They play a vital role in tracking operations and must be maintained in accordance with Article 19, highlighting their importance in the governance and oversight of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Logs refer to the records that detail the operations and activities of high-risk AI systems, maintained as part of compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b754e2170dea6f93253ec4fd1fa88d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2edb4e37d5b6a1ec68d071ea273b4e52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c852bda35515c8d5385ef007c8140254&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bece07e296fce9647a40a0dde904fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8af2de29a8b78dd2b512b6eb64d912a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f77911358a1d821f6b1731fac6d2dbd6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_19.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_13.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_71.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_16.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863013</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Compliance Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Technical Compliance Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical compliance requirements are criteria set forth that high-risk AI systems must adhere to for market approval.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f77911358a1d821f6b1731fac6d2dbd6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_22.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk Management">
      <data key="d0">Risk Management</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Risk management encompasses the identification, assessment, and mitigation strategies related to risks in deploying high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk management involves identifying and mitigating potential risks associated with high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk management refers to strategies and practices that aim to mitigate potential risks associated with AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f77911358a1d821f6b1731fac6d2dbd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c32bc5fa5cdfa35a393a42535dc4fdfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9685a1f72e235a3f5b9ee69878eedb21</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863356</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-Risk AI System">
      <data key="d0">High-Risk AI System</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">A High-Risk AI System is an artificial intelligence application recognized for posing significant risks to individuals and society, especially concerning health, safety, and fundamental rights. These systems are classified under stringent legal criteria that require detailed registration before they can enter the market, ensuring compliance with specific regulatory obligations and conformity criteria.

Given their potential for substantial harm in the event of failure, High-Risk AI Systems must undergo rigorous checks, providing documented evidence of adherence to safety measures. They are often capable of profiling individuals or making critical decisions autonomously, leading to concerns about their effects on fundamental rights and discrimination. As a result, compliance with established requirements is vital, as any deviation can create risks that may require corrective actions or even market withdrawal.

Additionally, High-Risk AI Systems must meet essential cybersecurity standards, reflecting a complex regulatory landscape. Regulatory measures include detailed impact assessments that evaluate the systems' implications, compelling deployers to actively identify risks and safeguard fundamental rights. 

These systems demand heightened compliance with design and accessibility standards to protect individuals with disabilities, and may be subject to new conformity assessments if substantial modifications occur. Overall, High-Risk AI Systems are distinguished by their significant societal impacts and necessitate comprehensive risk management measures along with effective data handling protocols. This underscores the importance of robust compliance mechanisms to ensure health, safety, and legal obligations align with Union harmonization legislation.&lt;SEP&gt;High-Risk AI Systems are AI systems identified by the EU that require specific compliance measures and documentation in accordance with the regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;A high-risk AI system is an artificial intelligence system that is subject to specific regulatory scrutiny due to potential risks to health, safety, or fundamental rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2edb4e37d5b6a1ec68d071ea273b4e52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4ac0ccf9bd954306cee6efbfd342416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-445327adc051facf545b6358f6f01466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad9c740a10a5c1577e578a593bd61fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d64a2a65aec35f8304efaaee30e0034d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85fb9638473c0974347ccab540b99b7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73fd7e801c2d8d41361f6b16b45c6ed0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3ee1fc3ca38d0fe1cd19861a325e159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb5ca2a2f12bb39286916d398b70ed9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b5e606b14946a1b388f008868e8e155&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21678b36bef336bf18e091bdfdb68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2298fd83910d35175065de74977bd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee04f6104a24650416810ede28f3790b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d2cf289e7ae9939fc7fe1d189daf51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7963b30391bfa3d5e28ecd9a95b61010&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eea61d03ab615ac5f518e77cd220c1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f13d730755b7535c59eb130d6f7ac62e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cc37264ee8f2a814b7b6f98953de48c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8efd21db4fc63a879493cbb376ae904&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e978e96ac6d99cf448b53260c07dded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de3f18a6d766d2baa57ae891b9da7741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8af2de29a8b78dd2b512b6eb64d912a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdf6e3e080867f88ec52fa9fabbeafd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17ccf2ddbeca1f4e8b771a2316b7d16c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65f69156748df83d9fa179140a3fe2aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c17bf6e803eec807c9fc7299d71d51d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33366c5df404f37775ccbf3ec455b578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4c7e75432b8ffa8e0b96687dc4dd380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bece07e296fce9647a40a0dde904fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be61089eed18cfaf2703713378c589a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2440fb0070f3198e96bd1ad753ae3e0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60a12c037b4dee54159c11f348ff3f11</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_78.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_75.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_51.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_80.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_13.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_93.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_88.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_84.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_86.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_67.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_82.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_83.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_87.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_64.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_128.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_31.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_47.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_16.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_63.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_20.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_6.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_49.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863789</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Competent Authority">
      <data key="d0">Competent Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">A Competent Authority is a regulatory body that oversees compliance and can request documentation regarding high-risk AI systems from distributors.&lt;SEP&gt;A Competent Authority oversees the regulation, guidance, and support within the AI regulatory sandbox, ensuring compliance and safety of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A competent authority is a designated body responsible for overseeing compliance and safety standards for high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Competent authorities are entities or individuals with the legal power to request documentation and information regarding the conformity of high-risk AI systems from providers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fa2b7ae4447e7d43e6030d6793c59ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8af2de29a8b78dd2b512b6eb64d912a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d08b537f9a5bb2b4f4bbdf442ba39bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73fd7e801c2d8d41361f6b16b45c6ed0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_21.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861101</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Provider">
      <data key="d0">Provider</data>
      <data key="d1">AIProvider</data>
      <data key="d2">The Provider is a vital entity within the artificial intelligence (AI) ecosystem, particularly concerning the development and supply of high-risk AI systems as outlined by regulatory frameworks. Providers can be individuals or legal organizations and play a multifaceted role encompassing the design, operation, and marketing of these systems.

Their significant responsibilities include the thorough assessment and documentation of risks associated with AI systems before their introduction to the market. Providers are tasked with ensuring compliance with relevant safety and regulatory standards, which necessitates delivering comprehensive documentation that meets all regulatory obligations and registering high-risk AI systems in appropriate databases, such as the European Union database.

In pursuing their responsibilities, Providers are accountable for organizing and overseeing the testing of AI systems, ensuring that all testing procedures are compliant with regulatory requirements, including informed consent and real-world testing conditions. They must develop risk mitigation strategies and designate an authorized representative to supervise the development of general-purpose AI models.

Additionally, Providers have a critical duty to offer guidance and instructions that facilitate the assessment of potential risks related to the use of their AI systems, aligning the systems' intended uses with established regulatory guidelines. They are also obliged to remain informed about any serious incidents concerning their systems, as they supply these AI systems to deployers.

Furthermore, Providers possess the right to request a reassessment of their AI models, particularly where systemic risks are identified. This includes accountability for submitting real-world testing plans and maintaining compliance with regulatory requirements throughout the AI systems' lifecycle. Providers are also responsible for pre-defining and assessing changes in the performance and operations of AI systems to ensure ongoing compliance.

In summary, Providers are integral to the AI landscape, charged with the safe and responsible development, operation, and deployment of AI technologies. Their comprehensive responsibilities encompass not only the creation, specification, and integration of AI systems but also adherence to extensive regulatory frameworks, ensuring the progressive evolution of AI technology occurs within a structured and compliant environment.&lt;SEP&gt;The Provider is an entity that supplies the AI system and is accountable for ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements and taking corrective actions as necessary.&lt;SEP&gt;The provider is responsible for ensuring compliance with obligations related to AI systems and may face fines for non-compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Provider is an entity that offers a general-purpose AI model but lacks legal personality, represented by authorized individuals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa9e2916955e882c73231ed69851f6ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c361162e59f587f531364714bb3e3c4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c4d127e5313d415dd94f6b6761da956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1ef1c9ca92c002cf6ad36264fe1292c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d64a2a65aec35f8304efaaee30e0034d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdd0ab3aadbdd5226fa3661ea9057181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-873c3732f26f3ace86c77cfec67991ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-610573a7c194ad780ed97782200a740c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73fd7e801c2d8d41361f6b16b45c6ed0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3ee1fc3ca38d0fe1cd19861a325e159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b5e606b14946a1b388f008868e8e155&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1ae06c8c76fc5976313d75e4ffabdfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2f186d6b95e69680f63fabb65ad924a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21678b36bef336bf18e091bdfdb68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee04f6104a24650416810ede28f3790b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7963b30391bfa3d5e28ecd9a95b61010&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe0c14a128bfd78c4c5056f7102cc152&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba5a4fee300868ea16940c9ea15f534a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b567607dbb431b0d294cd02679760039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4348ad8873ef2041aca94abc9297ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f6e14583352886a741ac1d51eada03a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0c31436f0e7ce27ce5952aa2bf9ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f13d730755b7535c59eb130d6f7ac62e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8af2de29a8b78dd2b512b6eb64d912a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb3519876fdebea487c9995e6d3ae4fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e23bb4c71b510fec0bbe6570de37cd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65f69156748df83d9fa179140a3fe2aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a64bfb94635a0df2f808b2f8a494bd3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7d62750f1113d24ac155fcd2b2ef02c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2ba08954f9ed754c2566e3c59b63ee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be61089eed18cfaf2703713378c589a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-075ecb5835777e6044264a23ca0cb20a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1516ad8d48077af0d59fc01578f33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78dcdae0f5d22df28405d8ae03e038d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_106.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_13.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_88.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_86.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_61.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_111.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_128.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_6.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_47.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_80.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_52.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_76.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_92.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_49.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863863</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Certificate">
      <data key="d0">Certificate</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">The Certificate indicates that the AI system meets the required standards and has been verified by a Notified Body.&lt;SEP&gt;The certificate is a formal document issued by a notified body that certifies the conformity of a high-risk AI system to regulatory standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b341fa074527a308a2434a3c68244d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8af2de29a8b78dd2b512b6eb64d912a6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863801</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Notified Body">
      <data key="d0">Notified Body</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">A Notified Body is a specific type of conformity assessment body recognized for its role in performing assessments in accordance with regulatory requirements. These organizations operate under Union harmonization laws and are designated to evaluate compliance and certification, particularly for high-risk AI systems. The primary responsibilities of a Notified Body include assessing the conformity of certain products, services, or systems before they can be marketed within the European Union. Established under national law, a Notified Body is assigned a unique identification number and plays a crucial role in ensuring legal compliance and quality management. They are also responsible for enforcing regulations related to AI systems and must be informed of any mandate terminations related to the products they assess. In summary, Notified Bodies are instrumental in ensuring that products adhere to established standards and regulations before entering the market.&lt;SEP&gt;A notified body is an organization designated by a Member State to assess conformity of certain products before being placed on the market.&lt;SEP&gt;A notified body is an organization designated to assess the conformity of certain products before they can be marketed in the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;The Notified Body is an organization designated to assess the compliance of AI systems with regulations and standards before certification.&lt;SEP&gt;The notified body is an entity that must fulfill specific obligations and meet requirements set forth in regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8caee37338a6383c30fe06ea2b3e4761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29241e99bddf5af77eca441d2d8dbc1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f55b689ece7aa049c38fdc38018dba8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c361162e59f587f531364714bb3e3c4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f79a9fca1518856b24fdcb7e59f040&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b341fa074527a308a2434a3c68244d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e978e96ac6d99cf448b53260c07dded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97182f6b8815d40f51faf3e8eaeb7c7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad9c740a10a5c1577e578a593bd61fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8af2de29a8b78dd2b512b6eb64d912a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cdf6e3e080867f88ec52fa9fabbeafd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-785d0dafc3a62a1aee53267d076b7533</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_33.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_48.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_35.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_20.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_31.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_37.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863782</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Scope of the Mandate">
      <data key="d0">Scope of the Mandate</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">The scope of the mandate outlines the authority and responsibilities of the authorized representative in overseeing compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8af2de29a8b78dd2b512b6eb64d912a6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_22.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Section 2">
      <data key="d0">Section 2</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Section 2 of this Chapter establishes specific requirements and obligations that must be met for compliance, particularly focusing on high-risk AI systems. It outlines the standards that these systems must conform to in order to be deemed compliant in the market and to demonstrate conformity. This section emphasizes the importance of adherence to specific requirements that the providers of these AI systems must follow for compliance purposes. Overall, Section 2 refers to the part of the regulation that dictates the necessary criteria for high-risk categories of AI systems to ensure they align with EU regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-010f171cc1a7f217689efe00fd8cb656&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f13d730755b7535c59eb130d6f7ac62e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8af2de29a8b78dd2b512b6eb64d912a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21678b36bef336bf18e091bdfdb68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69838403e8b59bb122436a0d25a9fc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdd0ab3aadbdd5226fa3661ea9057181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2739984aae71aa27a0af867bc197b730</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_40.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_41.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_47.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863630</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Access to Logs">
      <data key="d0">Access to Logs</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Access to logs generated by the high-risk AI system is necessary for compliance verification and demonstrating operational transparency.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8af2de29a8b78dd2b512b6eb64d912a6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_22.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Termination of the Mandate">
      <data key="d0">Termination of the Mandate</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Termination of the mandate is a condition where the assignment given to the provider is revoked, leading to the necessity for reporting to the relevant parties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c361162e59f587f531364714bb3e3c4c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_22.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857331</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Operator">
      <data key="d0">Operator</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">The term "Operator" encompasses a variety of roles related to the management and oversight of AI systems, including provider, importer, distributor, and deployer. An operator is an entity that not only runs or oversees the functioning of an AI system but is also responsible for ensuring compliance with relevant regulations, particularly concerning infringement scenarios. These entities may operate across borders and are tasked with managing technical and organizational measures pertinent to the deployment, manufacturing, or distribution of AI systems within the market. Moreover, operators play a critical role in making AI systems available to the market, while also being subject to specific rules regarding infringements and penalties associated with their operations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7d62750f1113d24ac155fcd2b2ef02c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad9c740a10a5c1577e578a593bd61fd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Output">
      <data key="d0">Output</data>
      <data key="d1">Output</data>
      <data key="d2">The output refers to the results produced by an AI system after processing data, which can be shared under regulatory conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_22.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857334</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Third Country">
      <data key="d0">Third Country</data>
      <data key="d1">LocalityOfUse</data>
      <data key="d2">A third country is a nation outside of the European Union with which agreements have been concluded regarding conformity assessments.&lt;SEP&gt;A third country is any nation outside the Union where AI operators may be established, affecting the regulation of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A third country refers to any nation that is not a member of the Union but may have agreements regarding conformity assessments with the Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-21da71f798625922669f14e575cb5dcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4337a268de724c492ca11805622faf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_127.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_39.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859216</data>
    </node>
    <node id="International Agreements">
      <data key="d0">International Agreements</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">International agreements are treaties or contracts established for cooperation between countries, particularly concerning law enforcement and AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_22.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deployers">
      <data key="d0">Deployers</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">Deployers are entities or individuals tasked with the deployment and operation of high-risk AI systems in real-world conditions. Their role is crucial as they must ensure compliance with relevant regulations and monitor the use of these systems to adhere to legal obligations. Deployers, which can include employers or public authorities, are required to be well-informed about compliance and risk considerations provided by the system developers. They also need to have a clear understanding of the functionality, strengths, and limitations of the AI systems they implement.

The responsibilities of Deployers encompass not only the practical implementation of high-risk AI technologies but also the ongoing oversight of their performance within the established regulatory framework. This necessitates effective communication from the AI system providers regarding performance expectations and any relevant testing aspects. Overall, Deployers play a vital role in managing the real-world application of AI technology while emphasizing regulatory compliance and the responsible use of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-20ac675fffdeba0fbc242b392d3af8da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bece07e296fce9647a40a0dde904fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e978e96ac6d99cf448b53260c07dded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a65ec6b0fbd17afe47587686523a725&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de3f18a6d766d2baa57ae891b9da7741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21acb22d994b8f65ea3709a99eb85032&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d2cf289e7ae9939fc7fe1d189daf51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8721c261d628c538814f61ffe3cec22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78dcdae0f5d22df28405d8ae03e038d0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_13.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_20.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_93.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_20.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_91.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863464</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Contracting Parties">
      <data key="d0">Contracting Parties</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Contracting Parties are entities engaged in international agreements that outline the use and governance of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_22.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Transfer">
      <data key="d0">Data Transfer</data>
      <data key="d1">Processing</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Transfer involves the movement of data from the Union to third countries, subject to regulatory compliance and protection of rights.&lt;SEP&gt;Data transfer refers to the movement of data collected and processed for AI testing to third countries under specific safeguards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ad1a115533e7d3b3ced9ea8e2e87b0e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_141.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861057</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cooperation Frameworks">
      <data key="d0">Cooperation Frameworks</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Cooperation Frameworks are agreements established between entities in the Union and third countries for law enforcement and AI collaboration.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e78bce1eaa5df9c186492b5e1482218</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_22.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Europol">
      <data key="d0">Europol</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Europol is the European Union's law enforcement agency that facilitates cooperation among Member States regarding criminal matters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a90a47461f525bba18d74c42ea04f88</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_22.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fundamental Rights and Freedoms">
      <data key="d0">Fundamental Rights and Freedoms</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Fundamental Rights and Freedoms refer to the essential human rights that must be protected in law enforcement and judicial cooperation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a90a47461f525bba18d74c42ea04f88</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_22.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Law Enforcement and Judicial Cooperation">
      <data key="d0">Law Enforcement and Judicial Cooperation</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Law Enforcement and Judicial Cooperation encompasses the efforts and agreements made to ensure effective policing and justice across borders.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a90a47461f525bba18d74c42ea04f88</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_22.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857336</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Judicial Cooperation">
      <data key="d0">Judicial Cooperation</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Judicial Cooperation refers to the collaborative efforts between judicial authorities across different countries to enhance legal processes and criminal justice.&lt;SEP&gt;Judicial cooperation encompasses the collaborative processes among EU member states in legal matters, particularly those involving AI systems and personal data handling.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a90a47461f525bba18d74c42ea04f88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a2f07f347fedfe788b6636feb212d5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_40.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859250</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Outputs">
      <data key="d0">Outputs</data>
      <data key="d1">Output</data>
      <data key="d2">Outputs are results or deliverables derived from law enforcement and judicial cooperation initiatives, which must comply with Union law.&lt;SEP&gt;Outputs generated by AI systems include various functions that reflect the system's operations, such as decisions and predictions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a90a47461f525bba18d74c42ea04f88&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-907dfa7ec80255255b81cd50cd6a4494</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_12.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858541</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Logging Capabilities">
      <data key="d0">Logging Capabilities</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Logging capabilities refer to the functions that allow high-risk AI systems to document relevant events, supporting traceability and monitoring.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aff0d16c0510c298943e3daa75fd581b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_12.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Event Recording">
      <data key="d0">Event Recording</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Event recording involves capturing essential information during the operation of high-risk AI systems, aimed at risk management and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aff0d16c0510c298943e3daa75fd581b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_12.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Post-Market Monitoring">
      <data key="d0">Post-Market Monitoring</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">Post-market monitoring pertains to the ongoing observation and assessment of high-risk AI systems to ensure safety and compliance after deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aff0d16c0510c298943e3daa75fd581b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_12.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Input Data">
      <data key="d0">Input Data</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Input data consists of the information fed into the high-risk AI systems to facilitate their processing and verification of results.&lt;SEP&gt;Input data includes the information used by an AI system to perform its tasks, which must be legally obtained.&lt;SEP&gt;Input data refers to data provided to or acquired by an AI system, which the system uses to produce output.&lt;SEP&gt;Input data refers to the data provided to an AI system, which is used to produce outputs.&lt;SEP&gt;Input data refers to the information provided to the AI system, which can be processed or analyzed to generate output.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-071372b252509d0e29e64264c0511359&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6570d0db42cf764ebb073d69da0137e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff0d16c0510c298943e3daa75fd581b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ac98f64f8751ad51246ca16d843f030</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_35.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_12.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_133.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863759</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Natural Persons Involved in Verification">
      <data key="d0">Natural Persons Involved in Verification</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeveloper</data>
      <data key="d2">Natural persons involved in verification are individuals responsible for evaluating the results provided by high-risk AI systems, as mandated by regulatory guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aff0d16c0510c298943e3daa75fd581b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_12.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 79(1)">
      <data key="d0">Article 79(1)</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 79(1) defines what constitutes a risk in the context of high-risk AI systems and outlines the responsibilities of distributors.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 79(1) outlines obligations for providers regarding risks associated with high-risk AI systems and the actions they must take when such risks are identified.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 79(1) outlines specific requirements for high-risk AI systems regarding risk management and operational accountability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1e978e96ac6d99cf448b53260c07dded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff0d16c0510c298943e3daa75fd581b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21678b36bef336bf18e091bdfdb68f0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_12.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_20.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861101</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 72">
      <data key="d0">Article 72</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 72 pertains to regulatory oversight mechanisms for post-market monitoring of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aff0d16c0510c298943e3daa75fd581b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_12.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 26(5)">
      <data key="d0">Article 26(5)</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 26(5) addresses operational compliance and monitoring stipulations for high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aff0d16c0510c298943e3daa75fd581b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_12.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857339</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Traceability">
      <data key="d0">Traceability</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Traceability refers to the ability to follow the history, application, or location of the event log data throughout the life cycle of the high-risk AI system.&lt;SEP&gt;Traceability refers to the ability to track the development and impact of AI systems to ensure accountability and transparency.&lt;SEP&gt;Traceability refers to the ability to track the history, application, or location of the AI systems and the documentation involved in their assessment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-849f8f0403e6b12fa8a9c24b84c094c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff0d16c0510c298943e3daa75fd581b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77093970e26d1be04734ed16ea88f777</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_27.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_12.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_53.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862736</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Monitoring Operations">
      <data key="d0">Monitoring Operations</data>
      <data key="d1">Metric</data>
      <data key="d2">Monitoring operations consist of the ongoing observation and assessment of the performance and compliance of high-risk AI systems during their use.&lt;SEP&gt;Monitoring operations involves continuously tracking the performance and compliance of AI systems after their deployment in the market.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b754e2170dea6f93253ec4fd1fa88d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aff0d16c0510c298943e3daa75fd581b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_12.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857584</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk-based approach">
      <data key="d0">Risk-based approach</data>
      <data key="d1">Risk</data>
      <data key="d2">A risk-based approach involves assessing and tailoring regulations based on the level of risk associated with AI systems, ensuring proportionality in rules.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0bd7056742f766183c11176d91fb1e8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857341</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-risk AI systems">
      <data key="d0">High-risk AI systems</data>
      <data key="d1">AISystem</data>
      <data key="d2">High-risk AI systems are categorized based on their potential to generate significant risks, requiring stricter regulatory requirements and obligations. These systems are defined by their potential impact and the risks they pose in various applications. They encompass AI models that have specific compliance requirements dependent on their operational context and certification status. Designed to ensure transparency in operation, high-risk AI systems enable deployers to interpret and use the system's output appropriately. Additionally, these systems are developed from training, validation, and testing data sets that meet specific quality and governance criteria. Overall, high-risk AI systems are subject to stringent regulations and standards due to their potential impacts on safety and compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems are defined by their need to perform consistently throughout their lifecycle, meeting necessary levels of accuracy, robustness, and cybersecurity, based on their intended purpose.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b2f186d6b95e69680f63fabb65ad924a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fde742696dfc1372a034cc9cadcb58d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0bd7056742f766183c11176d91fb1e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a67563c32c3414ab14ce22666bed23dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20ac675fffdeba0fbc242b392d3af8da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d423f15a7cbd742a57795f884434b60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2739984aae71aa27a0af867bc197b730</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_40.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_10.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_42.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_13.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_85.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862061</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Transparency obligations">
      <data key="d0">Transparency obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Transparency obligations mandate that certain AI systems disclose their operations and decision-making processes to users and stakeholders.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0bd7056742f766183c11176d91fb1e8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857341</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Binding Rules">
      <data key="d0">Binding Rules</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Binding rules are regulatory requirements that govern the operation and deployment of AI systems, ensuring compliance with established standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Binding rules refer to legally enforceable regulations governing AI development and deployment, ensuring compliance with ethical standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0bd7056742f766183c11176d91fb1e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-256a6003a5841f2764536c55f7086431</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Proportionate Approach">
      <data key="d0">Proportionate Approach</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">A proportionate approach entails adapting the regulatory framework to align with the specific risks posed by AI systems, balancing innovation with safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0bd7056742f766183c11176d91fb1e8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857341</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Unacceptable AI Practices">
      <data key="d0">Unacceptable AI Practices</data>
      <data key="d1">Hazard</data>
      <data key="d2">Unacceptable AI practices refer to certain actions or methodologies in AI development and deployment that are prohibited due to ethical or safety concerns.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0bd7056742f766183c11176d91fb1e8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857341</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Requirements for High-Risk AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Requirements for High-Risk AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Requirements for high-risk AI systems establish specific obligations and standards that these systems must meet to mitigate potential risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0bd7056742f766183c11176d91fb1e8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857341</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Operators of AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Operators of AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Operators of AI systems are individuals or organizations responsible for the deployment and management of AI technologies and must adhere to regulatory requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0bd7056742f766183c11176d91fb1e8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857341</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Intensity of Risks">
      <data key="d0">Intensity of Risks</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">The intensity of risks refers to the degree of potential harm or impact that AI systems can cause, influencing regulatory approaches.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0bd7056742f766183c11176d91fb1e8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857341</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Scope of Risks">
      <data key="d0">Scope of Risks</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">The scope of risks outlines the range and nature of potential dangers posed by AI systems, guiding the development of tailored regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0bd7056742f766183c11176d91fb1e8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857341</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Legal Framework">
      <data key="d0">Union Legal Framework</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">The Union legal framework establishes harmonized rules on AI to foster development and protection of public interests.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8f21b63428a38759e45ffcb10bac3d8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_8.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857342</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Interests">
      <data key="d0">Public Interests</data>
      <data key="d1">AreaOfImpact</data>
      <data key="d2">Public interests encompass the fundamental rights protected by Union law that may be affected by AI.&lt;SEP&gt;Public interests refer to health, safety, and fundamental rights, including democracy and environmental protection, as recognized by Union law.&lt;SEP&gt;Public interests refer to the health, safety, and fundamental rights that need protection within the framework of AI regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Public interests refer to the essential rights and safety of individuals in the Union that must be protected against the risks posed by high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Public interests encompass the welfare and safety of the general populace, which regulations aim to protect.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13b35a74627bd926656242d6545e09a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7114fa80a4a18326b68b2fd61f65c047&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8f21b63428a38759e45ffcb10bac3d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3e6894a9009f1db207c0ec639d8a39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ded1c99cfd152513a4ef07b96a9c5de</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_7.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_8.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_167.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863049</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Ecosystem">
      <data key="d0">European Ecosystem</data>
      <data key="d1">AIUser</data>
      <data key="d2">The European ecosystem consists of public and private actors creating AI systems that align with Union values and support innovation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8f21b63428a38759e45ffcb10bac3d8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_8.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857342</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs)">
      <data key="d0">Small and Medium Enterprises (SMEs)</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">SMEs are businesses that are monitored under the Regulation to assess their market entry and compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;SMEs including startups are emphasized for support under the Regulation to foster AI development and innovation.&lt;SEP&gt;SMEs, including start-ups, are small and medium-sized businesses that may have specific interests and needs when engaging with AI systems and codes of conduct.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8f21b63428a38759e45ffcb10bac3d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40f3761e589fb7702938fd4fbbecfdcc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_95.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_8.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863441</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Digital Transformation">
      <data key="d0">Digital Transformation</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Digital transformation refers to changes across all regions of the Union unlocked by the development and use of AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8f21b63428a38759e45ffcb10bac3d8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_8.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857342</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Council">
      <data key="d0">European Council</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Council is a key decision-making body of the European Union that addresses major issues, including ethical frameworks.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Council provides guidelines and objectives for the development of secure and ethical AI in Europe.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Council is involved in the legislative process of regulations impacting artificial intelligence within the EU framework.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Council shapes the EU's overall political direction and priorities, playing a significant role in data legislation.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Council plays a role in overseeing and contributing to the AI regulatory landscape.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b71cdb20a8fa5befb7c30c90163cd416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8f21b63428a38759e45ffcb10bac3d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119d91aacb77775b61f5eddaf23771be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3acb107043f5850a72cf1b047a443296&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f182220530b59a4450fc951016283bfc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_141.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_8.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_105.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863452</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Values">
      <data key="d0">European Values</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">European values encompass principles like democracy, the rule of law, and human rights that should guide AI development and implementation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8f21b63428a38759e45ffcb10bac3d8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_8.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857342</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Innovation Support Measures">
      <data key="d0">Innovation Support Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Innovation support measures include actions and regulations aimed at promoting new technology solutions and innovations, specifically for SMEs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8f21b63428a38759e45ffcb10bac3d8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_8.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857342</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ethical Principles">
      <data key="d0">Ethical Principles</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Ethical principles are standards that guide behavior, particularly in the context of developing best practices and standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Ethical principles guide the responsible development and deployment of AI technologies, ensuring they align with societal values.&lt;SEP&gt;Ethical principles serve as guidelines to ensure that AI systems are developed and used responsibly, respecting human rights and social values.&lt;SEP&gt;The ethical principles developed by the AI HLEG serve as benchmarks for assessing the trustworthiness and ethical soundness of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-849f8f0403e6b12fa8a9c24b84c094c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8f21b63428a38759e45ffcb10bac3d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-256a6003a5841f2764536c55f7086431&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54c5e21ac6860a002561ead75c49b95b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_8.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Free Movement of Goods and Services">
      <data key="d0">Free Movement of Goods and Services</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Free movement of goods and services is a foundational principle of the internal market that AI regulations aim to uphold while ensuring protection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8f21b63428a38759e45ffcb10bac3d8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_8.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857342</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Harmonized Rules">
      <data key="d0">Harmonized Rules</data>
      <data key="d1">Standard</data>
      <data key="d2">Harmonized rules are established principles and requirements to ensure consistency and safety in the implementation of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Harmonized rules are standardized legal frameworks established across the Union to ensure uniform application in the regulation of AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8f21b63428a38759e45ffcb10bac3d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b46b9cdd1723562953df9638581250</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_8.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_106.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858832</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Framework of Ethical Aspects of Artificial Intelligence">
      <data key="d0">Framework of Ethical Aspects of Artificial Intelligence</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">The framework refers to the guidelines and ethical considerations proposed by the European Parliament for the development and deployment of AI and robotics technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-119d91aacb77775b61f5eddaf23771be</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_8.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857342</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Parliament resolution of 20 October 2020">
      <data key="d0">European Parliament resolution of 20 October 2020</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">The resolution passed by the European Parliament includes recommendations concerning a framework for ethical aspects of AI, robotics, and related technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-119d91aacb77775b61f5eddaf23771be</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_8.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857342</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Special meeting of the European Council (1 and 2 October 2020)">
      <data key="d0">Special meeting of the European Council (1 and 2 October 2020)</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">The special meeting of the European Council discusses various important issues, including conclusions regarding AI ethics and frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-119d91aacb77775b61f5eddaf23771be</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_8.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857342</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ethical Aspects of Artificial Intelligence">
      <data key="d0">Ethical Aspects of Artificial Intelligence</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">This refers to the guidelines and standards set for measuring the ethical implications and responsibilities in the development of AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-119d91aacb77775b61f5eddaf23771be</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_8.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857342</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI and Robotics">
      <data key="d0">AI and Robotics</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">AI and robotics represent a significant area of technological advancement that requires careful ethical consideration.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-119d91aacb77775b61f5eddaf23771be</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_8.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857342</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Very Large Online Platforms">
      <data key="d0">Very Large Online Platforms</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">Very Large Online Platforms are entities that must adhere to regulations to identify and mitigate systemic risks associated with AI-generated content.&lt;SEP&gt;Very Large Online Platforms are major entities that must adhere to regulations concerning the identification and mitigation of risks from AI-generated content.&lt;SEP&gt;Very Large Online Platforms are significant digital services that must adhere to specific regulations regarding AI system usage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7570653f66cb58454b80be2046705a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cac929d0048fe34377179e8ecde4a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e1bc352c7c8d3a7ba58b9b1a4f9f37</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_136.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_118.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_120.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Very Large Online Search Engines">
      <data key="d0">Very Large Online Search Engines</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">Very Large Online Search Engines are digital search services subject to regulatory frameworks governing AI operations and risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Very Large Online Search Engines are providers impacted by regulations requiring them to manage the risks of disseminating AI-manipulated content.&lt;SEP&gt;Very Large Online Search Engines face obligations under the regulation to manage the risks of disseminating artificially generated or manipulated information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7570653f66cb58454b80be2046705a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cac929d0048fe34377179e8ecde4a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e1bc352c7c8d3a7ba58b9b1a4f9f37</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_136.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_118.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_120.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863167</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Disinformation">
      <data key="d0">Disinformation</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Disinformation is a risk source highlighted in the regulation, potentially affecting civic discourse and electoral processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Disinformation is recognized as a systemic risk influenced by AI-generated content that can negatively affect democratic processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Disinformation produced by AI models can threaten democratic values and harm privacy, affecting societal trust and stability.&lt;SEP&gt;Disinformation refers to the dissemination of false information that can undermine public trust and democratic processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3f46abe104a1bdb0fae1c25094db36d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-392a0705db576351b9cbccd6dcfdf33f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7570653f66cb58454b80be2046705a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e1bc352c7c8d3a7ba58b9b1a4f9f37</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_120.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_136.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_110.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863955</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Systemic Risks">
      <data key="d0">Systemic Risks</data>
      <data key="d1">RiskConcept</data>
      <data key="d2">Systemic Risks are potential dangers associated with the deployment of General-Purpose AI Models that could affect larger systems or societies.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic Risks are potential dangers associated with the design, deployment, and functioning of AI systems, particularly general-purpose AI models, across various services. These risks highlight the variety of hazards that can arise when such models are employed, potentially leading to detrimental effects on larger systems and communities. 

The implications of systemic risks are particularly concerning at a Union level, as they indicate possible widespread adverse effects that could disrupt safety, integrity, and the functionality of democratic processes and civic engagement. The use of AI-generated content raises significant concerns regarding its impact on societal processes, which necessitates careful management to prevent negative outcomes and ensure compliance with safety regulations.

Furthermore, systemic risks encompass inherent dangers linked to the high-impact capabilities of general-purpose AI models, which could result in substantial consequences for communities as well as for the regulatory framework governing these technologies. Therefore, addressing these risks is crucial to maintain overall stability and safety within the AI ecosystem, emphasizing the need for appropriate safeguards to mitigate potential harm or disruption.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic risks are defined as any foreseeable negative effects related to accidents, public health, and democratic processes arising from AI model capabilities and misuse.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3f46abe104a1bdb0fae1c25094db36d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-447d51c65bac6d28fd62c36c3e70e08b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cac929d0048fe34377179e8ecde4a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e1bc352c7c8d3a7ba58b9b1a4f9f37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-161f3120961644fbdc17c7b09b46e54b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c259012a2ff719418b0deb6cbd52130&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f3c3fe390cb5d40b199e1bcc024928f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1ef1c9ca92c002cf6ad36264fe1292c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-075ecb5835777e6044264a23ca0cb20a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bee8a141261944c2193bcb00b304b768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c49e78c25e30ed3a2557915010f14f3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4dc0271c68856282748506ff58069b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fb0ee5d200ca5b71eb6d9f53ad070ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b567607dbb431b0d294cd02679760039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7570653f66cb58454b80be2046705a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-873c3732f26f3ace86c77cfec67991ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa2a9a43bd7a2482ad876b406b9e9c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fcd3af92cad1d85ebf561f059acb114</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_115.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_52.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_56.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_97.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_136.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_164.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_92.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_114.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_68.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_111.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_110.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_120.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_118.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_53.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863955</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Civic Discourse">
      <data key="d0">Civic Discourse</data>
      <data key="d1">AreaOfImpact</data>
      <data key="d2">Civic Discourse involves community discussions and engagements that can be disrupted by disinformation spread through AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Civic Discourse refers to the dialogue and discussion that occurs in public life, which can be harmed by the dissemination of manipulated information from AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7570653f66cb58454b80be2046705a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e1bc352c7c8d3a7ba58b9b1a4f9f37</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_136.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_120.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859450</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Electoral Processes">
      <data key="d0">Electoral Processes</data>
      <data key="d1">AreaOfImpact</data>
      <data key="d2">Electoral Processes are the methods and practices through which elections are conducted, which may be influenced by AI-generated disinformation.&lt;SEP&gt;Electoral Processes are the systems in place for elections that can be adversely affected by disinformation propagated by AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7570653f66cb58454b80be2046705a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7e1bc352c7c8d3a7ba58b9b1a4f9f37</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_136.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_120.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859450</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Content Labeling">
      <data key="d0">Content Labeling</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Content Labeling refers to the requirement under the regulation for AI-generated content to be labeled to inform users of its nature.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7e1bc352c7c8d3a7ba58b9b1a4f9f37</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_136.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857344</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers of Hosting Services">
      <data key="d0">Providers of Hosting Services</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers of Hosting Services must comply with regulations regarding the handling of illegal content, including content generated by AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7e1bc352c7c8d3a7ba58b9b1a4f9f37</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_136.json</data>
