    <node id="Implementing Act">
      <data key="d0">Implementing Act</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">An implementing act is a legal measure that the Commission may adopt to suspend, restrict, or withdraw the designation of a notified body.&lt;SEP&gt;An implementing act is a legal mechanism used to enforce regulatory actions under established laws and guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;The implementing act refers to the legislation that delineates the structure and levels of fees for expert advice as laid out in Article 68(1).&lt;SEP&gt;An implementing act is a type of regulatory document that governs the application of EU legislation ensuring consistent implementation across Member States.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0695d12d62d4fd15a528842231db1850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea6a588c10ad2fe493ec8cc1913f72d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97182f6b8815d40f51faf3e8eaeb7c7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daa2a9a43bd7a2482ad876b406b9e9c3</data>
