      <data key="d5">1750863196</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Safety Components">
      <data key="d0">Safety Components</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Safety Components refer to essential elements within artificial intelligence (AI) systems that must comply with specific safety standards and stringent regulatory requirements as outlined in relevant regulations. These components are designed to function reliably and securely in environments where safety is paramount, ensuring operational safety in high-risk scenarios. The primary purpose of Safety Components is to protect the physical integrity of critical infrastructure while safeguarding the health and safety of individuals and property. Overall, Safety Components play a crucial role in the effective deployment of AI systems by adhering to the safety criteria set forth by industry regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Safety components refer to elements or systems in artificial intelligence that must meet specific safety requirements as per EU legislation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a4219a2a10d85ddd82f98b8d6267cb9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4ba1d5ee9be6a9378df917d6a467f31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a84d660603389dd91dcd96134d5bb46e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec6a8294e2a2ad2569029d260c4d7673&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eb5283f4e280f1ec77650d624699286&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2499910b26136c66e6e7a013d8f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7805654ce0fe0d8d9b6ba008562d2aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b</data>
