    <node id="European Parliament and Council">
      <data key="d0">European Parliament and Council</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Parliament and the Council are crucial legislative bodies in the European Union, actively involved in drafting, consulting, and approving regulations pertaining to various sectors, including artificial intelligence. They play a significant role in the regulatory process, contributing to the creation of vital legislation such as the AI Act, which governs artificial intelligence practices within the EU. Additionally, they are responsible for establishing fundamental regulations, including Directive (EU) 2016/797 concerning transportation safety standards, and the adoption of Regulation (EU) 2023/988. Through their collaborative efforts, the European Parliament and Council ensure the effective implementation of essential regulations across diverse areas in the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3f7d41ecd7ed7ec26e62e63255378cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a5a3ae528d10c9d38e017d520ab6719&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b7fd511ed97ef1a87c9783c3425b7d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eb5283f4e280f1ec77650d624699286&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6485ea34e7fea16b2f5a59242c8ef2a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2af15b193dbeb2497919d2971657871e</data>
