    <node id="market surveillance authority">
      <data key="d0">market surveillance authority</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">The market surveillance authority is a regulatory body responsible for overseeing and ensuring compliance with regulations related to high-risk AI systems, particularly in areas such as biometrics. This authority monitors both the deployment and operation of AI systems to ensure adherence to established regulations and standards. It acts as a notified body for specific high-risk AI systems utilized by law enforcement and other authorities. Designated by Member States, market surveillance authorities enforce compliance with Union harmonization legislation, playing a crucial role in maintaining the integrity and safety of AI systems in the market.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0efde0679d72a2d51e7acdaf09979bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a0a99b47c288a96d7474c796efb766&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f12c01099dadb1fc1008ce18c7d800e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f736e1ff707eaba05079b0f194d8a123&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8c5a915dca180e1c423cefa27ea6cd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69838403e8b59bb122436a0d25a9fc1e</data>
