    </node>
    <node id="Directive (EU) 2016/680 compliance">
      <data key="d0">Directive (EU) 2016/680 compliance</data>
      <data key="d1">RiskControl</data>
      <data key="d2">The adherence to the regulations set forth in Directive (EU) 2016/680 that govern the processing of personal data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f736e1ff707eaba05079b0f194d8a123</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_159.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857377</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CE Marking">
      <data key="d0">CE Marking</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">CE Marking is a certification mark indicating that a product conforms to European health, safety, and environmental protection standards.&lt;SEP&gt;CE Marking signifies that an AI system meets the requisite European Union legislation and requirements for conformity assessment. It serves as a certification mark indicating that the system conforms to regulatory requirements, ensuring compliance with Union harmonization legislation. Specifically, CE marking is crucial for high-risk AI systems, indicating their compliance with EU safety, health, and environmental protection standards. This certification is necessary for such systems to be legally placed on the market within the European Economic Area. Overall, CE marking is a vital indication of conformity with health, safety, and environmental protection standards for products sold in the region.&lt;SEP&gt;CE marking is a certification indicating conformity with European health, safety, and environmental protection standards required for certain products.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-29241e99bddf5af77eca441d2d8dbc1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb5ca2a2f12bb39286916d398b70ed9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43942ba7283893ebf128acb858a20c58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73fd7e801c2d8d41361f6b16b45c6ed0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_129.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_48.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_83.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_16.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861664</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Internal Market">
      <data key="d0">Internal Market</data>
      <data key="d1">Domain</data>
      <data key="d2">The Internal Market refers to the economic space in the European Union where goods, services, and capital can circulate freely.&lt;SEP&gt;The internal market is a key area of focus for the Regulation, aiming to streamline and enhance trade and commerce within the Union.&lt;SEP&gt;The internal market refers to the economic area of the European Union where goods, services, people, and capital move freely, without restrictions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43942ba7283893ebf128acb858a20c58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae8bdbb57af24d78fe2313201571bea7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0455405f9e173535e78c4ea589745cf4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_129.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_176.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863288</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-Risk AI Systems Embedded in a Product">
      <data key="d0">High-Risk AI Systems Embedded in a Product</data>
      <data key="d1">AISystem</data>
      <data key="d2">"High-risk AI systems embedded in products require a physical CE marking to indicate conformity.'</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43942ba7283893ebf128acb858a20c58</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_129.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857379</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-Risk AI Systems Provided Digitally">
      <data key="d0">High-Risk AI Systems Provided Digitally</data>
      <data key="d1">AISystem</data>
      <data key="d2">High-risk AI systems that are offered only in a digital format require a digital CE marking for compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43942ba7283893ebf128acb858a20c58</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_129.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857379</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Digital CE Marking">
      <data key="d0">Digital CE Marking</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Digital CE marking is a certification for high-risk AI systems provided digitally, indicating their regulatory compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Digital CE marking is a form of certification applied to high-risk AI systems that can be accessed easily through interfaces or machine-readable codes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-29241e99bddf5af77eca441d2d8dbc1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43942ba7283893ebf128acb858a20c58</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_129.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_48.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857936</data>
    </node>
    <node id="real-time remote biometric identification system">
      <data key="d0">real-time remote biometric identification system</data>
      <data key="d1">AISystem</data>
      <data key="d2">The real-time remote biometric identification system is an AI system used in publicly accessible spaces for law enforcement purposes, requiring authorisation before deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dc0db03f57b007cfc458657e88e273ae</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_35.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857381</data>
    </node>
    <node id="judicial authority">
      <data key="d0">judicial authority</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">Judicial authority is an independent administrative authority of a Member State that provides express and specific authorisation for the use of biometric identification systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dc0db03f57b007cfc458657e88e273ae</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_35.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857381</data>
    </node>
    <node id="law enforcement authority">
      <data key="d0">law enforcement authority</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">Law enforcement authority is responsible for overseeing the use of AI systems in urgent situations and requesting necessary authorisations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dc0db03f57b007cfc458657e88e273ae</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_35.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857381</data>
    </node>
    <node id="urgent situations">
      <data key="d0">urgent situations</data>
      <data key="d1">RiskConcept</data>
      <data key="d2">Urgent situations are scenarios where immediate action is needed, potentially justifying the bypassing of standard authorisation procedures for using AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dc0db03f57b007cfc458657e88e273ae</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_35.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857381</data>
    </node>
    <node id="input data">
      <data key="d0">input data</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Input data refers to information directly acquired by the AI system during its operation in public spaces for biometric identification.&lt;SEP&gt;Input data refers to the information provided to high-risk AI systems, which must be relevant and representative of the intended purpose.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dc0db03f57b007cfc458657e88e273ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8c5a915dca180e1c423cefa27ea6cd3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_35.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862998</data>
    </node>
    <node id="output of the AI system">
      <data key="d0">output of the AI system</data>
      <data key="d1">Output</data>
      <data key="d2">Output refers to the results generated by the AI system after processing input data during identification tasks for law enforcement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dc0db03f57b007cfc458657e88e273ae</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_35.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857381</data>
    </node>
    <node id="authorisation">
      <data key="d0">authorisation</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Authorisation is the formal consent needed from a judicial or administrative authority before the biometric identification system can be utilized in public areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Authorisation is the formal permission required under the regulation for certain uses of data, specifically for law enforcement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2035e81a92cf42f945220e637e40591a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0db03f57b007cfc458657e88e273ae</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_35.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_38.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862969</data>
    </node>
    <node id="independent administrative authority">
      <data key="d0">independent administrative authority</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">Independent administrative authority refers to the body that ensures the lawful operation of AI systems in the context of public safety and privacy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dc0db03f57b007cfc458657e88e273ae</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_35.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857381</data>
    </node>
    <node id="urgency">
      <data key="d0">urgency</data>
      <data key="d1">RiskConcept</data>
      <data key="d2">Urgency refers to critical scenarios where immediate action is required, justifying temporary bypasses of standard authorisation protocols.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dc0db03f57b007cfc458657e88e273ae</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_35.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857381</data>
    </node>
    <node id="results and outputs">
      <data key="d0">results and outputs</data>
      <data key="d1">Output</data>
      <data key="d2">Results and outputs are the insights or data produced by the biometric identification system after processing input data during identification tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dc0db03f57b007cfc458657e88e273ae</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_35.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857381</data>
    </node>
    <node id="data related to authorisation">
      <data key="d0">data related to authorisation</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Data related to authorisation includes all the information captured during the biometric identification process, which must be discarded if authorisation is denied.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dc0db03f57b007cfc458657e88e273ae</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_35.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857381</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Remote Biometric Identification System">
      <data key="d0">Remote Biometric Identification System</data>
      <data key="d1">AISystem</data>
      <data key="d2">A remote biometric identification system is a type of AI component that identifies individuals based on biological traits and may influence legal decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;A remote biometric identification system is designed to identify individuals without their involvement, typically at a distance, by comparing biometric data.&lt;SEP&gt;A remote biometric identification system is designed to remotely identify individuals based on their biometric traits.&lt;SEP&gt;The remote biometric identification system is an AI system designed for the identification of individuals from a distance using their biometric data compared to a reference database.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3ac98f64f8751ad51246ca16d843f030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f62cf38e10f73dd06a997571902c1ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e726a1ef8f481d54c995afc6a028f60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-071372b252509d0e29e64264c0511359</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_35.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_17.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859187</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Legal Acquisition">
      <data key="d0">Legal Acquisition</data>
      <data key="d1">LegalBasis</data>
      <data key="d2">Legal acquisition refers to obtaining input data in compliance with laws and regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-071372b252509d0e29e64264c0511359</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_35.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857381</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Output of Use">
      <data key="d0">Output of Use</data>
      <data key="d1">Output</data>
      <data key="d2">Outputs refer to the results generated by the AI system as a consequence of processing the input data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-071372b252509d0e29e64264c0511359</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_35.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857381</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Results and Outputs">
      <data key="d0">Results and Outputs</data>
      <data key="d1">Output</data>
      <data key="d2">The results and outputs of the AI system are the outcomes produced based on the input data received during its functioning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-071372b252509d0e29e64264c0511359</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_35.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857381</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Authorization">
      <data key="d0">Authorization</data>
      <data key="d1">LegalBasis</data>
      <data key="d2">Authorization refers to a formal approval process essential for high-risk AI systems to ensure compliance with established safety and legal standards before deployment. This process involves granting official permission to an AI system to process input data while meeting specific requirements aimed at safeguarding public interests. The authorization is examined and justified by a governing body, such as a commission, particularly in response to any objections raised. Additionally, authorization extends beyond AI systems, encompassing the permissions that must be secured from rightsholders before utilizing their copyrighted content, especially in the context of AI model training. Overall, authorization serves as a critical mechanism to ensure that high-risk AI technologies operate within regulatory frameworks and respect intellectual property rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-071372b252509d0e29e64264c0511359&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4c7e75432b8ffa8e0b96687dc4dd380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5429fed5961ecea1e5eed049e922476f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-244204be180c4ed9731f434ed67ee99b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-878d589bc7b69ae2d9c3a44284a1badc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07ee6b3452d764ccd9733dceadb1ac7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_35.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_30.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_130.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_105.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863673</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union or National Law">
      <data key="d0">Union or National Law</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Union or national law pertains to the legal regulations that govern the acquisition and use of data by AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Union or national law sets the legal framework guiding the testing of high-risk AI systems, including ethical reviews and regulatory requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ff61ec794793cf787d4a0473487a06f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-071372b252509d0e29e64264c0511359</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_35.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863073</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Legally Acquired Input">
      <data key="d0">Legally Acquired Input</data>
      <data key="d1">Input</data>
      <data key="d2">Legally acquired input refers to data that is obtained following proper legal guidelines and regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-071372b252509d0e29e64264c0511359</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_35.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857381</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Decision Making">
      <data key="d0">Decision Making</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Decision making refers to the capability of an AI system to make choices based on analyzed data, which may have legal implications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-071372b252509d0e29e64264c0511359</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_35.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857381</data>
    </node>
    <node id="General-Purpose AI Model">
      <data key="d0">General-Purpose AI Model</data>
      <data key="d1">AIModel</data>
      <data key="d2">General-purpose AI models are integrated into AI systems and are subject to specific regulatory obligations when placed on the market.&lt;SEP&gt;The General-Purpose AI Model is an advanced artificial intelligence system designed for a wide array of applications, distinguished by its versatility and adaptability across multiple domains. This model is capable of performing various tasks without the need for specific programming for each application, allowing it to be directly deployed or integrated into other AI systems, thereby emphasizing its broad usability.

Despite its extensive capabilities, the General-Purpose AI Model is associated with systemic risks that must be carefully managed. These risks can manifest under certain high-impact conditions, making thorough assessment and mitigation essential, especially in light of alerts from scientific panels or regulatory bodies. Compliance with specific regulations is critical for the model's deployment in the European Union market, as it must adhere to established regulatory standards that ensure ongoing risk evaluation and compliance.

Furthermore, the General-Purpose AI Model does not possess a legal personality; rather, it is represented by authorized individuals who facilitate access and evaluations of the system. This underscores the importance of regulatory adherence and the classification of the model concerning its capabilities and potential systemic risks.

In summary, while the General-Purpose AI Model offers significant advantages through its flexibility and broad applicability, careful attention to risk assessment and regulatory compliance is imperative to effectively manage its potential impacts and ensure its safe utilization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f4ac0ccf9bd954306cee6efbfd342416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-140dff8b8263721e25ea86a4104c273d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1ef1c9ca92c002cf6ad36264fe1292c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89491b02af0a00cbc13f9e8df827a6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fb0ee5d200ca5b71eb6d9f53ad070ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-decd01dd1bf25270eddf9979fe28678a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-873c3732f26f3ace86c77cfec67991ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c553a0db4b39033e7fcfeddeb912aac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-447d51c65bac6d28fd62c36c3e70e08b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c49e78c25e30ed3a2557915010f14f3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b567607dbb431b0d294cd02679760039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe0c14a128bfd78c4c5056f7102cc152&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ab4f338bfa06297d4c996d7d54dc70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90efb8f063f236753e4794005afa2a0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e519b84a1d0987cd3b0aab32a476aa33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8033b978339bfb2f89fde823ffa3f524&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0bef2c1dcc3d7b428c7611732f7ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7d62750f1113d24ac155fcd2b2ef02c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5406d942407c55f04629004d833f8196&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c259012a2ff719418b0deb6cbd52130&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-075ecb5835777e6044264a23ca0cb20a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec7c9ce58b650afe456517c2483e56c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_75.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_113.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_115.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_91.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_52.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_97.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_93.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_92.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_51.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_111.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_90.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_53.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863931</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Systemic Risk">
      <data key="d0">Systemic Risk</data>
      <data key="d1">Risk</data>
      <data key="d2">Systemic Risk is a term that encapsulates the broad and potential risks associated with the development, deployment, and market placement of general-purpose AI models. It pertains to the evaluations conducted to ascertain the capabilities and risks posed by these models, specifically relating to their ability to impact entire systems or markets. The concept of systemic risk highlights the potential for such AI models to introduce significant threats or vulnerabilities that could undermine the integrity of the overall system. It emphasizes the broader implications of AI model deployment, which can lead to widespread negative effects on users and the market. Systemic risk is therefore concerned with the comprehensive assessment of how AI capabilities can influence not just individual entities, but the entire system or Union level, raising awareness of the potential challenges and threats posed by these technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic Risk refers to the potential negative impact that a general-purpose AI model can present, necessitating regulatory oversight.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic risk refers to the potential impact of a general-purpose AI model on broader systems, necessitating evaluation and oversight.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic Risk refers to the potential for a failure within a specific AI model to negatively affect the broader system or environment, necessitating regulatory oversight.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic risk pertains to potential significantly negative effects of certain AI models and necessitates compliance with regulatory obligations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-212b902a4529db42951674775ac3ec73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90efb8f063f236753e4794005afa2a0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-140dff8b8263721e25ea86a4104c273d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e519b84a1d0987cd3b0aab32a476aa33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1ef1c9ca92c002cf6ad36264fe1292c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89491b02af0a00cbc13f9e8df827a6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cfbca03bf6afb99c3326dc8b02d083b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec7c9ce58b650afe456517c2483e56c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe0c14a128bfd78c4c5056f7102cc152&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e23bb4c71b510fec0bbe6570de37cd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0bef2c1dcc3d7b428c7611732f7ffc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_113.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_104.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_52.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_97.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_93.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_51.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_111.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_55.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_90.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863931</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Floating Point Operations">
      <data key="d0">Floating Point Operations</data>
      <data key="d1">Metric</data>
      <data key="d2">Floating Point Operations is a metric used to quantify the computation used for training an AI model, particularly when it exceeds 10^25.&lt;SEP&gt;Floating point operations are a computational metric that plays a critical role in determining the capabilities of AI models during training.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e519b84a1d0987cd3b0aab32a476aa33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fb0ee5d200ca5b71eb6d9f53ad070ef</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_51.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863246</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Benchmarks and Indicators">
      <data key="d0">Benchmarks and Indicators</data>
      <data key="d1">Metric</data>
      <data key="d2">Benchmarks and Indicators are tools used to evaluate the capabilities and risks associated with AI models in relation to evolving technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Benchmarks and indicators are used to measure and define the level of risk associated with AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e519b84a1d0987cd3b0aab32a476aa33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b7fd511ed97ef1a87c9783c3425b7d4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_173.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_51.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861943</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High Impact Capabilities">
      <data key="d0">High Impact Capabilities</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">High Impact Capabilities refer to the significant abilities of a general-purpose AI model as evaluated through technical tools, which may include bespoke indicators and benchmarks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e519b84a1d0987cd3b0aab32a476aa33</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_51.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857384</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Tools and Methodologies">
      <data key="d0">Technical Tools and Methodologies</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical Tools and Methodologies are the means by which high impact capabilities of AI models are assessed, including the use of indicators and benchmarks.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical tools and methodologies are the necessary frameworks for evaluating high-impact capabilities and systemic risks of general-purpose AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e519b84a1d0987cd3b0aab32a476aa33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c259012a2ff719418b0deb6cbd52130</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_51.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_111.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861980</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cumulative Amount of Computation">
      <data key="d0">Cumulative Amount of Computation</data>
      <data key="d1">Metric</data>
      <data key="d2">Cumulative Amount of Computation is a metric indicating the total computation used in training an AI model, impacting its classification regarding systemic risk.&lt;SEP&gt;The cumulative amount of computation used for training an AI model is measured in floating point operations and is a relevant indicator of model capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e519b84a1d0987cd3b0aab32a476aa33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c259012a2ff719418b0deb6cbd52130</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_51.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_111.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861980</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Criteria in Annex XIII">
      <data key="d0">Criteria in Annex XIII</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Criteria in Annex XIII outlines specific standards that AI models must meet regarding capabilities and impacts as evaluated by the Commission.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e519b84a1d0987cd3b0aab32a476aa33</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_51.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857384</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Thresholds">
      <data key="d0">Thresholds</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Thresholds are benchmarks used to assess the impact and capabilities of AI models, adjusted over time based on technological changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Thresholds refer to specific levels defined in the legislation that quantify when AI models are regarded as having high impact capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e519b84a1d0987cd3b0aab32a476aa33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90efb8f063f236753e4794005afa2a0d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_51.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_111.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 97">
      <data key="d0">Article 97</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 97 serves as a significant regulatory framework that empowers the Commission to adopt delegated acts concerning various aspects of artificial intelligence (AI) systems. It specifically allows for the amendment of conditions related to these systems based on new evidence, ensuring that regulations remain current and relevant. Through Article 97, the Commission has the authority to alter thresholds and criteria for AI evaluation, which directly influences how laws and regulations are amended.

Additionally, Article 97 provides the legal foundation for the Commission to adopt acts related to compliance methodologies, which are essential for ensuring adherence to established standards. The article also grants the Commission the ability to amend existing regulations concerning the EU declaration of conformity, adapting to ongoing technical progress and evolving compliance needs. Overall, Article 97 plays a critical role in shaping the regulatory landscape for AI, ensuring that it can respond effectively to changes in technology and information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8cb1edc11e8b8d0e952b15617a80f379&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5abff9e94aff7675c473268fd21bf551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e519b84a1d0987cd3b0aab32a476aa33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdd0ab3aadbdd5226fa3661ea9057181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bfb9287798720e37fcd8bae961e88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4d62babb1c5a144faeae6ac2f13628</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_51.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_11.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_6.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_47.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_53.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863780</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive (EU) 2019/1937">
      <data key="d0">Directive (EU) 2019/1937</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive (EU) 2019/1937 outlines protections for whistleblowers reporting infringements of Union law, enhancing their safety and encouraging reporting.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive (EU) 2019/1937 provides a legal framework for the reporting of infringements and safeguards for whistleblowers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e74c582b50b1dcae6565f7384ebbe5e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1265df2d2f07835cf2aadd7299c694a9</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_172.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_87.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861049</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Reporting of Infringements">
      <data key="d0">Reporting of Infringements</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Reporting of infringements relates to the requirement for individuals to disclose violations of the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1265df2d2f07835cf2aadd7299c694a9</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_87.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857386</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Protection of Persons Reporting Infringements">
      <data key="d0">Protection of Persons Reporting Infringements</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Protection of persons involves legal safeguards to defend whistleblowers from retaliation or discrimination.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1265df2d2f07835cf2aadd7299c694a9</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_87.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857386</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Protection of Whistleblowers">
      <data key="d0">Protection of Whistleblowers</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Protection of whistleblowers involves measures to safeguard individuals who report infringements from retaliation and discrimination.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1265df2d2f07835cf2aadd7299c694a9</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_87.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857386</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Infringements">
      <data key="d0">Infringements</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Infringements are violations of the Regulation that need to be reported by individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;Infringements refer to violations of established obligations by AI model providers, which the AI Office will investigate.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-af991f85166d6ddfbbf84e4a73207d3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1265df2d2f07835cf2aadd7299c694a9</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_87.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_162.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861467</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Persons Reporting Infringements">
      <data key="d0">Persons Reporting Infringements</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Persons reporting infringements are individuals who disclose violations and are afforded protection under the Directive.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1265df2d2f07835cf2aadd7299c694a9</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_87.json</data>
