    <node id="Compliance obligations">
      <data key="d0">Compliance obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Compliance obligations are the requirements that AI providers must meet to ensure that their systems adhere to established regulations and standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a67563c32c3414ab14ce22666bed23dc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_85.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857391</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk Management System">
      <data key="d0">Risk Management System</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">A Risk Management System refers to procedures that assess and mitigate risks associated with high-risk AI applications.&lt;SEP&gt;The risk management system involves policies and procedures implemented by AI system providers to identify, assess, and mitigate potential risks associated with AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The risk management system is a crucial capability for ensuring compliance and managing risks associated with high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The risk management system is designed to identify, assess, and mitigate risks associated with high-risk AI systems, ensuring compliance with relevant regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Risk Management System is a framework used by providers to mitigate the risks associated with high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6bf82c08e44c3a6e12c9472e052df840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a30c75209c0fbb0ca1bb4afe44c77d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c32bc5fa5cdfa35a393a42535dc4fdfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac68c725e087cb7c659f2dd75f0a6e34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1952e0d35566561db978f8ee1ebdbd3b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_8.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_9.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_64.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863750</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Harmonisation Legislation">
      <data key="d0">Union Harmonisation Legislation</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">The Union Harmonisation Legislation is a comprehensive set of regulations and directives established by the European Union to ensure consistent safety and compliance standards across its member states, particularly for products incorporating high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) systems. This legislation serves as the legal framework governing conformity assessment procedures, ensuring that all products, including high-risk AI systems, adhere to established safety, health, and consumer protection standards.

The primary objective of the Union Harmonisation Legislation is to create uniformity within the legal frameworks of the EU, facilitating the consistent application of regulatory requirements among member states. By prescribing essential safety and compliance standards, it addresses public safety concerns and safeguards consumer interests. The legislation provides a standardized approach to compliance and assessment for various industries, including those utilizing AI technologies.

In summary, the Union Harmonisation Legislation plays a crucial role in establishing a coherent legal framework across the European Union, aiding in the compliance processes for AI systems and a range of other products, thereby promoting regulatory coherence and enhancing safety within the market.&lt;SEP&gt;Union harmonisation legislation refers to the body of EU legislation that ensures uniform application of regulations across member states.&lt;SEP&gt;Union harmonisation legislation consists of directives and regulations that ensure consistent application of laws across member states pertaining to high-risk products, including AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Union harmonisation legislation sets the standards and requirements for products that may include AI systems to ensure safety and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad9c740a10a5c1577e578a593bd61fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70555b8168fcbd401cc11093ec15091a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f56b40e98f8949a37c3ab283b01f7050&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bf82c08e44c3a6e12c9472e052df840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3ee1fc3ca38d0fe1cd19861a325e159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3e6894a9009f1db207c0ec639d8a39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53fb2685a38836a165fa7637bbbadce2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ab1f3b6cbb052c58ff3b9fc75a6d7a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c168b1207668ad4ba646371f91bfce09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2298fd83910d35175065de74977bd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4348ad8873ef2041aca94abc9297ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13bd6c41d609ae7976a7b3ac4ab8e3fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f13d730755b7535c59eb130d6f7ac62e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8efd21db4fc63a879493cbb376ae904&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3177468233ec37ad2a71dc38caa17377&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff611ee371ea780574e9c16859c31f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c72b31b17ef0accd3df4ab25a063163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04f1483cdf6b84729e33ebc4a611375b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1952e0d35566561db978f8ee1ebdbd3b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_8.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_40.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_51.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_29.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_124.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_147.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_128.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_64.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_6.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_47.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863958</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 9">
      <data key="d0">Article 9</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 9 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 outlines specific duties and powers granted to regulatory authorities for overseeing AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 9 refers to the specific section of the regulation that addresses the risk management system applicable to high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1952e0d35566561db978f8ee1ebdbd3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe4515f5aa3b0876e436a8a0dffc23e</data>
