    <node id="Information Platform">
      <data key="d0">Information Platform</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">An information platform is a centralized resource provided by the Commission to offer guidance related to AI regulations for SMEs.&lt;SEP&gt;The information platform is a system developed to provide accessible information regarding obligations and regulations for AI operators across the Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e3d60cf6cbe0ae91a9793cb5c98a4a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6ed86abb2e8f0e12897e923d1e9964</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_62.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_143.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861724</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Best Practices in Public Procurement Procedures">
      <data key="d0">Best Practices in Public Procurement Procedures</data>
      <data key="d1">AITechnique</data>
      <data key="d2">Best practices refer to established guidelines that promote effectiveness and efficiency in public procurement related to AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3d6ed86abb2e8f0e12897e923d1e9964</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_143.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Translation Costs">
      <data key="d0">Translation Costs</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Translation costs are significant expenses related to mandatory documentation and communication with authorities, particularly for smaller providers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-712b56cbfc73c46eacde9204fa4e5c49</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_143.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Procurement Procedures">
      <data key="d0">Public Procurement Procedures</data>
      <data key="d1">AreaOfImpact</data>
      <data key="d2">Public procurement procedures are influenced by AI systems and require convergence of best practices as promoted by the Commission.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-712b56cbfc73c46eacde9204fa4e5c49</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_143.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cross-Border Deployers">
      <data key="d0">Cross-Border Deployers</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">Cross-border deployers are entities that operate in multiple jurisdictions and need to meet diverse regulatory requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-712b56cbfc73c46eacde9204fa4e5c49</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_143.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="medium-sized enterprises">
      <data key="d0">medium-sized enterprises</data>
      <data key="d1">AIUser</data>
      <data key="d2">Medium-sized enterprises are businesses that may face challenges in understanding and complying with regulations due to limited legal resources and training.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e215b390ecf16d1806ebe2ba8ac2c33d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_143.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Commission Recommendation of 6 May 2003">
      <data key="d0">Commission Recommendation of 6 May 2003</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">The Commission Recommendation provides definitions and guidance related to micro, small, and medium-sized enterprises.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e215b390ecf16d1806ebe2ba8ac2c33d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_143.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="legal resources">
      <data key="d0">legal resources</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Legal resources comprise the necessary documentation, legal advice, and support systems that businesses require to navigate regulations effectively.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e215b390ecf16d1806ebe2ba8ac2c33d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_143.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="training">
      <data key="d0">training</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Training encompasses the educational processes that individuals undergo to gain the required expertise in overseeing high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Training involves programs and activities aimed at equipping staff and stakeholders in medium-sized enterprises with the knowledge necessary to ensure compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Training is the process by which deployers acquire necessary skills and knowledge to effectively utilize and manage high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e215b390ecf16d1806ebe2ba8ac2c33d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8c5a915dca180e1c423cefa27ea6cd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a68b9cb2eff595118d2af9313b6c89f5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_9.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_143.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863750</data>
    </node>
    <node id="micro enterprises">
      <data key="d0">micro enterprises</data>
      <data key="d1">AIUser</data>
      <data key="d2">Micro enterprises are the smallest category of businesses, often requiring specific support and resources to comply with regulations in the same manner as medium-sized enterprises.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e215b390ecf16d1806ebe2ba8ac2c33d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_143.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="small enterprises">
      <data key="d0">small enterprises</data>
      <data key="d1">AIUser</data>
      <data key="d2">Small enterprises fall between micro and medium-sized enterprises in terms of size and also face similar challenges regarding regulatory compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e215b390ecf16d1806ebe2ba8ac2c33d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_143.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857411</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Transparency">
      <data key="d0">Transparency</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bbcf833252ce65fd6a1d8bd1f5a6efc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-849f8f0403e6b12fa8a9c24b84c094c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aca56f82b70892874784bcec5c2bb2c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9685a1f72e235a3f5b9ee69878eedb21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a65ec6b0fbd17afe47587686523a725&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6ed86abb2e8f0e12897e923d1e9964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-769497b509433ed0e4746ff50bbdec69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77093970e26d1be04734ed16ea88f777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b474f9815c7033ca1ad8daff4012eff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-256a6003a5841f2764536c55f7086431</data>
      <data key="d2">Transparency in AI systems relates to the clarity and openness about how such systems operate and make decisions, as mandated by the Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Transparency is a critical principle that emphasizes the importance of clear and open communication regarding the operations and decision-making processes of artificial intelligence (AI) systems. It involves making information about the AI system's operations, assessments, and potential risks available to relevant stakeholders, thereby promoting trust and understanding among users. Transparency in AI encompasses the development and usage of systems that allow for traceability and explainability. This ensures that users are aware of their interactions with AI and can comprehend how decisions are made. Additionally, transparency is crucial in ensuring that conformity assessment fees are fair and openly communicated, preventing small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) from facing disproportionate burdens. Overall, transparency serves as a foundational element in fostering accountability and ethical standards within AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Transparency refers to the clear communication of processes and requirements necessary for effective participation in AI regulatory sandboxes.&lt;SEP&gt;Transparency refers to the clarity and openness of AI systems in their operations, which is crucial for accountability.&lt;SEP&gt;Transparency refers to the clarity and openness of information provided about high-risk AI systems, enabling better understanding and informed decision-making.</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_59.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_143.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_102.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_27.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_58.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_9.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863464</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Literacy">
      <data key="d0">AI Literacy</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Literacy is a comprehensive measure of understanding and knowledge that staff and users possess regarding AI systems. It encompasses the skills and knowledge necessary for stakeholders to engage with AI technologies responsibly, while being aware of their potential risks and benefits. This concept involves developing an informed perspective on AI systems, which enables individuals to understand, deploy, and utilize these technologies effectively. 

AI Literacy provides essential knowledge and skills to stakeholders, aiding them in making informed decisions concerning AI systems and promoting both understanding and compliance with these technologies. It also highlights the implications of AI for developers, operators, and users, addressing the public's awareness of the benefits, risks, and obligations associated with AI. By fostering informed public discourse, AI Literacy plays a crucial role in ensuring that individuals are not only aware of AI technologies but are also equipped to participate meaningfully in discussions about their deployment and governance.&lt;SEP&gt;AI literacy refers to the understanding and knowledge of AI systems, particularly among users and developers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fe76292b9a553c383dab6b0a4a67cee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c9405f93ec3e0ccf6209ed15ef0263f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00e7606a0fa9d588f18d67d02cfcf654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8462fb6c49f462e0c2199ce80842ebde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98532c431ec75ae38c76dc0730337a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-064e3e5273a81cd8d9a47da9a3f51240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21acb22d994b8f65ea3709a99eb85032&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a77d0693b936376b7e0f7b222210759</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_4.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_20.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_95.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858929</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers of AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Providers of AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers are entities responsible for ensuring AI systems are designed to be transparent and compliant with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of AI Systems are entities responsible for creating and supplying AI technologies for deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of AI systems are entities participating in AI regulatory sandboxes to develop and validate their innovations before market release.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of AI Systems are responsible for ensuring compliance with regulations regarding output management, detection, and disclosure of potentially manipulated outputs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7570653f66cb58454b80be2046705a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a77d0693b936376b7e0f7b222210759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475967c83e624bc711a9ff13e8150163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bccefc944ad0794c75bc69b977c88a1</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_4.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_120.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859450</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Staff">
      <data key="d0">Staff</data>
      <data key="d1">AIUser</data>
      <data key="d2">Staff refers to personnel who operate and utilize AI systems in their respective contexts, relying on AI literacy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1a77d0693b936376b7e0f7b222210759</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_4.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857420</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Context of Use">
      <data key="d0">Context of Use</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Context of Use encapsulates the specific scenarios and environments where AI systems are implemented and utilized.&lt;SEP&gt;The context in which AI systems are used influences their design and the obligations of providers to inform users.&lt;SEP&gt;Context of use denotes the specific situation or environment where high-risk AI systems are deployed, affecting their impact and risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1a77d0693b936376b7e0f7b222210759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de3f18a6d766d2baa57ae891b9da7741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bccefc944ad0794c75bc69b977c88a1</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_4.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_93.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859410</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Operation of AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Operation of AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Operation of AI Systems encompasses the capability to manage, deploy, and use AI systems effectively in various settings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1a77d0693b936376b7e0f7b222210759</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_4.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857420</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Knowledge">
      <data key="d0">Technical Knowledge</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical Knowledge refers to the expertise and skills that individuals must possess to work with AI systems, including understanding algorithms and technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1a77d0693b936376b7e0f7b222210759</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_4.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857420</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Experience">
      <data key="d0">Experience</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Experience signifies the practical exposure and familiarity with AI systems that aids in their effective operation and use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1a77d0693b936376b7e0f7b222210759</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_4.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857420</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Education and Training">
      <data key="d0">Education and Training</data>
      <data key="d1">Domain</data>
      <data key="d2">Education and Training involve the formal and informal processes through which personnel gain the necessary skills and knowledge to work with AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Education and training benefit from AI through personalized learning experiences and resource optimization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1a77d0693b936376b7e0f7b222210759&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a975f3ad5ea339c199a21dd569a7acb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_4.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_4.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861629</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Persons or Groups of Persons">
      <data key="d0">Persons or Groups of Persons</data>
      <data key="d1">AISubject</data>
      <data key="d2">Persons or Groups of Persons are the end-users or stakeholders affected by the use of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1a77d0693b936376b7e0f7b222210759</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_4.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857420</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Scientific Panel">
      <data key="d0">Scientific Panel</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">The Scientific Panel consists of experts who evaluate AI models and advise the Commission on which models should be classified as posing systemic risk.&lt;SEP&gt;The Scientific Panel is an authoritative body composed of independent experts and scientists with specialized knowledge in artificial intelligence (AI). Its primary role is to support the enforcement of AI regulations by integrating the scientific community into AI governance. The Panel has the ability to request information from providers of general-purpose AI models to ensure compliance with relevant standards and guidelines.

In addition to its evaluative functions, the Scientific Panel is responsible for monitoring AI models, assessing potential risks, and issuing qualified alerts when necessary. It coordinates with the AI Office to execute specific tasks and respond effectively to identified risks, ensuring a proactive approach to AI governance. Overall, the Scientific Panel plays a crucial role in promoting safety and compliance within the AI landscape through its expert guidance and oversight.&lt;SEP&gt;The Scientific Panel is a group of experts consulted to contribute perspectives on AI practices and codes of conduct.&lt;SEP&gt;The scientific panel provides qualified alerts concerning systemic risks related to AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dbcc9707fb1611da88a5526a5558a165&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ab4f338bfa06297d4c996d7d54dc70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c553a0db4b39033e7fcfeddeb912aac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-140dff8b8263721e25ea86a4104c273d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a0c1908573a7d6a832a6b35befbd7ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f3c3fe390cb5d40b199e1bcc024928f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69b5f24963810305f2a7846d54923bf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6a5cc59273abbe42c743808026477c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec7c9ce58b650afe456517c2483e56c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_113.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_91.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_92.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_163.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_68.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_116.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_148.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_90.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863853</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Safeguard Procedure">
      <data key="d0">Union Safeguard Procedure</data>
      <data key="d1">AILifecyclePhase</data>
      <data key="d2">The Union Safeguard Procedure outlines steps for managing risks associated with AI systems at a union level.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1f3c3fe390cb5d40b199e1bcc024928f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_68.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857424</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Tools and Methodologies">
      <data key="d0">Tools and Methodologies</data>
      <data key="d1">AITechnique</data>
      <data key="d2">Tools and methodologies are developed for evaluating the capabilities of general-purpose AI models and systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1f3c3fe390cb5d40b199e1bcc024928f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_68.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857426</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Evaluation Criteria">
      <data key="d0">Evaluation Criteria</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Evaluation Criteria refer to the standards used to assess the performance and capabilities of AI models and systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1f3c3fe390cb5d40b199e1bcc024928f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_68.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857426</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Geographical Representation">
      <data key="d0">Geographical Representation</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Geographical Representation pertains to ensuring diverse expert representation from various regions in the Scientific Panel.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1f3c3fe390cb5d40b199e1bcc024928f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_68.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857426</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Expertise and Competence">
      <data key="d0">Expertise and Competence</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Expertise and Competence refer to the qualifications and skills required for members of the Scientific Panel.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1f3c3fe390cb5d40b199e1bcc024928f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_68.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857426</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Confidentiality of Information">
      <data key="d0">Confidentiality of Information</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Confidentiality of Information refers to the obligation of the Scientific Panel members to protect sensitive data obtained during their tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1f3c3fe390cb5d40b199e1bcc024928f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_68.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857426</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conflict of Interest Management">
      <data key="d0">Conflict of Interest Management</data>
      <data key="d1">RiskControl</data>
      <data key="d2">Conflict of Interest Management encompasses procedures to prevent bias in the members of the Scientific Panel.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1f3c3fe390cb5d40b199e1bcc024928f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_68.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857426</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 90">
      <data key="d0">Article 90</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 90 outlines specific requirements and provisions related to general-purpose AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1c408a5b914a49af8b42e7e84ad02be6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_68.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857426</data>
    </node>
    <node id="market surveillance authorities">
      <data key="d0">market surveillance authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">Market surveillance authorities are responsible for overseeing the compliance of AI systems and taking necessary actions against non-compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;market surveillance authorities are responsible for overseeing and ensuring compliance in the deployment of AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1c408a5b914a49af8b42e7e84ad02be6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345a8ba89ed0ea3325462384d5e16aaf</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_68.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861814</data>
    </node>
    <node id="scientific panel">
      <data key="d0">scientific panel</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">The scientific panel assists in identifying AI models that should be evaluated for systemic risk by the Commission.&lt;SEP&gt;The scientific panel consists of experts who evaluate the capabilities of AI models and maintain impartiality during their assessments.&lt;SEP&gt;The scientific panel provides qualified alerts regarding general-purpose AI models and their risks to the Commission.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8ec7c9ce58b650afe456517c2483e56c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c408a5b914a49af8b42e7e84ad02be6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e23bb4c71b510fec0bbe6570de37cd5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_113.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_68.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863273</data>
    </node>
    <node id="tools and methodologies">
      <data key="d0">tools and methodologies</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Tools and methodologies are developed to assess and benchmark the capabilities of general-purpose AI models and systems, facilitating accurate evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1c408a5b914a49af8b42e7e84ad02be6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_68.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857426</data>
    </node>
    <node id="systemic risk">
      <data key="d0">systemic risk</data>
      <data key="d1">RiskConcept</data>
      <data key="d2">Systemic risk addresses the potential for general-purpose AI models to pose risks that could impact the entire system or industry, necessitating careful classification and oversight.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic risk pertains to risks specific to high-impact AI capabilities that can have widespread negative effects across society.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic risk refers to risks specific to high-impact capabilities of general-purpose AI models, affecting public health, safety, fundamental rights, and society.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3266d68b5262e6852cabbe36178dec96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afea58b87ff95e4731bff6457b0b57c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c408a5b914a49af8b42e7e84ad02be6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_68.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="confidentiality of information">
      <data key="d0">confidentiality of information</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Confidentiality of information refers to practices that safeguard sensitive data obtained during evaluations, ensuring that trust and integrity are maintained.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1c408a5b914a49af8b42e7e84ad02be6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_68.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857426</data>
    </node>
    <node id="conflicts of interest">
      <data key="d0">conflicts of interest</data>
      <data key="d1">Risk</data>
      <data key="d2">Conflicts of interest may arise in the evaluation process, necessitating systems and procedures to manage and prevent potential biases or unfair evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1c408a5b914a49af8b42e7e84ad02be6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_68.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857426</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 74(11)">
      <data key="d0">Article 74(11)</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 74(11) outlines provisions related to the coordination of cross-border market surveillance activities to enhance regulatory oversight of AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1c408a5b914a49af8b42e7e84ad02be6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_68.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857426</data>
    </node>
    <node id="provisions on conditions and procedures">
      <data key="d0">provisions on conditions and procedures</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Provisions on conditions and procedures detail the operational framework and guidelines that the scientific panel and its members must follow during evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1c408a5b914a49af8b42e7e84ad02be6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_68.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857426</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Alerts">
      <data key="d0">Alerts</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Alerts are notifications generated by the Scientific Panel to communicate important information or updates.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dbcc9707fb1611da88a5526a5558a165</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_68.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857426</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Procedures">
      <data key="d0">Procedures</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Procedures outline the specific methods and arrangements established by the Scientific Panel for executing their responsibilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dbcc9707fb1611da88a5526a5558a165</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_68.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857426</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI-on-Demand Platform">
      <data key="d0">AI-on-Demand Platform</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">The AI-on-Demand Platform is a resource aimed at facilitating compliance with regulations and enhancing the expertise available in the market for AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ba662546e18e6e5f82c3cd1c5b4c3b75</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_145.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857427</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Digital Innovation Hubs">
      <data key="d0">European Digital Innovation Hubs</data>
      <data key="d1">AIProvider</data>
      <data key="d2">European Digital Innovation Hubs aim to provide resources and networks for developing digital technologies, including AI.&lt;SEP&gt;European Digital Innovation Hubs are centers established to support the digital transformation, providing technical and scientific support to SMEs and notified bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;European Digital Innovation Hubs are centers that provide support and services to facilitate access to tools and facilities for AI development.&lt;SEP&gt;European Digital Innovation Hubs are initiatives that support the adoption and innovation of AI technologies across Europe.&lt;SEP&gt;European Digital Innovation Hubs offer support and resources for SMEs and other actors in the AI ecosystem to foster innovation and development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7859a0c655f74761757b416c3b50bf36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba662546e18e6e5f82c3cd1c5b4c3b75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eae051373e28d701c4893438950556b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc97d8ad7f3aa0522d885f92ee323822&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0271020749ae70ce56cbd607a6f6662a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_145.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_68.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_139.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_58.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862804</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing and Experimentation Facilities">
      <data key="d0">Testing and Experimentation Facilities</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing and Experimentation Facilities are established by the Commission and Member States to assist providers and notified bodies with technological implementation and compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Testing and Experimentation Facilities are resources within the regulatory sandbox used for practical assessments of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Testing and experimentation facilities provide services for assessing conformity with Union harmonisation legislation.&lt;SEP&gt;Testing and experimentation facilities are environments where AI systems can be safely evaluated for performance and compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Testing and experimentation facilities are resources provided to participants in AI regulatory sandboxes to enable rigorous evaluation of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ba662546e18e6e5f82c3cd1c5b4c3b75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95424b9dff57302628c496570b4baff4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc97d8ad7f3aa0522d885f92ee323822&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0271020749ae70ce56cbd607a6f6662a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70555b8168fcbd401cc11093ec15091a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_145.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_139.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_147.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_58.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862804</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Notified Bodies">
      <data key="d0">Notified Bodies</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">Notified Bodies are organizations designated by EU countries and national authorities to assess the conformity of certain products, particularly high-risk artificial intelligence (AI) systems, prior to their market entry. These entities play a crucial role in ensuring that such products comply with the established regulatory standards and implementing regulations related to artificial intelligence. They are responsible for conducting conformity assessments in accordance with established procedures and must operate with independence, objectivity, and impartiality to effectively fulfill their duties.

The primary objective of Notified Bodies is to verify that AI systems meet the necessary regulatory requirements throughout their development and assessment phases. Within this context, they are tasked with evaluating the compliance of AI systems with relevant legal requirements and standards, and subsequently issuing certifications that reflect their assessment. Additionally, Notified Bodies communicate essential information with the European Commission and relevant authorities to maintain transparency and compliance within the regulatory framework. Overall, Notified Bodies are recognized entities vital for the oversight and approval of high-risk AI systems, ensuring their conformity to legal acts and standards prior to being placed on the market.&lt;SEP&gt;Notified bodies are organizations authorized to issue certificates confirming that AI systems comply with regulatory requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d9317b056c2a260423c79e368903cde7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2e0f993ca9c4e593e5fcbdd8fc03fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba662546e18e6e5f82c3cd1c5b4c3b75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a5e7031602556ef7d57e2811f58992&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1d974005cd87fc21678c732472ee11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c72b31b17ef0accd3df4ab25a063163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf8a675497acfbeb420b95621b7cb31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e5d20a8e9427a4698b84f758676994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eae051373e28d701c4893438950556b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97ee5867d3c03f24001b650ad752686d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28717558f1bb8bd2fd8b9542f8e2a99c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0461b38c664574f634a78148bfce0336&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4d62babb1c5a144faeae6ac2f13628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-397d6e2474c4f45e883f265653f2e715</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_78.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_38.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_34.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_45.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_126.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_68.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_44.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_31.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_145.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Distributor">
      <data key="d0">Distributor</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">A Distributor is an entity that makes high-risk AI systems available on the market and is responsible for ensuring compliance with legal regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;A distributor is a natural or legal person that makes an AI system available on the Union market, acting as an intermediary in the supply chain.&lt;SEP&gt;A distributor is considered a provider of a high-risk AI system and is subject to relevant regulations if they put their name on the system.&lt;SEP&gt;A person or entity in the supply chain that makes an AI system available on the Union market.&lt;SEP&gt;A distributor is a type of deployer who supplies AI systems to the market, which may require compliance with specific obligations if the system is classified as high-risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7d62750f1113d24ac155fcd2b2ef02c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73fd7e801c2d8d41361f6b16b45c6ed0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_84.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861098</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Importer">
      <data key="d0">Importer</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">An importer is defined as a natural or legal person located in the Union who places an Artificial Intelligence (AI) system from a third country onto the market. This entity plays a crucial role in the supply chain, as it essentially brings high-risk AI systems into the market and is categorized as a provider under the relevant regulations. According to the definitions outlined in the regulations, importers of high-risk AI systems must ensure that these systems comply with all necessary regulatory requirements. Consequently, the importer shares the responsibility for regulatory compliance, confirming that the AI systems meet all stipulated standards before being introduced into the market. Thus, the importer serves as a vital link in the distribution of AI technologies, particularly those classified as high-risk, and is tasked with upholding industry regulations and safety standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7d62750f1113d24ac155fcd2b2ef02c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21678b36bef336bf18e091bdfdb68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73fd7e801c2d8d41361f6b16b45c6ed0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_84.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861101</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deployer">
      <data key="d0">Deployer</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">The deployer is responsible for putting an AI system into operation and must report any serious incidents associated with it.&lt;SEP&gt;The term "Deployer" refers to an entity, which can be an individual or organization, that is responsible for the practical implementation, management, and utilization of AI systems, particularly those classified as high-risk. Deployers play a critical role in the adoption of these AI systems by collaborating in the testing process to ensure both safety and efficacy. They are tasked with understanding the foreseeable risks associated with the use of AI, ensuring compliance with specific regulations, and maintaining effective human oversight during the operation of these systems.

As providers of high-risk AI technologies, deployers are required to assess the impact of these systems, identify potential risks, and implement appropriate mitigation strategies to address them. Their responsibilities exclude personal, non-professional activities, focusing instead on the professional deployment and management of AI technology. Deployers also need to have clear instructions to accurately interpret and utilize the outputs generated by the AI systems they deploy, ensuring that they can effectively operate them within a practical environment.&lt;SEP&gt;The deployer is the entity responsible for implementing high-risk AI systems in practice, who must ensure compliance with oversight requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f6e14583352886a741ac1d51eada03a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0c31436f0e7ce27ce5952aa2bf9ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7d62750f1113d24ac155fcd2b2ef02c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ded7b0ac022304fae10651966b33d18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2f186d6b95e69680f63fabb65ad924a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2ba08954f9ed754c2566e3c59b63ee7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b28a4b325cc05a6cc4897f58ccdf00f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c4d127e5313d415dd94f6b6761da956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee04f6104a24650416810ede28f3790b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1516ad8d48077af0d59fc01578f33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65f69156748df83d9fa179140a3fe2aa</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_76.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_13.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_84.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_13.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863731</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Product Manufacturer">
      <data key="d0">Product Manufacturer</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">A product manufacturer can be a provider of a high-risk AI system when such a system is integrated into their products.&lt;SEP&gt;The product manufacturer is responsible for ensuring that the AI system embedded within the final product complies with relevant regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17ccf2ddbeca1f4e8b771a2316b7d16c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_87.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857772</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Area of Impact">
      <data key="d0">Area of Impact</data>
      <data key="d1">AreaOfImpact</data>
      <data key="d2">The area of impact refers to the effects and implications of deploying high-risk AI systems in various sectors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857434</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Documentation">
      <data key="d0">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Documentation encompasses a comprehensive and essential collection of information prepared by providers and deployers of high-risk AI systems to ensure compliance with regulations and facilitate oversight. This body of documentation serves multiple critical purposes, including demonstrating conformity to legal standards, protecting fundamental rights, and ensuring transparency in the operation and governance of AI systems.

It includes vital records, written policies, procedures, and instructions that address both compliance and operational aspects of high-risk AI systems. Furthermore, it comprises necessary compliance records and logs, which are crucial for assessing adherence to relevant financial services laws. These records must be accessible to relevant authorities and can be requested by scientific panels for assessment and verification.

Documentation also details the specifications and compliance requirements associated with high-risk AI systems and provides justifications for significant decisions made during the risk-management process. This includes maintaining thorough logs generated by these systems, particularly in the context of financial institutions, which highlights the necessity for meticulous record-keeping. Additionally, documentation encompasses records and data sets utilized in the development of AI systems, which are vital for validation and testing processes.

Ultimately, effective documentation is pivotal for ensuring accountability and management of AI systems, aligning with AI regulatory frameworks to promote their responsible operation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e853663a3f2d06a9cfea8582e10f089&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c852bda35515c8d5385ef007c8140254&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b5e606b14946a1b388f008868e8e155&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac68c725e087cb7c659f2dd75f0a6e34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe4515f5aa3b0876e436a8a0dffc23e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c553a0db4b39033e7fcfeddeb912aac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a0c1908573a7d6a832a6b35befbd7ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bece07e296fce9647a40a0dde904fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2b7ae4447e7d43e6030d6793c59ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2315cd7abb88dee440f081de5430a32f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2298fd83910d35175065de74977bd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85fb9638473c0974347ccab540b99b7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78dcdae0f5d22df28405d8ae03e038d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fcd3af92cad1d85ebf561f059acb114</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_91.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_164.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_19.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_64.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_163.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_21.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_77.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_157.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_16.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863711</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Substantial Modification">
      <data key="d0">Substantial Modification</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Substantial Modification refers to any significant change made to an AI system that affects its compliance status or intended purposes after market introduction.&lt;SEP&gt;Substantial modification refers to significant alterations made to an existing high-risk AI system that affect its classification.&lt;SEP&gt;Substantial modification refers to unforeseen changes to an AI system post-assessment that may affect its compliance or intended purpose.&lt;SEP&gt;Substantial modification refers to significant alterations in the design or functioning of an AI system and how such changes must be implemented practically.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857827</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-Risk AI System Classification">
      <data key="d0">High-Risk AI System Classification</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">High-risk AI system classification determines whether an AI system meets the criteria outlined in Article 6 of the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857434</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Obligations of Providers">
      <data key="d0">Obligations of Providers</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Obligations of providers involve complying with specific legal requirements when dealing with high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857434</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Access">
      <data key="d0">Technical Access</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical Access involves the provision of tools and technologies required for the deployment and functioning of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical access refers to the ability to obtain and use necessary information and functionalities related to AI systems, as mandated by the Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical access refers to the necessary access and assistance providers must offer to meet regulatory obligations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be61089eed18cfaf2703713378c589a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7963b30391bfa3d5e28ecd9a95b61010</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_86.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_88.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859558</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conformity Assessment Procedures">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Assessment Procedures</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Conformity assessment procedures are methods applied to evaluate whether AI systems meet specified regulatory compliance standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity assessment procedures are systematic evaluation processes required to ensure that high-risk AI systems meet specific regulatory standards. These procedures involve evaluations that verify compliance with set regulations before such AI systems are authorized for use. According to Article 43, these conformity assessment procedures outline the necessary steps for assessing high-risk AI systems to ensure that they satisfy all mandated requirements. Essentially, conformity assessment procedures serve as critical methods for evaluating whether a product adheres to the stipulated standards as dictated by regulatory frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-29241e99bddf5af77eca441d2d8dbc1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1d974005cd87fc21678c732472ee11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b7fd511ed97ef1a87c9783c3425b7d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0461b38c664574f634a78148bfce0336&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07ee6b3452d764ccd9733dceadb1ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-397d6e2474c4f45e883f265653f2e715</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_38.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_34.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_48.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_44.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_173.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Document Transfer">
      <data key="d0">Document Transfer</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Document transfer pertains to the provision of documentation that must occur when transitioning responsibility for high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857434</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 85">
      <data key="d0">Recital 85</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 85 outlines specific considerations in the regulation related to high-risk AI system providers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857434</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 84">
      <data key="d0">Recital 84</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 84 details additional considerations for the assessment and classification of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857434</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 86">
      <data key="d0">Recital 86</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 86 provides context related to the requirements placed on initial providers of AI systems when they transition into high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Recital 86 refers to the obligations of initial providers in the context of regulatory requirements for high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857434</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 87">
      <data key="d0">Recital 87</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 87 addresses the obligations of product manufacturers concerning the integration of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Recital 87 outlines the obligations of product manufacturers regarding high-risk AI systems integrated into their products.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857434</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI system">
      <data key="d0">AI system</data>
      <data key="d1">AISystem</data>
      <data key="d2">An AI system is a framework within which AI models operate, capable of fulfilling various purposes depending on the model integrated within it.&lt;SEP&gt;An AI system refers to software or algorithms that perform tasks and can be considered high-risk depending on their applications and integration in products.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9575387945b55e197ecb0c955ef00f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862178</data>
    </node>
    <node id="product manufacturer">
      <data key="d0">product manufacturer</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">The product manufacturer is viewed as the provider of the high-risk AI system when the system is associated with their products.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857434</data>
    </node>
    <node id="documentation">
      <data key="d0">documentation</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Documentation refers to the necessary information and compliance data required by providers and stakeholders under the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857434</data>
    </node>
    <node id="state of the art">
      <data key="d0">state of the art</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">State of the art refers to the generally acknowledged level of development in technology, necessary for compliance with the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857434</data>
    </node>
    <node id="safety components">
      <data key="d0">safety components</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">Safety components are essential parts of products utilizing AI systems, critical for ensuring the safety and compliance of the products.&lt;SEP&gt;Safety components are parts of products that can be considered high-risk AI systems and fall under related regulatory obligations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18cf1aa30864348514b20fe64038fba8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_47.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861479</data>
    </node>
    <node id="third party">
      <data key="d0">third party</data>
      <data key="d1">AIProvider</data>
      <data key="d2">Third parties are entities that supply tools, services, or components for high-risk AI systems and must adhere to compliance requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857434</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 16">
      <data key="d0">Article 16</data>
      <data key="d1">Document</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 16 outlines the obligations of providers under the Regulation regarding AI practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 16 outlines the specific obligations that must be adhered to regarding compliance for high-risk AI systems by the product manufacturer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857501</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 88">
      <data key="d0">Recital 88</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 88 outlines the need for written agreements between providers of high-risk AI systems and third parties involved. </data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857434</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 89">
      <data key="d0">Recital 89</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 89 discusses the development of voluntary model terms by the AI Office for enhancing compliance among providers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857434</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 90">
      <data key="d0">Recital 90</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 90 emphasizes the publication of voluntary model terms in an easily usable electronic format.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c9021d6cb53dceeddd1e648d3e37fbc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857434</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Third Party">
      <data key="d0">Third Party</data>
      <data key="d1">AISubject</data>
      <data key="d2">A third party refers to entities that provide tools, services, or components for AI systems but are not the primary providers of those systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7cc37264ee8f2a814b7b6f98953de48c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857437</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Open-Source License">
      <data key="d0">Open-Source License</data>
      <data key="d1">License</data>
      <data key="d2">An open-source license allows for the access, usage, modification, and distribution of AI models while ensuring transparency of parameters and architecture.&lt;SEP&gt;An open-source license allows the general-purpose AI model's parameters and architecture to be freely accessible, promoting transparency and collaboration.&lt;SEP&gt;An open-source license allows third parties to access, use, and modify AI tools and services freely, excluding general-purpose AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4dc89de2edca5d2bfe0d5e9e7c99665b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cc37264ee8f2a814b7b6f98953de48c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-212b902a4529db42951674775ac3ec73</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_104.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_53.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863102</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Voluntary Model Terms">
      <data key="d0">Voluntary Model Terms</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Voluntary model terms are recommended guidelines for contracts between AI system providers and third parties, aiming to protect intellectual property and ensure compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7cc37264ee8f2a814b7b6f98953de48c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857437</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Intellectual Property Rights">
      <data key="d0">Intellectual Property Rights</data>
      <data key="d1">Legal Basis</data>
      <data key="d2">Intellectual Property Rights protect the proprietary information and creative works of organizations involved in AI development.&lt;SEP&gt;Intellectual property rights are legal protections for creators and inventors of AI systems, crucial for maintaining confidentiality of source code.&lt;SEP&gt;Intellectual property rights are legal protections that ensure creators maintain control over their inventions and creative works in the context of AI development.&lt;SEP&gt;These rights protect creators' and inventors' works, which can intersect with AI-generated content and ownership issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Intellectual property rights protect creators’ and owners’ rights over their inventions and artistic works.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13b35a74627bd926656242d6545e09a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf8a675497acfbeb420b95621b7cb31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cc37264ee8f2a814b7b6f98953de48c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e284955c1d36330bd14d117bb417611&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7963b30391bfa3d5e28ecd9a95b61010</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_78.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_48.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_167.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_88.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863049</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Contractual Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Contractual Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Contractual Requirements are specific legal obligations that may apply in certain sectors or business cases relating to high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Contractual requirements are the stipulations and obligations that must be met in agreements between AI system providers and other parties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7cc37264ee8f2a814b7b6f98953de48c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8143bb5053cad47b9eaf4c05c9556429</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_90.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857707</data>
    </node>
    <node id="fines">
      <data key="d0">fines</data>
      <data key="d1">Metric</data>
      <data key="d2">Fines are financial penalties imposed by the Commission on AI model providers for regulatory infractions.&lt;SEP&gt;Fines are monetary penalties imposed for non-compliance with data protection regulations, contributing to the Union's general budget.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0b16c22014fb75795531a9a187b8fc81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-828a2d9070cae319b764e3b609bc9b81</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_101.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859985</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EUR 15 000 000">
      <data key="d0">EUR 15 000 000</data>
      <data key="d1">Metric</data>
      <data key="d2">EUR 15 000 000 is the maximum fine amount specified for non-compliance with AI regulations, subject to conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0b16c22014fb75795531a9a187b8fc81</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_101.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857442</data>
    </node>
    <node id="3 % of annual total worldwide turnover">
      <data key="d0">3 % of annual total worldwide turnover</data>
      <data key="d1">Metric</data>
      <data key="d2">It refers to the calculation method for imposing fines on providers based on their total annual revenue.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0b16c22014fb75795531a9a187b8fc81</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_101.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857442</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 91">
      <data key="d0">Article 91</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 91 outlines the obligations of AI providers to comply with document requests from the Commission.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0b16c22014fb75795531a9a187b8fc81</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_101.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857442</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 93">
      <data key="d0">Article 93</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 93 establishes measures that AI providers must follow to avoid penalties imposed by the Commission.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0b16c22014fb75795531a9a187b8fc81</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_101.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857442</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 92">
      <data key="d0">Article 92</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 92 describes the evaluation process of AI models with systemic risk that the Commission may undertake.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 92 mandates evaluations to determine if a general-purpose AI model poses serious systemic risks that must be mitigated.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0b16c22014fb75795531a9a187b8fc81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0bef2c1dcc3d7b428c7611732f7ffc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_93.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_101.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857768</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Court of Justice of the European Union">
      <data key="d0">Court of Justice of the European Union</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeveloper</data>
      <data key="d2">The Court of Justice of the European Union has jurisdiction to review decisions regarding fines and can cancel, reduce, or increase the fines imposed.&lt;SEP&gt;The Court of Justice oversees the review of decisions made by the Commission regarding fines and compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Court of Justice of the European Union reviews decisions made by the Commission regarding penalties and compliance of AI model providers.&lt;SEP&gt;The Court of Justice of the European Union operates independently in its judicial capacity, exempt from the oversight of market surveillance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0b16c22014fb75795531a9a187b8fc81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de6a0d59bb86cca6093fbb52cf156b4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae3ab8a3b5c5d0c61e8b99fa718913b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_169.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_101.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863700</data>
    </node>
    <node id="proportionality and appropriateness">
      <data key="d0">proportionality and appropriateness</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Proportionality and appropriateness are key principles considered by the Commission when determining the severity of fines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0b16c22014fb75795531a9a187b8fc81</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_101.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857442</data>
    </node>
    <node id="preliminary findings">
      <data key="d0">preliminary findings</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Preliminary findings are initial conclusions communicated by the Commission to AI providers regarding potential non-compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0b16c22014fb75795531a9a187b8fc81</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_101.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857442</data>
    </node>
    <node id="provider">
      <data key="d0">provider</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">A provider is responsible for supplying AI systems and may conduct relevant impact assessments to ensure the system's compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;A provider refers to any entity that offers general-purpose AI models and is subject to the regulatory oversight of the Commission.&lt;SEP&gt;The provider refers to an organization or individual who supplies AI systems, technologies, or services to users or other entities.&lt;SEP&gt;The provider is the entity responsible for ensuring that high-risk AI systems meet established regulatory compliance standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The provider is the entity responsible for the market placement and operational use of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0efde0679d72a2d51e7acdaf09979bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19283d37b8085eb0b86aff77d85558de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3266d68b5262e6852cabbe36178dec96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69838403e8b59bb122436a0d25a9fc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b16c22014fb75795531a9a187b8fc81</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_27.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_101.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863270</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fines">
      <data key="d0">Fines</data>
      <data key="d1">Penalty</data>
      <data key="d2">Fines are monetary penalties that may be imposed on Providers for failing to comply with regulations regarding their AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Fines are penalties that can be imposed for the infringement of obligations under the Regulation, aimed at ensuring compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Fines are penalties that can be imposed when there are violations, meant to be effective, proportionate and dissuasive.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de6a0d59bb86cca6093fbb52cf156b4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a64bfb94635a0df2f808b2f8a494bd3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae3ab8a3b5c5d0c61e8b99fa718913b0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_169.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_101.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_80.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863835</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article">
      <data key="d0">Article</data>
      <data key="d1">LegalBasis</data>
      <data key="d2">An article in legal texts typically refers to a specific clause or section that provides statutory requirements and guidelines that must be followed.&lt;SEP&gt;This Article outlines the framework for the imposition and review of fines, establishing the legal basis for regulatory penalties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a8512760339eb776d946a91a28089b34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de6a0d59bb86cca6093fbb52cf156b4e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_101.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_77.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863554</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Natural or Legal Person">
      <data key="d0">Natural or Legal Person</data>
      <data key="d1">AISubject</data>
      <data key="d2">A natural or legal person refers to any individual or entity, such as organizations, that are recognized in law and can act within the legal framework, particularly regarding AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Any individual or legal entity that believes there is an infringement may file a complaint to the relevant authority.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c27775e23d04f7dd6b8ec477a62efd1</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_85.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Infringement">
      <data key="d0">Infringement</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">An infringement refers to a violation of regulations set forth in the text, particularly concerning AI practices and the responsibilities of Union institutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Infringement refers to violations of the provisions outlined in a regulation, which warrant formal complaints.&lt;SEP&gt;Infringement refers to violations or breaches that may have adverse effects, necessitating reporting to authorities and mitigation efforts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9c27775e23d04f7dd6b8ec477a62efd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5da2f6b1c2fa5619efa26719534e9c35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_100.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_85.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859954</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Complaints">
      <data key="d0">Complaints</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Complaints are formal expressions of dissatisfaction submitted by natural or legal persons regarding alleged infringements of regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Complaints are reports lodged by downstream providers regarding potential infringements of the rules concerning AI models and systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9c27775e23d04f7dd6b8ec477a62efd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af991f85166d6ddfbbf84e4a73207d3d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_85.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_162.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861467</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Third-Party Conformity Assessments">
      <data key="d0">Third-Party Conformity Assessments</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Third-party conformity assessments are evaluations conducted to ensure compliance with specific standards and regulations, assessing various quality metrics.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-97ee5867d3c03f24001b650ad752686d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_126.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857448</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article R23 of Annex I to Decision No 768/2008/EC">
      <data key="d0">Article R23 of Annex I to Decision No 768/2008/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">This article pertains to the framework for conformity assessments and notification processes within the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-97ee5867d3c03f24001b650ad752686d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_126.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857456</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Commission">
      <data key="d0">European Commission</data>
      <data key="d1">AIUser</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Commission is a body that develops and manages regulatory requirements and tools pertaining to conformity assessments.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Commission is responsible for exploring international instruments and pursuing mutual recognition agreements to standardize trade practices.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Commission is a governing body responsible for implementing regulations and overseeing the compliance of Member States regarding AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Commission is an institution that ensures the application of transparency obligations related to AI content regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Commission issues standardisation requests to ensure that AI systems meet legal and regulatory requirements for safety and performance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-51cb0d95dff3b7f033b351a9352b26a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3177468233ec37ad2a71dc38caa17377&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4337a268de724c492ca11805622faf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97ee5867d3c03f24001b650ad752686d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cc9a7191827dda78eda5924876e5f7e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_135.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_40.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_127.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_126.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_81.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861623</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Electronic Notification Tool">
      <data key="d0">Electronic Notification Tool</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">The electronic notification tool is a system developed by the Commission for notifying authorities and Member States about conformity assessment bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;The electronic notification tool is a system developed by the Commission to facilitate communication regarding notifications of bodies during regulatory compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;The electronic notification tool is a system referenced in Article 30(2) used for notifying changes related to notified bodies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-34f79a9fca1518856b24fdcb7e59f040&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97ee5867d3c03f24001b650ad752686d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f94df6da4de89cee24b1bd8f504c377</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_30.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_126.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863789</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk">
      <data key="d0">Risk</data>
      <data key="d1">Risk</data>
      <data key="d2">Risk refers to potential systemic risks associated with AI models that require mitigation through internal safeguards.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk refers to the potential for harm or adverse effects, particularly in the context of using AI systems in high-risk scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk refers to the potential negative impacts and dangers associated with the deployment and use of high-risk AI systems, as outlined in regulatory guidelines. It encompasses the likelihood of harm occurring and the severity of that harm, indicating both the potential dangers these systems pose to users and society at large. Moreover, the concept of risk includes the implications that such dangers may necessitate market surveillance authorities to implement measures aimed at mitigating non-compliance. In essence, risk is the potential for loss or harm linked to specific events or decisions across various contexts, highlighting the need for careful management and mitigation strategies in relation to high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The potential for loss or adverse outcomes associated with the deployment of high-risk AI systems in financial contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Risk refers to the potential for significant negative impacts on safety, health, and fundamental rights during AI system development and testing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7d62750f1113d24ac155fcd2b2ef02c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99c78ffcf815fa82f05dcb7dc5871e1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3440467bfb3879bf5e30fbb107e28162&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62e8b28075fdfa33850ed4b5a4d9a52f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e978e96ac6d99cf448b53260c07dded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-075ecb5835777e6044264a23ca0cb20a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85fb9638473c0974347ccab540b99b7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77093970e26d1be04734ed16ea88f777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0711090702fd9b1787822998d5deac9</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_109.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_140.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_92.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_20.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_156.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863863</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Institutions">
      <data key="d0">Union Institutions</data>
      <data key="d1">AISystem</data>
      <data key="d2">Union institutions are entities within the European Union that are subject to the guidelines and oversight of market surveillance authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;Union institutions include various bodies that collaborate to enhance AI regulations and standards within the Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Union institutions, agencies, and bodies are subject to penalties imposed by the European Data Protection Supervisor when infringing upon the Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Union institutions include various bodies within the European Union that may employ AI systems in law enforcement and regulatory contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Union institutions include various bodies, offices, or agencies within the European Union that are relevant to the application of specific regulations for AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1b43f399350f0fc36795c0ce358459d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-577494efd5ce842563e6974b0da9707b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ba8e0dd4981bd71dedb04a86b45601&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0711090702fd9b1787822998d5deac9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_59.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_168.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_156.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863707</data>
    </node>
    <node id="bias detection and correction">
      <data key="d0">bias detection and correction</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Bias detection and correction refers to the AI capability necessary for identifying and mitigating biases in AI systems, particularly in high-risk applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-602b68fe088482c0037845fc0b520c30</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_70.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857460</data>
    </node>
    <node id="special categories of personal data">
      <data key="d0">special categories of personal data</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Special categories of personal data include sensitive information that requires higher protection levels due to the greater risk of harm from its processing.&lt;SEP&gt;Special categories of personal data refer to sensitive information requiring strict regulations during processing to avoid biases.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d5ee58307a02a795e806984f0ff4abe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602b68fe088482c0037845fc0b520c30</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861116</data>
    </node>
    <node id="fundamental rights and freedoms of natural persons">
      <data key="d0">fundamental rights and freedoms of natural persons</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">The fundamental rights and freedoms of natural persons refer to the essential legal rights that individuals hold, particularly concerning data protection and privacy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-602b68fe088482c0037845fc0b520c30</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_70.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857460</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bias Detection and Correction">
      <data key="d0">Bias Detection and Correction</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Bias Detection and Correction are capabilities that help in identifying and mitigating biases in AI systems, ensuring fairness in AI applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Bias detection and correction is an AI capability aimed at identifying and mitigating bias in AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Bias detection and correction refer to the processes implemented to identify and mitigate biases within AI systems to ensure fair treatment of individuals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0639a0bd62e8b0bbe41bc1bee4a3098&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602b68fe088482c0037845fc0b520c30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68df7ac042ba1913236779113868f934</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861116</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Special Categories of Personal Data">
      <data key="d0">Special Categories of Personal Data</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Special Categories of Personal Data refer to sensitive information types that require enhanced protection measures due to the associated risks of harm.&lt;SEP&gt;Special categories of personal data are defined under various regulations, including Article 9(1) of Regulation (EU) 2016/679, which pertains to sensitive information.)&lt;SEP&gt;Special categories of personal data refer to sensitive personal data defined in specific EU regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Special categories of personal data include sensitive information that may be processed exceptionally under strict conditions for bias detection and correction.&lt;SEP&gt;Special categories of personal data refer to sensitive information that requires enhanced protection under EU regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0639a0bd62e8b0bbe41bc1bee4a3098&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e726a1ef8f481d54c995afc6a028f60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602b68fe088482c0037845fc0b520c30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68df7ac042ba1913236779113868f934&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ac98f64f8751ad51246ca16d843f030</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_70.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_10.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861116</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fundamental Rights and Freedoms of Natural Persons">
      <data key="d0">Fundamental Rights and Freedoms of Natural Persons</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Fundamental Rights and Freedoms of Natural Persons encompass the legal rights and protections granted to individuals, especially concerning data privacy and protection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-602b68fe088482c0037845fc0b520c30</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_70.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857460</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Processing">
      <data key="d0">Processing</data>
      <data key="d1">Processing</data>
      <data key="d2">Processing refers to any operation or set of operations performed on personal data, including collection, storage, and use, especially within AI contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-602b68fe088482c0037845fc0b520c30</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_70.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857460</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Safeguards">
      <data key="d0">Safeguards</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">Safeguards are measures incorporated within AI systems to mitigate risks and promote responsible innovation.&lt;SEP&gt;Safeguards refer to measures that ensure the legitimate and necessary use of post-remote biometric identification systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Safeguards refer to the measures implemented to protect individuals’ rights and data against potential misuse, especially in AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de40ca48bf7dafc1db86f4d8a18d2bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdf1c7e7ad7fe2c6b1b8f1b0b12db35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602b68fe088482c0037845fc0b520c30</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_138.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_95.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_70.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858901</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Advisory Forum">
      <data key="d0">Advisory Forum</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">The Advisory Forum is a body established to provide technical expertise and advice on the involvement of various stakeholders in the implementation of regulations related to artificial intelligence (AI) at both Union and national levels. It consists of representatives who contribute stakeholder input and may participate in discussions as observers in sub-groups and meetings of the Board. The Advisory Forum holds meetings at least biannually, during which it invites experts and stakeholders to discuss various issues pertinent to its mission. Its primary objective is to ensure a balanced selection of stakeholders is represented, facilitating informed discussions and effective advisory processes for the Board and the Commission regarding the Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;The advisory forum is a group that provides input and consultation to the Commission during the drafting of common specifications.&lt;SEP&gt;The advisory forum is consulted by the Commission during the drafting of common specifications and implementing acts.&lt;SEP&gt;The Advisory Forum is a consultative body that the Commission consults for relevant expertise when preparing standardisation requests.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-83ca16d466deaa751e3b9dc390e91e2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-010f171cc1a7f217689efe00fd8cb656&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e28e08bfb7b1ae3208e2c91ea6f1e4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad86065dee426d0a1db7444552c4a385&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f76666cf495bb0f0810313fe42e2c882&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f41337092de45470ab838aff17309ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-699c5fa3a4d8d093e6a599637df82443&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6a5cc59273abbe42c743808026477c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e24261c10195e33e965bd7e966c33337</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_121.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_41.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_67.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_148.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_150.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fundamental Rights Agency">
      <data key="d0">Fundamental Rights Agency</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">The Fundamental Rights Agency is a permanent member of the Advisory Forum, contributing to discussions on fundamental rights in AI.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fundamental Rights Agency provides expertise and insights on fundamental rights in the context of the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ad86065dee426d0a1db7444552c4a385&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f76666cf495bb0f0810313fe42e2c882</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_150.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_67.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENISA">
      <data key="d0">ENISA</data>
      <data key="d1">Organization</data>
      <data key="d2">ENISA is the European Union Agency for Cybersecurity and a permanent member of the Advisory Forum.&lt;SEP&gt;ENISA, the European Union Agency for Cybersecurity, contributes technical expertise to the stakeholder engagement process related to the Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;ENISA is the European Union Agency for Cybersecurity responsible for coordinating cybersecurity efforts across the EU, especially in relation to AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;ENISA, the European Union Agency for Cybersecurity, plays a role in cybersecurity policy and compliance for AI systems under the regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ad86065dee426d0a1db7444552c4a385&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f76666cf495bb0f0810313fe42e2c882&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60a12c037b4dee54159c11f348ff3f11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ec0d2d3cbe2a53a3bbf6373c775edf2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_78.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_150.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_67.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861074</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CEN">
      <data key="d0">CEN</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Committee for Standardization (CEN) plays a role in setting standards relevant to the Regulation and stakeholder interests.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f76666cf495bb0f0810313fe42e2c882</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_150.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857470</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CENELEC">
      <data key="d0">CENELEC</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Committee for Electrotechnical Standardization (CENELEC) is involved in standardization efforts related to the regulation and its stakeholders.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f76666cf495bb0f0810313fe42e2c882</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_150.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857470</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ETSI">
      <data key="d0">ETSI</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Telecommunications Standards Institute (ETSI) contributes to the regulatory framework through its standardization efforts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f76666cf495bb0f0810313fe42e2c882</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_150.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857470</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Stakeholder">
      <data key="d0">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Stakeholders are individuals or groups involved in the standardisation process, ensuring diverse interests are represented in decision-making.&lt;SEP&gt;Stakeholders are individuals or groups that have an interest and are involved in the implementation and application of the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f76666cf495bb0f0810313fe42e2c882&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3177468233ec37ad2a71dc38caa17377</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_150.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_40.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861623</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Civil Society">
      <data key="d0">Civil Society</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Civil Society includes non-profit organizations and community groups engaging in the regulatory discourse.&lt;SEP&gt;Civil society includes individuals and organizations advocating for ethical standards and the responsible deployment of AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-90efb8f063f236753e4794005afa2a0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f76666cf495bb0f0810313fe42e2c882</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_150.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_111.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861984</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex III">
      <data key="d0">Annex III</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex III is a significant component of regulatory documentation concerning artificial intelligence (AI) practices, specifically focusing on high-risk AI systems that are subject to stringent regulatory requirements and oversight. This annex includes a detailed list of AI systems classified as high-risk, which necessitates additional evaluation due to their potential impact on health, safety, and fundamental rights. 

The descriptions within Annex III provide clear criteria for the classification of high-risk AI systems under EU legislation, specifying not only the types of systems that fall under this designation but also the requirements that must be met to ensure compliance prior to deployment. Key areas outlined include law enforcement and migration, emphasizing the significant implications these AI systems may have in such fields.

Moreover, Annex III serves as a comprehensive guide for compliance requirements and assessment procedures, highlighting the conditions and classifications required for effective market surveillance by the relevant authorities. It also suggests the possibility of incorporating additional area headings for future amendments, ensuring the framework remains up-to-date and relevant in response to ongoing regulatory discussions.

Overall, Annex III plays a pivotal role in the governance and regulatory framework surrounding the deployment of high-risk AI systems, establishing a structured approach to their oversight and evaluation in order to mitigate any associated risks to society.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8cb1edc11e8b8d0e952b15617a80f379&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c1d05b847c03fe702172f787883fc33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a0a99b47c288a96d7474c796efb766&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b71cdb20a8fa5befb7c30c90163cd416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff61ec794793cf787d4a0473487a06f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c72b31b17ef0accd3df4ab25a063163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb0291da832d9defa94aaf2262ad3761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0779dfb4a5c0f82f05a67985fe0224a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69838403e8b59bb122436a0d25a9fc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8da189e7622be67a80b2e12945a657cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe49d95d50900e82a706b2766339562f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d64a2a65aec35f8304efaaee30e0034d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4348ad8873ef2041aca94abc9297ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4d62babb1c5a144faeae6ac2f13628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_27.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_6.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_49.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_7.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863895</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 71">
      <data key="d0">Article 71</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 71 outlines the conditions under which specific information must be stored in the EU database, ensuring protection and privacy.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 71 pertains to the registration process for high-risk AI systems in the EU database.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 71 stipulates that an AI system must be registered in the EU database to be deployed, creating a safety net for regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9bece07e296fce9647a40a0dde904fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f74259ac0ec20e9f3989df868f56b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_49.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex VIII">
      <data key="d0">Annex VIII</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex VIII includes detailed sections A, B, and C that specify the type of information to be included in the EU database.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex VIII specifies the information requirements for the registration of high-risk AI systems in the EU database.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d7f74259ac0ec20e9f3989df868f56b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_49.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857491</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 6(3)">
      <data key="d0">Article 6(3)</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 6(3) determines the classification criteria for AI systems being categorized as high-risk or not.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_49.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857491</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Authorities">
      <data key="d0">National Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">National authorities are responsible for managing the local registrations and overseeing compliance related to high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;National authorities are responsible for overseeing the access and use of sensitive data stored in the EU database.&lt;SEP&gt;National authorities refer to local or national bodies that supervise the application of Union harmonization legislation, working alongside market surveillance authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d7f74259ac0ec20e9f3989df868f56b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_49.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863707</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Points 1 to 10 of Annex VIII">
      <data key="d0">Points 1 to 10 of Annex VIII</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">These points detail the specific information needed for the registration of high-risk AI systems in the EU database.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_49.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857491</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Points 1 to 5 of Annex VIII">
      <data key="d0">Points 1 to 5 of Annex VIII</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">These points outline additional information requirements for the registration process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_49.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857491</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Points 1, 2, 3, and 5 of Annex IX">
      <data key="d0">Points 1, 2, 3, and 5 of Annex IX</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">These points specify further necessary details for the registration of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_49.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857491</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex IX">
      <data key="d0">Annex IX</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex IX contains specifications for the information that must be included in the Real-World Testing Plan.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex IX further details the requirements for the registration and access protocols for high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d7f74259ac0ec20e9f3989df868f56b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa9e2916955e882c73231ed69851f6ec</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_49.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863082</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Section A">
      <data key="d0">Section A</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Section A of Annex VIII describes the specific points and types of information that need to be included in the EU database.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d7f74259ac0ec20e9f3989df868f56b4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_49.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857491</data>
    </node>
