      <data key="d0">Section B</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Section B of Annex VIII outlines additional categories of information required for the EU database, focusing on access and restrictions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d7f74259ac0ec20e9f3989df868f56b4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_49.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857491</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Section C">
      <data key="d0">Section C</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Section C of Annex VIII specifies further details regarding the data management and storage protocols.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d7f74259ac0ec20e9f3989df868f56b4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_49.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857491</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Practices">
      <data key="d0">AI Practices</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Practices refer to the actions and methodologies associated with the development and deployment of AI systems that must comply with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;AI practices refer to the specific activities that are subject to administrative fines if non-compliant with regulatory standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-28daf57045ce50f0bd160cddd41ffc14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861814</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Administrative Fines">
      <data key="d0">Administrative Fines</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Administrative Fines are the penalties enacted by Member States against entities that breach the AI Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Administrative fines are financial penalties imposed for non-compliance with regulations, specifically under the Regulation governing artificial intelligence practices. These fines can reach significant amounts, with specified limits varying from EUR 15,000,000 or up to 3% of an entity's total worldwide annual turnover, to a maximum of EUR 1,500,000 and EUR 750,000 dependent on the severity and type of violation. The application and enforcement of these fines may differ across Member States, reflecting the varying rules in place. Administrative fines serve as a mechanism to ensure compliance and safeguard against infringements, with specific penalties also applicable to non-compliance during sandbox experimentation periods. These established upper limits are crucial for maintaining regulatory oversight and encouraging adherence to established guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1b43f399350f0fc36795c0ce358459d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85bb41c1db2d2e1883172e505d5f7b71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-111c71f234a0f2d1b26490907acae6eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5da2f6b1c2fa5619efa26719534e9c35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_168.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863446</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Penalties">
      <data key="d0">Penalties</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Penalties are the consequences established by the Regulation for non-compliance with AI practices, serving as a crucial enforcement mechanism. These penalties primarily include administrative fines imposed by Member States for violations of the Regulation, and they are designed to ensure adherence to its provisions. If the provisions of the Regulation are not properly implemented by the specified deadline, penalties are applied as sanctions to reinforce compliance effectively. Overall, penalties play an essential role in the enforcement of the Regulation, highlighting their significance in maintaining proper AI practices across jurisdictions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1b43f399350f0fc36795c0ce358459d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40a9e2a0fc4601f4b3d4f583384b6a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ad9752391e53e840a2d8ac0861f8948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b837dd750c95d041180fa3d735328672&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_179.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_168.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863443</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Operators">
      <data key="d0">Operators</data>
      <data key="d1">AIOperator</data>
      <data key="d2">Operators are entities involved in the value chain of AI systems who have specific obligations under the Regulation, such as importers and distributors.&lt;SEP&gt;Operators are individuals or entities that must comply with the provisions of the Regulation regarding AI practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Operators are responsible for ensuring compliance with the Regulation concerning the high-risk AI systems they deploy, especially those interacting with public authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-197c7357cf5fefe6ca4e08f847ff6a75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b8c1122e1044e4445aa96d7fa6d5b6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_177.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_83.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863638</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Warnings">
      <data key="d0">Warnings</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Warnings are non-monetary measures that can be imposed as enforcement actions under the Regulation for non-compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857501</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Enforcement Measures">
      <data key="d0">Enforcement Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">RiskControl</data>
      <data key="d2">Enforcement measures are actions taken to ensure compliance with the Regulation, which may include penalties and administrative fines.&lt;SEP&gt;Enforcement measures refer to the actions taken by Member States to ensure compliance with the Regulation on AI practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1b43f399350f0fc36795c0ce358459d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_168.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859117</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Non-Monetary Measures">
      <data key="d0">Non-Monetary Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Non-monetary measures are alternative enforcement actions, such as warnings, that can be imposed on operators for violations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857501</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Total Worldwide Annual Turnover">
      <data key="d0">Total Worldwide Annual Turnover</data>
      <data key="d1">Metric</data>
      <data key="d2">Total Worldwide Annual Turnover refers to the financial performances of undertakings used to calculate fines as stipulated in the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857501</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Financial Year">
      <data key="d0">Financial Year</data>
      <data key="d1">Frequency</data>
      <data key="d2">Financial Year is the accounting year used to assess an operator’s total annual turnover for penalty calculations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857501</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 22">
      <data key="d0">Article 22</data>
      <data key="d1">Document</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 22 describes the obligations of authorized representatives in relation to the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857501</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 23">
      <data key="d0">Article 23</data>
      <data key="d1">Document</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 23 sets forth the obligations of importers in compliance with the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857501</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 24">
      <data key="d0">Article 24</data>
      <data key="d1">Document</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 24 specifies the obligations of distributors covered under the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857501</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 26">
      <data key="d0">Article 26</data>
      <data key="d1">Document</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 26 details the obligations of deployers in connection with AI practices outlined in the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857501</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 31">
      <data key="d0">Article 31</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 31 defines the general requirements and responsibilities that notified bodies must fulfill under the relevant legislation.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 31 outlines specific provisions and requirements concerning the assessment and conformity of high-risk AI systems. It details the obligations of notified bodies as per the relevant regulation, emphasizing the necessary qualifications and responsibilities these bodies must fulfill. Additionally, Article 31 specifies the criteria that conformity assessment bodies must meet in order to receive notification and authorization from authorities under the regulation. This article serves as a legal framework, describing the requirements that these bodies must adhere to for achieving compliance, ensuring that high-risk AI systems are appropriately evaluated and regulated.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 31 is a specific regulation that outlines requirements that must be met, which are presumed to be complied with if covered by applicable harmonised standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 31 lays down requirements for notifying authorities and notified bodies regarding their obligations and designations.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 31 outlines the requirements that a notified body must fulfill to maintain its designation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8caee37338a6383c30fe06ea2b3e4761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21da71f798625922669f14e575cb5dcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9db4c15b43d1b7a1a1138d5a7403b240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff611ee371ea780574e9c16859c31f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f79a9fca1518856b24fdcb7e59f040&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e5d20a8e9427a4698b84f758676994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97182f6b8815d40f51faf3e8eaeb7c7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b479c56b927c79a74d3a19d8470ff1da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f94df6da4de89cee24b1bd8f504c377</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_30.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_39.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_29.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_37.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_32.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863782</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 50">
      <data key="d0">Article 50</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 50 involves transparency obligations for providers and deployers regarding AI operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 50 refers to provisions within the regulation that maintain legal parameters for high-risk AI systems and their use.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 50 outlines the transparency measures required for AI systems as per the Commission's assessments.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 50 specifies AI systems that require additional transparency measures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c1d05b847c03fe702172f787883fc33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b71cdb20a8fa5befb7c30c90163cd416&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863441</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Provider Obligations">
      <data key="d0">Provider Obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers are required to comply with defined obligations as per Article 16, which are subject to administrative fines if violated.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857501</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Authorised Representatives Obligations">
      <data key="d0">Authorised Representatives Obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Authorised representatives have specific obligations laid out in Article 22, non-compliance leads to administrative penalties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857501</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Importer Obligations">
      <data key="d0">Importer Obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Importers must adhere to obligations defined in Article 23, with penalties for violations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857501</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Distributor Obligations">
      <data key="d0">Distributor Obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Distributors are subjected to obligations described in Article 24, non-compliance results in administrative fines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857501</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deployer Obligations">
      <data key="d0">Deployer Obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Deployer obligations are the responsibilities outlined in the Regulation that govern how deployers should operate high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Deployers must follow regulations stated in Article 26 and can incur fines for non-adherence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a65ec6b0fbd17afe47587686523a725</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_72.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863464</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Notified Bodies Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Notified Bodies Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Obligations of notified bodies are governed by Article 31 and related articles, imposing stringent standards and obligations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857501</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Transparency Obligations">
      <data key="d0">Transparency Obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">Requirement</data>
      <data key="d2">The Transparency Obligations encompass a set of requirements aimed at ensuring clarity and accountability in the functioning of AI systems. According to Article 50 of the relevant Regulation, both providers and deployers are mandated to uphold these transparency obligations to avoid potential penalties. These obligations involve the disclosure of vital information regarding the purpose and functioning of AI systems, particularly during interactions with users, to prevent deception. Additionally, the obligations stipulate that natural persons must be informed when engaging with AI tools. They also dictate the necessary protocols for detecting and labeling any artificially generated or manipulated content. Overall, the Transparency Obligations are essential in regulating how AI systems communicate their operations and outputs, thereby promoting trust and safety in their deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;Transparency obligations refer to the requirements for AI systems to disclose certain information to users and authorities, ensuring accountability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-51cb0d95dff3b7f033b351a9352b26a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83f37d4143e19486af167d7acee5bee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb43ec5a01dc502046ab6ffbe3a25504&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0044fdddd0a21caecd46a12639588d98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0373d38f7600f51def3b5e5cb5061d17</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_137.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_135.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_132.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_174.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Incorrect Information Supply">
      <data key="d0">Incorrect Information Supply</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Supplying incorrect information to notified bodies may result in administrative fines of 7,500,000 EUR or 1% of total worldwide annual turnover.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857501</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SMEs and Start-ups">
      <data key="d0">SMEs and Start-ups</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Small and Medium-sized Enterprises (SMEs) and start-ups face specific limitations on fines as per paragraphs 3, 4, and 5.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857501</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Infringement Severity Factors">
      <data key="d0">Infringement Severity Factors</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Factors for deciding on administrative fines include the nature, gravity, duration of infringement, and consequences suffered by affected persons.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857501</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Infringement Factors">
      <data key="d0">Infringement Factors</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Factors considered when determining administrative fines include the nature and gravity of the infringement, and the number of affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e7b8a0eb1cb8c27dfd822da15429870</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857504</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Administrative Fine">
      <data key="d0">Administrative Fine</data>
      <data key="d1">Metric</data>
      <data key="d2">Administrative fines are penalties imposed for infringements related to AI regulations, taking into account various factors such as severity and cooperation.&lt;SEP&gt;An administrative fine is a monetary penalty that may be imposed on Union institutions for non-compliance with regulations regarding AI practices, with specified maximum amounts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5da2f6b1c2fa5619efa26719534e9c35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859954</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Relevant Circumstances">
      <data key="d0">Relevant Circumstances</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Relevant circumstances refer to factors considered when assessing penalties, including the nature, gravity, duration of the infringement, and the size of the provider.&lt;SEP&gt;Relevant circumstances refer to various factors considered when deciding the amount of an administrative fine, including nature and consequences of infringements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1b43f399350f0fc36795c0ce358459d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_168.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859117</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Nature of Infringement">
      <data key="d0">Nature of Infringement</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">The nature of infringement assesses the type and seriousness of AI regulatory violations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Gravity of Infringement">
      <data key="d0">Gravity of Infringement</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Gravity of infringement evaluates the severity of the impact caused by the violation, including potential harm to affected individuals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Duration of Infringement">
      <data key="d0">Duration of Infringement</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Duration of infringement indicates the length of time over which the infringement occurred and its implications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Consequences of Infringement">
      <data key="d0">Consequences of Infringement</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Consequences of infringement take into account the harm experienced by individuals impacted by the infringement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Level of Damage">
      <data key="d0">Level of Damage</data>
      <data key="d1">Metric</data>
      <data key="d2">Level of damage quantifies the degree of harm suffered by affected persons due to the infringement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Administrative Fine Amount">
      <data key="d0">Administrative Fine Amount</data>
      <data key="d1">Metric</data>
      <data key="d2">Administrative fine amount is the financial penalty imposed on an operator for an infringement, determined based on various factors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Previous Violations">
      <data key="d0">Previous Violations</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Previous violations refer to any past instances of regulatory noncompliance by the operator, which may influence penalties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cooperation with Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Cooperation with Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Cooperation with authorities denotes the operator's collaboration with regulatory bodies in addressing and rectifying the infringement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Measures">
      <data key="d0">Technical Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical measures are actions taken by the operator to prevent infringements and mitigate risks associated with AI system operations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Organizational Measures">
      <data key="d0">Organizational Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">Organizational measures involve policies and practices established by the operator to ensure compliance with AI regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Intentional Character of Infringement">
      <data key="d0">Intentional Character of Infringement</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Intentional character of infringement assesses whether the violation occurred deliberately or due to negligence by the operator.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Notification of Infringement">
      <data key="d0">Notification of Infringement</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Notification of infringement refers to the process by which operators inform authorities of any regulatory breaches observed in their operations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Harm Mitigation Actions">
      <data key="d0">Harm Mitigation Actions</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Actions taken by the operator to lessen the negative impact on affected persons after an infringement.&lt;SEP&gt;Harm mitigation actions are steps taken by the operator to alleviate damage suffered by affected persons following an infringement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-599d61ad7be34e2603c3fef13f2ff8dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Judicial Remedies">
      <data key="d0">Judicial Remedies</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Judicial remedies are the legal recourses available to affected persons ensuring due process and fairness under national law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Adverse Effects">
      <data key="d0">Adverse Effects</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Adverse effects refer to negative outcomes resulting from infringements, which require mitigation actions by the operator.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Degree of Responsibility">
      <data key="d0">Degree of Responsibility</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">The degree of responsibility assesses the operator's accountability based on technical and organizational measures taken.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Competent Authorities Notification">
      <data key="d0">National Competent Authorities Notification</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">The process where operators must inform national authorities of infringements, including the extent of the notification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Negligent Character of Infringement">
      <data key="d0">Negligent Character of Infringement</data>
      <data key="d1">RiskConcept</data>
      <data key="d2">The negligent character of infringement considers whether the violation was intentional or due to carelessness, affecting penalty severity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Administrative Rules">
      <data key="d0">Administrative Rules</data>
      <data key="d1">Standard</data>
      <data key="d2">Administrative rules are guidelines established by Member States regarding the imposition and handling of fines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Competent Courts">
      <data key="d0">Competent Courts</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeveloper</data>
      <data key="d2">Competent courts are judicial bodies that can impose administrative fines based on the legal framework of the Member State.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Procedural Safeguards">
      <data key="d0">Procedural Safeguards</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Procedural safeguards are legal protections that ensure fair processes in imposing fines and addressing infringements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annual Reporting">
      <data key="d0">Annual Reporting</data>
      <data key="d1">Frequency</data>
      <data key="d2">Annual reporting refers to the obligation of Member States to present data on fines issued and related litigation to the Commission.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8c31e49eb2274702ec6ced9550f1ca86</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_99.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857506</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Facial Recognition Databases">
      <data key="d0">Facial Recognition Databases</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Facial recognition databases are compiled collections of facial images that are created or expanded through various means, including the scraping of images from the internet.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a46d97529092ce970fc3194f0ff15f99</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_43.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857511</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Mass Surveillance">
      <data key="d0">Mass Surveillance</data>
      <data key="d1">RiskConcept</data>
      <data key="d2">Mass surveillance is the practice of monitoring large numbers of people, which can lead to infringements on privacy rights and fundamental freedoms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a46d97529092ce970fc3194f0ff15f99</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_43.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857511</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Placing on the Market">
      <data key="d0">Placing on the Market</data>
      <data key="d1">LegalBasis</data>
      <data key="d2">Placing on the Market refers to the act of making an AI model available for commercial use, triggering applicable regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Placing on the market refers to the act of making AI systems available for use, which involves various regulatory considerations.&lt;SEP&gt;Placing on the market refers to the initial introduction of an AI system or model to the commercial marketplace.&lt;SEP&gt;The initial act of making an AI system or model available in the Union market.&lt;SEP&gt;Placing on the market refers to the introduction of products, including AI systems, into a market, subject to regulatory compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e7d62750f1113d24ac155fcd2b2ef02c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15eee417af0ebe299ed66be76a0b845a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b89491b02af0a00cbc13f9e8df827a6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a46d97529092ce970fc3194f0ff15f99</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_10.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_97.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863931</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Putting into Service">
      <data key="d0">Putting into Service</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Putting into service describes the phase when an AI system is first utilized for its intended purpose after being made available on the market.&lt;SEP&gt;Putting into service is the act of deploying AI systems for their intended purpose within a legal framework.&lt;SEP&gt;The action of supplying an AI system for first use directly to the deployer.&lt;SEP&gt;Putting into service indicates the process of deploying AI systems in operational environments after market placement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-15eee417af0ebe299ed66be76a0b845a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a46d97529092ce970fc3194f0ff15f99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7d62750f1113d24ac155fcd2b2ef02c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_10.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862268</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Systems Creation">
      <data key="d0">AI Systems Creation</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">The capability to create AI systems that can process and analyze data, particularly in relation to facial recognition.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a46d97529092ce970fc3194f0ff15f99</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_43.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857511</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Untargeted Scraping">
      <data key="d0">Untargeted Scraping</data>
      <data key="d1">Methodology</data>
      <data key="d2">Untargeted scraping is the practice of collecting data from the internet indiscriminately, often raising ethical issues related to privacy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a46d97529092ce970fc3194f0ff15f99</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_43.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857511</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Feeling of Mass Surveillance">
      <data key="d0">Feeling of Mass Surveillance</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">The feeling of mass surveillance is a psychological impact resulting from widespread monitoring of individuals' activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a46d97529092ce970fc3194f0ff15f99</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_43.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857511</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Regulatory Sandbox">
      <data key="d0">AI Regulatory Sandbox</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">The AI Regulatory Sandbox allows for the development, training, and testing of AI systems while ensuring compliance with data protection regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Regulatory Sandbox is a controlled environment established by Member States and competent authorities to facilitate the development, testing, training, and validation of innovative artificial intelligence (AI) systems. This framework allows AI system providers to experiment with their technologies while ensuring compliance with relevant regulations and identifying potential risks. The primary goal of the AI Regulatory Sandbox is to foster collaboration between authorities and providers, supporting innovation in AI while adhering to existing laws. By providing a supervised setting, the sandbox enables the testing and operation of AI technologies under regulatory oversight, which aids in both compliance and the advancement of AI technologies. Overall, the AI Regulatory Sandbox serves as a comprehensive framework that helps mitigate risks and encourages the responsible development of AI systems within established standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI regulatory sandbox is a controlled environment where AI systems can be developed and tested under regulatory oversight.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI Regulatory Sandbox is a testing environment under which innovative AI systems can be developed and evaluated under controlled conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7859a0c655f74761757b416c3b50bf36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85bb41c1db2d2e1883172e505d5f7b71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94b20fb25052b5f99e867bd24213f8f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aca56f82b70892874784bcec5c2bb2c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdf1c7e7ad7fe2c6b1b8f1b0b12db35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475967c83e624bc711a9ff13e8150163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe76292b9a553c383dab6b0a4a67cee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a46250ea72037444e96653239f2893b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-184360d53ae652d7f48a919e168f375a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d08b537f9a5bb2b4f4bbdf442ba39bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6adb64ff4e7b459fa1df815eac98b096&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc97d8ad7f3aa0522d885f92ee323822&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2612abd3c26dca69a0acec30add3ef15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0271020749ae70ce56cbd607a6f6662a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1516ad8d48077af0d59fc01578f33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-699b82035d71a633a86a67090e5a61e8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_140.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_138.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_141.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_76.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_139.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_58.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_59.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863374</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Prospective Provider">
      <data key="d0">Prospective Provider</data>
      <data key="d1">AIProvider</data>
      <data key="d2">A Prospective Provider is a potential entity preparing to conduct AI system testing, subject to similar regulations as Providers.&lt;SEP&gt;Prospective Providers are individuals or organizations planning to deploy AI systems, needing to comply with certain regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The prospective provider refers to entities that may become involved in deploying or operating AI systems in the future.&lt;SEP&gt;The prospective provider is an entity that controls the data processing within the sandbox and has authorized access to personal data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb3519876fdebea487c9995e6d3ae4fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-800752b66b6fe0cd70bb0290efc2fbbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1516ad8d48077af0d59fc01578f33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f6e14583352886a741ac1d51eada03a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_76.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_59.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863383</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Serious Incident">
      <data key="d0">Serious Incident</data>
      <data key="d1">Risk</data>
      <data key="d2">A Serious Incident pertains to significant events related to AI systems that suggest potential non-compliance during testing phases, particularly involving high-risk AI systems. These incidents can include events that lead to death or serious harm, highlighting critical failures in AI functionality. Such incidents necessitate immediate notification to relevant authorities due to their serious nature and the potential negative consequences they may impose. A Serious Incident is characterized by its noteworthy status, posing risks associated with AI systems that require timely reporting and prompt investigation. Overall, it encompasses any significant occurrence that may have substantial impacts or implications, warranting urgent attention and oversight.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4518ca313d8493e277775e1a9267b84d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0c31436f0e7ce27ce5952aa2bf9ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a94885e0b736d24263914e9a9d565900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0dc307b8b7cb1f0e39aa9b4b1839c408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1516ad8d48077af0d59fc01578f33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78dcdae0f5d22df28405d8ae03e038d0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_76.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863494</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Compliance with Articles 60 and 61">
      <data key="d0">Compliance with Articles 60 and 61</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Compliance with Articles 60 and 61 sets out the necessary conditions for testing AI systems in real-world conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43a1516ad8d48077af0d59fc01578f33</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_76.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Real World Conditions">
      <data key="d0">Real World Conditions</data>
      <data key="d1">Domain</data>
      <data key="d2">Real World Conditions refer to the actual environment where AI system testing occurs, emphasizing practical application and ethical concerns.&lt;SEP&gt;Real World Conditions refer to the actual environments where AI Systems are tested to validate their performance in practical scenarios.&lt;SEP&gt;Real World Conditions refer to the environments and scenarios that AI systems must be tested in to ensure their efficacy and safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7859a0c655f74761757b416c3b50bf36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f6e14583352886a741ac1d51eada03a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43a1516ad8d48077af0d59fc01578f33</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_139.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_76.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863092</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Decision by Market Surveillance Authority">
      <data key="d0">Decision by Market Surveillance Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Decisions made by the Market Surveillance Authorities can lead to changes in the testing or deployment of AI systems due to compliance issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43a1516ad8d48077af0d59fc01578f33</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_76.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857519</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 60(4)">
      <data key="d0">Article 60(4)</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 60(4) refers to a regulatory guideline that governs decisions or objections related to AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb3519876fdebea487c9995e6d3ae4fd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_76.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857522</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Objection Decision">
      <data key="d0">Objection Decision</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">The objection decision indicates the grounds for objection and the manner in which it can be contested by providers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb3519876fdebea487c9995e6d3ae4fd</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_76.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857522</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing Plan">
      <data key="d0">Testing Plan</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">A testing plan outlines the procedures and protocols required for the testing of AI systems in compliance with regulatory requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;The testing plan outlines the methodologies and parameters under which the AI systems are evaluated by authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb3519876fdebea487c9995e6d3ae4fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_141.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_76.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861057</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers of General-Purpose AI Models">
      <data key="d0">Providers of General-Purpose AI Models</data>
      <data key="d1">AIProvider</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers are responsible for identifying, assessing, and mitigating risks associated with their AI models, particularly those with systemic implications.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers who develop and manage general-purpose AI models and are tasked with assessing risks associated with their deployment and use.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of general-purpose AI models are responsible for ensuring their models are well-documented and transparent for downstream usage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-11bdaa862215570a86eed137e3092ea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bee8a141261944c2193bcb00b304b768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-447d51c65bac6d28fd62c36c3e70e08b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_101.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_114.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_115.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862855</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cybersecurity Protection">
      <data key="d0">Cybersecurity Protection</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Cybersecurity protection ensures that AI models maintain integrity and are safeguarded against external threats, a critical concern for systemic risk management.&lt;SEP&gt;Cybersecurity protection is necessary for safeguarding general-purpose AI models and their physical infrastructure from threats.&lt;SEP&gt;Cybersecurity protection related to systemic risks ensures the model and its infrastructure are safeguarded against threats like cyberattacks or unauthorized access.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bee8a141261944c2193bcb00b304b768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cfbca03bf6afb99c3326dc8b02d083b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-447d51c65bac6d28fd62c36c3e70e08b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_114.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_55.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_115.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859573</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Model Evaluations">
      <data key="d0">Model Evaluations</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Model evaluations involve assessing AI models before their market release to ensure compliance with safety and risk management standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bee8a141261944c2193bcb00b304b768</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_114.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857524</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Adversarial Testing">
      <data key="d0">Adversarial Testing</data>
      <data key="d1">AITechnique</data>
      <data key="d2">Adversarial testing is a technique used to identify vulnerabilities in AI models by challenging them with deceptive inputs.&lt;SEP&gt;Adversarial testing is a testing capability aimed at identifying vulnerabilities in AI models through simulated attacks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bee8a141261944c2193bcb00b304b768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cfbca03bf6afb99c3326dc8b02d083b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_55.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_114.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857803</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk-Management Policies">
      <data key="d0">Risk-Management Policies</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Risk-management policies are strategic measures implemented to address and mitigate risks throughout the lifecycle of AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bee8a141261944c2193bcb00b304b768</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_114.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857524</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Value Chain">
      <data key="d0">AI Value Chain</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">The AI Value Chain represents the comprehensive cycle of activities involved in the development, deployment, and operation of artificial intelligence systems. It encompasses all actors and stakeholders implicated in these processes, emphasizing the importance of cooperation among various entities. The AI Value Chain outlines the various stages of development, highlighting the roles and responsibilities of multiple parties that provide essential tools, services, and components necessary for the successful integration and maintenance of AI systems. This chain includes not only the technological aspects but also the regulatory considerations, reflecting a series of interconnected activities crucial for the effective utilization and governance of AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-778cb9e68fcb25e3f810e3cea927f7b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11bdaa862215570a86eed137e3092ea6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7963b30391bfa3d5e28ecd9a95b61010&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21acb22d994b8f65ea3709a99eb85032&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bee8a141261944c2193bcb00b304b768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b474f9815c7033ca1ad8daff4012eff</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_101.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_89.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_114.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_88.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_20.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_9.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863145</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Model's Lifecycle">
      <data key="d0">Model's Lifecycle</data>
      <data key="d1">AILifecyclePhase</data>
      <data key="d2">The model's lifecycle encompasses all phases of development, deployment, and evaluation of AI models to manage risks effectively.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bee8a141261944c2193bcb00b304b768</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_114.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857524</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Internal Testing">
      <data key="d0">Internal Testing</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Internal Testing refers to the process conducted by the provider to evaluate the AI model's functionality and safety before external access is granted.&lt;SEP&gt;Internal testing involves evaluations conducted by providers to ensure their models meet safety and performance standards before being released.&lt;SEP&gt;Internal testing refers to the evaluation procedures implemented by providers to ensure the safety of AI models against systemic risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bee8a141261944c2193bcb00b304b768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-075ecb5835777e6044264a23ca0cb20a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23ab4f338bfa06297d4c996d7d54dc70</data>
