      <data key="d5">1750863853</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Independent External Testing">
      <data key="d0">Independent External Testing</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Independent external testing refers to assessments conducted by third-party organizations to validate the efficacy and safety of AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bee8a141261944c2193bcb00b304b768</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_114.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857524</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk-Management Processes">
      <data key="d0">Risk-Management Processes</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Risk-management processes are implemented by providers to address and reduce potential risks throughout the use and deployment of AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bee8a141261944c2193bcb00b304b768</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_114.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857524</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Accountability Processes">
      <data key="d0">Accountability Processes</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Accountability processes ensure that AI providers take responsibility for the risks associated with their models and their outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bee8a141261944c2193bcb00b304b768</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_114.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857524</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Governance Processes">
      <data key="d0">Governance Processes</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Governance processes outline the frameworks and policies that guide the ethical development and deployment of AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bee8a141261944c2193bcb00b304b768</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_114.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857524</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Quality Management System">
      <data key="d0">Quality Management System</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">A Quality Management System is a structured system of procedures and processes that ensures the consistent quality of AI systems in compliance with regulatory standards.&lt;SEP&gt;A Quality Management System is a structured system that aims to ensure consistent quality in the production and delivery of high-risk AI systems, encompassing various processes and procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Quality Management System consists of guidelines and standards necessary for ensuring that services and products meet customer requirements and regulatory compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Quality Management System is a framework that organizations use to ensure they meet customer and regulatory requirements effectively and efficiently.&lt;SEP&gt;A Quality Management System is an organized system of policies, procedures, and instructions ensuring compliance with regulations in high-risk AI development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e4f07f79ad3c90c82b86c0a02d0fae9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44eafa4c222bb60e722eca942751cf7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac68c725e087cb7c659f2dd75f0a6e34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad25bfaa86145b8556e5d82696b8bab4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_146.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_63.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_81.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_16.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863344</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Relevant Documentation">
      <data key="d0">Relevant Documentation</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Relevant Documentation includes all necessary records and documents that support the quality management system and compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Relevant documentation includes the necessary records and proofs needed for conformity assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-44eafa4c222bb60e722eca942751cf7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1d974005cd87fc21678c732472ee11a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_34.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_81.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858827</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Post-Market Monitoring System">
      <data key="d0">Post-Market Monitoring System</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">The Post-Market Monitoring System is a comprehensive procedure established by providers to continuously monitor the performance and safety of AI systems after they have been deployed in the market. This system is essential for ensuring ongoing compliance with regulatory standards and for tracking the effectiveness of these high-risk AI systems throughout their operational lifetime. 

It encompasses various processes and activities that facilitate feedback collection from the use of AI systems. This feedback is critical for compliance and safety assessments, allowing providers to systematically document and analyze performance data. By gathering insights from user experiences, the Post-Market Monitoring System enables AI providers to identify necessary corrective actions and improve system reliability. Overall, it plays a vital role in maintaining the accountability and safety of AI technologies after market placement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44eafa4c222bb60e722eca942751cf7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99c78ffcf815fa82f05dcb7dc5871e1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c32bc5fa5cdfa35a393a42535dc4fdfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac68c725e087cb7c659f2dd75f0a6e34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f56b40e98f8949a37c3ab283b01f7050</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_81.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863348</data>
    </node>
