    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2024/1689">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2024/1689</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 establishes harmonised rules concerning artificial intelligence (AI) and amends various previous regulations related to AI technologies. This regulation lays down unified standards that influence both safety and technical aspects surrounding AI deployments. By amending several pre-existing regulations pertinent to the field, Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 aims to create a comprehensive framework that enhances the safety and effectiveness of AI applications across the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 establishes harmonized rules on artificial intelligence and amends previous regulations, focusing on safety components of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 lays down harmonised rules on artificial intelligence, addressing safety components and implementing acts for AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 lays down harmonized rules on artificial intelligence and amends multiple previous regulations to include AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 establishes harmonised rules on artificial intelligence and revises previous regulations related to this field.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a4219a2a10d85ddd82f98b8d6267cb9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b46b9cdd1723562953df9638581250&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a84d660603389dd91dcd96134d5bb46e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a5a3ae528d10c9d38e017d520ab6719&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eb5283f4e280f1ec77650d624699286&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3acb107043f5850a72cf1b047a443296&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2499910b26136c66e6e7a013d8f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6485ea34e7fea16b2f5a59242c8ef2a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7805654ce0fe0d8d9b6ba008562d2aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_109.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_102.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_106.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_103.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_104.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_105.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_110.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_108.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863880</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Artificial Intelligence systems">
      <data key="d0">Artificial Intelligence systems</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Artificial Intelligence systems are technologies that may involve safety components under the new legislative framework set out in Regulation (EU) 2024/1689.&lt;SEP&gt;Artificial Intelligence systems refer to technologies that utilize AI methodologies, with specific regulations outlined for their deployment in safety contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Artificial Intelligence systems that are categorized as safety components under certain European regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Artificial Intelligence systems refer to technology systems that utilize AI for various applications, particularly in safety components.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4219a2a10d85ddd82f98b8d6267cb9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3acb107043f5850a72cf1b047a443296&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b46b9cdd1723562953df9638581250</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_106.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_108.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_105.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_107.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862700</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Artificial Intelligence Systems">
      <data key="d0">Artificial Intelligence Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">AISystem</data>
      <data key="d2">Artificial Intelligence Systems are advanced technology systems that utilize artificial intelligence to perform tasks traditionally requiring human-like intelligence, such as decision-making and problem-solving. These systems are categorized as safety components and are governed by specific regulatory requirements set forth in the European Union. In particular, they fall under Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, which mandates adherence to outlined safety standards. As a result, Artificial Intelligence Systems are subject to stringent safety regulations to ensure their responsible deployment and operation in various applications, particularly those that involve critical safety functions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e0b46b9cdd1723562953df9638581250&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a84d660603389dd91dcd96134d5bb46e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c2f867de2be6cb439557f91700b051c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a5a3ae528d10c9d38e017d520ab6719&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eb5283f4e280f1ec77650d624699286&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3acb107043f5850a72cf1b047a443296</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_102.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_106.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_1.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_103.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_104.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_105.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863880</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Specifications">
      <data key="d0">Technical Specifications</data>
      <data key="d1">Standard</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical Specifications outline the requirements and standards that must be adhered to within the context of the Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical Specifications refer to the detailed descriptions and standards set forth for the implementation of AI systems as per regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical specifications refer to detailed criteria that govern the approval and use of technology, including security equipment relating to AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical specifications define the standards and requirements necessary for the development and operation of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d4058e2567f154203a2d9dacec4bdf7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3acb107043f5850a72cf1b047a443296&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac68c725e087cb7c659f2dd75f0a6e34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a5a3ae528d10c9d38e017d520ab6719</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_102.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_149.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_105.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863356</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing Standards">
      <data key="d0">Testing Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">Standard</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing Standards are the measures by which the safety and performance of Artificial Intelligence systems are evaluated and validated.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3acb107043f5850a72cf1b047a443296</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_105.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857580</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Chapter III, Section 2">
      <data key="d0">Chapter III, Section 2</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Chapter III, Section 2 of Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 provides a comprehensive framework for the governance and oversight of artificial intelligence (AI) systems, particularly focusing on those categorized as high-risk and safety components. This section establishes a set of specific requirements that providers must adhere to in order to ensure the safe and compliant integration of AI technologies within regulated frameworks. It includes detailed technical specifications and standards essential for the implementation of related acts and the adoption of delegated acts concerning AI systems. Furthermore, Chapter III, Section 2 serves as a reference point for understanding the approval processes and requirements pertinent to AI systems, emphasizing the importance of compliance with established safety standards in the deployment of these technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter III, Section 2 of Regulation (EU) No 168/2013 includes requirements that must be considered when adopting acts regarding AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a4219a2a10d85ddd82f98b8d6267cb9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b46b9cdd1723562953df9638581250&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a84d660603389dd91dcd96134d5bb46e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00e7606a0fa9d588f18d67d02cfcf654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a5a3ae528d10c9d38e017d520ab6719&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eb5283f4e280f1ec77650d624699286&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3acb107043f5850a72cf1b047a443296&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2499910b26136c66e6e7a013d8f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-064e3e5273a81cd8d9a47da9a3f51240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7805654ce0fe0d8d9b6ba008562d2aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-610573a7c194ad780ed97782200a740c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_109.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_102.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_106.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_103.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_80.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_107.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_104.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_105.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_95.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_108.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863880</data>
    </node>
    <node id="The Commission">
      <data key="d0">The Commission</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeveloper</data>
      <data key="d2">The Commission is an authoritative body within the European Union, responsible for overseeing the development and implementation of regulations related to artificial intelligence (AI). It collaborates with market surveillance authorities to promote compliance and coordinate joint investigations regarding AI systems throughout the EU. As a legislative body, the Commission evaluates and designates AI models that present systemic risks, ensuring that high-risk AI systems adhere to established standards. Additionally, it is empowered to adopt delegated acts, amend regulations, and enforce compliance among AI model providers. The Commission also plays a pivotal role in the governance of AI regulatory sandboxes and their corresponding regulations, thereby reinforcing its commitment to fostering a safe and compliant AI ecosystem.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3acb107043f5850a72cf1b047a443296&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1ef1c9ca92c002cf6ad36264fe1292c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6adb64ff4e7b459fa1df815eac98b096&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c49e78c25e30ed3a2557915010f14f3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4d62babb1c5a144faeae6ac2f13628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82b1b08be1175d2e6d49ab5a294ef86a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_52.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_160.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_105.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_53.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863109</data>
    </node>
    <node id="http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj">
      <data key="d0">http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">The URI represents a specific legal document or regulation that provides information relevant to data management and sharing within Europe.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec3aceb64afa671f57d404e61126379b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_105.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857582</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ELI Regulation 2024/1689">
      <data key="d0">ELI Regulation 2024/1689</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">ELI Regulation 2024/1689 is a legal document that outlines specific regulations pertaining to data management, ensuring compliance and governance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec3aceb64afa671f57d404e61126379b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_105.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857582</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Management">
      <data key="d0">Data Management</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Management refers to the practice of collecting, storing, and utilizing data in a structured manner in compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec3aceb64afa671f57d404e61126379b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_105.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857582</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Sharing">
      <data key="d0">Data Sharing</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Sharing involves the exchange of data between entities while adhering to legal and regulatory frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec3aceb64afa671f57d404e61126379b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_105.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857582</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Legal Compliance">
      <data key="d0">Legal Compliance</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Legal Compliance is the adherence to laws and regulations governing data practices and ensuring that entities meet established standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Legal compliance refers to the requirement for organizations to meet established laws and regulations, affecting the deployment of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec3aceb64afa671f57d404e61126379b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0044fdddd0a21caecd46a12639588d98</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_137.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_105.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861066</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Governance">
      <data key="d0">Governance</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Governance refers to the frameworks and processes that ensure accountability and compliance within data management practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec3aceb64afa671f57d404e61126379b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_105.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857582</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Compliance Verification">
      <data key="d0">Compliance Verification</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Compliance verification is the process of ensuring that AI systems meet required regulations and standards during their development and use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b754e2170dea6f93253ec4fd1fa88d5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857584</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk-Management System">
      <data key="d0">Risk-Management System</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">A risk-management system is implemented to assess and mitigate risks associated with high-risk AI systems throughout their lifecycle.&lt;SEP&gt;The risk-management system is an integral, continuous, and iterative process aimed at identifying and mitigating risks associated with high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7b5e606b14946a1b388f008868e8e155&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b754e2170dea6f93253ec4fd1fa88d5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859145</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Lifetime of AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Lifetime of AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">AILifecyclePhase</data>
      <data key="d2">The lifetime of AI systems refers to the entire duration from development, deployment, to post-market monitoring.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b754e2170dea6f93253ec4fd1fa88d5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857584</data>
    </node>
    <node id="General Characteristics">
      <data key="d0">General Characteristics</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">General characteristics refer to the essential features and functionalities of high-risk AI systems that must be documented.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b754e2170dea6f93253ec4fd1fa88d5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857584</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Capabilities and Limitations">
      <data key="d0">Capabilities and Limitations</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Capabilities and limitations describe what high-risk AI systems can and cannot do, which must be included in technical documentation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b754e2170dea6f93253ec4fd1fa88d5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857584</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Algorithms">
      <data key="d0">Algorithms</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">Algorithms are the computational methods employed by AI models to process data and make predictions or decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Algorithms are the sets of rules or instructions that govern how high-risk AI systems process data and make decisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b754e2170dea6f93253ec4fd1fa88d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-447d51c65bac6d28fd62c36c3e70e08b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_115.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_71.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859573</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Providers of high-risk AI systems">
      <data key="d0">Providers of high-risk AI systems</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers of high-risk AI systems are entities that must implement a quality management system to ensure compliance with regulations regarding their systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of high-risk AI systems are entities that supply AI systems categorized as high-risk and must comply with specific documentation requirements and confidentiality obligations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fa2b7ae4447e7d43e6030d6793c59ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac68c725e087cb7c659f2dd75f0a6e34</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_21.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_17.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863344</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Automatically Generated Logs">
      <data key="d0">Automatically Generated Logs</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Automatically generated logs consist of data collected by high-risk AI systems, which serve as an audit trail and are subject to access requests by competent authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fa2b7ae4447e7d43e6030d6793c59ef7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_21.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857587</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Requirements Set Out in Section 2">
      <data key="d0">Requirements Set Out in Section 2</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">The requirements set out in Section 2 detail the necessary compliance measures for high-risk AI systems, providing a framework for conformity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fa2b7ae4447e7d43e6030d6793c59ef7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_21.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857587</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 12(1)">
      <data key="d0">Article 12(1)</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 12(1) outlines the requirements for log retention related to high-risk AI systems under applicable Union law.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 12(1) specifies the obligations of providers regarding the access and management of automatically generated logs for high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c852bda35515c8d5385ef007c8140254&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2b7ae4447e7d43e6030d6793c59ef7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_19.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_21.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862235</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Reasoned Request">
      <data key="d0">Reasoned Request</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">A reasoned request is a formal demand made by the AI Office or competent authorities for additional compliance documentation or actions from the authorised representative or provider.&lt;SEP&gt;A reasoned request is a formal solicitation made by competent authorities to acquire necessary information or documentation from AI system providers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fa2b7ae4447e7d43e6030d6793c59ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-873c3732f26f3ace86c77cfec67991ee</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_21.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_54.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859888</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Official Languages of the Institutions of the Union">
      <data key="d0">Official Languages of the Institutions of the Union</data>
      <data key="d1">Language</data>
      <data key="d2">Official Languages of the Institutions of the Union are the languages recognized and used for communication and documentation within EU institutions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fa2b7ae4447e7d43e6030d6793c59ef7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_21.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857587</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Confidentiality Obligations set out in Article 78">
      <data key="d0">Confidentiality Obligations set out in Article 78</data>
      <data key="d1">CodeOfConduct</data>
      <data key="d2">Confidentiality obligations set out in Article 78 dictate how information obtained should be safeguarded to protect sensitive details.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fa2b7ae4447e7d43e6030d6793c59ef7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_21.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857587</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human-Centric AI">
      <data key="d0">Human-Centric AI</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Human-centric AI focuses on designing artificial intelligence systems that prioritize human welfare, rights, and values.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0455405f9e173535e78c4ea589745cf4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_176.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857620</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Trustworthy AI">
      <data key="d0">Trustworthy AI</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Trustworthy AI encompasses systems that adhere to ethical guidelines to ensure safety, fairness, and transparency in AI operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Trustworthy AI is the ability of AI systems to function reliably and ethically in society, ensuring compliance with fundamental rights.&lt;SEP&gt;Trustworthy AI refers to AI systems developed and used in accordance with fundamental rights obligations and ethical standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ae8bdbb57af24d78fe2313201571bea7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41cdee30f8345bc3690d876d77e6845c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0455405f9e173535e78c4ea589745cf4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_176.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863288</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Health Protection">
      <data key="d0">Health Protection</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Health protection is a key purpose of the Regulation, aimed to safeguard individuals from the potential harmful effects of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Health protection refers to measures ensuring that health standards are maintained as per the Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Health protection measures aim to safeguard individuals against risks posed by AI systems, ensuring they do not compromise physical or mental wellbeing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c2f867de2be6cb439557f91700b051c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-739e3d9c7841d79a7701d630f8c7fa26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0455405f9e173535e78c4ea589745cf4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_176.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_1.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863728</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Environmental Protection">
      <data key="d0">Environmental Protection</data>
      <data key="d1">AreaOfImpact</data>
      <data key="d2">Environmental Protection encompasses a range of policies and actions intended to conserve the natural environment while promoting sustainability. It is a critical framework aimed at safeguarding ecosystems and natural resources, particularly against the potential detrimental effects of high-risk AI systems. The aim of environmental protection includes preventing harmful impacts such technologies may have on the environment, ensuring that environmental quality, biodiversity, pollution control, and climate change interventions are prioritized. Furthermore, the right to a high level of environmental protection is recognized as an important aspect of related regulations, emphasizing the need to assess adverse impacts resulting from AI deployment. Overall, environmental protection seeks to address the urgent need for a balance between technological advancement and the preservation of the natural environment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e284955c1d36330bd14d117bb417611&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41cdee30f8345bc3690d876d77e6845c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0455405f9e173535e78c4ea589745cf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-878d589bc7b69ae2d9c3a44284a1badc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07ee6b3452d764ccd9733dceadb1ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-699b82035d71a633a86a67090e5a61e8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_48.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_130.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_176.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_59.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863378</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Subsidiarity Principle">
      <data key="d0">Subsidiarity Principle</data>
      <data key="d1">Standard</data>
      <data key="d2">The subsidiarity principle dictates that action is only taken at the Union level when necessary, and is a guiding principle of governance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0455405f9e173535e78c4ea589745cf4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_176.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857620</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Proportionality Principle">
      <data key="d0">Proportionality Principle</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">The proportionality principle ensures that intervention by the Union does not exceed what is necessary to achieve a given objective.&lt;SEP&gt;The proportionality principle requires that penalties and measures must be appropriate and balanced in relation to the infringement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0455405f9e173535e78c4ea589745cf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae3ab8a3b5c5d0c61e8b99fa718913b0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_169.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_176.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859671</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Compliance Assessment">
      <data key="d0">Compliance Assessment</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Compliance Assessment is the evaluation process to ensure AI systems meet regulatory requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Compliance assessment is the procedure to evaluate AI systems against regulatory standards, particularly for high-risk classifications.&lt;SEP&gt;Compliance assessment is the process of evaluating whether AI systems adhere to the regulations and standards set forth by governing bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;Compliance assessment is the process of evaluating whether a system meets the requirements set forth in relevant regulations and directives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fdf8a675497acfbeb420b95621b7cb31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bfb9287798720e37fcd8bae961e88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be61089eed18cfaf2703713378c589a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c168b1207668ad4ba646371f91bfce09</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_11.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_78.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_86.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_124.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863780</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Storage or Transport Conditions">
      <data key="d0">Storage or Transport Conditions</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Storage or Transport Conditions refer to the conditions under which high-risk AI systems are stored or transported, affecting their compliance status.&lt;SEP&gt;Storage or transport conditions refer to the requirements that must be maintained to ensure compliance of the AI system while in custody of importers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73fd7e801c2d8d41361f6b16b45c6ed0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861101</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Certificate issued by the Notified Body">
      <data key="d0">Certificate issued by the Notified Body</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">The certificate issued by the notified body confirms compliance of the high-risk AI system with regulatory standards and must be kept for 10 years.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_23.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857660</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Importers">
      <data key="d0">Importers</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">Importers are entities responsible for bringing high-risk AI systems into the market and ensuring compliance with regulatory standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Importers are entities responsible for ensuring that the high-risk AI system complies with regulatory requirements before placing it on the market.&lt;SEP&gt;Importers are operators who bring AI systems into a market and must comply with relevant obligations for their role.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-197c7357cf5fefe6ca4e08f847ff6a75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85fb9638473c0974347ccab540b99b7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_83.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863638</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 43">
      <data key="d0">Article 43</data>
      <data key="d1">DocumentSection</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 43 addresses implementing acts related to AI systems classified as safety components, stipulating compliance with specific requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 43 outlines specific conformity assessment procedures that must be followed for high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 43 outlines specific provisions allowing market surveillance authorities to authorize high-risk AI systems under certain conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 43 outlines the conformity assessment procedure necessary for high-risk AI systems to be certified before market placement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d7805654ce0fe0d8d9b6ba008562d2aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07ee6b3452d764ccd9733dceadb1ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1d974005cd87fc21678c732472ee11a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_108.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_34.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_46.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862693</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex IV">
      <data key="d0">Annex IV</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex IV contains specific details regarding the requirements and modifications relevant to AI system documentation.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex IV contains the specific technical documentation requirements that must be met by providers for high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex IV refers to the section that contains guidelines regarding the testing results of the AI system within the technical documentation.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex IV contains the technical documentation required to assess compliance of systems according to legal acts.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex IV enumerates elements that must be included in the technical documentation for high-risk AI systems, ensuring compliance with regulatory standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4d62babb1c5a144faeae6ac2f13628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bfb9287798720e37fcd8bae961e88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2612abd3c26dca69a0acec30add3ef15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36cb0fd5abf1b169a8aa13021f58c7b2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_11.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_59.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863761</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 11">
      <data key="d0">Article 11</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 11 of Regulation (EU) 2019/2144 specifies requirements for the adoption of implementing acts in relation to AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 11 specifies the requirements for the technical documentation related to high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2499910b26136c66e6e7a013d8f0b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_109.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_23.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861673</data>
    </node>
    <node id="10 Years">
      <data key="d0">10 Years</data>
      <data key="d1">Frequency</data>
      <data key="d2">10 Years refers to the duration for which the EU Declaration of Conformity must be retained by the provider after the high-risk AI system is placed on the market.&lt;SEP&gt;10 years is the duration for which importers must keep documentation related to the compliance of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f13d730755b7535c59eb130d6f7ac62e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_47.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_23.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863630</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Falsified Documentation">
      <data key="d0">Falsified Documentation</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Falsified documentation refers to incorrect or misleading papers that accompany high-risk AI systems, which can lead to non-compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_23.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857660</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Contact Information">
      <data key="d0">Contact Information</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Contact information is required to be indicated on the high-risk AI system's packaging to allow for communication with the importer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_23.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857660</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Safety Standards">
      <data key="d0">Safety Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">Standard</data>
      <data key="d2">Safety standards are established guidelines that AI systems must adhere to in order to ensure user and public safety during operation.&lt;SEP&gt;Safety standards refer to levels of safety and efficacy that high-risk AI systems must meet to ensure they do not pose risks to users or the public.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c2f867de2be6cb439557f91700b051c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_1.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863728</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulations">
      <data key="d0">Regulations</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulations outline the requirements and compliance standards that high-risk AI systems must meet to operate safely.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-85fb9638473c0974347ccab540b99b7b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_23.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857660</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Certificate from Notified Body">
      <data key="d0">Certificate from Notified Body</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">The certificate from a notified body verifies that a high-risk AI system meets specified safety and compliance standards prior to market placement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-85fb9638473c0974347ccab540b99b7b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_23.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857660</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 10 of Directive (EU) 2016/680">
      <data key="d0">Article 10 of Directive (EU) 2016/680</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 10 of Directive (EU) 2016/680 deals specifically with the processing of personal data for law enforcement purposes, providing additional safeguards.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 10 of Directive (EU) 2016/680 establishes the legal framework governing the processing of biometric data, ensuring necessary conditions and safeguards are met.&lt;SEP&gt;This article contains provisions that require compliance when processing biometric data linked to law enforcement.&lt;SEP&gt;Article 10 outlines specific rules on the processing of biometric data that intersect with the Regulation's requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc038db2f25d511bf84cccc9550e10c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-737358b61293029e1a6d7326160654fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4882abf1dd869d3dff00b8d88ee946a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee1f186f5aed070bc8e6e813caed9967</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_94.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_39.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_38.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863020</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 9(1) of Regulation (EU) 2016/679">
      <data key="d0">Article 9(1) of Regulation (EU) 2016/679</data>
      <data key="d1">LegalBasis</data>
      <data key="d2">This article outlines the limitations and prohibitions on the processing of biometric data, with specific exceptions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc038db2f25d511bf84cccc9550e10c2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_39.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857683</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Prohibition Decisions by National Data Protection Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Prohibition Decisions by National Data Protection Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">Decision</data>
      <data key="d2">These decisions are made regarding the use of remote biometric identification for non-law enforcement purposes, enforcing data protection rules.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc038db2f25d511bf84cccc9550e10c2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_39.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857683</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Remote Biometric Identification">
      <data key="d0">Remote Biometric Identification</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Remote biometric identification refers to the ability to identify individuals from a distance using biometric data, subject to legal restrictions.&lt;SEP&gt;Remote biometric identification refers to the capability of AI systems to identify individuals based on biometric data collected in real-time.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc038db2f25d511bf84cccc9550e10c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab148daacc5693b15ec462635a5502a7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_39.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_32.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863281</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Exceptions to Prohibition">
      <data key="d0">Exceptions to Prohibition</data>
      <data key="d1">LegalBasis</data>
      <data key="d2">Certain exceptions allow for the processing of biometric data under specific circumstances, as defined in relevant regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bc038db2f25d511bf84cccc9550e10c2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_39.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857683</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conformity Assessment Body">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Assessment Body</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">A Conformity Assessment Body is an organization that performs third-party evaluations, including testing and certification, to ensure that AI systems comply with relevant regulations and standards. It is responsible for assessing AI systems to ensure they meet specified requirements and demonstrating conformity with applicable harmonized standards. Furthermore, these bodies are evaluated and monitored by notifying authorities to guarantee compliance with set standards. In addition to evaluations, the conformity assessment body engages in consultations when objections arise regarding compliance, thereby playing a critical role in maintaining the integrity and trustworthiness of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9db4c15b43d1b7a1a1138d5a7403b240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c712c6235ebe0b7ee5102919bbe87d08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-244204be180c4ed9731f434ed67ee99b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f94df6da4de89cee24b1bd8f504c377</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_28.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_30.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_32.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863476</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Accreditation Body">
      <data key="d0">National Accreditation Body</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">National Accreditation Bodies may be involved in the assessment and monitoring processes related to conformity assessment bodies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c712c6235ebe0b7ee5102919bbe87d08</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_28.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857697</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EC) No 765/2008">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EC) No 765/2008</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EC) No 765/2008 outlines essential rules for the market placement of high-risk AI systems across sectors.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EC) No 765/2008 outlines the requirements for accreditation and operation of national accreditation bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;This regulation establishes the framework for the CE marking, governing its usage and compliance measurement for various products.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EC) No 765/2008 outlines the requirements for accreditation and repeals a previous regulation, aimed at ensuring proper compliance and standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-29241e99bddf5af77eca441d2d8dbc1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c712c6235ebe0b7ee5102919bbe87d08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5ff05678672211287e9053ebcd9c1c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c28a81721b7de3ef4442495cc499b1cb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_28.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_48.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_9.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863124</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Competent Personnel">
      <data key="d0">Competent Personnel</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Competent Personnel are individuals with necessary expertise to ensure proper performance of tasks related to notifying authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;Competent personnel are individuals with the necessary expertise for their functions, particularly in fields such as information technologies and AI.&lt;SEP&gt;Competent personnel are individuals responsible for overseeing the testing of AI systems to ensure compliance with safety and ethical standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Competent personnel are individuals responsible for oversight and management of real-world testing of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ad1a115533e7d3b3ced9ea8e2e87b0e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c712c6235ebe0b7ee5102919bbe87d08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58a25c0dd884625561b248cf275f154e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_141.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_28.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861057</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conflict of Interest">
      <data key="d0">Conflict of Interest</data>
      <data key="d1">Risk</data>
      <data key="d2">Conflict of Interest refers to situations where the impartiality of Notifying Authorities could be compromised in their dealings with Conformity Assessment Bodies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c712c6235ebe0b7ee5102919bbe87d08</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_28.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857697</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Confidentiality">
      <data key="d0">Confidentiality</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Confidentiality is a key principle that governs how information collected by market surveillance authorities is handled, especially regarding high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Confidentiality of the information obtained by Notifying Authorities must be safeguarded according to Article 78.&lt;SEP&gt;Confidentiality refers to the protection of sensitive information and data from unauthorized access or disclosure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-13b35a74627bd926656242d6545e09a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c712c6235ebe0b7ee5102919bbe87d08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0fa7bd172fb09094c2d62c87957967</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_75.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_28.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_167.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863049</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Objectivity and Impartiality">
      <data key="d0">Objectivity and Impartiality</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Objectivity and Impartiality are essential qualities that Notifying Authorities must ensure in their activities concerning conformity assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c712c6235ebe0b7ee5102919bbe87d08</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_28.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857697</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Information Technologies">
      <data key="d0">Information Technologies</data>
      <data key="d1">Domain</data>
      <data key="d2">Information technologies encompass the use of systems for storing, retrieving, and sending information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-58a25c0dd884625561b248cf275f154e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_28.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857697</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI">
      <data key="d0">AI</data>
      <data key="d1">AISubject</data>
      <data key="d2">AI is a fast-evolving family of technologies that offers various benefits across different industries and social activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Artificial Intelligence (AI) is a transformative technology that encompasses a wide range of systems and technologies designed to perform tasks traditionally requiring human intelligence. AI is recognized as a powerful tool with the potential to bring about significant benefits across various fields; however, it also carries risks of misuse in manipulative practices. These risks highlight the necessity for regulatory oversight to ensure that AI aligns with frameworks that respect human rights and protect public interests. As a rapidly developing family of technologies, AI requires careful consideration and regulation to promote safe experimentation and foster innovation while mitigating any unacceptable risks associated with its deployment. Overall, AI stands at the intersection of opportunity and caution, necessitating a balanced approach to its integration into society.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4cdf1c7e7ad7fe2c6b1b8f1b0b12db35&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40a9e2a0fc4601f4b3d4f583384b6a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f663363e3d8f01aa5c0b361bddc380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7114fa80a4a18326b68b2fd61f65c047&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cde8f1eff9bf42001a30603a860556d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58a25c0dd884625561b248cf275f154e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a975f3ad5ea339c199a21dd569a7acb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_138.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_6.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_4.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_28.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_179.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_28.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861629</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Law">
      <data key="d0">Law</data>
      <data key="d1">Domain</data>
      <data key="d2">Law involves the system of rules created and enforced through social or governmental institutions to regulate behavior.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-58a25c0dd884625561b248cf275f154e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_28.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857697</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Supervision of Fundamental Rights">
      <data key="d0">Supervision of Fundamental Rights</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Supervision of fundamental rights refers to the capacity of competent personnel to ensure that AI systems and practices align with human rights standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-58a25c0dd884625561b248cf275f154e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_28.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857697</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Third Parties">
      <data key="d0">Third Parties</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">Third parties refer to entities that provide tools, services, or AI components, particularly those accessible to the public.&lt;SEP&gt;Third parties supply tools, services, components or processes that are utilized or integrated into high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-778cb9e68fcb25e3f810e3cea927f7b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8143bb5053cad47b9eaf4c05c9556429</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_90.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_89.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862035</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Contractual Terms">
      <data key="d0">Contractual Terms</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Contractual terms are legal agreements between the Commission and AI system providers, facilitating cooperation in the AI value chain.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8143bb5053cad47b9eaf4c05c9556429</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_90.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857707</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Value Chain">
      <data key="d0">Value Chain</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">The value chain for AI systems encompasses all activities needed to develop, distribute, and support AI technologies, highlighting the interconnected roles of various operators.&lt;SEP&gt;The value chain includes all actors involved in the creation, distribution, and verification of content, especially concerning AI-generated material.&lt;SEP&gt;The value chain represents the interconnected activities involved in developing, providing, and integrating high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-197c7357cf5fefe6ca4e08f847ff6a75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51cb0d95dff3b7f033b351a9352b26a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8143bb5053cad47b9eaf4c05c9556429</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_90.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_135.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_83.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863638</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Voluntary Model Contractual Terms">
      <data key="d0">Voluntary Model Contractual Terms</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Voluntary Model Contractual Terms are agreements developed to facilitate cooperation among stakeholders in high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8143bb5053cad47b9eaf4c05c9556429</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_90.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857707</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Tools, Services, Components, and Processes">
      <data key="d0">Tools, Services, Components, and Processes</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">These are various elements supplied by third parties that assist in the functioning or enhancement of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8143bb5053cad47b9eaf4c05c9556429</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_90.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857707</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Vulnerable Persons">
      <data key="d0">Vulnerable Persons</data>
      <data key="d1">AISubject</data>
      <data key="d2">Vulnerable Persons are individuals who may be especially at risk regarding AI applications and require additional attention during AI system design to ensure inclusivity and protection.&lt;SEP&gt;Vulnerable persons are individuals or groups who may require special attention and support, particularly regarding accessibility and equality.&lt;SEP&gt;Vulnerable persons are those affected by the decisions of public authorities in migration and asylum contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Vulnerable persons include groups that may be negatively impacted by AI systems, requiring special considerations in design and deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d44e4d07784e334a8ded2c1da49b969e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40f3761e589fb7702938fd4fbbecfdcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c14e1756e1d8d71ac3ba07125f122da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-064e3e5273a81cd8d9a47da9a3f51240</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_165.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_95.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EC) No 810/2009">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EC) No 810/2009</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EC) No 810/2009 establishes a Community Code on Visas and outlines procedural requirements for visa applications in the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EC) No 810/2009 establishes a Community Code on Visas relevant to the use of AI systems in migration.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d44e4d07784e334a8ded2c1da49b969e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbb30099cdacdc2f1eb2ed182c6b4491</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857709</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2013/32/EU">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2013/32/EU</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2013/32/EU is a regulation by the European Parliament concerning procedures for granting and withdrawing international protection.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2013/32/EU pertains to procedures for granting and withdrawing international protection in the EU.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2013/32/EU specifies the common procedures for granting and withdrawing international protection within the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d44e4d07784e334a8ded2c1da49b969e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-511a9744e58c5bca320f1c98646693c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbb30099cdacdc2f1eb2ed182c6b4491</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857709</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UN Convention relating to the Status of Refugees">
      <data key="d0">UN Convention relating to the Status of Refugees</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">The UN Convention sets international obligations for the treatment and rights of refugees to ensure their protection.&lt;SEP&gt;This convention outlines the international obligations for the treatment of refugees.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d44e4d07784e334a8ded2c1da49b969e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbb30099cdacdc2f1eb2ed182c6b4491</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857709</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Applications in Migration">
      <data key="d0">AI Applications in Migration</data>
      <data key="d1">Domain</data>
      <data key="d2">AI applications in migration encompass various uses of AI technologies in assessing risks and managing asylum claims.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d44e4d07784e334a8ded2c1da49b969e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857709</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Non-Refoulement Principle">
      <data key="d0">Non-Refoulement Principle</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">The non-refoulement principle prohibits the deportation of refugees to a country where they face risk of persecution.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d44e4d07784e334a8ded2c1da49b969e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857709</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk Assessment Tools">
      <data key="d0">Risk Assessment Tools</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Risk assessment tools, such as AI systems, are designed to evaluate the risks associated with individuals in migration processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d44e4d07784e334a8ded2c1da49b969e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857709</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Migration AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Migration AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">Migration AI Systems are AI technologies applied in managing migration, asylum, and border control, subject to strict regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bbb30099cdacdc2f1eb2ed182c6b4491</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857709</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Members States">
      <data key="d0">Members States</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Member States are the individual countries that are part of the European Union and are subject to its laws and regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bbb30099cdacdc2f1eb2ed182c6b4491</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857715</data>
    </node>
    <node id="International Protection">
      <data key="d0">International Protection</data>
      <data key="d1">Purpose</data>
      <data key="d2">International Protection is a status granted to individuals fleeing persecution or serious harm in their home countries, which Directive 2013/32/EU aims to regulate.&lt;SEP&gt;International Protection refers to the legal protection granted to individuals fleeing persecution or serious harm in their home countries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-511a9744e58c5bca320f1c98646693c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbb30099cdacdc2f1eb2ed182c6b4491</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857715</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Border Control Management">
      <data key="d0">Border Control Management</data>
      <data key="d1">AreaOfImpact</data>
      <data key="d2">Border Control Management involves the processes and systems used to regulate the entry and exit of individuals at national borders.&lt;SEP&gt;Border control management is specified as a high-risk area for AI where systems are to be registered for oversight.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bbb30099cdacdc2f1eb2ed182c6b4491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2806e288e0b71013209c4ad85ecaa38b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_131.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863659</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Asylum Management">
      <data key="d0">Asylum Management</data>
      <data key="d1">Domain</data>
      <data key="d2">Asylum Management refers to the procedures and practices involved in handling requests for asylum by individuals seeking refuge.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bbb30099cdacdc2f1eb2ed182c6b4491</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857715</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Council of the European Union">
      <data key="d0">Council of the European Union</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">The Council of the European Union is an important legislative body that works alongside the European Parliament to shape EU regulations and policies.&lt;SEP&gt;The Council of the European Union is another legislative body that collaborates with the European Parliament in evaluating and adopting regulations such as Directive 2013/32/EU.&lt;SEP&gt;The Council of the European Union works alongside the European Parliament to establish legislation, including directives concerning the Digital Single Market.&lt;SEP&gt;The Council of the European Union works alongside the European Parliament to establish legislative initiatives, including AI regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Council of the European Union is involved in the legislative process alongside the European Parliament, contributing to regulations like Regulation (EU) 2022/2065.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74def3a33d9c60f3c11227adf7704a09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-feb00b9eef4af47cdd3264cd99d6b2e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-511a9744e58c5bca320f1c98646693c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5ff05678672211287e9053ebcd9c1c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2499910b26136c66e6e7a013d8f0b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_104.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_109.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_11.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_9.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863149</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Common Procedures">
      <data key="d0">Common Procedures</data>
      <data key="d1">Process</data>
      <data key="d2">Common Procedures refer to standardized methods outlined in Directive 2013/32/EU for processing asylum applications within EU member states.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-511a9744e58c5bca320f1c98646693c6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857715</data>
    </node>
    <node id="General-Purpose AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">General-Purpose AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">AIModel</data>
      <data key="d2">General-purpose AI systems can generate synthetic content such as audio, image, video, or text and must mark their outputs accordingly.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2bccefc944ad0794c75bc69b977c88a1</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857722</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Emotion Recognition System">
      <data key="d0">Emotion Recognition System</data>
      <data key="d1">AISystem</data>
      <data key="d2">An emotion recognition system is an AI system designed to identify or infer emotions based on biometric data of individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;An emotion recognition system is an AI system designed to identify or infer emotions or intentions based on biometric data.&lt;SEP&gt;An emotion recognition system is designed to detect and interpret human emotions using AI technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Emotion recognition systems analyze emotional states of individuals and must inform affected natural persons of their operation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Emotion Recognition System is defined as an AI system designed to identify or infer emotions or intentions of natural persons based on their biometric data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61cbf514bcfe4869e269c00a2dc9e712&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e726a1ef8f481d54c995afc6a028f60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bccefc944ad0794c75bc69b977c88a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ac98f64f8751ad51246ca16d843f030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0373d38f7600f51def3b5e5cb5061d17</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_18.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857832</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Biometric Categorisation System">
      <data key="d0">Biometric Categorisation System</data>
      <data key="d1">AISystem</data>
      <data key="d2">A biometric categorisation system is an AI system used to assign individuals to specific categories based on their biometric data.&lt;SEP&gt;A biometric categorisation system uses AI to classify individuals based on biometric data like fingerprints or facial recognition.&lt;SEP&gt;Biometric categorisation systems classify individuals based on their biometric data and have specific legal obligations.&lt;SEP&gt;A biometric categorization system uses biometric data to assign individuals to specific categories, emphasizing the importance of technical necessity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3ac98f64f8751ad51246ca16d843f030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bccefc944ad0794c75bc69b977c88a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e726a1ef8f481d54c995afc6a028f60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0373d38f7600f51def3b5e5cb5061d17</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulations (EU) 2016/679">
      <data key="d0">Regulations (EU) 2016/679</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulations concerning data protection and privacy in the European Union that apply to the processing of personal data.&lt;SEP&gt;This regulation pertains to the protection of personal data and privacy in the European Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2bccefc944ad0794c75bc69b977c88a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0373d38f7600f51def3b5e5cb5061d17</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857722</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulations (EU) 2018/1725">
      <data key="d0">Regulations (EU) 2018/1725</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulations that apply to the processing of personal data by EU institutions and bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;This regulation covers the protection of personal data in the EU, focusing on processing personal data by Union institutions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2bccefc944ad0794c75bc69b977c88a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0373d38f7600f51def3b5e5cb5061d17</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857722</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deep Fake Content">
      <data key="d0">Deep Fake Content</data>
      <data key="d1">Output</data>
      <data key="d2">Deep fake content refers to audio, image, or video that has been artificially generated or manipulated using AI technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Deep fake content refers to media that has been altered using AI techniques, often for deceptive purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2bccefc944ad0794c75bc69b977c88a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0373d38f7600f51def3b5e5cb5061d17</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857722</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Synthetic Content">
      <data key="d0">Synthetic Content</data>
      <data key="d1">Output</data>
      <data key="d2">Synthetic content is the output generated by AI systems, which must be labeled to indicate that it is artificially created or manipulated.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2bccefc944ad0794c75bc69b977c88a1</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857722</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Biometric Categorization System">
      <data key="d0">Biometric Categorization System</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Biometric categorization systems classify individuals based on their biometric data and must adhere to strict legal obligations for data processing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2bccefc944ad0794c75bc69b977c88a1</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857722</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Standards">
      <data key="d0">Technical Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">Standard</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical standards guide the development and implementation of AI systems, influencing their effectiveness and interoperability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2bccefc944ad0794c75bc69b977c88a1</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857722</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI System that Generates or Manipulates Content">
      <data key="d0">AI System that Generates or Manipulates Content</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">This AI system is capable of generating or altering image, audio, or video content, raising obligations for transparency in its use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0373d38f7600f51def3b5e5cb5061d17</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857722</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human Review Process">
      <data key="d0">Human Review Process</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">A process where AI-generated content is reviewed and controlled by a human, ensuring accountability and editorial responsibility.&lt;SEP&gt;The human review process involves assessing AI-generated content to ensure compliance with relevant laws and standards.&lt;SEP&gt;The human review process is a measure of oversight that should be applied to AI-generated content to ensure editorial responsibility.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4acea71d2f59038573b7ec13db4ad10b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50cb89ed7d0d818018d373ebefa65267&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0373d38f7600f51def3b5e5cb5061d17</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_134.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859267</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Natural Persons Concerned">
      <data key="d0">Natural Persons Concerned</data>
      <data key="d1">AISubject</data>
      <data key="d2">Individuals who are directly affected by the deployment and output of AI systems, requiring clear information about the content.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural persons concerned are individuals who may be affected by the deployment of AI systems and their data processing activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50cb89ed7d0d818018d373ebefa65267&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0373d38f7600f51def3b5e5cb5061d17</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857725</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI System for Generating Content">
      <data key="d0">AI System for Generating Content</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">This AI system is capable of creating or altering digital content, including texts and multimedia, which raises potential ethical concerns.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0373d38f7600f51def3b5e5cb5061d17</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857725</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Interest">
      <data key="d0">Public Interest</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Public Interest refers to the welfare or well-being of the general public that can be impacted by the dissemination of information, including AI-generated content.&lt;SEP&gt;The primary goal of the AI system to inform the public on significant matters, requiring transparency in content generation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50cb89ed7d0d818018d373ebefa65267&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03f09b5ce9e149c51cfde2a77cd90759</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_134.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859267</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Disclosure Obligation">
      <data key="d0">Disclosure Obligation</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">The legal requirement for deployers of AI systems to inform users when text content is artificially generated or manipulated.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50cb89ed7d0d818018d373ebefa65267</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857728</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Generated Content">
      <data key="d0">Generated Content</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">Content that is produced by an AI system, which may be manipulated or created with the intent to inform the public.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50cb89ed7d0d818018d373ebefa65267</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857728</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Manipulated Content">
      <data key="d0">Manipulated Content</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">Content that has been modified by an AI system, potentially affecting the integrity and authenticity of the information presented.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50cb89ed7d0d818018d373ebefa65267</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857728</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Transparency Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Transparency Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Standards governing how information about the use of AI-generated content should be disclosed to users.&lt;SEP&gt;Transparency requirements are standards within the Regulation ensuring that AI systems operate within the bounds of fundamental rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50cb89ed7d0d818018d373ebefa65267&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2315cd7abb88dee440f081de5430a32f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_157.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="First Interaction">
      <data key="d0">First Interaction</data>
      <data key="d1">Moment</data>
      <data key="d2">The initial point at which users engage with AI-generated content, marking a critical time for disclosure of its nature.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50cb89ed7d0d818018d373ebefa65267</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857728</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Accessibility Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Accessibility Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Accessibility Requirements are standards that technologies and services must meet to ensure that they are usable by persons with disabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Accessibility Requirements refer to conditions that ensure high-risk AI systems are usable by individuals with disabilities, mandated by EU directives.&lt;SEP&gt;Accessibility requirements are stipulations outlined in Directives (EU) 2016/2102 and (EU) 2019/882 for high-risk AI systems to ensure they are usable by all individuals, including those with disabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Guidelines that ensure information is available in an understandable format for all users, especially concerning AI-generated content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c17bf6e803eec807c9fc7299d71d51d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50cb89ed7d0d818018d373ebefa65267&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33366c5df404f37775ccbf3ec455b578</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_80.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_16.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862926</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Chapter III">
      <data key="d0">Chapter III</data>
      <data key="d1">Document</data>
      <data key="d2">Reference to a specific section within the regulatory document outlining additional obligations related to AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50cb89ed7d0d818018d373ebefa65267</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857728</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 56 (6)">
      <data key="d0">Article 56 (6)</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 56 (6) outlines the procedure for approving codes of practice by the Commission.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3034aa8ff1b6d41ac6e0b8ff655b76ec</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857728</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Examination Procedure">
      <data key="d0">Examination Procedure</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">The examination procedure laid down in Article 98(2) is used by the Commission to assess the adequacy of the codes of practice.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3034aa8ff1b6d41ac6e0b8ff655b76ec</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857728</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Detection of Artificially Generated Content">
      <data key="d0">Detection of Artificially Generated Content</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">The detection of artificially generated or manipulated content refers to procedures and technologies that identify when content has been created or altered by artificial means.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3034aa8ff1b6d41ac6e0b8ff655b76ec</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857728</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Labelling of Content">
      <data key="d0">Labelling of Content</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">Labelling of content involves marking or classifying content to indicate whether it is artificially generated or manipulated, ensuring transparency.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3034aa8ff1b6d41ac6e0b8ff655b76ec</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_50.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857728</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Common Rules">
      <data key="d0">Common Rules</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Common rules are standardized guidelines established for implementing obligations regarding content detection and labelling.&lt;SEP&gt;Common rules help provide guidelines for the implementation of obligations under the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c8a6b92fbe8d93eb878957c5ed60aa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3034aa8ff1b6d41ac6e0b8ff655b76ec</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_50.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_117.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863523</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Making Available on the Market">
      <data key="d0">Making Available on the Market</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Making available on the market includes actions related to distributing or supplying AI systems for use in commercial activities.&lt;SEP&gt;The supply of an AI system or model for distribution on the Union market as part of a commercial activity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7d62750f1113d24ac155fcd2b2ef02c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Safety Component">
      <data key="d0">Safety Component</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">A safety component is an integral part of a product that ensures the product functions safely and effectively, especially in relation to AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A safety component is integral to an AI system and ensures safety compliance, essential for protecting health and property.&lt;SEP&gt;A safety component is part of an AI system that ensures the safe operation of the system and protects users from harm.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4348ad8873ef2041aca94abc9297ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857850</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Instructions for Use">
      <data key="d0">Instructions for Use</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Instructions for use are guidelines provided by the provider to ensure the safe and proper operation of the AI system.&lt;SEP&gt;Instructions for use are provided to the deployer by the provider to clarify the intended purpose and proper use of the AI system.&lt;SEP&gt;Instructions for use provide essential information on how to properly utilize an AI system, including intended purpose and operational guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;Instructions for use provide essential guidance on the correct and appropriate usage of the AI system, ensuring users are informed of limitations and intended uses.&lt;SEP&gt;Instructions for use provide necessary guidance on the operational and safety aspects of high-risk AI systems to assist deployers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-07e8d113bd66975dbb8053a37cc427fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a65ec6b0fbd17afe47587686523a725&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65f69156748df83d9fa179140a3fe2aa</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863464</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recall of an AI System">
      <data key="d0">Recall of an AI System</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Recall refers to actions taken to return, disable, or remove an AI system from the market or service.&lt;SEP&gt;Recall refers to the actions taken to retrieve an AI system from deployers to address issues related to safety or compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Withdrawal of an AI System">
      <data key="d0">Withdrawal of an AI System</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Withdrawal involves measures to prevent an AI system from being made available in the market after it has been assessed.&lt;SEP&gt;Withdrawal is the action of removing an AI system from the market or service due to safety concerns or regulatory non-compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Written Mandate">
      <data key="d0">Written Mandate</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">A written mandate is a formal document given by a provider of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model, outlining the obligations and procedures to be followed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market Availability">
      <data key="d0">Market Availability</data>
      <data key="d1">AreaOfImpact</data>
      <data key="d2">Market availability refers to the conditions under which an AI system is placed on the market for distribution or use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Foreseeable Misuse">
      <data key="d0">Foreseeable Misuse</data>
      <data key="d1">Misuse</data>
      <data key="d2">Foreseeable misuse involves potential incorrect usage of the AI system that could lead to adverse outcomes and risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Foreseeable misuse refers to instances when an AI system is used in ways not intended by the provider, which may arise from expected human behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;Foreseeable misuse refers to potential incorrect applications of high-risk AI systems that could lead to risks for health and safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2f186d6b95e69680f63fabb65ad924a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65f69156748df83d9fa179140a3fe2aa</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_13.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859149</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Safety Function">
      <data key="d0">Safety Function</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">The safety function is a component within an AI system designed to protect health and safety during its operation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Obligations and Procedures">
      <data key="d0">Obligations and Procedures</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Obligations and procedures refer to the responsibilities that organizations dealing with AI systems must follow as mandated by regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recall Measures">
      <data key="d0">Recall Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Recall measures are actions taken to retrieve or disable an AI system from use, ensuring compliance with safety or regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Withdrawal Measures">
      <data key="d0">Withdrawal Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Withdrawal measures are steps taken to remove an AI system from the market due to safety or compliance concerns.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7dbd41da6ea2a77fff5beb18c8e7c896</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Reasonably Foreseeable Misuse">
      <data key="d0">Reasonably Foreseeable Misuse</data>
      <data key="d1">Misuse</data>
      <data key="d2">Reasonably foreseeable misuse involves using an AI system in ways not intended by its provider, arising from human interaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Reasonably foreseeable misuse refers to potential incorrect uses of the AI system that could lead to negative outcomes, despite not being directly intended or specified.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7b5e606b14946a1b388f008868e8e155&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859149</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Performance of an AI System">
      <data key="d0">Performance of an AI System</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Performance indicates how effectively an AI system meets its intended purpose and operational capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Performance of an AI System refers to its ability to meet the intended purposes and requirements as defined during its development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Supply Chain">
      <data key="d0">Supply Chain</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Supply chain refers to the network of entities involved in the production and distribution of AI systems, impacting compliance responsibilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Supply chain refers to the system involved in the production and distribution of AI systems and components.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1ad9c740a10a5c1577e578a593bd61fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861814</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Harmonised Standard">
      <data key="d0">Harmonised Standard</data>
      <data key="d1">Standard</data>
      <data key="d2">A harmonised standard defines the technical specifications and requirements under Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012.&lt;SEP&gt;Harmonised Standards define technical specifications compliant with regulatory requirements for AI systems in the European context.&lt;SEP&gt;A harmonised standard is a technical standard that aligns with requirements set by EU legislation, aiding in compliance for various products and services.&lt;SEP&gt;A harmonised standard is a regulatory standard developed to ensure compliance with EU legislation, providing a presumption of conformity if met.&lt;SEP&gt;A harmonised standard provides a framework for compliance and grants presumption of conformity for AI model providers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c8a6b92fbe8d93eb878957c5ed60aa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0695d12d62d4fd15a528842231db1850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c49e78c25e30ed3a2557915010f14f3c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_117.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_41.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863523</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Common Specification">
      <data key="d0">Common Specification</data>
      <data key="d1">Standard</data>
      <data key="d2">Common Specification is a set of defined technical specifications providing guidelines for the compliance of AI systems with regulatory frameworks.&lt;SEP&gt;The common specification is a set of technical specifications providing means to comply with established requirements under the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Training Data">
      <data key="d0">Training Data</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Training Data refers to data utilized to train AI systems, enabling them to adjust and optimize their parameters for better performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Training data is used to train AI systems, ensuring the fitting of their learnable parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;Training data consists of the examples and information used to teach a model, which is critical for achieving competence and generality.&lt;SEP&gt;Training data refers to the content used by AI models to learn and develop, which must adhere to copyright regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32556db3a80f72f1db354810bba21be7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e93dbcfb179aa98bf5518ab208d544fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_98.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_108.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863612</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI System in Supply Chain">
      <data key="d0">AI System in Supply Chain</data>
      <data key="d1">AISystem</data>
      <data key="d2">An AI System in Supply Chain is a technology solution intended to optimize processes and decisions in the supply chain management context.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Assessment Procedures">
      <data key="d0">Assessment Procedures</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Assessment Procedures are documented protocols that guide the conformity assessment process conducted by notified bodies for high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Assessment Procedures are the specific processes used to evaluate AI systems against established standards and compliance regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Assessment procedures are documented processes that notified bodies must follow to maintain consistency and quality in their evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2e0f993ca9c4e593e5fcbdd8fc03fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulatory Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Regulatory Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">Standard</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulatory Requirements encompass the mandatory standards and protocols that AI systems need to meet for market approval.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulatory requirements outline the standards and criteria that notified bodies must meet in order to maintain their designation and validity of certificates issued.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-34f79a9fca1518856b24fdcb7e59f040&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c237e1a0b42db9afb10cc8a045dbb751</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_36.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863789</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Validation Data">
      <data key="d0">Validation Data</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Validation data is employed to evaluate the performance of AI systems and tune parameters to avoid underfitting or overfitting.&lt;SEP&gt;Validation data refers to data used for evaluating the trained AI system and tuning its parameters to prevent underfitting or overfitting.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3ac98f64f8751ad51246ca16d843f030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Validation Data Set">
      <data key="d0">Validation Data Set</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Validation data set comprises a separate dataset used for performance evaluation of trained AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Validation data set is a separate or part of the training data set used for validation, either as a fixed or variable split.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3ac98f64f8751ad51246ca16d843f030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing Data">
      <data key="d0">Testing Data</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing data is meant for providing an independent evaluation of the AI system to confirm its expected performance prior to market release.&lt;SEP&gt;Testing data provides an independent evaluation of an AI system’s expected performance prior to market placement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3ac98f64f8751ad51246ca16d843f030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Biometric Identification">
      <data key="d0">Biometric Identification</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Biometric identification involves the automated recognition of human features for identity establishment through comparison of biometric data.&lt;SEP&gt;Biometric identification refers to the automated recognition of individual features for identity establishment using stored data.&lt;SEP&gt;Biometric identification refers to the use of unique physical characteristics for the identification or verification of individuals, especially in law enforcement contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;The technique of identifying individuals through their biometric data, enabling targeted searches to assist in criminal investigations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3ac98f64f8751ad51246ca16d843f030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4988a00689afb1245e0f0ce4ceef5921&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a23e03a78af2035b69e69bd4fc65a435</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_33.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863015</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012 describes general product safety measures that are amended by Regulation (EU) 2023/988.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012 establishes a comprehensive framework for common specifications and harmonized standards pertaining to Artificial Intelligence (AI) systems within the European Union. It outlines the roles and responsibilities of various stakeholders involved in the standardization process, ensuring clarity and coherence in the implementation of standards. The regulation specifically addresses the procedures for applying harmonized standards in the context of AI compliance, facilitating a structured approach to meet established requirements. Additionally, it encompasses definitions related to harmonized standards and common specifications, supporting the European standardization framework as a whole. The regulation also includes provisions for the assessment of these harmonized standards by the Commission, further reinforcing its alignment with EU law and policies regarding standardization. Overall, Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012 plays a crucial role in ensuring that AI systems developed and used within the EU adhere to specific compliance requirements, fostering innovation while maintaining safety and effectiveness.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012 governs European standardisation and outlines the requirements for compliance with harmonised standards in the single market.&lt;SEP&gt;The Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012 pertains to European standardization and the obligations of providers in conformity with standardization requests.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-43e82a7af456b2ae813a7217f92c2008&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3177468233ec37ad2a71dc38caa17377&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-010f171cc1a7f217689efe00fd8cb656&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3f7d41ecd7ed7ec26e62e63255378cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0695d12d62d4fd15a528842231db1850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f41337092de45470ab838aff17309ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cc9a7191827dda78eda5924876e5f7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6fc829d58f1a7bbf3defd5cbe758b8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e24261c10195e33e965bd7e966c33337&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2739984aae71aa27a0af867bc197b730</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_121.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_40.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_41.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_81.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_166.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Biometric Verification">
      <data key="d0">Biometric Verification</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Biometric verification is the automated verification of identity by comparing biometric data to previously submitted data.&lt;SEP&gt;Biometric verification refers to the automated process of verifying the identity of individuals by comparing their biometric data to previously provided data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3ac98f64f8751ad51246ca16d843f030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e726a1ef8f481d54c995afc6a028f60</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Post Remote Biometric Identification System">
      <data key="d0">Post Remote Biometric Identification System</data>
      <data key="d1">AISystem</data>
      <data key="d2">A post remote biometric identification system operates similarly to the real-time system but does not require immediate identification.&lt;SEP&gt;A system for remote biometric identification that does not operate in real-time, differing from real-time systems in functionality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a94885e0b736d24263914e9a9d565900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e726a1ef8f481d54c995afc6a028f60</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Publicly Accessible Space">
      <data key="d0">Publicly Accessible Space</data>
      <data key="d1">Location</data>
      <data key="d2">Publicly accessible spaces are areas available to the public, regardless of ownership or access conditions, where individuals may gather.&lt;SEP&gt;Refers to any physical location that is open to the public or private individuals, regardless of access conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a94885e0b736d24263914e9a9d565900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e726a1ef8f481d54c995afc6a028f60</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Law Enforcement Authority">
      <data key="d0">Law Enforcement Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">A public authority responsible for the prevention, investigation, and prosecution of criminal offenses as well as maintaining public security.&lt;SEP&gt;Law enforcement authorities are public bodies responsible for overseeing criminal investigations, prevention measures, and maintaining public security.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a94885e0b736d24263914e9a9d565900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e726a1ef8f481d54c995afc6a028f60</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857741</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Competent Authority">
      <data key="d0">National Competent Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">The National Competent Authority is an essential regulatory body tasked with ensuring compliance and governance regarding AI systems in accordance with EU regulations. This authority holds the responsibility of notifying and enforcing compliance for high-risk AI systems, which includes requesting conformity demonstrations to validate their adherence to established standards. Additionally, the National Competent Authority oversees the regulation and authorization processes within the AI regulatory sandbox, allowing for the controlled testing and development of AI technologies. It plays a crucial role in managing and certifying the validity of AI system certifications within its jurisdiction, thereby ensuring that all AI systems operate within the framework of applicable laws and regulations. Overall, the National Competent Authority functions as a key player in the implementation and oversight of AI regulations, safeguarding public interests and promoting responsible AI deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c17bf6e803eec807c9fc7299d71d51d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a94885e0b736d24263914e9a9d565900&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0779dfb4a5c0f82f05a67985fe0224a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b341fa074527a308a2434a3c68244d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0271020749ae70ce56cbd607a6f6662a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_58.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_16.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863801</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI System for Identifying Natural Persons">
      <data key="d0">AI System for Identifying Natural Persons</data>
      <data key="d1">AISystem</data>
      <data key="d2">An AI System designed to identify individuals without their active involvement, utilizing biometric data comparison against a reference database.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a94885e0b736d24263914e9a9d565900</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857746</data>
    </node>
    <node id="national competent authority">
      <data key="d0">national competent authority</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">The national competent authority is a notifying or market surveillance authority responsible for overseeing AI systems used by Union institutions and agencies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857746</data>
    </node>
    <node id="serious incident">
      <data key="d0">serious incident</data>
      <data key="d1">Risk</data>
      <data key="d2">A serious incident refers to an AI system malfunction that can result in severe outcomes, including death, serious injury, or substantial disruption of critical infrastructure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857746</data>
    </node>
    <node id="non-personal data">
      <data key="d0">non-personal data</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Non-personal data refers to any data that does not fall under the definition of personal data according to Regulation (EU) 2016/679.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857746</data>
    </node>
    <node id="profiling">
      <data key="d0">profiling</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Profiling is the automated processing of personal data to evaluate specific personal aspects concerning an individual, as defined in Regulation (EU) 2016/679.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857746</data>
    </node>
    <node id="real-world testing plan">
      <data key="d0">real-world testing plan</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">A real-world testing plan outlines the objectives, methodology, scope, monitoring, and conduct of testing AI systems in real-world conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857746</data>
    </node>
    <node id="sandbox plan">
      <data key="d0">sandbox plan</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">The sandbox plan is an agreement between a provider and the competent authority detailing the objectives, conditions, and methodology for sandbox activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857746</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI regulatory sandbox">
      <data key="d0">AI regulatory sandbox</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">An AI regulatory sandbox is a controlled framework established by an authority to allow AI system providers to develop, train, and validate their solutions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857746</data>
    </node>
    <node id="public authority">
      <data key="d0">public authority</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeveloper</data>
      <data key="d2">Public authority refers to the governmental and administrative bodies responsible for the prevention and enforcement of laws in relation to public security and criminal offenses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857746</data>
    </node>
    <node id="criminal offences">
      <data key="d0">criminal offences</data>
      <data key="d1">RiskConcept</data>
      <data key="d2">Criminal offences include illegal activities punishable by law, which relate to the areas of law enforcement and public security.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857746</data>
    </node>
    <node id="criminal penalties">
      <data key="d0">criminal penalties</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Criminal penalties are sanctions imposed by legal authorities in case of violation of laws, which involve punishment for criminal offences.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857746</data>
    </node>
    <node id="public security threats">
      <data key="d0">public security threats</data>
      <data key="d1">Threat</data>
      <data key="d2">Public security threats are risks or dangers that potentially harm the safety and well-being of the public, necessitating preventive measures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857746</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Commission Decision of 24 January 2024">
      <data key="d0">Commission Decision of 24 January 2024</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">This decision outlines the roles and responsibilities of the AI Office in the context of AI systems and governance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857746</data>
    </node>
    <node id="serious harm to health">
      <data key="d0">serious harm to health</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Serious harm to health refers to significant injury or medical issues that can result from malfunctions of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857746</data>
    </node>
    <node id="critical infrastructure">
      <data key="d0">critical infrastructure</data>
      <data key="d1">AreaOfImpact</data>
      <data key="d2">Critical infrastructure encompasses the systems and assets that are vital to national security, economic security, and public health and safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Critical infrastructure includes essential facilities and services that are vital for the functioning of society and economy, and whose disruption can lead to severe consequences.&lt;SEP&gt;Critical infrastructure is defined as essential systems and assets that are vital for the functioning of a society.&lt;SEP&gt;Critical infrastructure includes essential systems and assets that provide vital services to the public and their disruption poses risks to safety and security.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3266d68b5262e6852cabbe36178dec96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54948128ea5a4b84a219d7dbaa346a50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d91755cda6acde2b40257e6d4cef1695</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_155.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_33.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857870</data>
    </node>
    <node id="fundamental rights">
      <data key="d0">fundamental rights</data>
      <data key="d1">Impact</data>
      <data key="d2">Fundamental rights are the inherent rights protected under the Regulation, ensuring safety and privacy in the deployment of AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Fundamental rights refer to the basic rights afforded to individuals, which may be adversely impacted by high-risk AI system decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Fundamental rights represent the basic rights and freedoms entitled to individuals, which need protection under Union law.&lt;SEP&gt;Fundamental rights include the basic legal rights that must be protected from adverse impacts caused by AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71f538bc77dea56a19150de3c7514990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5928be36056ac91865bd3e4d596159e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe49d95d50900e82a706b2766339562f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_86.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_1.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_7.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863895</data>
    </node>
    <node id="data protection regulations">
      <data key="d0">data protection regulations</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Data protection regulations govern the processing and storage of personal data to ensure individual privacy and security.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857746</data>
    </node>
    <node id="testing in real-world conditions">
      <data key="d0">testing in real-world conditions</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing in real-world conditions involves evaluating the performance and safety of AI systems in practical scenarios, ensuring effectiveness and compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Testing in real-world conditions refers to evaluating an AI system's performance in environments that accurately reflect its intended use and functionality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3266d68b5262e6852cabbe36178dec96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857747</data>
    </node>
    <node id="sandbox activities">
      <data key="d0">sandbox activities</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">Sandbox activities refer to controlled experiments within a regulatory framework aimed at fostering innovation while ensuring safety and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cfc036b3a79fdcd1eb36c0af6aafbb4d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857747</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Critical Infrastructure">
      <data key="d0">Critical Infrastructure</data>
      <data key="d1">AreaOfImpact</data>
      <data key="d2">Critical Infrastructure refers to essential systems and assets that are fundamental for the functioning and stability of a society. This includes critical services such as water, gas, heating, and electricity. These infrastructures are so vital that their disruption or destruction could lead to significant harm, impacting not only the economy but also public health and safety. Defined by EU regulations, critical infrastructure encompasses various components crucial to national security and societal well-being. Additionally, in the context of modern challenges, high-risk AI systems that operate within these infrastructures must be registered at the national level to ensure compliance and security, highlighting the intersection of technology and public safety in maintaining the integrity of critical infrastructure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fe76292b9a553c383dab6b0a4a67cee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a23e03a78af2035b69e69bd4fc65a435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec6a8294e2a2ad2569029d260c4d7673&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c9405f93ec3e0ccf6209ed15ef0263f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-166a35f517674f4ceba2754c65f88c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2806e288e0b71013209c4ad85ecaa38b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_55.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_33.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_131.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863659</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Non-Personal Data">
      <data key="d0">Non-Personal Data</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Non-personal data is defined as data that does not relate to an identified or identifiable individual and is also delineated in Regulation (EU) 2016/679.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fe76292b9a553c383dab6b0a4a67cee8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Profiling">
      <data key="d0">Profiling</data>
      <data key="d1">AITechnique</data>
      <data key="d2">Profiling in the context of AI refers to the automated processing of personal data to evaluate certain aspects of an individual, potentially posing risks if mismanaged.&lt;SEP&gt;Profiling involves analyzing characteristics such as nationality or personality traits to make predictions about behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;Profiling refers to any form of automated processing of personal data to evaluate certain personal aspects related to a natural person, as defined by Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679.&lt;SEP&gt;Profiling involves the collection and analysis of personal data to assess certain aspects related to individuals, such as behavior or preferences, usually within the context of automated decision-making.&lt;SEP&gt;Profiling is a technique used by AI systems to analyze characteristics and behaviors of individuals, often in investigations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bbcf833252ce65fd6a1d8bd1f5a6efc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4274f38f6b4aeff6dc2959e9e1a87f1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe76292b9a553c383dab6b0a4a67cee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15eee417af0ebe299ed66be76a0b845a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77093970e26d1be04734ed16ea88f777</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_59.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_10.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_42.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862933</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Real-World Testing Plan">
      <data key="d0">Real-World Testing Plan</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">A real-world testing plan is a detailed document outlining the objectives, methodology, geographical, population, and temporal scope for testing AI systems in actual conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Real-World Testing Plan outlines the methodology and criteria for evaluating AI systems under real-world conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;The real-world testing plan outlines the necessary steps and conditions for testing high-risk AI systems in real-world environments, as mandated by regulatory authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ff61ec794793cf787d4a0473487a06f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe76292b9a553c383dab6b0a4a67cee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa9e2916955e882c73231ed69851f6ec</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863063</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sandbox Plan">
      <data key="d0">Sandbox Plan</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">A Sandbox Plan outlines the agreed procedures and objectives for the operation of an AI Regulatory Sandbox, detailing how AI systems will be developed and tested in a controlled environment.&lt;SEP&gt;A sandbox plan allows the testing of AI systems in controlled environments under specific regulatory conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;A sandbox plan is an agreement between a provider and a competent authority detailing objectives, conditions, timeframe, methodology, and requirements for activities in a regulatory sandbox.&lt;SEP&gt;Sandbox Plan refers to the agreed-upon strategy for testing AI systems within the regulatory sandbox, outlining expected activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fe76292b9a553c383dab6b0a4a67cee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475967c83e624bc711a9ff13e8150163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d08b537f9a5bb2b4f4bbdf442ba39bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c9405f93ec3e0ccf6209ed15ef0263f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858696</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing in Real-World Conditions">
      <data key="d0">Testing in Real-World Conditions</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing in real-world conditions helps evaluate the effectiveness and safety of AI systems when deployed outside controlled environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Testing in real-world conditions refers to the evaluation of an AI system's performance in environments that mimic its intended operational settings, ensuring compliance with regulatory standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Testing in real-world conditions refers to the temporary evaluation of an AI system in its intended environment to gather reliable data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ad1a115533e7d3b3ced9ea8e2e87b0e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe76292b9a553c383dab6b0a4a67cee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c9405f93ec3e0ccf6209ed15ef0263f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_141.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861057</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Subject">
      <data key="d0">Subject</data>
      <data key="d1">AISubject</data>
      <data key="d2">A subject is a natural person participating in testing in real-world conditions, who must provide informed consent.&lt;SEP&gt;In the context of real-world testing, a subject is a natural person who participates in the evaluation of AI systems under real conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fe76292b9a553c383dab6b0a4a67cee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c9405f93ec3e0ccf6209ed15ef0263f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Informed Consent">
      <data key="d0">Informed Consent</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Informed Consent is a fundamental requirement for testing, particularly in the context of AI system evaluation. It ensures that participants are fully informed about the testing conditions and voluntarily agree to partake in the process. This legal prerequisite safeguards the rights of subjects, allowing them the freedom to withdraw from participation at any time and to request the deletion of their personal data.

The process of informed consent encompasses a clear communication of pertinent aspects of the testing, emphasizing that subjects must understand the implications of their involvement. It is crucial that the consent provided is specific and unambiguous, reflecting the participants' genuine willingness to engage in the testing activities. Overall, Informed Consent serves as a critical mechanism to protect the autonomy and rights of individuals involved in testing AI systems under real-world conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4518ca313d8493e277775e1a9267b84d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f6e14583352886a741ac1d51eada03a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe76292b9a553c383dab6b0a4a67cee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c9405f93ec3e0ccf6209ed15ef0263f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba5a4fee300868ea16940c9ea15f534a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_61.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_141.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863087</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Serious Disruption">
      <data key="d0">Serious Disruption</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Serious Disruption signifies a significant disturbance to the management or operation of critical infrastructure that could lead to major failures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fe76292b9a553c383dab6b0a4a67cee8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Obligations under Union Law">
      <data key="d0">Obligations under Union Law</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Obligations under Union law are legal commitments established to protect fundamental rights and other legal provisions within the European Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fe76292b9a553c383dab6b0a4a67cee8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Harm to Property or Environment">
      <data key="d0">Harm to Property or Environment</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Harm to Property or Environment encompasses damage to physical assets or ecological damage resulting from actions or failures in compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fe76292b9a553c383dab6b0a4a67cee8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Deep Fake">
      <data key="d0">Deep Fake</data>
      <data key="d1">AIModel</data>
      <data key="d2">A deep fake is AI-generated content, such as images or videos, designed to appear authentic, often manipulating reality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c9405f93ec3e0ccf6209ed15ef0263f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Widespread Infringement">
      <data key="d0">Widespread Infringement</data>
      <data key="d1">Risk</data>
      <data key="d2">Widespread infringement indicates a serious incident that affects multiple users or systems and requires immediate reporting.&lt;SEP&gt;Widespread infringement involves actions contrary to Union law affecting collective interests across multiple Member States.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0dc307b8b7cb1f0e39aa9b4b1839c408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c9405f93ec3e0ccf6209ed15ef0263f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulatory Supervision">
      <data key="d0">Regulatory Supervision</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulatory supervision ensures that the testing and deployment of AI systems comply with legal requirements and standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0c9405f93ec3e0ccf6209ed15ef0263f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="deep fake">
      <data key="d0">deep fake</data>
      <data key="d1">AIConcept</data>
      <data key="d2">Deep fake refers to AI-generated or manipulated content that resembles real persons or entities, misleadingly appearing authentic.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3266d68b5262e6852cabbe36178dec96</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="widespread infringement">
      <data key="d0">widespread infringement</data>
      <data key="d1">LegalConcept</data>
      <data key="d2">Widespread infringement describes actions contrary to Union law that harm collective interests of individuals in multiple Member States.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3266d68b5262e6852cabbe36178dec96</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="general-purpose AI model">
      <data key="d0">general-purpose AI model</data>
      <data key="d1">AIModel</data>
      <data key="d2">A general-purpose AI model is an AI system that is designed for diverse applications and may involve systemic risks that need to be identified and regulated.&lt;SEP&gt;A general-purpose AI model is an advanced artificial intelligence system trained on extensive datasets using self-supervision, which enables it to exhibit significant generality. This model is designed to be adaptable to perform a variety of distinct tasks across multiple domains and applications. As a versatile AI framework, it can be integrated into different AI systems, providing diverse capabilities across various functions. Furthermore, the deployment of a general-purpose AI model necessitates an evaluation for systemic risks, ensuring its responsible use in a broad range of contexts. Overall, this type of AI exemplifies the potential for performing numerous tasks effectively while adhering to regulatory standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9575387945b55e197ecb0c955ef00f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afea58b87ff95e4731bff6457b0b57c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5406d942407c55f04629004d833f8196&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8affbc363cca00e716c4494cb81a558a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3266d68b5262e6852cabbe36178dec96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec7c9ce58b650afe456517c2483e56c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e23bb4c71b510fec0bbe6570de37cd5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_113.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_52.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_91.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_100.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_94.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863273</data>
    </node>
    <node id="high-impact capabilities">
      <data key="d0">high-impact capabilities</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">High-impact capabilities are those that match or exceed the capabilities recorded in the most advanced general-purpose AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;High-impact capabilities refer to advanced features that match or exceed those in state-of-the-art general-purpose AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3266d68b5262e6852cabbe36178dec96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afea58b87ff95e4731bff6457b0b57c5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="subject's decision to participate">
      <data key="d0">subject's decision to participate</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">This refers to the informed consent process in which individuals understand the implications and potential risks associated with participating in AI-related testing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3266d68b5262e6852cabbe36178dec96</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union law">
      <data key="d0">Union law</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Union law consists of a comprehensive set of regulations and directives established by the European Union (EU) to govern member states, ensuring compliance and the protection of rights for individuals. It encompasses legal frameworks designed to regulate various aspects, including the accuracy and fairness of measuring instruments, which also impact artificial intelligence systems. Additionally, Union law serves to protect the collective interests of individuals within member states and outlines the legislative framework governing the conduct of scientific research and related activities. Moreover, it includes provisions that restrict access to certain public spaces to safeguard public safety and security, clearly defining who is permitted to enter such areas. Overall, Union law comprises a variety of legal instruments and regulations enacted by the EU to ensure common legal protections and governance among its member states.&lt;SEP&gt;Union law refers to laws set forth by the Union which framework the deployment and regulation of high-risk AI systems and individuals' rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fe4d7c8b1c65cb7b9f5021681b13c271&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3266d68b5262e6852cabbe36178dec96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f1adc61864fb9c4d0f971c9290506f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c582b50b1dcae6565f7384ebbe5e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71f538bc77dea56a19150de3c7514990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20ac675fffdeba0fbc242b392d3af8da</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_52.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_172.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_19.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_74.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_86.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="collective interests of individuals">
      <data key="d0">collective interests of individuals</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Collective interests represent the shared rights and safety of individuals across multiple jurisdictions, particularly in the context of law and AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3266d68b5262e6852cabbe36178dec96</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI-generated content">
      <data key="d0">AI-generated content</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">AI-generated content refers to any content produced by artificial intelligence systems, particularly relevant when discussing editorial standards and responsibility.&lt;SEP&gt;AI-generated content refers to media such as images, audio, or video that is created or manipulated by artificial intelligence technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3266d68b5262e6852cabbe36178dec96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03f09b5ce9e149c51cfde2a77cd90759</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_134.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859267</data>
    </node>
    <node id="negative effects on public health, safety, public security, fundamental rights, or society">
      <data key="d0">negative effects on public health, safety, public security, fundamental rights, or society</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">These adverse impacts refer to potential harms involving individuals or groups caused by AI systems or regulatory failures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3266d68b5262e6852cabbe36178dec96</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="deployer">
      <data key="d0">deployer</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">The deployer is an individual or organization tasked with the deployment and operational management of high-risk AI systems. This role requires adequate training and technical knowledge to ensure that AI systems are put into operation ethically and safely, adhering to verified identification processes. Deployers are responsible for conducting impact assessments, notifying relevant authorities about compliance, and making decisions based on the outputs of these AI systems. They must also provide explanations to affected individuals regarding the use and implications of the AI technologies. Deployers can be either entities governed by public law or private organizations that deliver public services, highlighting their significant role in the ethical implementation of AI systems in society.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0efde0679d72a2d51e7acdaf09979bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a0a99b47c288a96d7474c796efb766&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3266d68b5262e6852cabbe36178dec96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a68b9cb2eff595118d2af9313b6c89f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5644d48de211c02e29152f909c69640b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71f538bc77dea56a19150de3c7514990</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_27.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_86.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_9.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863750</data>
    </node>
    <node id="operator">
      <data key="d0">operator</data>
      <data key="d1">AIOperator</data>
      <data key="d2">An operator is the individual or organization that manages the operations of AI systems in a deployed environment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3266d68b5262e6852cabbe36178dec96</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="general-purpose AI system">
      <data key="d0">general-purpose AI system</data>
      <data key="d1">AISystem</data>
      <data key="d2">A general-purpose AI system is an AI model not classified as high-risk but can become high-risk through modifications in intended use.&lt;SEP&gt;A general-purpose AI system is based on a general-purpose AI model and can serve various purposes, including integration in other AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A general-purpose AI system is characterized by its ability to serve various purposes thanks to the integration of a general-purpose AI model.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9575387945b55e197ecb0c955ef00f65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afea58b87ff95e4731bff6457b0b57c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_100.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_84.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862178</data>
    </node>
    <node id="floating-point operation">
      <data key="d0">floating-point operation</data>
      <data key="d1">Metric</data>
      <data key="d2">Floating-point operation refers to mathematical operations involving floating-point numbers, typically represented on computers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-afea58b87ff95e4731bff6457b0b57c5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="downstream provider">
      <data key="d0">downstream provider</data>
      <data key="d1">AIProvider</data>
      <data key="d2">A downstream provider is an entity that provides an AI system, integrating an AI model which may be obtained from themselves or other entities under contractual relations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-afea58b87ff95e4731bff6457b0b57c5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union market">
      <data key="d0">Union market</data>
      <data key="d1">Market</data>
      <data key="d2">The Union market refers to the economic environment in which general-purpose AI systems operate, subject to regulation and oversight to ensure public safety and welfare.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-afea58b87ff95e4731bff6457b0b57c5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="data">
      <data key="d0">data</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Data refers to the large sets of information used to train AI models, influencing their performance and capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-afea58b87ff95e4731bff6457b0b57c5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="value chain">
      <data key="d0">value chain</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">The value chain encompasses all the steps involved in developing, marketing, and supporting AI systems, critical for assessing systemic risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-afea58b87ff95e4731bff6457b0b57c5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Floating-Point Operation">
      <data key="d0">Floating-Point Operation</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">A Floating-Point Operation is defined as any mathematical operation involving floating-point numbers, essential for various computational tasks in AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-decd01dd1bf25270eddf9979fe28678a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Downstream Provider">
      <data key="d0">Downstream Provider</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">A Downstream Provider refers to an entity that provides an AI system, integrating an AI model regardless of direct provision or contract-based relationships.&lt;SEP&gt;Downstream provider refers to the entity deploying the AI system and is responsible for facilitating compliance with specific obligations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-decd01dd1bf25270eddf9979fe28678a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6570d0db42cf764ebb073d69da0137e3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_133.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863759</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Model">
      <data key="d0">AI Model</data>
      <data key="d1">AIModel</data>
      <data key="d2">An AI Model is a specific configuration of algorithms used by AI systems to learn from inputs and provide output.&lt;SEP&gt;The AI model is a subset of the AI system that includes general-purpose capabilities for generating content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-decd01dd1bf25270eddf9979fe28678a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6570d0db42cf764ebb073d69da0137e3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_133.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863752</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Quality Measurement">
      <data key="d0">Quality Measurement</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f5fc2b531499a81e154196ee1e86ac6</data>
      <data key="d2">Performance measurement evaluates how well an AI system achieves its intended purpose and regulatory requirements.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Serious Harm">
      <data key="d0">Serious Harm</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fe76292b9a553c383dab6b0a4a67cee8</data>
      <data key="d2">Critical infrastructure is at risk of serious harm due to potential disruptions or failures, making it essential to protect and manage effectively.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857751</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Charter">
      <data key="d0">Charter</data>
      <data key="d1">Document</data>
      <data key="d2">The Charter encompasses various fundamental rights, including human dignity, freedom of expression, and protection of personal data. It outlines the rights that must be protected in the context of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Charter establishes fundamental rights and principles to be upheld in AI governance and application's legality.&lt;SEP&gt;The Charter outlines fundamental rights including the right to nondiscrimination, data protection, privacy, and rights of the child, framing the legal context for AI regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Charter enshrines the values of the Union, serving as a foundational document for rights and principles.&lt;SEP&gt;The Charter outlines fundamental rights and principles guiding the regulation of AI systems and personal data usage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-14f663363e3d8f01aa5c0b361bddc380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eea61d03ab615ac5f518e77cd220c1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e284955c1d36330bd14d117bb417611&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ded1c99cfd152513a4ef07b96a9c5de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41cdee30f8345bc3690d876d77e6845c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_7.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_63.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_48.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_28.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863405</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Declaration on Digital Rights and Principles for the Digital Decade">
      <data key="d0">European Declaration on Digital Rights and Principles for the Digital Decade</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">This declaration outlines the ethical and digital rights considerations that must be factored into AI governance and deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3ded1c99cfd152513a4ef07b96a9c5de</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_7.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857762</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ethics Guidelines for Trustworthy AI">
      <data key="d0">Ethics Guidelines for Trustworthy AI</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Ethics Guidelines for Trustworthy AI provide a framework for AI developers to follow, promoting trustworthiness, accountability, and sustainability in AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ethics guidelines for trustworthy AI provided by the AI HLEG highlight the principles necessary for the development and use of AI applications responsibly.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3ded1c99cfd152513a4ef07b96a9c5de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c14e1756e1d8d71ac3ba07125f122da</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_165.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_7.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI HLEG">
      <data key="d0">AI HLEG</data>
      <data key="d1">AIProvider</data>
      <data key="d2">The AI HLEG (High-Level Expert Group on Artificial Intelligence) is an independent group appointed by the Commission to develop ethical guidelines for AI.&lt;SEP&gt;The High-Level Expert Group on Artificial Intelligence is a European advisory group that provides guidelines and ethical frameworks for AI development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3ded1c99cfd152513a4ef07b96a9c5de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-256a6003a5841f2764536c55f7086431</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_7.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Common Rules for High-Risk AI Systems">
      <data key="d0">Common Rules for High-Risk AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Common rules for high-risk AI systems are regulatory guidelines aimed at ensuring safety and non-discrimination in AI technology.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3ded1c99cfd152513a4ef07b96a9c5de</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_7.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857762</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Unions International Trade Commitments">
      <data key="d0">Unions International Trade Commitments</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">The Union’s international trade commitments refer to the obligations and standards to which member states adhere in trade agreements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3ded1c99cfd152513a4ef07b96a9c5de</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_7.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857766</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Mitigation Measures">
      <data key="d0">Mitigation Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Actions taken to address and reduce risks associated with any serious incidents identified during testing procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Mitigation Measures are a set of strategies developed within the AI Regulatory Sandbox to address and manage the various risks associated with AI systems. These measures are designed to ensure compliance and safety, specifically targeting systemic risks that may arise from AI models. They encompass a wide array of actions implemented by providers to minimize identified risks or adverse impacts that may result from the deployment and operation of high-risk AI systems. Furthermore, Mitigation Measures are aimed at reducing or eliminating risks linked to the development and testing of AI systems, as well as addressing vulnerabilities inherent in these technologies. Overall, Mitigation Measures play a crucial role in enhancing the safety and reliability of AI applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Mitigation Measures are actions taken to address serious incidents identified during AI system testing, ensuring participant safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Mitigation Measures are strategies or actions implemented by the provider to reduce potential risks associated with the AI model.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7859a0c655f74761757b416c3b50bf36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4518ca313d8493e277775e1a9267b84d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed5ccbca443324af303d8bca3aa31a38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f6e14583352886a741ac1d51eada03a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b5e606b14946a1b388f008868e8e155&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c4d127e5313d415dd94f6b6761da956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d08b537f9a5bb2b4f4bbdf442ba39bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-075ecb5835777e6044264a23ca0cb20a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0bef2c1dcc3d7b428c7611732f7ffc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_15.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_93.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_92.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_139.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863869</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Structured Dialogue">
      <data key="d0">Structured Dialogue</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">Structured dialogue is a process initiated by the AI Office to discuss compliance and risk mitigation commitments with providers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1a0bef2c1dcc3d7b428c7611732f7ffc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_93.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857768</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Articles 53 and 54">
      <data key="d0">Articles 53 and 54</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Articles 53 and 54 outline obligations for providers of general-purpose AI models to manage systemic risks associated with their technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Articles 53 and 54 outline specific obligations that providers must comply with to ensure safety and risk management in AI deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7cfbca03bf6afb99c3326dc8b02d083b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0bef2c1dcc3d7b428c7611732f7ffc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_55.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_93.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857803</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Commitments">
      <data key="d0">Commitments</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Commitments are binding agreements made by providers to implement measures addressing systemic risks identified during dialogues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1a0bef2c1dcc3d7b428c7611732f7ffc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_93.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857768</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Harmonization Legislation">
      <data key="d0">Union Harmonization Legislation</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Union harmonization legislation establishes requirements for manufacturers regarding AI systems and product safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-17ccf2ddbeca1f4e8b771a2316b7d16c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_87.json</data>
