    <node id="New Legislative Framework">
      <data key="d0">New Legislative Framework</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">The New Legislative Framework establishes essential legal requirements and standards that govern compliance within the value chain of artificial intelligence (AI) systems. It aims to harmonize product legislation across the European Union (EU) by providing a structured approach to the development and compliance of these systems within EU legislation. The framework serves as the foundation for implementing EU product rules and harmonization legislation specifically related to AI systems. Additionally, it incorporates more detailed provisions regarding the regulation and compliance of various AI systems, particularly those designated as high-risk. Ultimately, the New Legislative Framework seeks to create uniform regulations across different sectors to ensure consistent market access and uphold safety standards throughout the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-197c7357cf5fefe6ca4e08f847ff6a75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3e6894a9009f1db207c0ec639d8a39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c168b1207668ad4ba646371f91bfce09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2298fd83910d35175065de74977bd4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c28a81721b7de3ef4442495cc499b1cb</data>
