      <data key="d0">Human-Machine Interface Tools</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">Human-machine interface tools are necessary for the effective oversight and interaction between people and high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4c4d127e5313d415dd94f6b6761da956</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human Oversight">
      <data key="d0">Human Oversight</data>
      <data key="d1">HumanInvolvement</data>
      <data key="d2">Human oversight ensures that humans can intervene in AI system operations to enhance safety and accountability.&lt;SEP&gt;Human oversight is aimed at preventing or minimizing risks to health, safety, or fundamental rights associated with high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Human oversight refers to the measures enabling humans to monitor and intervene in the operation of AI systems to ensure compliance and mitigate risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ee04f6104a24650416810ede28f3790b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c4d127e5313d415dd94f6b6761da956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9685a1f72e235a3f5b9ee69878eedb21</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_96.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861626</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Automation Bias">
      <data key="d0">Automation Bias</data>
      <data key="d1">RiskConcept</data>
      <data key="d2">Automation bias is the tendency for users to over-rely on outputs from high-risk AI systems, potentially leading to adverse outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4c4d127e5313d415dd94f6b6761da956</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json</data>
