    <node id="Stop Button">
      <data key="d0">Stop Button</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">The stop button is a safety mechanism that allows users to halt the operation of high-risk AI systems to ensure safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4c4d127e5313d415dd94f6b6761da956</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Decision-Making Support">
      <data key="d0">Decision-Making Support</data>
      <data key="d1">Purpose</data>
      <data key="d2">Decision-making support refers to the role of high-risk AI systems in providing information or recommendations to users.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4c4d127e5313d415dd94f6b6761da956</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="high-risk AI system">
      <data key="d0">high-risk AI system</data>
      <data key="d1">AISystem</data>
      <data key="d2">A high-risk AI system is defined as a type of AI technology that presents significant risks and must comply with specific documentation and regulatory requirements before being placed on the market or put into service.&lt;SEP&gt;A high-risk AI system is defined as an artificial intelligence technology that poses significant risks to individuals or society, thus necessitating specific obligations for its providers. These systems require stringent oversight and thorough documentation to ensure compliance with legal and safety standards. They are characterized by their substantial influence on decisions made by natural persons, thereby necessitating careful monitoring and governance to ensure their safe operation.

High-risk AI systems must undergo specific assessments prior to deployment to evaluate their impact on fundamental rights and must comply with particular regulatory frameworks. This includes obligations related to impact assessments to mitigate risks associated with their operation. Moreover, high-risk AI systems are recognized as those that can affect health and safety and have legal implications or significantly influence individuals' rights.

Additionally, high-risk AI systems are trained and tested on specific data that is relevant to their geographical and contextual applications. Overall, these systems are subject to careful oversight and monitoring, emphasizing their notable impact and the critical regulatory requirements governing their use.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems are those that are subject to stringent risk management requirements due to their potential impact on safety and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0efde0679d72a2d51e7acdaf09979bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19283d37b8085eb0b86aff77d85558de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a0a99b47c288a96d7474c796efb766&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2118453abd880b63eddb91fa3806c3f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75ffbd2452fab424919d626f5688692d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07b79b1855840c81b5d9079a82c7e9fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8c5a915dca180e1c423cefa27ea6cd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a68b9cb2eff595118d2af9313b6c89f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc0fa7bd172fb09094c2d62c87957967&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46418d497e0c090818a97380d173293d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71f538bc77dea56a19150de3c7514990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36cb0fd5abf1b169a8aa13021f58c7b2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_75.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_27.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_48.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_18.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_11.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_84.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_122.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_86.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_9.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863761</data>
    </node>
