    <node id="stop button">
      <data key="d0">stop button</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">The stop button is a safety feature that allows users to halt the operation of a high-risk AI system to ensure it comes to a safe state when necessary.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2118453abd880b63eddb91fa3806c3f3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="verification requirement">
      <data key="d0">verification requirement</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">The verification requirement mandates that outputs from high-risk AI systems must be confirmed by at least two competent persons before any action is taken based on them.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2118453abd880b63eddb91fa3806c3f3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union or national law">
      <data key="d0">Union or national law</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Union or national law can influence the application of certain regulations regarding high-risk AI systems, especially concerning law enforcement and border control.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2118453abd880b63eddb91fa3806c3f3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI system operation">
      <data key="d0">AI system operation</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">The operational capacity of an AI system encompasses its ability to function correctly, which includes monitoring for anomalies and performance issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2118453abd880b63eddb91fa3806c3f3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="needed competencies">
      <data key="d0">needed competencies</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Needed competencies represent the skills and training necessary for individuals verifying outputs from high-risk AI systems to ensure accurate assessment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2118453abd880b63eddb91fa3806c3f3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="border control">
      <data key="d0">border control</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Border control areas restrict public access to maintain security at national boundaries.&lt;SEP&gt;Border control involves the regulation of people entering or exiting a country and may utilize high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5644d48de211c02e29152f909c69640b</data>
