    </node>
    <node id="Training">
      <data key="d0">Training</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Training consists of the education and skill development necessary for natural persons to competently perform verifications of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5644d48de211c02e29152f909c69640b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Authority">
      <data key="d0">Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Authority denotes the power vested in natural persons to validate AI system outputs and identifications.&lt;SEP&gt;Authority refers to the power or right assigned to personnel to make decisions regarding the operation of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c8721c261d628c538814f61ffe3cec22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5644d48de211c02e29152f909c69640b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_91.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859046</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Verification Requirement">
      <data key="d0">Verification Requirement</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">The verification requirement mandates that actions based on biometric identification must be confirmed by at least two different natural persons to prevent incorrect matches.&lt;SEP&gt;The verification requirement mandates that identification must be confirmed by at least two natural persons before deployment of the AI system.&lt;SEP&gt;Verification Requirement refers to the need for confirmation by natural persons before proceeding, ensuring accountability and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ded7b0ac022304fae10651966b33d18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ed67e673a6fe0a3c79a41bb9102d44b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5644d48de211c02e29152f909c69640b</data>
