      <data key="d5">1750857803</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Harmonised Standards">
      <data key="d0">Harmonised Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">Standard</data>
      <data key="d2">Harmonised Standards are developed specifications and official guidelines aimed at supporting regulations and ensuring compliance among various stakeholders, particularly within the European Union (EU). These standards are critical for aligning technical requirements with EU regulations, especially concerning Artificial Intelligence (AI) systems. They serve as benchmarks that promote uniformity and adherence across different AI developments, facilitating manufacturers' compliance with legal obligations, notably for high-risk AI systems.

Additionally, Harmonised Standards establish specific criteria that financial institutions must meet under Union financial services law, primarily focusing on quality management systems. Overall, Harmonised Standards are essential documents that help demonstrate compliance with various regulations and support a cohesive approach to regulatory adherence in the rapidly evolving field of AI, while also ensuring that common specifications are developed for compliance across member states.&lt;SEP&gt;Harmonised standards are standards that have been developed to ensure compliance with European Union legislation and are referenced in the Official Journal of the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Harmonised Standards are established guidelines accepted across the EU aimed at ensuring compliance with regulations while respecting fundamental rights.&lt;SEP&gt;Harmonised standards are established standards that reflect the state of the art, allowing providers to demonstrate conformity with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee6d94a5f64203f09d02387acbdb39c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9db4c15b43d1b7a1a1138d5a7403b240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-010f171cc1a7f217689efe00fd8cb656&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e5d20a8e9427a4698b84f758676994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f41337092de45470ab838aff17309ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98532c431ec75ae38c76dc0730337a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cc9a7191827dda78eda5924876e5f7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc662d7e26079b23ad5010b8671bfb7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6fc829d58f1a7bbf3defd5cbe758b8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b837dd750c95d041180fa3d735328672&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e24261c10195e33e965bd7e966c33337&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cfbca03bf6afb99c3326dc8b02d083b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_121.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_41.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_81.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_55.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_32.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863576</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Provider of General-Purpose AI Models">
      <data key="d0">Provider of General-Purpose AI Models</data>
      <data key="d1">AIProvider</data>
      <data key="d2">A Provider of General-Purpose AI Models is an individual or organization responsible for offering AI Models for market placement.&lt;SEP&gt;The provider is responsible for ensuring that general-purpose AI models comply with regulations, especially regarding systemic risks.</data>
