    <node id="Union and national law">
      <data key="d0">Union and national law</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Union and national law encompass the legal frameworks established by the European Union and individual countries governing law enforcement practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Union and national law sets legal standards to govern how AI systems should operate, particularly in relation to individual rights and evaluation practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-28efea7f8fe5945cce5b7be57e88efe7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d91755cda6acde2b40257e6d4cef1695</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_33.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861584</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Law Enforcement Authorities">
      <data key="d0">Law Enforcement Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Law Enforcement Authorities are deployers who provide operational data that may be subject to specific exclusions in the monitoring of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Law Enforcement Authorities are organizations and governmental agencies dedicated to maintaining public order, preventing, and investigating crimes in accordance with laws and regulations. They are responsible for detaining individuals involved in criminal activities and ensuring public safety. As public institutions, Law Enforcement Authorities play a significant role in the deployment of high-risk AI systems, utilizing these technologies to enhance their operational capabilities in crime-related assessments and investigations. In specific circumstances, they may deploy AI technologies for public safety without prior market authorization, provided there are justified reasons for such actions. Ultimately, Law Enforcement Authorities uphold the law and may use AI systems to assist in achieving their mission of maintaining law and order.&lt;SEP&gt;Law enforcement authorities are governmental agencies responsible for enforcing laws, preventing crime, and maintaining public order, including the deployment of high-risk AI systems for biometric identification.&lt;SEP&gt;Law Enforcement Authorities are the entities responsible for public safety, prevention, investigation, and prosecution of criminal offenses.&lt;SEP&gt;Law enforcement authorities are organizations responsible for maintaining public safety and investigating crimes, particularly in relation to data processing in AI sandboxes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bbcf833252ce65fd6a1d8bd1f5a6efc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a23e03a78af2035b69e69bd4fc65a435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf8a675497acfbeb420b95621b7cb31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-878d589bc7b69ae2d9c3a44284a1badc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ba8e0dd4981bd71dedb04a86b45601&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75ec68339f2da8ef06976767a0d5b494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f56b40e98f8949a37c3ab283b01f7050&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2612abd3c26dca69a0acec30add3ef15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-800752b66b6fe0cd70bb0290efc2fbbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4882abf1dd869d3dff00b8d88ee946a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6badc71855b10bbd17a31c7dfef0c442</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_26.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_78.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_59.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_33.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_130.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_59.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863383</data>
    </node>
