    </node>
    <node id="Harmonised Rules">
      <data key="d0">Harmonised Rules</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Harmonised Rules are regulations developed to ensure consistency and compliance across the EU regarding AI and safety standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Harmonised rules refer to standardized regulations that ensure uniformity in governance and oversight of artificial intelligence technologies across the EU member states.&lt;SEP&gt;Harmonised rules set common standards and regulations that must be followed regarding artificial intelligence usage.&lt;SEP&gt;Harmonised rules establish consistent standards across the EU for the use and governance of AI systems, facilitating compliance and accountability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-15eee417af0ebe299ed66be76a0b845a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9e2499910b26136c66e6e7a013d8f0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a84d660603389dd91dcd96134d5bb46e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_10.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_109.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_103.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_107.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862268</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Member States">
      <data key="d0">EU Member States</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">EU Member States are individual countries within the European Union that must comply with regulations established by the European Parliament, including those related to AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c472ba24566e25512f738275d98a9e3b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_107.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857814</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Common Specifications">
      <data key="d0">Common Specifications</data>
      <data key="d1">Standard</data>
      <data key="d2">Common Specifications define the technical requirements that must be adhered to by AI systems to ensure safety and compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Common Specifications provide detailed requirements that AI systems must meet to comply with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Common specifications are technical directives that relate to the enforcement of the Regulation and standards of the Union law.&lt;SEP&gt;Common specifications refer to technical standards that must be met by high-risk AI systems and general-purpose AI models.&lt;SEP&gt;Common specifications refer to the agreed-upon criteria and requirements that AI systems must fulfill to be deemed compliant.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee6d94a5f64203f09d02387acbdb39c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0695d12d62d4fd15a528842231db1850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f41337092de45470ab838aff17309ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cc9a7191827dda78eda5924876e5f7e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_81.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_41.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862836</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Articles 8 to 15">
      <data key="d0">Articles 8 to 15</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">These articles within the Regulation detail specific requirements and obligations related to AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_96.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857827</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 25">
      <data key="d0">Article 25</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 25 of the Regulation addresses particular provisions and exceptions applicable to AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_96.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857827</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex I">
      <data key="d0">Annex I</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex I contains a list of Union harmonization legislation relevant to the high-risk AI systems under the regulation, guiding market surveillance activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex I is a critical component of the Regulation, encompassing a comprehensive list of Union harmonization legislation that is pertinent to the enforcement of the Regulation. It details the specific types of products and AI systems that may necessitate high-risk compliance assessments according to EU law, ensuring that high-risk AI systems are subject to stringent legal standards. Additionally, Annex I outlines the legal acts that govern high-risk AI systems and their corresponding assessment procedures, fostering compliance and regulatory adherence. Furthermore, it includes guidelines for post-market monitoring of AI systems, aimed at ensuring ongoing compliance and protection under the relevant legislation. Overall, Annex I serves as a foundational reference for the harmonization of standards applied to AI technologies within the Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99c78ffcf815fa82f05dcb7dc5871e1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e5d20a8e9427a4698b84f758676994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00e7606a0fa9d588f18d67d02cfcf654&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98532c431ec75ae38c76dc0730337a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4348ad8873ef2041aca94abc9297ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc8a3a685818e1a12850434d4ddcb5cb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_6.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_74.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863707</data>
    </node>
    <node id="State of the Art on AI">
      <data key="d0">State of the Art on AI</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">The generally acknowledged state of the art on AI refers to the most advanced development level in AI technology and methods.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b235644744fa597c94328afbeaa7e56b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_96.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857827</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Guidelines">
      <data key="d0">Guidelines</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Guidelines are documents issued by regulatory bodies that outline the requirements and best practices for implementing quality management systems in businesses.&lt;SEP&gt;Guidelines refer to the formal recommendations or instructions that outline necessary actions or standards regarding AI initiatives and updates.&lt;SEP&gt;Guidelines refer to the written instructions provided by the Commission for the effective implementation of regulatory measures concerning AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Guidelines specify practical implementations and examples for AI systems, distinguishing high-risk from non-high-risk use cases.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ad25bfaa86145b8556e5d82696b8bab4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e75ee11aa912f1497b2a91ae655e7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c742eff7a2b610bb01c8c0ec233b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d64a2a65aec35f8304efaaee30e0034d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_146.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863327</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Update">
      <data key="d0">Update</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Update refers to the act of revising or modifying previously established guidelines to ensure they remain relevant and effective.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-21c742eff7a2b610bb01c8c0ec233b62</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_96.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857827</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI Regulations">
      <data key="d0">AI Regulations</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">AI Regulations are the rules and standards established to govern the development and implementation of artificial intelligence technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-21c742eff7a2b610bb01c8c0ec233b62</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_96.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857827</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Commission's Initiative">
      <data key="d0">Commission's Initiative</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Commission's Initiative indicates the proactive role of the Commission in updating AI guidelines, reflecting its capability to adapt regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-21c742eff7a2b610bb01c8c0ec233b62</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_96.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857827</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Stakeholder Involvement">
      <data key="d0">Stakeholder Involvement</data>
      <data key="d1">AreaOfImpact</data>
      <data key="d2">Stakeholder Involvement encompasses the participation of various entities, such as Member States, in influencing and shaping AI policies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-21c742eff7a2b610bb01c8c0ec233b62</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_96.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857827</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Physical States">
      <data key="d0">Physical States</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Physical states like pain or fatigue are excluded from the capabilities of the emotion recognition system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61cbf514bcfe4869e269c00a2dc9e712</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_18.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857832</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Expressions">
      <data key="d0">Expressions</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Expressions refer to the physical manifestations of emotions, such as facial expressions or body movements, that the system does not include for detecting emotions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61cbf514bcfe4869e269c00a2dc9e712</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_18.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857832</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Gestures">
      <data key="d0">Gestures</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Gestures are movements of hands, arms, or head which the system does not consider for inferring emotions unless they are used in conjunction with other biometric data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61cbf514bcfe4869e269c00a2dc9e712</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_18.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857832</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Voice Characteristics">
      <data key="d0">Voice Characteristics</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Voice characteristics such as tone, volume, or pitch are aspects of communication that can indicate emotions but are also excluded in direct detection by the system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61cbf514bcfe4869e269c00a2dc9e712</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_18.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857832</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Professional Pilots and Drivers">
      <data key="d0">Professional Pilots and Drivers</data>
      <data key="d1">AISubject</data>
      <data key="d2">Professional pilots and drivers are specific natural persons mentioned in the context of detecting states of fatigue to prevent accidents, which is outside the emotion recognition system's scope.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61cbf514bcfe4869e269c00a2dc9e712</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_18.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857832</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Prohibitions">
      <data key="d0">Prohibitions</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Prohibitions outlined in the Regulation refer to specific activities involving AI that are deemed to pose unacceptable risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-40a9e2a0fc4601f4b3d4f583384b6a06</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_179.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857843</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Governance and Enforcement Structure">
      <data key="d0">Governance and Enforcement Structure</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">The governance and enforcement structure refers to the organizational framework established to oversee the implementation and adherence to the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-40a9e2a0fc4601f4b3d4f583384b6a06</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_179.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857843</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conformity Assessment System">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Assessment System</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">The conformity assessment system is a mechanism established to evaluate compliance with the Regulation's standards and requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-40a9e2a0fc4601f4b3d4f583384b6a06</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_179.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857843</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2 August 2026">
      <data key="d0">2 August 2026</data>
      <data key="d1">Date</data>
      <data key="d2">The date from which the regulation is set to apply formally without exceptions, marking the beginning of enforcement.&lt;SEP&gt;The date when the Regulation is fully applicable, marking the end of the transitional provisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-40a9e2a0fc4601f4b3d4f583384b6a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e93fbd1f7fc7cbb860b708f989987b57</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_113.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_179.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859218</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2 February 2025">
      <data key="d0">2 February 2025</data>
      <data key="d1">Date</data>
      <data key="d2">The date from which Chapters I and II of the Regulation will take effect, indicating a phased implementation.&lt;SEP&gt;The date when the prohibitions and general provisions of the Regulation first come into effect, due to unacceptable risk considerations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-40a9e2a0fc4601f4b3d4f583384b6a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e93fbd1f7fc7cbb860b708f989987b57</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_113.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_179.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859218</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Application Date">
      <data key="d0">Application Date</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">The date of application refers to the specific time when the provisions of the Regulation will go into effect, which is set for 2 August 2025.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2ad9752391e53e840a2d8ac0861f8948</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_179.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857843</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Provisions">
      <data key="d0">Provisions</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Provisions are specific requirements set within the Regulation that must be properly implemented by the designated application date.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2ad9752391e53e840a2d8ac0861f8948</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_179.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857843</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation Implementation">
      <data key="d0">Regulation Implementation</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation Implementation refers to the act of enforcing the specified provisions of the Regulation as of the application date.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2ad9752391e53e840a2d8ac0861f8948</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_179.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857843</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Effective Date">
      <data key="d0">Effective Date</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">The Effective Date is the date when the Regulation's provisions must be fully operational, which is aligned with the application date of 2 August 2025.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2ad9752391e53e840a2d8ac0861f8948</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_179.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857843</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Penalties Provisions">
      <data key="d0">Penalties Provisions</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Penalties Provisions outline the consequences that will be enforced from the application date if the Regulation's requirements are not met.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2ad9752391e53e840a2d8ac0861f8948</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_179.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857843</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Third-Party Conformity Assessment">
      <data key="d0">Third-Party Conformity Assessment</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">A third-party conformity assessment is an evaluation process necessary for the approval of high-risk AI systems to ensure safety and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b4348ad8873ef2041aca94abc9297ee</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857850</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-Risk Status">
      <data key="d0">High-Risk Status</data>
      <data key="d1">RiskConcept</data>
      <data key="d2">High-risk status indicates that an AI system meets certain criteria that necessitate adherence to strict safety and regulatory standards to protect health and rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b4348ad8873ef2041aca94abc9297ee</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857850</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Documentation Obligation">
      <data key="d0">Documentation Obligation</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Documentation obligation refers to the requirement for providers to maintain comprehensive records and evaluations of AI systems prior to market introduction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6b4348ad8873ef2041aca94abc9297ee</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857853</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Significant Risk of Harm">
      <data key="d0">Significant Risk of Harm</data>
      <data key="d1">Risk</data>
      <data key="d2">Significant Risk of Harm refers to the potential adverse effects on health, safety, or fundamental rights posed by an AI system.&lt;SEP&gt;Significant risk of harm pertains to potential adverse impacts that an AI system might pose to human health, safety, or fundamental rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d64a2a65aec35f8304efaaee30e0034d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4348ad8873ef2041aca94abc9297ee</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857853</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Narrow Procedural Task">
      <data key="d0">Narrow Procedural Task</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">A narrow procedural task is a focused function that an AI system performs without significant impact on prior decision-making processes.&lt;SEP&gt;A narrow procedural task is an intended function of an AI system that does not significantly affect decision-making or operate outside predefined parameters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d64a2a65aec35f8304efaaee30e0034d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4348ad8873ef2041aca94abc9297ee</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857853</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human Activity Improvement">
      <data key="d0">Human Activity Improvement</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Human activity improvement involves AI systems enhancing outcomes based on human-generated data or actions without replacing human oversight.&lt;SEP&gt;Improving the result of previously completed human activity refers to an AI system's capability to enhance prior outcomes without replacing human judgment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d64a2a65aec35f8304efaaee30e0034d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4348ad8873ef2041aca94abc9297ee</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857853</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Decision-Making Patterns">
      <data key="d0">Decision-Making Patterns</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Decision-Making Patterns are the trends or regularities in human decisions that an AI system may be designed to detect without influencing human assessments.&lt;SEP&gt;Decision-making patterns relate to the methodologies that AI systems utilize to analyze past human decisions and ensure their evaluations are reliable under human review.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d64a2a65aec35f8304efaaee30e0034d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4348ad8873ef2041aca94abc9297ee</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857853</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Artificial Intelligence Board">
      <data key="d0">European Artificial Intelligence Board</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeveloper</data>
      <data key="d2">The European AI Board is consulted for creating guidelines to ensure proper implementation of regulations regarding AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Artificial Intelligence Board is responsible for consulting and providing guidelines related to the implementation of AI regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Artificial Intelligence Board aims to support the promotion of AI literacy tools and public understanding of AI-related issues.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Artificial Intelligence Board is established to oversee the development and implementation of AI regulations across Member States.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7e28e08bfb7b1ae3208e2c91ea6f1e4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cb1edc11e8b8d0e952b15617a80f379&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d64a2a65aec35f8304efaaee30e0034d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21acb22d994b8f65ea3709a99eb85032</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_20.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_6.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_65.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858748</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Registration Obligation">
      <data key="d0">Registration Obligation</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">The Registration Obligation refers to the requirement for providers to document their assessments of AI systems before market deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d64a2a65aec35f8304efaaee30e0034d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857863</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Recital 53">
      <data key="d0">Recital 53</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Recital 53 is a note in the regulation that references the importance of documentation associated with the assessment of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Recital 53 provides context for regulations regarding high-risk AI systems and the necessary assessments related to them.&lt;SEP&gt;Recital 53 provides context or justification for specified provisions in the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d64a2a65aec35f8304efaaee30e0034d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cb1edc11e8b8d0e952b15617a80f379&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-739e3d9c7841d79a7701d630f8c7fa26</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857863</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Proper Human Review">
      <data key="d0">Proper Human Review</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Proper Human Review indicates that an AI system's outputs must be evaluated by humans to ensure accuracy and alignment with ethical standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d64a2a65aec35f8304efaaee30e0034d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857863</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Use Cases Listed in Annex III">
      <data key="d0">Use Cases Listed in Annex III</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Use Cases Listed in Annex III provide examples of AI system applications for which risk classifications are established.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d64a2a65aec35f8304efaaee30e0034d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857863</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Assessment Document">
      <data key="d0">Assessment Document</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">An Assessment Document is the required paperwork that a provider must compile detailing the risk assessment of an AI system before deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d64a2a65aec35f8304efaaee30e0034d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857863</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conclusive Evidence">
      <data key="d0">Conclusive Evidence</data>
      <data key="d1">Indicator</data>
      <data key="d2">Conclusive Evidence refers to the substantial proof needed to categorize an AI system as high-risk or not high-risk according to regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d64a2a65aec35f8304efaaee30e0034d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857863</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 96">
      <data key="d0">Article 96</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 96 outlines the requirements for practical implementation guidelines for AI systems within the legislative framework.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8cb1edc11e8b8d0e952b15617a80f379</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857863</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Health and Safety Regulations">
      <data key="d0">Health and Safety Regulations</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Health and safety regulations are maintained to protect individuals' fundamental rights and safety in the context of AI deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8cb1edc11e8b8d0e952b15617a80f379</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857863</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Health">
      <data key="d0">Health</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Health is a crucial dimension to consider during the AI system lifecycle, aiming to prevent adverse effects on human well-being.&lt;SEP&gt;Health refers to the well-being and fundamental rights of individuals that must be protected within AI regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Health refers to physical and mental well-being that could be affected by the deployment of AI systems, pertaining to safety measures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8cb1edc11e8b8d0e952b15617a80f379&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb0291da832d9defa94aaf2262ad3761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62e8b28075fdfa33850ed4b5a4d9a52f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_140.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_7.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863914</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Safety">
      <data key="d0">Safety</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Safety emphasizes the protection mechanisms needed to ensure that AI systems do not harm individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;Safety in AI entails preventing harm and ensuring secure operation in the development and deployment of AI technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Safety is a key dimension in evaluating the risks associated with AI development, ensuring that technology does not compromise health or rights.&lt;SEP&gt;Safety in the context of AI systems pertains to the measures taken to ensure that the systems do not cause harm to users or society.&lt;SEP&gt;Safety refers to the measures and standards ensured by Union law to prevent harm arising from AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8cb1edc11e8b8d0e952b15617a80f379&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb0291da832d9defa94aaf2262ad3761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62e8b28075fdfa33850ed4b5a4d9a52f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a65ec6b0fbd17afe47587686523a725&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-256a6003a5841f2764536c55f7086431</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_140.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_27.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_6.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_72.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_7.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863914</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Paragraph 3, second subparagraph">
      <data key="d0">Paragraph 3, second subparagraph</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Paragraph 3, second subparagraph outlines specific conditions that must be amended without decreasing overall protection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-739e3d9c7841d79a7701d630f8c7fa26</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857863</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Paragraph 6">
      <data key="d0">Paragraph 6</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Paragraph 6 relates to the process for adopting amendments and adjustments in regulatory conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-739e3d9c7841d79a7701d630f8c7fa26</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857863</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Paragraph 7">
      <data key="d0">Paragraph 7</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Paragraph 7 describes additional considerations for amendments to the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-739e3d9c7841d79a7701d630f8c7fa26</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857863</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Safety Protection">
      <data key="d0">Safety Protection</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Safety protection ensures that safety standards are upheld within the scope of the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-739e3d9c7841d79a7701d630f8c7fa26</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857863</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fundamental Rights Protection">
      <data key="d0">Fundamental Rights Protection</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Fundamental Rights Protection involves ensuring that AI systems do not violate fundamental rights during their deployment and operational phases.&lt;SEP&gt;Fundamental rights protection relates to safeguarding individual rights as stipulated in the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-739e3d9c7841d79a7701d630f8c7fa26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95424b9dff57302628c496570b4baff4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_139.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861382</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market Developments">
      <data key="d0">Market Developments</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Market developments refer to changes in market conditions that must be taken into account in the context of the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-739e3d9c7841d79a7701d630f8c7fa26</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857863</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technological Developments">
      <data key="d0">Technological Developments</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Technological developments refer to advancements that must be factored into regulatory amendments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-739e3d9c7841d79a7701d630f8c7fa26</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_6.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857863</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 6(2)">
      <data key="d0">Article 6(2)</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 6(2) contains provisions related to the deployment of high-risk AI systems, outlining assessments needed for approval.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77a0a99b47c288a96d7474c796efb766</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857866</data>
    </node>
    <node id="fundamental rights impact assessment">
      <data key="d0">fundamental rights impact assessment</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">A fundamental rights impact assessment evaluates how the use of a high-risk AI system may affect individuals' rights prior to deployment.&lt;SEP&gt;The fundamental rights impact assessment is a comprehensive evaluation of potential impacts on fundamental rights in the context of data processing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77a0a99b47c288a96d7474c796efb766&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f4621c3d73dca675e991da5d0c9317</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857866</data>
    </node>
    <node id="data protection impact assessment">
      <data key="d0">data protection impact assessment</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">A data protection impact assessment analyzes the implications of data processing activities on privacy rights.&lt;SEP&gt;A data protection impact assessment is conducted to evaluate the effects of data processing on individual privacy rights, ensuring compliance with data protection laws.&lt;SEP&gt;The data protection impact assessment is a formal process for evaluating risks to the data subjects' privacy and protecting their rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0efde0679d72a2d51e7acdaf09979bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a0a99b47c288a96d7474c796efb766&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f4621c3d73dca675e991da5d0c9317</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857866</data>
    </node>
    <node id="previously conducted fundamental rights impact assessments">
      <data key="d0">previously conducted fundamental rights impact assessments</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Previously conducted assessments may be used by deployers to verify compliance regarding high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77a0a99b47c288a96d7474c796efb766</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857866</data>
    </node>
    <node id="risks of harm">
      <data key="d0">risks of harm</data>
      <data key="d1">Risk</data>
      <data key="d2">Risks of harm refer to potential negative outcomes that may affect specific categories of natural persons or groups when using high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77a0a99b47c288a96d7474c796efb766</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857866</data>
    </node>
    <node id="human oversight measures">
      <data key="d0">human oversight measures</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">Human oversight measures involve strategies and protocols to ensure that AI systems operate within ethical and legal boundaries.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77a0a99b47c288a96d7474c796efb766</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857866</data>
    </node>
    <node id="internal governance and complaint mechanisms">
      <data key="d0">internal governance and complaint mechanisms</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">These mechanisms are put in place to address issues arising from the deployment of high-risk AI systems, facilitating accountability and redress.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-77a0a99b47c288a96d7474c796efb766</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857866</data>
    </node>
    <node id="impact assessments">
      <data key="d0">impact assessments</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Impact assessments evaluate the potential effects and risks associated with the deployment of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0efde0679d72a2d51e7acdaf09979bfc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857866</data>
    </node>
    <node id="fundamental rights impact assessments">
      <data key="d0">fundamental rights impact assessments</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Fundamental rights impact assessments are evaluations to ensure that AI systems comply with fundamental rights during their use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0efde0679d72a2d51e7acdaf09979bfc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857866</data>
    </node>
    <node id="impact assessment">
      <data key="d0">impact assessment</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">An impact assessment evaluates the potential consequences of deploying an AI system on users' rights and societal norms.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0efde0679d72a2d51e7acdaf09979bfc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857866</data>
    </node>
    <node id="notification">
      <data key="d0">notification</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Notification is the process of informing relevant authorities and the Commission about compliance measures or non-compliance issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Notification refers to the obligation of the deployer to inform market surveillance authorities about compliance with AI regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0efde0679d72a2d51e7acdaf09979bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345a8ba89ed0ea3325462384d5e16aaf</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861814</data>
    </node>
    <node id="template">
      <data key="d0">template</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">A template is a standardized form or document designed to streamline the process of conducting assessments and reporting compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0efde0679d72a2d51e7acdaf09979bfc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857866</data>
    </node>
    <node id="internal governance">
      <data key="d0">internal governance</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">Internal governance refers to the organizational processes and structures that manage the implementation and oversight of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0efde0679d72a2d51e7acdaf09979bfc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857866</data>
    </node>
    <node id="complaint mechanisms">
      <data key="d0">complaint mechanisms</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Complaint mechanisms are procedures established to address grievances related to the use or impact of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0efde0679d72a2d51e7acdaf09979bfc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857866</data>
    </node>
    <node id="questionnaire template">
      <data key="d0">questionnaire template</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">The questionnaire template is designed by the AI Office to assist deployers in the compliance process regarding data protection.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a3f4621c3d73dca675e991da5d0c9317</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857866</data>
    </node>
    <node id="obligations under this Article">
      <data key="d0">obligations under this Article</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">The obligations under this Article pertain to compliance requirements set forth in legal frameworks governing AI deployment and its assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a3f4621c3d73dca675e991da5d0c9317</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857866</data>
    </node>
    <node id="providers">
      <data key="d0">providers</data>
      <data key="d1">AISubject</data>
      <data key="d2">Providers are entities responsible for supplying high-risk AI systems, requiring monitoring for risk management and incident reporting.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-54948128ea5a4b84a219d7dbaa346a50</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_155.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857870</data>
    </node>
    <node id="post-market monitoring system">
      <data key="d0">post-market monitoring system</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">A post-market monitoring system is essential for tracking the performance and risks of AI systems after they have been deployed.&lt;SEP&gt;The post-market monitoring system is designed to gather data about risks associated with high-risk AI systems after they are deployed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-54948128ea5a4b84a219d7dbaa346a50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ca7c773df7242c37f506b8ad3db475b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_155.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_9.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863746</data>
    </node>
    <node id="law enforcement authorities">
      <data key="d0">law enforcement authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">Law enforcement authorities are identified as deployers of AI systems and are excluded from certain data monitoring to protect sensitive operational data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-54948128ea5a4b84a219d7dbaa346a50</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_155.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857870</data>
    </node>
    <node id="serious incidents">
      <data key="d0">serious incidents</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Serious incidents refer to grave outcomes resulting from the malfunctioning of AI systems, leading to severe health issues or infrastructural disruptions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-54948128ea5a4b84a219d7dbaa346a50</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_155.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857870</data>
    </node>
    <node id="analysis of the interaction">
      <data key="d0">analysis of the interaction</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">The analysis of interaction refers to assessing how AI systems behave when interacting with other systems and software, important for risk evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-54948128ea5a4b84a219d7dbaa346a50</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_155.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857870</data>
    </node>
    <node id="post-market monitoring">
      <data key="d0">post-market monitoring</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">A system established to continuously gather and assess data regarding the risks posed by high-risk AI systems after they are deployed.&lt;SEP&gt;Post-market monitoring refers to the system employed by providers to assess and improve the performance and safety of AI systems after deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-54948128ea5a4b84a219d7dbaa346a50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ca7c773df7242c37f506b8ad3db475b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_155.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_9.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863746</data>
    </node>
    <node id="risk management">
      <data key="d0">risk management</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Risk management is the process through which providers assess, monitor, and mitigate risks associated with the deployment of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-54948128ea5a4b84a219d7dbaa346a50</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_155.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857870</data>
    </node>
    <node id="serious incidents reporting">
      <data key="d0">serious incidents reporting</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Serious incidents reporting is a regulatory requirement for providers to inform authorities about significant adverse events related to AI systems operation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-54948128ea5a4b84a219d7dbaa346a50</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_155.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857870</data>
    </node>
    <node id="corrective action">
      <data key="d0">corrective action</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Corrective action involves the steps taken to remedy any detected issues with high-risk AI systems to prevent negative outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-54948128ea5a4b84a219d7dbaa346a50</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_155.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857870</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union law obligations">
      <data key="d0">Union law obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Union law obligations refer to the legal requirements imposed by the European Union to protect fundamental rights and safety regarding AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-54948128ea5a4b84a219d7dbaa346a50</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_155.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857870</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI providers">
      <data key="d0">AI providers</data>
      <data key="d1">AIProvider</data>
      <data key="d2">AI providers are entities responsible for the development and operational management of AI systems, especially high-risk variants that require oversight.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-54948128ea5a4b84a219d7dbaa346a50</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_155.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857870</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Model">
      <data key="d0">Model</data>
      <data key="d1">AIModel</data>
      <data key="d2">A model is a mathematical representation trained with data to perform various tasks, assessed by its parameter count and generality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e93dbcfb179aa98bf5518ab208d544fc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_98.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Parameters">
      <data key="d0">Parameters</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Parameters are the quantifiable inputs that define the model's behavior and performance, influencing its generality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e93dbcfb179aa98bf5518ab208d544fc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_98.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Large Amount of Data">
      <data key="d0">Large Amount of Data</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">A large amount of data refers to the substantial dataset used for training the model, crucial for achieving generality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e93dbcfb179aa98bf5518ab208d544fc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_98.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Self-Supervision at Scale">
      <data key="d0">Self-Supervision at Scale</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Self-supervision at scale is an advanced training technique that allows models to learn from data without extensive labeled examples, enhancing generality and performance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e93dbcfb179aa98bf5518ab208d544fc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_98.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Model Generality">
      <data key="d0">Model Generality</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Model generality refers to the ability of a model to perform well across a wide range of tasks, influenced by its design and training parameters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e93dbcfb179aa98bf5518ab208d544fc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_98.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Parameters Count">
      <data key="d0">Parameters Count</data>
      <data key="d1">Metric</data>
      <data key="d2">Parameters count is a specific measurement indicating the number of parameters a model includes, which is a determinant of its capability and generality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e93dbcfb179aa98bf5518ab208d544fc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_98.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857872</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Distinctive Tasks">
      <data key="d0">Distinctive Tasks</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Distinctive tasks are specific functions or activities that a model is capable of performing, highlighting its versatility and application scope.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e93dbcfb179aa98bf5518ab208d544fc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_98.json</data>
