    <node id="Codes of Conduct">
      <data key="d0">Codes of Conduct</data>
      <data key="d1">CodeOfConduct</data>
      <data key="d2">Codes of Conduct are voluntary guidelines established to enhance AI literacy and promote ethical standards in the use of AI systems. These guidelines are designed to encourage the voluntary adherence to ethical requirements in the deployment of AI technologies. They are typically developed by AI system providers or stakeholders with the intention of ensuring responsible and ethical practices in the development and implementation of AI systems. Codes of Conduct serve as frameworks that guide the ethical development and use of AI technologies, facilitating compliance with regulatory standards, especially within AI sandboxes. Overall, these codes aim to foster ethical practices among AI providers to encourage responsible and conscientious deployment of their systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-849f8f0403e6b12fa8a9c24b84c094c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c14e1756e1d8d71ac3ba07125f122da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aca56f82b70892874784bcec5c2bb2c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40f3761e589fb7702938fd4fbbecfdcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-064e3e5273a81cd8d9a47da9a3f51240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21acb22d994b8f65ea3709a99eb85032</data>
