    <node id="Feedback Loops">
      <data key="d0">Feedback Loops</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">Feedback loops are mechanisms where data outputs influence future inputs and operations, impacting performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Feedback loops refer to the cycles in AI systems where outputs influence future inputs, potentially leading to biases and discrimination.&lt;SEP&gt;Feedback loops are processes that allow systems to adjust based on operational results and inputs.&lt;SEP&gt;Feedback loops involve outputs from AI systems being used as inputs for future operations, which can potentially introduce biases if not properly managed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d7eb8204c84c6a7310e75effed716fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed5ccbca443324af303d8bca3aa31a38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-445327adc051facf545b6358f6f01466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-671e76af4a78aebc96c988f0504bfa99</data>
