    <node id="Biases">
      <data key="d0">Biases</data>
      <data key="d1">Risk</data>
      <data key="d2">Biases in data sets can lead to discrimination, particularly affecting vulnerable groups, and influence the results of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d7eb8204c84c6a7310e75effed716fcf</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_67.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857892</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Vulnerable Groups">
      <data key="d0">Vulnerable Groups</data>
      <data key="d1">AISubject</data>
      <data key="d2">Vulnerable Groups are individuals who may face heightened risks or ethical considerations in the context of AI testing.&lt;SEP&gt;Vulnerable Groups are subjects of testing identified as being at risk due to age or disability and require special protection during AI testing procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Vulnerable groups encompass various categories of individuals who are at a heightened risk of experiencing adverse outcomes due to the use of AI systems. This includes individuals with special needs, such as the elderly or those with disabilities, who require tailored notifications for effective interaction with AI technologies. Additionally, vulnerable groups comprise persons from racial or ethnic minorities who might be disproportionately affected by biased AI systems. They also refer to specific populations that necessitate extra protections and safeguards during the testing and implementation of AI technologies. This includes demographics that are often disadvantaged or discriminated against in employment contexts, such as women, disabled individuals, and ethnic minorities. Overall, vulnerable groups demand specific attention and considerations in the evaluation and deployment of AI systems to ensure equitable and just outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Vulnerable Groups refer to specific populations, such as individuals under the age of 18, that may be adversely affected by high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Vulnerable groups refer to specific populations such as the elderly, disabled, or economically disadvantaged who are at risk of exploitation, particularly through AI practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b3ba2302e956849a6be7455071577d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa9e2916955e882c73231ed69851f6ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7eb8204c84c6a7310e75effed716fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35a30c75209c0fbb0ca1bb4afe44c77d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de3f18a6d766d2baa57ae891b9da7741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fa05c618cc92c392c091a0299038b25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb43ec5a01dc502046ab6ffbe3a25504&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb2802f1b508b813d06e58ae27a1f77</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_29.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_141.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_132.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_67.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_93.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_57.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_60.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_9.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863949</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Sets">
      <data key="d0">Data Sets</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Data sets are collections of data used for training, validating, and testing AI models, which must be protected against unauthorized access and leaks.&lt;SEP&gt;Data sets must be complete and accurate to ensure effective AI system performance and avoid perpetuating biases.&lt;SEP&gt;Data sets refer to collections of data that should be relevant, sufficiently representative, and error-free, intended for training, validation, and testing AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d7eb8204c84c6a7310e75effed716fcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0639a0bd62e8b0bbe41bc1bee4a3098&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-447d51c65bac6d28fd62c36c3e70e08b</data>
