      <data key="d5">1750863659</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cyber Resilience of an AI System">
      <data key="d0">Cyber Resilience of an AI System</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Cyber resilience refers to the ability of an AI system to withstand and recover from cyber threats, important for maintaining its integrity and performance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6370e960da03a6bbdee69f64993cdae6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_77.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857905</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI-Specific Vulnerabilities">
      <data key="d0">AI-Specific Vulnerabilities</data>
      <data key="d1">Vulnerability</data>
      <data key="d2">AI-specific vulnerabilities include risks like data poisoning and adversarial attacks that can compromise the functioning of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6370e960da03a6bbdee69f64993cdae6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_77.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857905</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Essential Cybersecurity Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Essential Cybersecurity Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Essential cybersecurity requirements are standards that products with digital elements must meet under this Regulation to ensure safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Essential cybersecurity requirements are the minimum standards that high-risk AI systems must meet to ensure safety and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6370e960da03a6bbdee69f64993cdae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60a12c037b4dee54159c11f348ff3f11</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_78.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_77.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861074</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Unauthorized Third Parties">
      <data key="d0">Unauthorized Third Parties</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Unauthorized third parties are individuals or groups that seek to exploit vulnerabilities in AI systems for malicious intent.&lt;SEP&gt;Unauthorized third parties refer to individuals or entities that attempt to exploit vulnerabilities in high-risk AI systems, impacting their operation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6370e960da03a6bbdee69f64993cdae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed5ccbca443324af303d8bca3aa31a38</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_15.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_77.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861695</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Digital Elements">
      <data key="d0">Digital Elements</data>
      <data key="d1">Domain</data>
      <data key="d2">Digital elements are components of digital products, including software and hardware that may be associated with high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6370e960da03a6bbdee69f64993cdae6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_77.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857905</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Compliance with Regulation">
      <data key="d0">Compliance with Regulation</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Compliance with regulation describes the necessary changes high-risk AI systems must undergo to meet established cybersecurity standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6370e960da03a6bbdee69f64993cdae6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_77.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857905</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Digital Single Market">
      <data key="d0">Digital Single Market</data>
      <data key="d1">Domain</data>
      <data key="d2">The Digital Single Market refers to an EU initiative aimed at ensuring the free movement of goods and services, and fostering online access and digital trade.&lt;SEP&gt;The Digital Single Market refers to an integrated digital environment that aims to strengthen the functioning of the market across the Union.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-feb00b9eef4af47cdd3264cd99d6b2e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6a5cc59273abbe42c743808026477c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_104.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_148.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858853</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EuroHPC Joint Undertaking">
      <data key="d0">EuroHPC Joint Undertaking</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">The EuroHPC Joint Undertaking focuses on high-performance computing resources, relevant to AI capabilities at the Union level.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e6a5cc59273abbe42c743808026477c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_148.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857907</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Digital Europe Programme">
      <data key="d0">Digital Europe Programme</data>
      <data key="d1">AIProvider</data>
      <data key="d2">The Digital Europe Programme includes AI testing and experimentation facilities to support development and innovation in AI.&lt;SEP&gt;The Digital Europe Programme is an EU funding initiative aimed at enhancing digital capabilities across member states.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-86aff1d72a3f6226d0b5db29d9910a59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6a5cc59273abbe42c743808026477c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_148.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_144.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862852</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Expertise and Capabilities">
      <data key="d0">Union Expertise and Capabilities</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Union Expertise and Capabilities refer to the collective knowledge and skills developed to ensure effective AI regulation and implementation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e6a5cc59273abbe42c743808026477c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_148.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857907</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Artificial Intelligence Office">
      <data key="d0">European Artificial Intelligence Office</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Artificial Intelligence Office is an entity established to oversee the regulation and development of artificial intelligence within Europe.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Artificial Intelligence Office is an organization responsible for overseeing AI compliance and reducing administrative burdens for AI deployers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bb2945aab237268f7fcb2f55fd258be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f89a194b461fcebd5ec31a53d66c4dde</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_148.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_96.json</data>
