      <data key="d3">chunk-eb43ec5a01dc502046ab6ffbe3a25504</data>
      <data key="d2">Transparency obligations include providing information in accessible formats for individuals with disabilities.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_132.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857932</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Experts of the Scientific Panel">
      <data key="d0">Experts of the Scientific Panel</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeveloper</data>
      <data key="d2">Experts of the scientific panel are specialists consulted by Member States to provide advice and support for implementing the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5ea6a588c10ad2fe493ec8cc1913f72d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_69.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857934</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Support Activities">
      <data key="d0">Support Activities</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Support activities include the various services and functions provided by Union AI testing support and experts to assist Member States.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5ea6a588c10ad2fe493ec8cc1913f72d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_69.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857934</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fees for Advice and Support">
      <data key="d0">Fees for Advice and Support</data>
      <data key="d1">Metric</data>
      <data key="d2">Fees for advice and support are financial charges incurred by Member States for utilizing expert consultation as per the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5ea6a588c10ad2fe493ec8cc1913f72d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_69.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857934</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Objectives of Implementation">
      <data key="d0">Objectives of Implementation</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Objectives of implementation are targets set to ensure the effective and efficient application of the Regulation, taking into account cost-effectiveness and access to expertise.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5ea6a588c10ad2fe493ec8cc1913f72d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_69.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857934</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union AI Testing Support">
      <data key="d0">Union AI Testing Support</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Union AI testing support comprises activities designed to assist Member States in their enforcement tasks related to AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5ea6a588c10ad2fe493ec8cc1913f72d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_69.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857934</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Combination of Support Activities">
      <data key="d0">Combination of Support Activities</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">The combination of support activities refers to the coordinated efforts of both Union AI testing support and scientific panel experts to provide comprehensive assistance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5ea6a588c10ad2fe493ec8cc1913f72d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_69.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857934</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Access to Experts">
      <data key="d0">Access to Experts</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Access to experts denotes the availability and means by which Member States can engage with the scientific panel for assistance under the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5ea6a588c10ad2fe493ec8cc1913f72d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_69.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857934</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Identification Number">
      <data key="d0">Identification Number</data>
      <data key="d1">Metric</data>
      <data key="d2">An identification number is a unique code assigned to each notified body for identification purposes under regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;The identification number is a unique code assigned to the notified body that must be affixed to indicate its role in the conformity assessment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-29241e99bddf5af77eca441d2d8dbc1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-785d0dafc3a62a1aee53267d076b7533</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_48.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_35.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858634</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Machine-Readable Code">
      <data key="d0">Machine-Readable Code</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">A machine-readable code is a digital representation or pattern that can be scanned or recognized by machines, often used to access digital content like CE marking information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-29241e99bddf5af77eca441d2d8dbc1b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_48.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857936</data>
    </node>
    <node id="law">
      <data key="d0">law</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Law represents legal frameworks that AI systems must adhere to, particularly concerning their operation and impact.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-75ffbd2452fab424919d626f5688692d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_48.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857936</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union and National Law">
      <data key="d0">Union and National Law</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Union and national law established effective remedies for individuals whose rights and freedoms are impacted by AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bb040a8b4e6e3fa6f26776f560b6591c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_170.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857938</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Natural and Legal Persons">
      <data key="d0">Natural and Legal Persons</data>
      <data key="d1">AISubject</data>
      <data key="d2">Natural and legal persons are individuals and organizations who may have their rights affected by the use of AI systems and can seek remedies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bb040a8b4e6e3fa6f26776f560b6591c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_170.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857938</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Effective Remedies">
      <data key="d0">Effective Remedies</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Effective remedies are legal provisions that provide recourse to natural and legal persons adversely affected by the use of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bb040a8b4e6e3fa6f26776f560b6591c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_170.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857950</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Legal Persons">
      <data key="d0">Legal Persons</data>
      <data key="d1">AISubject</data>
      <data key="d2">Legal persons are entities such as corporations whose rights and freedoms may also be impacted by AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bb040a8b4e6e3fa6f26776f560b6591c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_170.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750857950</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Complaint">
      <data key="d0">Complaint</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">A complaint is a formal assertion made by a natural or legal person indicating an infringement of rights due to the use of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A complaint is a formal expression of dissatisfaction alleging an infringement of regulations by providers of AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18d33fd192f06f727ac6bb21becbaa57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb040a8b4e6e3fa6f26776f560b6591c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_170.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_89.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862426</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Relevant Market Surveillance Authority">
      <data key="d0">Relevant Market Surveillance Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">Authorities that oversee and ensure compliance with regulations regarding the deployment of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The relevant market surveillance authority is the entity responsible for addressing complaints related to AI system regulations and monitoring compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bb040a8b4e6e3fa6f26776f560b6591c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a1d78baf29c07c65edc311f0ca04126</data>
