      <data key="d5">1750858038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human Oversight Arrangements">
      <data key="d0">Human Oversight Arrangements</data>
      <data key="d1">RiskControl</data>
      <data key="d2">Governance arrangements that include human oversight to mitigate risks associated with the deployment of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3a1d78baf29c07c65edc311f0ca04126</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_96.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Complaint Handling and Redress Procedures">
      <data key="d0">Complaint Handling and Redress Procedures</data>
      <data key="d1">RiskControl</data>
      <data key="d2">Complaint handling and redress procedures provide mechanisms for affected individuals to lodge complaints and seek remedies following AI-related grievances.&lt;SEP&gt;Procedures established to address grievances that may arise from the deployment of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ee04f6104a24650416810ede28f3790b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a1d78baf29c07c65edc311f0ca04126</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_96.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Relevant Instructions for Use">
      <data key="d0">Relevant Instructions for Use</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Documentation that contains the information provided by the provider of high-risk AI systems for their proper use, which informs impact assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3a1d78baf29c07c65edc311f0ca04126</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_96.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Materialisation of Risks">
      <data key="d0">Materialisation of Risks</data>
      <data key="d1">RiskConcept</data>
      <data key="d2">The occurrence of identified risks that may negatively affect fundamental rights during the deployment of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3a1d78baf29c07c65edc311f0ca04126</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_96.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Impact Assessment">
      <data key="d0">Impact Assessment</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Impact assessment evaluates the potential negative consequences of AI systems on various stakeholders, particularly on vulnerable groups.&lt;SEP&gt;Impact assessment involves evaluating risks and their potential effects on fundamental rights of affected groups.&lt;SEP&gt;Impact assessments evaluate the effects of AI systems on society and the environment, guiding regulatory decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Impact assessments are evaluations conducted to determine the effects of restricting or withdrawing designations on health and safety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ee04f6104a24650416810ede28f3790b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8caee37338a6383c30fe06ea2b3e4761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83f37d4143e19486af167d7acee5bee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-064e3e5273a81cd8d9a47da9a3f51240</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_95.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_174.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_96.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863789</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Relevant Stakeholders">
      <data key="d0">Relevant Stakeholders</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Relevant stakeholders include affected groups, independent experts, and civil society organizations involved in the assessment process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ee04f6104a24650416810ede28f3790b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_96.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Governance Arrangements">
      <data key="d0">Governance Arrangements</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Governance arrangements may include measures such as human oversight and complaint handling procedures to mitigate identified risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ee04f6104a24650416810ede28f3790b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_96.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Groups">
      <data key="d0">Groups</data>
      <data key="d1">AISubject</data>
      <data key="d2">Groups consist of collections of individuals who may also be affected by the impacts of high-risk AI systems, and their collective rights should be assessed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ee04f6104a24650416810ede28f3790b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_96.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risks of Harm">
      <data key="d0">Risks of Harm</data>
      <data key="d1">RiskConcept</data>
      <data key="d2">Potential adverse effects associated with the utilization of AI systems in certain applications, particularly in relation to health and safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Risks of harm refer to potential negative impacts on the fundamental rights of affected persons or groups due to AI system deployment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ee04f6104a24650416810ede28f3790b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4672fd3df7077626af67d20e46d3fcb4</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_53.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_96.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862736</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Proper Assessment of Impact">
      <data key="d0">Proper Assessment of Impact</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Proper assessment of impact involves a thorough evaluation of how AI system deployments may affect rights and welfare of the subjects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ee04f6104a24650416810ede28f3790b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_96.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Artificial Intelligence Office (AI Office)">
      <data key="d0">European Artificial Intelligence Office (AI Office)</data>
      <data key="d1">AIProvider</data>
      <data key="d2">The European AI Office is responsible for developing guidelines, templates, and resources to support compliance with AI deployment standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ee04f6104a24650416810ede28f3790b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_96.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Questionnaire Template">
      <data key="d0">Questionnaire Template</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">The questionnaire template is a tool developed by the AI Office to facilitate compliance for AI deployers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f89a194b461fcebd5ec31a53d66c4dde</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_96.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858038</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risks">
      <data key="d0">Risks</data>
      <data key="d1">Risk</data>
      <data key="d2">Risks associated with AI are potential threats that can harm public interests and fundamental rights.&lt;SEP&gt;Risks refer to potential negative outcomes associated with deploying artificial intelligence systems, necessitating assessment and management.&lt;SEP&gt;Risks refer to the potential negative consequences and uncertainties associated with the deployment of AI models at the Union level.&lt;SEP&gt;Risks refer to the potential negative consequences identified during the development and testing of AI systems in regulatory sandboxes.&lt;SEP&gt;Risks encompass potential threats associated with the deployment of AI, including data breaches and ethical violations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7114fa80a4a18326b68b2fd61f65c047&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95424b9dff57302628c496570b4baff4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c553e9efc5dc64a6a2019d8e611bb1c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a0c1908573a7d6a832a6b35befbd7ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f89a194b461fcebd5ec31a53d66c4dde</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_5.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_104.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_163.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_139.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_96.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863887</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Administrative Burden">
      <data key="d0">Administrative Burden</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Administrative Burden refers to the time, effort, and resources that businesses must expend to comply with regulations, which can hinder innovation for smaller entities.&lt;SEP&gt;Administrative burden refers to the challenges and workload faced by AI deployers due to complex compliance requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ad25bfaa86145b8556e5d82696b8bab4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f89a194b461fcebd5ec31a53d66c4dde</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_146.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_96.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863319</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Detailed Rules of National Law">
      <data key="d0">Detailed Rules of National Law</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">The detailed rules of national law consist of specific regulations that a Member State may establish to govern the authorized use of AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67ecee9ae9852fb675f5c9c9cb2f2de6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_37.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858121</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Territory of a Member State">
      <data key="d0">Territory of a Member State</data>
      <data key="d1">LocalityOfUse</data>
      <data key="d2">The Territory of a Member State refers to the defined geographical area where the regulation applies and dictates the conditions under which AI can be authorized.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67ecee9ae9852fb675f5c9c9cb2f2de6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_37.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858121</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Possibility to Authorise Such Use">
      <data key="d0">Possibility to Authorise Such Use</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">The Possibility to Authorise Such Use indicates the conditions under which a Member State can allow AI deployment as per its national laws.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67ecee9ae9852fb675f5c9c9cb2f2de6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_37.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858121</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Objectives Capable of Justifying Authorised Use">
      <data key="d0">Objectives Capable of Justifying Authorised Use</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Objectives Capable of Justifying Authorised Use are specific goals set within the regulation that define what constitutes acceptable AI implementations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-67ecee9ae9852fb675f5c9c9cb2f2de6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_37.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858121</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Market">
      <data key="d0">Union Market</data>
      <data key="d1">Domain</data>
      <data key="d2">The Union Market is the collective marketplace within the European Union where artificial intelligence (AI) systems and products are made available for commercial activities. This market is governed by Union laws that regulate the availability and use of AI technologies. Within the Union Market, providers must ensure that their offerings comply with applicable regulations, particularly in regard to safety and operational requirements. Specifically, the marketplace encompasses provisions for high-risk AI systems, which must adhere to mandatory compliance requirements before being placed into service or widely used. Additionally, general-purpose AI models must meet specific regulatory standards prior to their deployment in this economic area. Overall, the Union Market serves as a regulated environment designed to promote safe and compliant AI technologies across the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;The Union market refers to the collective market of European Union member states where high-risk AI systems are deployed and subject to regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ca3e6894a9009f1db207c0ec639d8a39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0dc307b8b7cb1f0e39aa9b4b1839c408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1ae06c8c76fc5976313d75e4ffabdfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad9c740a10a5c1577e578a593bd61fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb2802f1b508b813d06e58ae27a1f77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2440fb0070f3198e96bd1ad753ae3e0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-873c3732f26f3ace86c77cfec67991ee</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_106.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_82.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863499</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2017/745">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2017/745</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2017/745 establishes safety requirements for medical devices that include AI systems as components.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2017/745 pertains to medical devices and establishes criteria for assessing the risk levels of these products, including AI systems used within them.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2017/745 pertains to medical devices and sets out the requirements for placing such devices in the market.&lt;SEP&gt;This regulation establishes requirements for certain devices, including those in the context of high-risk AI systems classified as medical devices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b8efd21db4fc63a879493cbb376ae904&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3e6894a9009f1db207c0ec639d8a39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0779dfb4a5c0f82f05a67985fe0224a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_51.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_84.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863507</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2017/746">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2017/746</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2017/746 deals with in vitro diagnostic medical devices and outlines mandatory compliance requirements for these products.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2017/746 governs in vitro diagnostic medical devices and includes provisions regarding the classification and assessment of risk for medical products incorporating AI.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation (EU) 2017/746 sets out requirements for in vitro diagnostic devices, which may include AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b8efd21db4fc63a879493cbb376ae904&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3e6894a9009f1db207c0ec639d8a39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0779dfb4a5c0f82f05a67985fe0224a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_51.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_73.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863507</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 2006/42/EC">
      <data key="d0">Directive 2006/42/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 2006/42/EC is a regulatory framework established by the European Parliament concerning machinery safety and standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Directive 2006/42/EC relates to machinery and establishes safety requirements to ensure health and safety during the use of machinery in the Union.&lt;SEP&gt;This directive addresses machinery regulations to enhance safety and performance standards in the EU market as of May 2006.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ca3e6894a9009f1db207c0ec639d8a39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a48f68b8943ab2f8e6bdbb9ccf3e17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04f1483cdf6b84729e33ebc4a611375b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_46.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858130</data>
    </node>
    <node id="International Trade">
      <data key="d0">International Trade</data>
      <data key="d1">AreaOfImpact</data>
      <data key="d2">International trade may be impacted by the limitations placed on high-risk AI systems to ensure compliance with union regulations and the protection of public interests.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ca3e6894a9009f1db207c0ec639d8a39</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_46.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858130</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Flexibility in Compliance">
      <data key="d0">Flexibility in Compliance</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Flexibility in compliance refers to the operational decisions that providers of high-risk AI systems can make to meet regulatory requirements effectively.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ca3e6894a9009f1db207c0ec639d8a39</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_46.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858130</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Significant Harmful Impact">
      <data key="d0">Significant Harmful Impact</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Significant harmful impact is a measure used to assess the potential risks associated with the deployment of high-risk AI systems on individuals' health and rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ca3e6894a9009f1db207c0ec639d8a39</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_46.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858130</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Parliament and Council Regulation (EU) 2017/745">
      <data key="d0">European Parliament and Council Regulation (EU) 2017/745</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">This regulation pertains to medical devices, ensuring compliance with applicable European legislation as of April 2017.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-04f1483cdf6b84729e33ebc4a611375b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_46.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858130</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Parliament and Council Regulation (EU) 2017/746">
      <data key="d0">European Parliament and Council Regulation (EU) 2017/746</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">This regulation focuses on in vitro diagnostic medical devices and outlines compliance requirements post-April 2017.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-04f1483cdf6b84729e33ebc4a611375b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_46.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858130</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Harmful Impact">
      <data key="d0">Harmful Impact</data>
      <data key="d1">Impact</data>
      <data key="d2">Harmful impact refers to the negative effects that high-risk AI systems can have on health, safety, and fundamental rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-04f1483cdf6b84729e33ebc4a611375b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_46.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858130</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Regulation (EU) 2017/745">
      <data key="d0">European Regulation (EU) 2017/745</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">This regulation outlines the compliance requirements for medical devices and impacts AI systems integrated in healthcare applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-04f1483cdf6b84729e33ebc4a611375b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_46.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858130</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Regulation (EU) 2017/746">
      <data key="d0">European Regulation (EU) 2017/746</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation focused on in vitro diagnostic medical devices, ensuring compliance for AI systems employed in diagnostic contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-04f1483cdf6b84729e33ebc4a611375b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_46.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858130</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Directive 95/16/EC">
      <data key="d0">Directive 95/16/EC</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive 95/16/EC is an earlier regulation concerning machinery that was amended by Directive 2006/42/EC.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3a48f68b8943ab2f8e6bdbb9ccf3e17d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_46.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858132</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OJ L 157">
      <data key="d0">OJ L 157</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">OJ L 157 is the official journal where legislation, including Directive 2006/42/EC and its revisions, is published.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3a48f68b8943ab2f8e6bdbb9ccf3e17d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_46.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858132</data>
    </node>
    <node id="May 17, 2006">
      <data key="d0">May 17, 2006</data>
      <data key="d1">Date</data>
      <data key="d2">May 17, 2006 is the date when Directive 2006/42/EC was issued by the European Parliament.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3a48f68b8943ab2f8e6bdbb9ccf3e17d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_46.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858132</data>
    </node>
    <node id="distributor">
      <data key="d0">distributor</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">A distributor is a party that supplies AI systems to the market, and under certain conditions, can be considered a provider of high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_84.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858141</data>
    </node>
    <node id="importer">
      <data key="d0">importer</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">An importer is a party that brings AI systems into a market, possibly assuming obligations associated with high-risk AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_84.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858141</data>
    </node>
    <node id="third-party">
      <data key="d0">third-party</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">A third-party can be involved in the distribution or modification of an AI system, thereby potentially being considered a provider of a high-risk system under certain conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_84.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858141</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Third-Party">
      <data key="d0">Third-Party</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">A third-party can be involved in the distribution or modification of AI systems and could be classified as a provider of high-risk AI systems under specific conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_84.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858143</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Modification">
      <data key="d0">Modification</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Modification is the process by which users can change software and data to suit their needs, encouraged by open-source licensing.&lt;SEP&gt;Modification refers to any substantial changes made to an AI system, which can impact its compliance and classification as a high-risk system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-769497b509433ed0e4746ff50bbdec69</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_102.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_84.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858300</data>
    </node>
    <node id="General-Purpose AI System">
      <data key="d0">General-Purpose AI System</data>
      <data key="d1">AIModel</data>
      <data key="d2">A general-purpose AI system is an AI model that is not initially classified as high-risk but can become high-risk through changes in its intended purpose.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6a8bd64d122f5a09e9e3859bf77c6931</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_84.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858143</data>
    </node>
    <node id="medical devices">
      <data key="d0">medical devices</data>
      <data key="d1">Domain</data>
      <data key="d2">Medical devices are defined and regulated items that are intended for medical use and are applicable within the scope of AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cc1203d6797827fbb6dbb7dc7c8d7d26</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_84.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858143</data>
    </node>
    <node id="changes">
      <data key="d0">changes</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Changes refer to actions or modifications in the context of AI systems that may affect compliance and operational requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cc1203d6797827fbb6dbb7dc7c8d7d26</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_84.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858143</data>
    </node>
    <node id="device">
      <data key="d0">device</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">Device is a component of AI systems which must adhere to compliance requirements as per regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cc1203d6797827fbb6dbb7dc7c8d7d26</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_84.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858143</data>
    </node>
    <node id="compliance">
      <data key="d0">compliance</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Compliance measures the adherence of AI systems and devices to established regulations and standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cc1203d6797827fbb6dbb7dc7c8d7d26</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_84.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858143</data>
    </node>
    <node id="applicable requirements">
      <data key="d0">applicable requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Applicable requirements are the legal and operational standards that AI systems and devices must meet to ensure safety and efficacy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cc1203d6797827fbb6dbb7dc7c8d7d26</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_84.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858143</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Public Authorities">
      <data key="d0">National Public Authorities</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">National bodies that the market surveillance authority cooperates with for evaluating AI systems to maintain public safety.&lt;SEP&gt;National public authorities are bodies that supervise the application of Union law and ensure compliance with fundamental rights.&lt;SEP&gt;National public authorities are bodies tasked with implementing public policies and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;National public authorities or bodies that supervise or enforce compliance with Union law regarding high-risk AI systems, ensuring the protection of fundamental rights.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9cb2802f1b508b813d06e58ae27a1f77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e853663a3f2d06a9cfea8582e10f089&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2315cd7abb88dee440f081de5430a32f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8512760339eb776d946a91a28089b34</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_77.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_157.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863550</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Prohibited Systems">
      <data key="d0">Prohibited Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">Risk</data>
      <data key="d2">Prohibited systems are AI technologies that may not be placed on the market or used due to their violation of established regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2315cd7abb88dee440f081de5430a32f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_157.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Enforcement Procedure">
      <data key="d0">Enforcement Procedure</data>
      <data key="d1">Risk</data>
      <data key="d2">The enforcement procedure is established to ensure compliance and appropriate actions against AI systems that present risks in accordance with the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2315cd7abb88dee440f081de5430a32f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_157.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conformity Assessment Activities">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Assessment Activities</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Conformity Assessment Activities refer to a series of tasks and processes carried out by notified bodies to evaluate the compliance of artificial intelligence (AI) systems with relevant regulations, standards, and requirements. These activities are particularly focused on high-risk AI systems, ensuring that they meet established compliance standards set by regulatory authorities. The primary objective of these conformity assessment activities is to thoroughly assess whether AI systems adhere to the necessary regulatory frameworks and standards, thus guaranteeing their safety and reliability in practical applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Conformity assessment activities include a set of procedures to determine whether a product meets the required standards and regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be2e0f993ca9c4e593e5fcbdd8fc03fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a5e7031602556ef7d57e2811f58992&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff611ee371ea780574e9c16859c31f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f79a9fca1518856b24fdcb7e59f040&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28717558f1bb8bd2fd8b9542f8e2a99c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f94df6da4de89cee24b1bd8f504c377</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_30.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_29.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_45.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863782</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Independence">
      <data key="d0">Independence</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Independence is a critical quality measurement for notified bodies to ensure that assessments are conducted objectively and without bias.&lt;SEP&gt;Independence is a critical quality measurement for notified bodies, ensuring their judgments are free from influence or conflict of interest during assessments.&lt;SEP&gt;Independence refers to the quality expectation that national competent authorities should operate without external influences in their decision-making.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fe05ef9eea0acc63f05d5b9d6a147298&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2e0f993ca9c4e593e5fcbdd8fc03fe</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_154.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Impartiality">
      <data key="d0">Impartiality</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Impartiality is a fundamental principle for notified bodies, ensuring that assessment outcomes are fair and equitable.&lt;SEP&gt;Impartiality measures an unbiased approach in the conformity assessment activities, ensuring fairness and neutrality in evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2e0f993ca9c4e593e5fcbdd8fc03fe</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858290</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Liability Insurance">
      <data key="d0">Liability Insurance</data>
      <data key="d1">LegalBasis</data>
      <data key="d2">Liability Insurance is essential for notified bodies to cover potential legal responsibilities arising from their assessment activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Liability insurance is required for notified bodies to cover their conformity assessment activities unless liability is assumed by the Member State.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be2e0f993ca9c4e593e5fcbdd8fc03fe</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858290</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Legal Personality">
      <data key="d0">Legal Personality</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Legal Personality indicates that a notified body has the legal status necessary to perform functions defined under national law.&lt;SEP&gt;Legal Personality refers to the capacity of an entity to have legal rights and obligations, which the provider lacks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-075ecb5835777e6044264a23ca0cb20a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_92.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863863</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Organisational Structure">
      <data key="d0">Organisational Structure</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">The Organisational Structure refers to the internal arrangement of roles and responsibilities within a notified body to ensure effective operation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Quality Management">
      <data key="d0">Quality Management</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Quality Management involves the processes and systems that a notified body must implement to ensure high standards in its assessment activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cybersecurity Requirements">
      <data key="d0">Cybersecurity Requirements</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Cybersecurity Requirements define the necessary measures that a notified body must adopt to protect sensitive information during assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Reporting Lines">
      <data key="d0">Reporting Lines</data>
      <data key="d1">AIComponent</data>
      <data key="d2">Reporting Lines are the established pathways of communication and authority within the organizational structure of a notified body.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fb8e27222ad9e21f792d1e7ee0a1e255</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_31.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750858294</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Economic Interest">
      <data key="d0">Economic Interest</data>
      <data key="d1">RiskConcept</data>
      <data key="d2">Economic Interest refers to any financial stake or influence that could potentially compromise the independence of a notified body.</data>
