    <node id="Accuracy">
      <data key="d0">Accuracy</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Accuracy is a critical quality measurement that high-risk AI systems must achieve to ensure reliable performance and outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Accuracy is a metric that measures how close the output of the high-risk AI system is to the actual or expected outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Accuracy measures how closely an AI system's outputs match the correct or expected results.&lt;SEP&gt;Accuracy refers to the degree to which the performance of high-risk AI systems meets the defined standards and expectations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-671e76af4a78aebc96c988f0504bfa99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20ac675fffdeba0fbc242b392d3af8da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2f186d6b95e69680f63fabb65ad924a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9685a1f72e235a3f5b9ee69878eedb21</data>
