      <data key="d5">1750863273</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Enforcement Capacity">
      <data key="d0">Enforcement Capacity</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Enforcement Capacity describes the ability of organizations and governments, particularly Member States, to implement and uphold AI regulations effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Enforcement capacity refers to the ability of Member States to effectively implement and enforce the legal requirements of the Regulation on AI.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9c76dd7edbc6dcf218d6558d18116d52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6579442a2f027e643cf907006333003a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_152.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_151.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863521</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Distributors">
      <data key="d0">Distributors</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeveloper</data>
      <data key="d2">Distributors are entities involved in the distribution of high-risk AI systems, responsible for handling the systems once they are placed on the market.&lt;SEP&gt;Distributors are entities that make high-risk AI systems available in the market and are responsible for compliance with regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Distributors are operators who supply AI systems to end users and are responsible for adhering to compliance regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-197c7357cf5fefe6ca4e08f847ff6a75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e978e96ac6d99cf448b53260c07dded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21678b36bef336bf18e091bdfdb68f0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_83.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_20.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863638</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Corrective Actions">
      <data key="d0">Corrective Actions</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Corrective Actions are measures implemented by distributors, providers, and operators of high-risk AI systems to address and rectify any non-compliance issues that may arise. These actions are specified in Article 20 and are crucial for ensuring that high-risk AI systems meet established safety and compliance requirements. Corrective Actions can include disabling or recalling the AI systems when necessary, as well as other measures aimed at resolving detected non-conformities. Overall, these actions are vital for maintaining the integrity, safety, and compliance of AI systems in the market.&lt;SEP&gt;Corrective actions are measures that providers must undertake to rectify compliance issues identified by notified bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;Corrective Actions refer to the steps that Providers must take to rectify non-compliance as determined by the Market Surveillance Authority's evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a64bfb94635a0df2f808b2f8a494bd3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-397d6e2474c4f45e883f265653f2e715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e978e96ac6d99cf448b53260c07dded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68d6983d829937a84d37118dacc3e39c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad9c740a10a5c1577e578a593bd61fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21678b36bef336bf18e091bdfdb68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb2802f1b508b813d06e58ae27a1f77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73fd7e801c2d8d41361f6b16b45c6ed0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_80.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_20.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_44.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_16.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863835</data>
    </node>
