      <data key="d0">Types of AI Systems</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Types of AI systems refer to the various categories of artificial intelligence that can be assessed based on their functions and applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f94df6da4de89cee24b1bd8f504c377</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_30.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859059</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Relevant Attestation of Competence">
      <data key="d0">Relevant Attestation of Competence</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Relevant attestation of competence provides proof that the conformity assessment body is qualified to perform conformity assessments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f94df6da4de89cee24b1bd8f504c377</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_30.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859059</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Accreditation Process">
      <data key="d0">Accreditation Process</data>
      <data key="d1">Procedure</data>
      <data key="d2">The accreditation process ensures conformity assessment bodies meet established criteria to carry out their functions effectively.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f94df6da4de89cee24b1bd8f504c377</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_30.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859059</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Objections">
      <data key="d0">Objections</data>
      <data key="d1">Risk</data>
      <data key="d2">Objections refer to concerns raised about the conformity assessment activities carried out by a specific body, potentially impacting their authorization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f94df6da4de89cee24b1bd8f504c377</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_30.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859059</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Consultations">
      <data key="d0">Consultations</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Consultations are discussions between the Commission and Member States regarding objections raised against conformity assessments.&lt;SEP&gt;Consultations refer to the discussions held by the Commission with Member States and the conformity assessment body regarding objections.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-244204be180c4ed9731f434ed67ee99b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f94df6da4de89cee24b1bd8f504c377</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_30.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859059</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Effective Penalties">
      <data key="d0">Effective Penalties</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Effective penalties are sanctions that are proportionate and dissuasive, ensuring the deterrence of non-compliance with the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1b43f399350f0fc36795c0ce358459d9</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_168.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859117</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ne bis in idem Principle">
      <data key="d0">ne bis in idem Principle</data>
      <data key="d1">LegalBasis</data>
      <data key="d2">The ne bis in idem principle is a legal principle that protects individuals from being tried twice for the same offense, which must be respected under the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1b43f399350f0fc36795c0ce358459d9</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_168.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859117</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Size of the Provider">
      <data key="d0">Size of the Provider</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">The size of the provider, particularly if it is a Small and Medium Enterprise (SME) or a start-up, is a critical factor in determining the proportionality of penalties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1b43f399350f0fc36795c0ce358459d9</data>
