    <node id="Non-Compliance">
      <data key="d0">Non-Compliance</data>
      <data key="d1">RiskConcept</data>
      <data key="d2">Non-Compliance indicates the failure of an AI system to meet established regulatory standards as assessed by the Commission.&lt;SEP&gt;Non-compliance refers to situations where the high-risk AI system does not meet the established requirements, leading to obligations for corrective actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Non-compliance refers to the failure to meet regulatory requirements, which can lead to legal and market consequences for providers of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Non-compliance signifies the failure of an AI system or its operator to adhere to established regulatory requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Non-Compliance indicates the failure to meet established regulatory standards, which poses risks associated with the use of certain AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ddb5ca2a2f12bb39286916d398b70ed9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cc9a7191827dda78eda5924876e5f7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ad9c740a10a5c1577e578a593bd61fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21678b36bef336bf18e091bdfdb68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82b1b08be1175d2e6d49ab5a294ef86a</data>
