    </node>
    <node id="Directive (EU) 2019/882">
      <data key="d0">Directive (EU) 2019/882</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Directive (EU) 2019/882 establishes comprehensive accessibility requirements for products and services across the European Union. Its primary focus is on harmonizing accessibility standards across various sectors, particularly emphasizing the relevance for AI systems and their interaction with users. The Directive aims to aid persons with disabilities by ensuring that products and services are accessible to them.

Furthermore, Directive (EU) 2019/882 sets forth specific requirements related to the functionality of the EU Database and outlines data management practices to ensure compliance. It includes additional compliance obligations that ensure the public availability and effective use of this database.

Moreover, the Directive encapsulates regulations on the exploitation of vulnerabilities in individuals by AI systems, highlighting its commitment to protect vulnerable groups from potential exploitation. Overall, Directive (EU) 2019/882 serves as a crucial framework for enhancing accessibility and safeguarding the rights of individuals in the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-41b3ba2302e956849a6be7455071577d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a0ae2ebdd7c0c6e56069b878ca85c78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c17bf6e803eec807c9fc7299d71d51d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-166a35f517674f4ceba2754c65f88c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33366c5df404f37775ccbf3ec455b578&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2806e288e0b71013209c4ad85ecaa38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17045c951f494f621b2305960aade53f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_29.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_131.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_80.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_16.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863940</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Conformity Demonstration">
      <data key="d0">Conformity Demonstration</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Conformity Demonstration is the process by which a responsible entity proves compliance with regulatory standards for AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c17bf6e803eec807c9fc7299d71d51d6</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_16.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859437</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Democratic Processes">
      <data key="d0">Democratic Processes</data>
      <data key="d1">AreaOfImpact</data>
      <data key="d2">Democratic Processes encompass the mechanisms by which democratic governance operates, which can be negatively impacted by disinformation spread by AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Democratic processes are susceptible to interference from AI models that could propagate disinformation or biased content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3f46abe104a1bdb0fae1c25094db36d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7570653f66cb58454b80be2046705a29</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_120.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_110.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863955</data>
    </node>
    <node id="2019 Ethics Guidelines for Trustworthy AI">
      <data key="d0">2019 Ethics Guidelines for Trustworthy AI</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">The 2019 Ethics Guidelines for Trustworthy AI detail seven ethical principles for developing trustworthy and ethically sound AI systems, established by the independent AI HLEG.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-256a6003a5841f2764536c55f7086431</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Seven Non-Binding Ethical Principles">
      <data key="d0">Seven Non-Binding Ethical Principles</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">The seven principles aim to ensure that AI systems are trustworthy, focusing on human agency, technical safety, privacy, transparency, diversity, social well-being, and accountability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-256a6003a5841f2764536c55f7086431</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Human Agency and Oversight">
      <data key="d0">Human Agency and Oversight</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Human agency and oversight ensures that AI serves people, respects human dignity, and is controllable by humans.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-256a6003a5841f2764536c55f7086431</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Robustness and Safety">
      <data key="d0">Technical Robustness and Safety</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical robustness refers to the reliability and resilience of AI systems in preventing unlawful uses and minimizing unintended harm.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-256a6003a5841f2764536c55f7086431</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Privacy and Data Governance">
      <data key="d0">Privacy and Data Governance</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Privacy and data governance ensures that AI systems respect data protection rules and maintain high standards of data quality and integrity.&lt;SEP&gt;Privacy and data governance entail ensuring AI systems are developed in accordance with rules regarding privacy and data protection, focusing on quality and integrity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-849f8f0403e6b12fa8a9c24b84c094c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-256a6003a5841f2764536c55f7086431</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Diversity, Non-Discrimination and Fairness">
      <data key="d0">Diversity, Non-Discrimination and Fairness</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">This principle promotes equal access and cultural diversity in AI, while preventing discriminatory impacts and biases.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-256a6003a5841f2764536c55f7086431</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Social and Environmental Well-Being">
      <data key="d0">Social and Environmental Well-Being</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">This principle emphasizes the sustainable development of AI systems that contribute positively to societal and environmental aspects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-256a6003a5841f2764536c55f7086431</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk-Based Approach">
      <data key="d0">Risk-Based Approach</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">The risk-based approach is a strategy for establishing effective rules for AI development and usage, focusing on potential risks and ethical outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-256a6003a5841f2764536c55f7086431</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Personal Autonomy">
      <data key="d0">Personal Autonomy</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Personal autonomy relates to the ability of individuals to make informed choices and have control over their interactions with AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-256a6003a5841f2764536c55f7086431</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Robustness">
      <data key="d0">Technical Robustness</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical robustness encompasses the reliability of AI systems, ensuring they function safely under various circumstances.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical robustness refers to the resilience of high-risk AI systems against harmful or undesirable behaviors arising from system limitations or environmental factors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f15de033aa4361b6dbf4b5d72ede05a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-256a6003a5841f2764536c55f7086431</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_27.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_75.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863951</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Privacy">
      <data key="d0">Privacy</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Privacy involves protecting personal data and ensuring AI systems conform to data protection regulations and ethical guidelines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-256a6003a5841f2764536c55f7086431</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Transparency Principle">
      <data key="d0">Transparency Principle</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">The transparency principle mandates that AI systems be designed to allow users to understand their operations, capabilities, and limitations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-256a6003a5841f2764536c55f7086431</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Diversity and Fairness">
      <data key="d0">Diversity and Fairness</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Diversity and fairness include efforts to ensure that AI technologies are inclusive and equitable, representing various demographic backgrounds.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-256a6003a5841f2764536c55f7086431</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Societal Well-Being">
      <data key="d0">Societal Well-Being</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Societal well-being incorporates considerations of how AI impacts communities and promotes social good.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-256a6003a5841f2764536c55f7086431</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_27.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859455</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Environmental Sustainability">
      <data key="d0">Environmental Sustainability</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Environmental Sustainability pertains to criteria used to evaluate the impact of AI systems on ecological systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental Sustainability refers to considerations made regarding the impact of AI technology on the environment and the effectiveness of measures for improvement.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental sustainability highlights the need for AI to contribute positively to ecological balance and resource management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7a69b68c9998277692ac6c6341fcdcac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-256a6003a5841f2764536c55f7086431&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b837dd750c95d041180fa3d735328672</data>
