    <node id="Term of Office">
      <data key="d0">Term of Office</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">The term of office for members of the Advisory Forum is two years, extendable by a maximum of four years.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ad86065dee426d0a1db7444552c4a385</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_67.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Meetings">
      <data key="d0">Meetings</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">The Advisory Forum holds meetings at least twice a year to facilitate discussions among members and invited experts.&lt;SEP&gt;The advisory forum holds meetings at least twice a year to discuss and prepare contributions and recommendations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ad86065dee426d0a1db7444552c4a385&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-699c5fa3a4d8d093e6a599637df82443</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_67.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Membership">
      <data key="d0">Membership</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">The membership of the Advisory Forum includes a balanced selection of representatives from various sectors, including industry and academia.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ad86065dee426d0a1db7444552c4a385</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_67.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Opinions and Recommendations">
      <data key="d0">Opinions and Recommendations</data>
      <data key="d1">Output</data>
      <data key="d2">The Advisory Forum may prepare opinions, recommendations, and written contributions at the request of the Board or the Commission.&lt;SEP&gt;These are contributions prepared by the advisory forum at the request of the Board or the Commission, guiding policy decisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ad86065dee426d0a1db7444552c4a385&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-699c5fa3a4d8d093e6a599637df82443</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_67.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Co-Chairs">
      <data key="d0">Co-Chairs</data>
      <data key="d1">AreaOfImpact</data>
      <data key="d2">The co-chairs have a term of two years, with the possibility of being renewed once, overseeing the activities of the advisory forum.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-699c5fa3a4d8d093e6a599637df82443</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_67.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Temporary Sub-Groups">
      <data key="d0">Temporary Sub-Groups</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">These are established by the advisory forum to examine specific questions related to the objectives of the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-699c5fa3a4d8d093e6a599637df82443</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_67.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sub-Groups">
      <data key="d0">Sub-Groups</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Standing or temporary sub-groups established by the advisory forum to examine specific questions related to the objectives of the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-699c5fa3a4d8d093e6a599637df82443</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_67.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859618</data>
    </node>
    <node id="publicly accessible space">
      <data key="d0">publicly accessible space</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Publicly accessible space refers to any physical space that is available to an undetermined number of natural persons regardless of ownership or intended activity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="physical space">
      <data key="d0">physical space</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">A physical space is defined as an area that can be either publicly or privately owned and used for various activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
