      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="transport stations">
      <data key="d0">transport stations</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Transport stations like buses, metros, and railway stations facilitate public transportation access.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="airports">
      <data key="d0">airports</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Airports are key transportation hubs that provide public access for air travel.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="cinemas">
      <data key="d0">cinemas</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Cinemas are entertainment venues that allow the public to view films.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="theatres">
      <data key="d0">theatres</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Theatres are performance spaces for arts and entertainment accessible to the public.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="museums">
      <data key="d0">museums</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Museums provide cultural and educational access to art and history for the public.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="public roads">
      <data key="d0">public roads</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Public roads are thoroughfares that enable movement and access for the public.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="parks">
      <data key="d0">parks</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Parks are green spaces available for recreation and leisure activities by the public.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="playgrounds">
      <data key="d0">playgrounds</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Playgrounds are designated areas for children to play, typically open to the public.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ticket">
      <data key="d0">ticket</data>
      <data key="d1">Input</data>
      <data key="d2">Tickets are prerequisites for entry to certain publicly accessible spaces, often established as a condition for access.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="registration">
      <data key="d0">registration</data>
      <data key="d1">Input</data>
      <data key="d2">Registration may serve as a criteria for access to specific publicly accessible areas, allowing predetermined conditions to be met.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="national law">
      <data key="d0">national law</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">National law consists of the various legal statutes and guidelines that may support or complement the provisions of the regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;National law outlines specific conditions for access to spaces to maintain security and public order.&lt;SEP&gt;National law refers to the laws enacted by individual countries within the Union, which govern the rights and obligations of their citizens and businesses.&lt;SEP&gt;National law encompasses the legal guidelines of a specific country regarding the deployment and functioning of AI systems, potentially influencing the regulations set by Union law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2035e81a92cf42f945220e637e40591a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71f538bc77dea56a19150de3c7514990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe4d7c8b1c65cb7b9f5021681b13c271</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_86.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_38.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_19.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863481</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Company premises">
      <data key="d0">Company premises</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Company premises are defined spaces that restrict access to authorized personnel only, hence not publicly accessible.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="office spaces">
      <data key="d0">office spaces</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Office spaces are designed for employee use and are typically private, limiting public access.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="prisons">
      <data key="d0">prisons</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Prisons are secure facilities that are not publicly accessible, designed for the detention of offenders.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="private residential building">
      <data key="d0">private residential building</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Private residential buildings may have restricted access to certain areas while allowing public access to specific facilities such as doctors' offices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="airport">
      <data key="d0">airport</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">The airport, while generally publicly accessible, may have private sections which restrict public access.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="company premises">
      <data key="d0">company premises</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Company premises are areas intended for employee use that are not publicly accessible.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="factory premises">
      <data key="d0">factory premises</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Factory premises are typically restricted workspaces where public access is not allowed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="case-by-case basis">
      <data key="d0">case-by-case basis</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Determining whether a space is publicly accessible is done on a case-by-case basis, depending on specific circumstances.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-19ac689968d1b5ce1db014f781096bd3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Company Premises">
      <data key="d0">Company Premises</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Company premises are defined as areas specifically designated for access by employees and service providers, which prevents public access.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4013941d0b165f5643b927164f2ffd1c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Factory Premises">
      <data key="d0">Factory Premises</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Factory premises refer to physical locations where manufacturing activities occur, intended to be accessed only by authorized personnel.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4013941d0b165f5643b927164f2ffd1c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Offices">
      <data key="d0">Offices</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Offices are designated workspaces meant for employees and service providers, restricting public access.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4013941d0b165f5643b927164f2ffd1c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Workplaces">
      <data key="d0">Workplaces</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Workplaces cover locations where employees perform their duties, emphasizing access limitations for the general public.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4013941d0b165f5643b927164f2ffd1c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Non-Publicly Accessible Spaces">
      <data key="d0">Non-Publicly Accessible Spaces</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Non-publicly accessible spaces are locations where access is limited and controlled, often requiring special permission.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4013941d0b165f5643b927164f2ffd1c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Private Residential Building">
      <data key="d0">Private Residential Building</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Private residential buildings can have areas that are both publicly and non-publicly accessible, such as hallways leading to medical offices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4013941d0b165f5643b927164f2ffd1c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Airport">
      <data key="d0">Airport</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Airports may contain areas that are accessible to the public but also have restricted zones that are off-limits to average travelers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4013941d0b165f5643b927164f2ffd1c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Space">
      <data key="d0">Space</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Space encompasses physical locations, such as buildings or areas, which can be classified based on their accessibility to the public.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4013941d0b165f5643b927164f2ffd1c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Locked Door">
      <data key="d0">Locked Door</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">A locked door indicates restricted access, signaling that entry is controlled and not open to the general public.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4013941d0b165f5643b927164f2ffd1c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Open Gate">
      <data key="d0">Open Gate</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">An open gate typically suggests potential access to a space, but it may not signify public accessibility depending on other factors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4013941d0b165f5643b927164f2ffd1c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Signs Prohibiting Access">
      <data key="d0">Signs Prohibiting Access</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimenson</data>
      <data key="d2">Signs that prohibit access serve as indicators that a space is not open for public entry and restrict usage to authorized individuals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4013941d0b165f5643b927164f2ffd1c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Prisons">
      <data key="d0">Prisons</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Prisons are strongly regulated facilities meant to detain individuals and are not publicly accessible due to security concerns.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4013941d0b165f5643b927164f2ffd1c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Border Control">
      <data key="d0">Border Control</data>
      <data key="d1">AreaOfImpact</data>
      <data key="d2">Border Control is the process where authorities monitor and manage the entry and exit of individuals across borders.&lt;SEP&gt;Border control areas are locations where access is strictly controlled to ensure national security and are not accessible to the general public.&lt;SEP&gt;Border control involves managing the entry and exit of individuals, where high-risk AI systems may be used for identity verification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ded7b0ac022304fae10651966b33d18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4013941d0b165f5643b927164f2ffd1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ed67e673a6fe0a3c79a41bb9102d44b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863737</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Case-by-Case Determination">
      <data key="d0">Case-by-Case Determination</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Case-by-case determination refers to the process of evaluating access to spaces based on specific situational factors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4013941d0b165f5643b927164f2ffd1c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Employees and Service Providers">
      <data key="d0">Employees and Service Providers</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Employees and service providers are individuals with authorized access to company and factory premises, allowing them entry to restricted areas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4013941d0b165f5643b927164f2ffd1c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Accessibility Criteria">
      <data key="d0">Public Accessibility Criteria</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Public accessibility criteria are the standards that help define whether a space can be accessed by the general public or remains restricted.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4013941d0b165f5643b927164f2ffd1c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_19.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859621</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 261 TFEU">
      <data key="d0">Article 261 TFEU</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 261 TFEU outlines the jurisdiction of the Court of Justice regarding penalties imposed on AI model providers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ae3ab8a3b5c5d0c61e8b99fa718913b0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_169.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859671</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Obligations on Providers">
      <data key="d0">Obligations on Providers</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Obligations imposed on providers of General-Purpose AI models by the Regulation, which need to be adhered to avoid penalties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ae3ab8a3b5c5d0c61e8b99fa718913b0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_169.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859671</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Infringement of Obligations">
      <data key="d0">Infringement of Obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Infringement of Obligations refers to any violations of Union law protecting fundamental rights in relation to AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Infringement of obligations refers to the non-compliance with the requirements outlined in the Regulation, which can lead to penalties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6e853663a3f2d06a9cfea8582e10f089&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae3ab8a3b5c5d0c61e8b99fa718913b0</data>
