      <data key="d5">1750863550</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Commission's Measures">
      <data key="d0">Commission's Measures</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Measures requested by the Commission are actions that providers must take in accordance with the Regulation to maintain compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ae3ab8a3b5c5d0c61e8b99fa718913b0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_169.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859671</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Limitation Periods">
      <data key="d0">Limitation Periods</data>
      <data key="d1">LegalBasis</data>
      <data key="d2">Limitation periods are legal timeframes within which actions or penalties must be enforced under the principles of proportionality in the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ae3ab8a3b5c5d0c61e8b99fa718913b0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_169.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859671</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Decisions by the Commission">
      <data key="d0">Decisions by the Commission</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Decisions made by the Commission regarding AI providers' compliance under the Regulation are subject to review and must adhere to legal standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ae3ab8a3b5c5d0c61e8b99fa718913b0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_169.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859671</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Unlimited Jurisdiction of the Court">
      <data key="d0">Unlimited Jurisdiction of the Court</data>
      <data key="d1">LegalBasis</data>
      <data key="d2">The unlimited jurisdiction of the Court allows for comprehensive review of penalties imposed by the Commission on AI model providers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ae3ab8a3b5c5d0c61e8b99fa718913b0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_169.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859671</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Copyright and Related Rights">
      <data key="d0">Copyright and Related Rights</data>
      <data key="d1">LegalBasis</data>
      <data key="d2">Copyright and Related Rights regulate how creative works can be used, emphasizing the importance of identifying rights holders in relation to AI model training.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f1ae06c8c76fc5976313d75e4ffabdfc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_106.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859731</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Copyright Standards">
      <data key="d0">Copyright Standards</data>
      <data key="d1">Standard</data>
      <data key="d2">Copyright Standards represent the legal benchmarks that providers must meet when dealing with copyrighted material in AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f1ae06c8c76fc5976313d75e4ffabdfc</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_106.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859736</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Member States'">
      <data key="d0">"Member States'</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">Member States are national governments responsible for national security and defense, as specified by legal articles.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5981afe4b9fb547c64f49e76b1d9c0a7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859786</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 4(2) TEU">
      <data key="d0">Article 4(2) TEU</data>
      <data key="d1">LegalBasis</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 4(2) TEU specifies the responsibilities of Member States regarding national security, integrating public international law into the regulation of AI systems used for military purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5981afe4b9fb547c64f49e76b1d9c0a7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859786</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Civilian Purposes">
      <data key="d0">Civilian Purposes</data>
      <data key="d1">Purpose</data>
      <data key="d2">Civilian purposes encompass the use of AI systems for non-military applications, including everyday functions and societal benefits.&lt;SEP&gt;Civilian purposes refer to the use of AI systems in contexts that do not involve military or defense activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ffa7662f1a996e8ed97ec3caf0ae564&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5981afe4b9fb547c64f49e76b1d9c0a7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859786</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Lethal Force">
      <data key="d0">Lethal Force</data>
      <data key="d1">RiskConcept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lethal force addresses the implications of using AI systems in military contexts where they may engage in life-threatening actions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5981afe4b9fb547c64f49e76b1d9c0a7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859786</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Public Entity">
      <data key="d0">Public Entity</data>
      <data key="d1">Stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d2">A public entity refers to government bodies responsible for compliance with regulations and oversight of AI system usage for national security.&lt;SEP&gt;Public Entities are potential candidates designated by Member States to perform tasks of national competent authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1dbe8a4749b15b91fcb1062fee4fa778&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5981afe4b9fb547c64f49e76b1d9c0a7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_153.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862964</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Private Entity">
      <data key="d0">Private Entity</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">A private entity refers to non-governmental organizations that also engage in activities involving AI systems for various purposes, including those related to national security.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5981afe4b9fb547c64f49e76b1d9c0a7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859786</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Exclusion Clause">
      <data key="d0">Exclusion Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">The exclusion clause stipulates that certain AI systems used exclusively for military and national security purposes may be excluded from broader regulatory requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5981afe4b9fb547c64f49e76b1d9c0a7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859786</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Defence Purposes">
      <data key="d0">Defence Purposes</data>
      <data key="d1">AreaOfImpact</data>
      <data key="d2">Defence purposes involve the utilization of AI within national defense strategies and operations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ffa7662f1a996e8ed97ec3caf0ae564</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859786</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Non-Excluded Purposes">
      <data key="d0">Non-Excluded Purposes</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Non-excluded purposes refer to applications of AI systems that are permissible under regulations, such as civilian and law enforcement uses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ffa7662f1a996e8ed97ec3caf0ae564</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859786</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Excluded Purposes">
      <data key="d0">Excluded Purposes</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Excluded purposes pertain to uses of AI systems that are clearly outside the regulatory scope, particularly military and similar applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ffa7662f1a996e8ed97ec3caf0ae564</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859786</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Exclusions">
      <data key="d0">Exclusions</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Exclusions refer to specific applications of AI that are not covered by regulations, particularly those related to national security.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ffa7662f1a996e8ed97ec3caf0ae564</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_24.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859786</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Obligations">
      <data key="d0">Technical Obligations</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical obligations are requirements specified in applicable articles that need to be fulfilled by providers regarding the AI model's documentation and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-873c3732f26f3ace86c77cfec67991ee</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_54.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859888</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex XI">
      <data key="d0">Annex XI</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex XI contains specific guidelines and requirements for the technical documentation necessary for compliance with AI regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex XI includes specific points that detail measurement and calculation methodologies for AI compliance documentation.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex XI outlines specific points and criteria relevant to compliance and documentation under the regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex XI specifies the minimum required elements that must be included in the technical documentation of AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4dc89de2edca5d2bfe0d5e9e7c99665b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5abff9e94aff7675c473268fd21bf551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-873c3732f26f3ace86c77cfec67991ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c49e78c25e30ed3a2557915010f14f3c</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_54.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_53.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863102</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Institution">
      <data key="d0">Union Institution</data>
      <data key="d1">AISubject</data>
      <data key="d2">Union institutions are the entities subject to regulations imposed by the European Data Protection Supervisor, and are evaluated based on their compliance and responsibility regarding AI practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5da2f6b1c2fa5619efa26719534e9c35</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859954</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Purpose of AI System">
      <data key="d0">Purpose of AI System</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">The purpose of the AI system relates to its intended function and objectives, which should be considered when determining the severity of an infringement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5da2f6b1c2fa5619efa26719534e9c35</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859954</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Risk of Damage">
      <data key="d0">Risk of Damage</data>
      <data key="d1">Risk</data>
      <data key="d2">The risk of damage describes the potential negative impact suffered by affected persons due to non-compliance with AI-related regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5da2f6b1c2fa5619efa26719534e9c35</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859954</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cooperation with the Supervisor">
      <data key="d0">Cooperation with the Supervisor</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Cooperation with the European Data Protection Supervisor refers to actions taken by Union institutions to remedy infringements and comply with previous orders.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5da2f6b1c2fa5619efa26719534e9c35</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859954</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annual Budget">
      <data key="d0">Annual Budget</data>
      <data key="d1">Metric</data>
      <data key="d2">The annual budget of a Union institution can influence the decision-making process regarding the imposition of administrative fines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5da2f6b1c2fa5619efa26719534e9c35</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859954</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Non-compliance with Prohibition of AI Practices">
      <data key="d0">Non-compliance with Prohibition of AI Practices</data>
      <data key="d1">RiskConcept</data>
      <data key="d2">Non-compliance with prohibitions set in the regulations can lead to administrative fines and sanctions against the Union institutions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5da2f6b1c2fa5619efa26719534e9c35</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859954</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union institution, body, office or agency">
      <data key="d0">Union institution, body, office or agency</data>
      <data key="d1">AISubject</data>
      <data key="d2">The Union institution, body, office or agency is subject to regulation and must adhere to the obligations laid out in data protection laws.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-111c71f234a0f2d1b26490907acae6eb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859985</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Administrative fines">
      <data key="d0">Administrative fines</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Administrative fines can reach up to EUR 1,500,000 for non-compliance with AI practices as specified in the Regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-111c71f234a0f2d1b26490907acae6eb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750859985</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Rights of defence">
      <data key="d0">Rights of defence</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">The rights of defence ensure that parties have access to files and are able to comment on decisions affecting them in the proceedings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-111c71f234a0f2d1b26490907acae6eb</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_100.json</data>
