    </node>
    <node id="Reporting of infringements">
      <data key="d0">Reporting of infringements</data>
      <data key="d1">Process</data>
      <data key="d2">The process of reporting infringements involves whistleblowers notifying authorities about violations of laws or regulations, protected under the Directive.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e74c582b50b1dcae6565f7384ebbe5e1</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_172.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861055</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Protection of whistleblowers">
      <data key="d0">Protection of whistleblowers</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">The protection of whistleblowers is a quality measurement ensuring that individuals can report infringements without fear of retaliation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e74c582b50b1dcae6565f7384ebbe5e1</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_172.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861055</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Data Protection Law">
      <data key="d0">Union Data Protection Law</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Union Data Protection Law establishes regulations regarding how personal data should be handled and protected in the context of AI.&lt;SEP&gt;Union data protection law governs the processing of personal data and the rights of data subjects in the context of AI testing and consent.&lt;SEP&gt;Union data protection law governs the processing of personal data, ensuring individuals' rights are maintained when their data is used in AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Union data protection law governs the processing and sharing of personal data to ensure individuals' rights are protected.&lt;SEP&gt;Union data protection law sets the framework under which personal data must be handled, ensuring the rights of data subjects are protected.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad1a115533e7d3b3ced9ea8e2e87b0e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d18c3755735a13a436e766a5ca73fc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-800752b66b6fe0cd70bb0290efc2fbbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-699b82035d71a633a86a67090e5a61e8</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_141.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_69.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_59.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863374</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulations (EU) 2022/868">
      <data key="d0">Regulations (EU) 2022/868</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulations (EU) 2022/868 are legal frameworks related to European data governance, impacting AI system data handling and transfers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_141.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861057</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulations (EU) 2023/2854">
      <data key="d0">Regulations (EU) 2023/2854</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulations (EU) 2023/2854 outline further provisions concerning the protection and transfer of data under AI regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_141.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861057</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Real-World Conditions">
      <data key="d0">Real-World Conditions</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Real-World Conditions represent the actual environmental and operational circumstances under which high-risk AI systems are tested.&lt;SEP&gt;Real-world conditions refer to the environments in which AI systems are tested to assess their performance and compliance with regulatory frameworks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-35a30c75209c0fbb0ca1bb4afe44c77d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_141.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_9.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863750</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Effective Oversight">
      <data key="d0">Effective Oversight</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Effective oversight refers to competent personnel monitoring the AI system during real-world testing to ensure compliance and safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Effective oversight refers to the mechanisms established to monitor and control AI systems testing to minimize risks to individuals and ensure compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ad1a115533e7d3b3ced9ea8e2e87b0e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_141.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861057</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2022/868">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2022/868</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2022/868 relates to European data governance and needs amending to include provisions for AI testing with personal data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ad1a115533e7d3b3ced9ea8e2e87b0e2</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_141.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861057</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Regulation (EU) 2023/2854">
      <data key="d0">Regulation (EU) 2023/2854</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Regulation (EU) 2023/2854 establishes harmonized rules on fair access to and use of data, important for ensuring proper data handling in AI.&lt;SEP&gt;This regulation sets harmonised rules on fair access to and use of data, and amend previous regulations and directives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f182220530b59a4450fc951016283bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad1a115533e7d3b3ced9ea8e2e87b0e2</data>
