    </node>
    <node id="Annex VI">
      <data key="d0">Annex VI</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex VI contains guidelines on the internal control mechanisms for evaluating the risks associated with high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex VI outlines the internal control measures for assessing high-risk AI systems without a notified body.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex VI outlines the internal control measures relevant to the conformity assessment processes for AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-41e5d20a8e9427a4698b84f758676994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4d62babb1c5a144faeae6ac2f13628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69838403e8b59bb122436a0d25a9fc1e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_43.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861443</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex VII">
      <data key="d0">Annex VII</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex VII describes conformity assessment procedures, including those involving notified bodies for high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex VII describes the framework for the conformity assessment procedures that high-risk AI systems must undergo.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex VII outlines specific procedures and requirements for the conformity assessment of high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex VII outlines the conformity assessment procedures specifically for high-risk AI systems under the outlined regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex VII outlines the requirements for certificates issued by notified bodies in compliance with relevant authorities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6c72b31b17ef0accd3df4ab25a063163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41e5d20a8e9427a4698b84f758676994&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69838403e8b59bb122436a0d25a9fc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4d62babb1c5a144faeae6ac2f13628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-397d6e2474c4f45e883f265653f2e715</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_44.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863231</data>
    </node>
    <node id="harmonised standards">
      <data key="d0">harmonised standards</data>
      <data key="d1">Standard</data>
      <data key="d2">Harmonised standards are established specifications that help ensure that products, including AI systems, meet safety and regulatory requirements across member states.&lt;SEP&gt;Harmonised standards are regulatory guidelines that high-risk AI systems can follow to demonstrate compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Harmonised standards provide guidelines that define the minimum requirements for ensuring the safety and efficacy of AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Harmonised standards provide guidelines and compliance requirements but can sometimes be insufficient regarding fundamental rights concerns.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69838403e8b59bb122436a0d25a9fc1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6fc829d58f1a7bbf3defd5cbe758b8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07b79b1855840c81b5d9079a82c7e9fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-345a8ba89ed0ea3325462384d5e16aaf</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_122.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_79.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_121.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863619</data>
    </node>
    <node id="common specifications">
      <data key="d0">common specifications</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Common specifications are developed by the Commission to address cases where harmonised standards are inadequate.&lt;SEP&gt;Common specifications refer to additional requirements that may apply when harmonised standards do not exist or are not applicable.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d6fc829d58f1a7bbf3defd5cbe758b8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69838403e8b59bb122436a0d25a9fc1e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_121.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863579</data>
    </node>
    <node id="conformity assessment procedures">
      <data key="d0">conformity assessment procedures</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Conformity assessment procedures are evaluations designed to determine whether high-risk AI systems meet compliance requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69838403e8b59bb122436a0d25a9fc1e</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_43.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861443</data>
    </node>
    <node id="internal control">
      <data key="d0">internal control</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Internal control is a method outlined in Annex VI for assessing high-risk AI systems without needing an external notified body.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69838403e8b59bb122436a0d25a9fc1e</data>
