    </node>
    <node id="Model Poisoning">
      <data key="d0">Model Poisoning</data>
      <data key="d1">Risk</data>
      <data key="d2">Model poisoning involves manipulating pre-trained components used in the training of AI systems, potentially leading to flawed outputs.&lt;SEP&gt;Model poisoning refers to attacks aimed at altering pre-trained components of AI systems to lead to erroneous outputs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ed5ccbca443324af303d8bca3aa31a38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-671e76af4a78aebc96c988f0504bfa99</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_15.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750861692</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Adversarial Examples">
      <data key="d0">Adversarial Examples</data>
      <data key="d1">Risk</data>
      <data key="d2">Adversarial examples are carefully crafted inputs designed to deceive AI models into making incorrect predictions.&lt;SEP&gt;Adversarial examples are specially crafted inputs designed to deceive AI models into making incorrect predictions or classifications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ed5ccbca443324af303d8bca3aa31a38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-671e76af4a78aebc96c988f0504bfa99</data>
