    <node id="Article 51(1), point (a)">
      <data key="d0">Article 51(1), point (a)</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 51(1), point (a) outlines the conditions under which a provider must notify the Commission about a general-purpose AI model.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e23bb4c71b510fec0bbe6570de37cd5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862904</data>
    </node>
    <node id="systemic risks">
      <data key="d0">systemic risks</data>
      <data key="d1">Risk</data>
      <data key="d2">Systemic risks refer to the multifaceted risks associated with the deployment of general-purpose AI models and their potential impacts on society.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic risks refer to the potential for widespread negative impacts from failures or issues within general-purpose AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-69b5f24963810305f2a7846d54923bf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e23bb4c71b510fec0bbe6570de37cd5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_116.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863315</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Annex XIII">
      <data key="d0">Annex XIII</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex XIII contains criteria that the Commission may use to assess whether a general-purpose AI model presents systemic risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Annex XIII includes criteria that define the designation process for general-purpose AI models with systemic risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c1ef1c9ca92c002cf6ad36264fe1292c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e23bb4c71b510fec0bbe6570de37cd5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862916</data>
    </node>
    <node id="list of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk">
      <data key="d0">list of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk</data>
      <data key="d1">Output</data>
      <data key="d2">The list contains identified general-purpose AI models that are deemed to present systemic risks and must be published by the Commission.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e23bb4c71b510fec0bbe6570de37cd5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862916</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 51(1)">
      <data key="d0">Article 51(1)</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 51(1) establishes the conditions under which a provider must notify authorities about a general-purpose AI model.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e23bb4c71b510fec0bbe6570de37cd5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862916</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Point (a)">
      <data key="d0">Point (a)</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Point (a) specifies a requirement for providers regarding the notification of systemic risks associated with general-purpose AI models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e23bb4c71b510fec0bbe6570de37cd5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862916</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Criteria">
      <data key="d0">Criteria</data>
      <data key="d1">Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Criteria are the principles or standards by which conformity is assessed within the framework of harmonized standards and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Criteria are the standards set by the Commission for assessing whether an AI model presents systemic risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9db4c15b43d1b7a1a1138d5a7403b240&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e23bb4c71b510fec0bbe6570de37cd5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_32.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863476</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ex Officio Designation">
      <data key="d0">Ex Officio Designation</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Ex officio designation refers to the Commission's ability to independently classify AI models as presenting systemic risks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e23bb4c71b510fec0bbe6570de37cd5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862916</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Reassessment Request">
      <data key="d0">Reassessment Request</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">A Reassessment Request is a formal appeal made by a Provider to the Commission to review the risk status of their AI Model after it has been designated.&lt;SEP&gt;A reassessment request allows a provider to ask the Commission to reevaluate the systemic risk status of their AI model.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c1ef1c9ca92c002cf6ad36264fe1292c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e23bb4c71b510fec0bbe6570de37cd5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862916</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Six Months">
      <data key="d0">Six Months</data>
      <data key="d1">Temporal Dimension</data>
      <data key="d2">Six months is the minimum time frame after which providers can request a reassessment regarding their designated AI model.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3e23bb4c71b510fec0bbe6570de37cd5</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_52.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750862916</data>
    </node>
