      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Pursuant to Article 5, specific prohibitions are noted regarding high-risk AI systems, guiding lawful testing practices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ff61ec794793cf787d4a0473487a06f3</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863076</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 71(4)">
      <data key="d0">Article 71(4)</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 71(4) specifies the requirements for registering a Real-World Testing Plan and how it must include a unique identification number.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aa9e2916955e882c73231ed69851f6ec</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863082</data>
    </node>
    <node id="High-Risk AI Systems Annex III">
      <data key="d0">High-Risk AI Systems Annex III</data>
      <data key="d1">AIModel</data>
      <data key="d2">Annex III categorizes certain high-risk AI systems and outlines specific regulations and testing requirements for these systems in law enforcement and management areas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aa9e2916955e882c73231ed69851f6ec</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863082</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EU Database Section 49(4)">
      <data key="d0">EU Database Section 49(4)</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Section 49(4) of the EU Database governs the secure storage and access of information about high-risk AI systems and their testing requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aa9e2916955e882c73231ed69851f6ec</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863082</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing Duration">
      <data key="d0">Testing Duration</data>
      <data key="d1">Metric</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing Duration is defined as the maximum time for which testing can occur, initially not exceeding six months, with a possibility of extension under certain conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Testing Duration outlines the maximum permissible length for real-world testing of AI systems, set at no more than six months.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa9e2916955e882c73231ed69851f6ec</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863082</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 49(4)">
      <data key="d0">Article 49(4)</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 49(4) outlines procedures for testing high-risk AI systems and data management within the EU framework.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863082</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 49(5)">
      <data key="d0">Article 49(5)</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 49(5) specifies regulations regarding high-risk AI systems and the conditions for their testing in real-world scenarios.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863087</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Data Collected">
      <data key="d0">Data Collected</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Data Collected during testing in real-world conditions must adhere to the regulations outlined in Union law regarding processing and transfer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863087</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI System Instructions">
      <data key="d0">AI System Instructions</data>
      <data key="d1">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d2">AI System Instructions are the guidelines provided to deployers regarding the operation of AI systems in testing scenarios.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863087</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Compliance Agreement">
      <data key="d0">Compliance Agreement</data>
      <data key="d1">LegalBasis</data>
      <data key="d2">Compliance Agreement specifies the roles, responsibilities, and obligations of the provider and deployers with respect to AI system testing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863087</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Prospective Deployer">
      <data key="d0">Prospective Deployer</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">A Prospective Deployer is a potential entity that may collaborate in the deployment of AI systems for testing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f6e14583352886a741ac1d51eada03a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863087</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Testing Outcome">
      <data key="d0">Testing Outcome</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">Testing Outcome is the result of AI system evaluation conducted in real-world conditions, pivotal for ensuring system reliability.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f6e14583352886a741ac1d51eada03a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863092</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Withdrawal of Consent">
      <data key="d0">Withdrawal of Consent</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">The act of a subject or their legally designated representative withdrawing their consent to participate in testing, allowing them to request deletion of their personal data.&lt;SEP&gt;Withdrawal of Consent permits participants to revoke their agreement to be part of the AI system testing at any time.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4518ca313d8493e277775e1a9267b84d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f6e14583352886a741ac1d51eada03a</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863092</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI System Predictions">
      <data key="d0">AI System Predictions</data>
      <data key="d1">Output</data>
      <data key="d2">The predictions, recommendations or decisions made by an AI system that can be reversed and disregarded if necessary.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4518ca313d8493e277775e1a9267b84d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863092</data>
    </node>
    <node id="National Market Surveillance Authority">
      <data key="d0">National Market Surveillance Authority</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">A national authority responsible for overseeing AI system testing, ensuring compliance, and reporting serious incidents.&lt;SEP&gt;The National Market Surveillance Authority manages the oversight and regulation of AI testing in the Member State to ensure compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4518ca313d8493e277775e1a9267b84d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a350089bbf860c041d514aa2041d9455</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863092</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Compliance with Regulations">
      <data key="d0">Compliance with Regulations</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">The requirement for AI providers and systems to adhere to established laws and guidelines during testing and operational phases.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4518ca313d8493e277775e1a9267b84d</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863092</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union and National Liability Law">
      <data key="d0">Union and National Liability Law</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">The Union and national liability law holds providers accountable for any damages that occur during the testing of the AI system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a350089bbf860c041d514aa2041d9455</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863092</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Procedure for Prompt Recall">
      <data key="d0">Procedure for Prompt Recall</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">The Procedure for Prompt Recall defines the steps necessary to quickly recall or terminate the AI System after testing, ensuring safety and compliance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a350089bbf860c041d514aa2041d9455</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863092</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Suspension or Termination of Testing">
      <data key="d0">Suspension or Termination of Testing</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Suspension or termination of testing refers to the halting of testing in real world conditions, requiring notification to authorities regarding the status and outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a350089bbf860c041d514aa2041d9455</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863092</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Final Outcomes">
      <data key="d0">Final Outcomes</data>
      <data key="d1">Data</data>
      <data key="d2">Final Outcomes refer to the results or conclusions derived from the testing of the AI System in real world conditions, which must be reported.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a350089bbf860c041d514aa2041d9455</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863092</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Market Surveillance Authority Notification">
      <data key="d0">Market Surveillance Authority Notification</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">The Market Surveillance Authority Notification is a regulatory requirement that mandates providers notify authorities about the status of AI System testing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a350089bbf860c041d514aa2041d9455</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863092</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Liability for Damage">
      <data key="d0">Liability for Damage</data>
      <data key="d1">Consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">Liability for damage indicates the legal responsibility providers bear for any adverse effects resulting from the AI System's testing procedures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a350089bbf860c041d514aa2041d9455</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863092</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Provider or Prospective Provider">
      <data key="d0">Provider or Prospective Provider</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877</data>
      <data key="d2">A Legal Representative acts for the provider or prospective provider in all matters related to high-risk AI systems as stipulated by the regulation.</data>
      <data key="d1">UNKNOWN</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_60.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863097</data>
    </node>
    <node id="European Data Protection Board">
      <data key="d0">European Data Protection Board</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeveloper</data>
      <data key="d2">The European Data Protection Board is an independent European body responsible for ensuring consistent application of data protection laws across the EU and for promoting cooperation between national data protection authorities.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Data Protection Board is an independent authority that advises on data protection laws within the EU and is consulted regarding the Regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;The European Data Protection Board provides guidance and oversight on data protection issues related to AI regulations in the EU.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d1b92a727425c41637e16da3cb9ac9c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-472b03a027e3fcae21e86e23849e4510&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae8bdbb57af24d78fe2313201571bea7</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_180.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_3.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863288</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Article 42(1) and (2)">
      <data key="d0">Article 42(1) and (2)</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Article 42(1) and (2) of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725 refers to provisions regarding the consultation process of the European Data Protection Supervisor and the European Data Protection Board.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-472b03a027e3fcae21e86e23849e4510</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_180.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863099</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Joint Opinion">
      <data key="d0">Joint Opinion</data>
      <data key="d1">QualityMeasurement</data>
      <data key="d2">The Joint Opinion refers to the collaborative assessment produced by the European Data Protection Supervisor and the European Data Protection Board, reflecting their views on compliance with the mentioned regulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-472b03a027e3fcae21e86e23849e4510</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_180.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863099</data>
    </node>
    <node id="18 June 2021">
      <data key="d0">18 June 2021</data>
      <data key="d1">Date</data>
      <data key="d2">18 June 2021 is the date on which the joint opinion of the European Data Protection Supervisor and the European Data Protection Board was delivered.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-472b03a027e3fcae21e86e23849e4510</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_180.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863099</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Consultation Process">
      <data key="d0">Consultation Process</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">The Consultation Process is the procedural framework wherein the European Data Protection Supervisor and the European Data Protection Board provide opinions on compliance matters.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-472b03a027e3fcae21e86e23849e4510</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_180.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863099</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Union Law on Copyright">
      <data key="d0">Union Law on Copyright</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Union law on copyright governs the rights related to the usage and distribution of AI models and their training data.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4dc89de2edca5d2bfe0d5e9e7c99665b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_53.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863102</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Code of Practice">
      <data key="d0">Code of Practice</data>
      <data key="d1">CodeOfConduct</data>
      <data key="d2">A code of practice provides guidelines for AI model providers to comply with regulations until harmonised standards are established.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4dc89de2edca5d2bfe0d5e9e7c99665b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_53.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863102</data>
