    <node id="Adequate Means of Compliance">
      <data key="d0">Adequate Means of Compliance</data>
      <data key="d1">Regulation</data>
      <data key="d2">Adequate means of compliance refers to the standards and methodologies required for assessment by regulatory bodies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5abff9e94aff7675c473268fd21bf551</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_53.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Measurement Methodologies">
      <data key="d0">Measurement Methodologies</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Measurement methodologies are systematic approaches adopted by the Commission to create verifiable and comparable documentation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5abff9e94aff7675c473268fd21bf551</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_53.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Calculation Methodologies">
      <data key="d0">Calculation Methodologies</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">Calculation methodologies pertain to the techniques and processes established by the Commission for compliance verification.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5abff9e94aff7675c473268fd21bf551</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_53.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Power to Adopt Delegated Acts">
      <data key="d0">Power to Adopt Delegated Acts</data>
      <data key="d1">AICapability</data>
      <data key="d2">The Commission possesses the power to adopt delegated acts that detail compliance measures, enhancing regulatory effectiveness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5abff9e94aff7675c473268fd21bf551</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_53.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Evolving Technological Developments">
      <data key="d0">Evolving Technological Developments</data>
      <data key="d1">Change</data>
      <data key="d2">Evolving technological developments signify ongoing advancements that may necessitate updates to existing regulations and annexes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5abff9e94aff7675c473268fd21bf551</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/article_53.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Agency">
      <data key="d0">Agency</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">An agency is a type of organization that acts as a deployer of AI systems, potentially impacting others in its operational environment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2b28a4b325cc05a6cc4897f58ccdf00f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_13.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863122</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Body">
      <data key="d0">Body</data>
      <data key="d1">AIDeployer</data>
      <data key="d2">Any other recognized body that may use AI systems under the authority of the Regulation can also be considered a deployer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2b28a4b325cc05a6cc4897f58ccdf00f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_13.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1750863122</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AI System Usage">
      <data key="d0">AI System Usage</data>
      <data key="d1">Purpose</data>
      <data key="d2">AI system usage by deployers refers to the deployment of AI technologies under the authority of a person or entity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2b28a4b325cc05a6cc4897f58ccdf00f</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_docs/recital_13.json</data>
