      <data key="d11">1750863600</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="Union harmonisation legislation">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Regulation establishes that high-risk AI systems must comply with Union harmonisation legislation for market approval.</data>
      <data key="d8">legal compliance,safety standards</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-13991bdab077b3114e8913f89a1371e5</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/article_2.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1750857239</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="Member States">
      <data key="d6">125.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Member States are obligated to adhere to the guidelines set forth by the Regulation for the implementation and compliance of AI systems. They are required to take necessary actions to prevent any obstacles that may arise for high-risk AI systems and must enforce the Regulation at a national level to ensure compliance within their jurisdictions. This includes adapting their local laws to align with the stipulations of the Regulation.

Additionally, the Regulation delineates the competencies of Member States, particularly in matters of national security, underscoring their significant role in the overall framework. Member States are responsible for supporting the implementation of the Regulation by ensuring that local AI providers meet its requirements. They are also tasked with developing and establishing rules that resonate with the provisions of the Regulation, which include penalties for violations. Overall, Member States play a crucial role in enforcing the Regulation's measures for the protection and safety of AI systems, all while adhering to their obligations within the European Union.&lt;SEP&gt;Member States hold a crucial role in enforcing the Regulation and ensuring its implementation within their jurisdiction.&lt;SEP&gt;The tasks of Member States are defined by the Regulation to support the AI Office.&lt;SEP&gt;Member States must implement the Regulation while respecting fundamental rights, thus they are key stakeholders in its application.&lt;SEP&gt;The Regulation empowers Member States to enforce a common approach towards AI systems while allowing certain restrictions only if explicitly authorized.</data>
      <data key="d8">collaborative governance,compliance,compliance support,enforcement,enforcement responsibility,governance,government responsibility,implementation,jurisdiction,legal adaptation,legal framework,legal obligation,mandatory compliance,market access,national implementation,regulation enforcement,regulatory adherence,regulatory authority,regulatory compliance,regulatory enforcement,responsibilities,stakeholder</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-63ef16386f45c7bc364061cc094254fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b43f399350f0fc36795c0ce358459d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40a9e2a0fc4601f4b3d4f583384b6a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba662546e18e6e5f82c3cd1c5b4c3b75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fa5fe9ac042448be58de6c82bb33ea4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c2f867de2be6cb439557f91700b051c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b474f9815c7033ca1ad8daff4012eff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98532c431ec75ae38c76dc0730337a16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dbe8a4749b15b91fcb1062fee4fa778&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43942ba7283893ebf128acb858a20c58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13991bdab077b3114e8913f89a1371e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7365f713d09e74d49090cb78cb3e19b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0455405f9e173535e78c4ea589745cf4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f892644f7a3eab6b024d8a386777f23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3105f8ed20ed5608a4571fe7b1d8f942</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/recital_129.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_9.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_1.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_153.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_168.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_99.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_175.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_2.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_64.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_176.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_179.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_145.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1750863728</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Regulation" target="national security purposes">
      <data key="d6">9.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Regulation explicitly excludes AI systems used for national security purposes from its scope, emphasizing the unique legal considerations involved.</data>
