    <edge source="Regulation" target="High-Risk AI Systems">
      <data key="d6">123.0</data>
      <data key="d7">High-risk AI systems are specifically governed by a comprehensive Regulation aimed at ensuring their safe deployment. This Regulation establishes clear guidelines for the identification, management, and compliance of these systems, emphasizing the importance of ethical use throughout their lifecycle. It includes strict compliance criteria that ensure the safety and accountability of high-risk AI systems, reflecting a commitment to responsible management and operational standards.

The Regulation provides specific protocols related to the development, modification, and deployment of high-risk AI systems, aiming to mitigate risks associated with their use. Furthermore, it delineates the rights of individuals affected by these systems, ensuring that their interests are taken into consideration. Overall, the Regulation mandates that high-risk AI systems comply with defined requirements, reinforcing a commitment to safety and ethical standards in the deployment of these advanced technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems must adhere to the provisions outlined in the Regulation for their development and market entry.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems fall under the scope of the Regulation, necessitating regular assessments and possible amendments.&lt;SEP&gt;High-risk AI systems must comply with regulations that mandate transparency and documentation before being deployed.</data>
