    <edge source="Regulation" target="General-Purpose AI Models">
      <data key="d6">69.0</data>
      <data key="d7">General-Purpose AI Models must adhere to compliance requirements set forth in the existing Regulation to ensure legal usage.&lt;SEP&gt;Providers of General-Purpose AI Models are subject to a comprehensive Regulation that governs their operation within the Union market. This Regulation is designed to address the potential risks associated with the widespread use of such AI models and mandates adherence to specific obligations and deadlines. It includes detailed guidelines for the monitoring and evaluation of these models to ensure they are used responsibly and effectively. Additionally, the Regulation focuses on the enforcement of compliance, specifying the responsibilities that providers must meet to avoid penalties. Overall, it establishes a framework aimed at safeguarding interests while promoting the safe deployment of General-Purpose AI Models.&lt;SEP&gt;Regulation establishes rules specifically for General-Purpose AI Models to ensure legal certainty and address systemic risks.</data>
