    <edge source="Regulation" target="High-Risk AI System">
      <data key="d6">57.0</data>
      <data key="d7">High-Risk AI Systems are specifically addressed under the Regulation due to their significant impact on safety and rights. These systems are defined and regulated under specific legal frameworks outlined in the Regulation. Due to their elevated status, high-risk AI systems are subject to defined obligations, which indicate the required assessments and compliance standards before they can be placed on the market. The Regulation also establishes the obligations of both deployers and developers concerning high-risk AI systems and their users, ensuring that all parties are aware of their responsibilities. Furthermore, the classification of high-risk AI systems is governed by these specific regulations, which outline the necessary compliance requirements for their use.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,compliance requirements,legal definition,legal framework,market requirements,regulatory compliance,regulatory framework,risk assessment,risk management,safety</data>
