    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="Fundamental Rights">
      <data key="d6">54.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Fundamental Rights and High-Risk AI Systems are intricately connected, as compliance with fundamental rights is a core consideration in evaluating the impact of high-risk AI systems. These systems have the potential to infringe upon the fundamental rights of individuals if they are not carefully designed and regulated. Therefore, it is imperative that high-risk AI systems are managed in a manner that protects the fundamental rights of those affected by their decisions. The deployment of such systems must respect and uphold these rights, ensuring ethical compliance throughout their implementation. Additionally, the assessment of high-risk AI systems is directly tied to the protection of fundamental rights as mandated by Union law, further emphasizing the necessity of considering these rights during their evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d8">ethical implications,ethical management,ethical standards,human rights,rights,rights protection,risk evaluation,risk management,safety</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-431ae031d4ead528e84df75526b0f1dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb0291da832d9defa94aaf2262ad3761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37d88f95110db00bbf8230a2632a2035&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9685a1f72e235a3f5b9ee69878eedb21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de3f18a6d766d2baa57ae891b9da7741&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c4d62babb1c5a144faeae6ac2f13628</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_52.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_58.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_66.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_93.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_7.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1750863922</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="EU Database">
      <data key="d6">50.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The EU Database serves as a comprehensive registry for high-risk AI systems, necessitating their registration as part of compliance processes with regulatory standards. This database not only contains records of the high-risk AI systems but also includes registered testing plans associated with these systems, thereby ensuring proper identification and adherence to regulations. To maintain oversight and ensure compliance, it is required that high-risk AI systems, along with their testing data, be registered in the EU Database. Furthermore, the information stored within the EU Database is accessible to the public, reinforcing transparency in the management and regulation of high-risk AI technologies.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,data management,data registration,data transparency,registration,registration requirement,regulation compliance,regulatory requirement,system registration,transparency</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f8022b105f5e7e2d0ba74bbe75f31f87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa9e2916955e882c73231ed69851f6ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-166a35f517674f4ceba2754c65f88c5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2806e288e0b71013209c4ad85ecaa38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-675b49fdde07175ec9a1afb693d1d877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3</data>
