    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="Commission">
      <data key="d6">52.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Commission plays a pivotal role in the oversight and regulation of High-Risk AI Systems in accordance with EU regulations. It is responsible for assessing and enforcing compliance requirements to ensure that these systems meet established standards. To facilitate regulation and compliance, the Commission develops model contractual terms specifically applicable to high-risk AI systems. Its decisions regarding authorisations directly impact the deployment of these systems in the market, highlighting the Commission's emphasis on maintaining regulatory control.

Furthermore, the Commission oversees coordination and cooperation related to high-risk AI systems, working alongside market surveillance authorities to ensure proper handling and compliance. In situations where High-Risk AI Systems are deemed to no longer pose significant risks, the Commission holds the authority to remove their classifications, thus adapting to the evolving landscape of AI technology and its associated risks.</data>
      <data key="d8">AI governance,compliance assessment,cooperation,governance authority,oversight,regulatory impact,regulatory oversight,regulatory responsibility,risk assessment</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-8143bb5053cad47b9eaf4c05c9556429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0695d12d62d4fd15a528842231db1850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13bd6c41d609ae7976a7b3ac4ab8e3fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb0291da832d9defa94aaf2262ad3761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0461b38c664574f634a78148bfce0336&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82b1b08be1175d2e6d49ab5a294ef86a</data>
