    <edge source="High-Risk AI Systems" target="Market Surveillance Authorities">
      <data key="d6">58.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Market Surveillance Authorities are responsible for overseeing and regulating the deployment of High-Risk AI Systems within their jurisdiction. Their main focus is ensuring compliance with established safety standards and regulations related to these systems. They monitor high-risk AI systems at the national level, specifically concerning compliance with the EU database and relevant regulatory frameworks. These authorities assess conformity by reviewing documentation and, when necessary, acquiring access to source code. Their mission includes a comprehensive monitoring process to ensure that high-risk AI systems adhere to the necessary compliance standards as defined under the regulation.</data>
