    <edge source="Union Law" target="National Law">
      <data key="d6">50.0</data>
      <data key="d7">National Law must align with Union Law, which can modify the application of Verification Requirements based on national contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;National law and Union law are closely interconnected, particularly in the realm of regulating AI systems and data protection. National law is aligned with Union law, ensuring that the implementation of regulations is appropriate when AI systems impact local jurisdictions. This coordination establishes that both national and Union laws set the conditions for performing identity checks.

National law operates in conjunction with Union law, working to ensure that country-specific regulations comply with EU obligations regarding AI systems. It is essential for national law to be compatible with Union law when applying rules related to AI systems and data protection. Additionally, Union law provides a foundational legal framework that is complemented by national law in regulating the processing of personal data within each state. Together, they create a cohesive legal environment for the oversight of AI systems and the protection of personal data.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,governance,jurisdiction,jurisdictional interaction,law integration,legal alignment,legal compliance,legal framework,regulatory alignment,regulatory compliance,regulatory synergy</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-1eea61d03ab615ac5f518e77cd220c1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a23e03a78af2035b69e69bd4fc65a435&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf8a675497acfbeb420b95621b7cb31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c664ec81872dda212b64d449aa7a2014&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ed67e673a6fe0a3c79a41bb9102d44b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2612abd3c26dca69a0acec30add3ef15</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/recital_73.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_78.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_63.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_33.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_92.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_59.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1750863737</data>
    </edge>
