    <edge source="Commission" target="Market Surveillance Authorities">
      <data key="d6">57.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Market surveillance authorities monitor compliance with the regulations set by the Commission regarding high-risk AI systems.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission and Market Surveillance Authorities collaborate closely to ensure compliance with regulations governing artificial intelligence (AI) systems. They conduct joint investigations, promoting adherence to established standards. The Commission oversees the activities of Market Surveillance Authorities, which are responsible for monitoring compliance with these regulatory standards. In this regulatory relationship, the Commission interacts with Market Surveillance Authorities to fulfill the tasks outlined in AI regulations. Additionally, the Commission provides these authorities access to the EU Database, enhancing their capability to enforce compliance effectively. Furthermore, Market Surveillance Authorities can request the Commission to exercise its powers for regulatory enforcement, underscoring a cooperative dynamic between the two entities in the enforcement of regulations pertaining to AI model providers.</data>
      <data key="d8">collaboration,compliance enforcement,compliance monitoring,compliance oversight,data access,governance,oversight,regulatory compliance,regulatory enforcement,regulatory interaction,regulatory supervision</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ea1514e01d99729cb280141a24250142&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af991f85166d6ddfbbf84e4a73207d3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18e4ea35b819263359794e3a968f44ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2806e288e0b71013209c4ad85ecaa38b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72498ec90c19419f10373dde7e7b51b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d58805118916ede230a82a4ec3f60b3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82b1b08be1175d2e6d49ab5a294ef86a</data>
