    <edge source="Commission" target="European Parliament">
      <data key="d6">57.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Commission and the European Parliament engage in a collaborative legislative process that necessitates consultation before the adoption of delegated acts. This relationship ensures that the European Parliament is kept informed and involved in the legislative framework of the European Union. After the adoption of each delegated act, the Commission is obligated to notify the European Parliament, reinforcing a system of transparency and accountability.

In addition to these notifications, the Commission is responsible for providing the European Parliament with detailed reports and assessments related to various legislative proposals, including those specifically concerning artificial intelligence (AI) regulations. This includes sharing findings on AI regulations and their impacts, as well as evaluations of these regulations over time. The Commission submits these reports for legislative scrutiny, thereby facilitating informed legislative actions by the European Parliament.</data>
      <data key="d8">8,collaboration,legislative process,legislative review,notification,regulatory compliance,regulatory governance,regulatory process,reporting,stakeholder engagement,stakeholder involvement</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-da5fbf959baa6ee8e86278864a9144cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eab6e21707d57be17832ef8dfd7180a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83f37d4143e19486af167d7acee5bee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b837dd750c95d041180fa3d735328672&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de5a0c7f560be7dcbe4301aed20bcb98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-762d138929f27b0266d948c0aad50daa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a69b68c9998277692ac6c6341fcdcac</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/recital_174.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_112.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_97.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1750863456</data>
    </edge>
