    <edge source="Commission" target="Member State">
      <data key="d6">48.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Commission plays a pivotal role in regulating and guiding Member States in the management of artificial intelligence (AI) systems. Member States are required to notify the Commission of their detailed regulatory rules following adoption, ensuring that there is regulatory alignment across jurisdictions. The Commission addresses its decisions regarding authorizations directly to Member States, thereby indicating a collaborative and regulatory relationship.

Furthermore, the Commission oversees the actions of Member States, mandating them to inform it about their AI regulatory measures and compliance issues. Member States are responsible for reporting to the Commission on both compliance matters and the specifications of AI systems they implement. Through effective communication of regulatory decisions, the Commission coordinates actions with Member States, ensuring a comprehensive approach to managing AI risks and ensuring adherence to established guidelines and certification processes.</data>
      <data key="d8">communication,compliance communication,decision-making,governance,notification,regulatory authority,regulatory compliance,regulatory coordination,regulatory oversight,regulatory process,stakeholder report</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-0695d12d62d4fd15a528842231db1850&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13bd6c41d609ae7976a7b3ac4ab8e3fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67ecee9ae9852fb675f5c9c9cb2f2de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b341fa074527a308a2434a3c68244d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cc9a7191827dda78eda5924876e5f7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2440fb0070f3198e96bd1ad753ae3e0a</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/article_46.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_36.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_41.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_81.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_37.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_82.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1750863809</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Commission" target="Market Surveillance Authority">
      <data key="d6">38.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Commission is informed of authorizations issued by the Market Surveillance Authority and can intervene if necessary.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission reviews authorizations from market surveillance authorities to ensure compliance with Union laws and regulations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Commission works alongside Market Surveillance Authorities to ensure compliance with authorisations in the market.&lt;SEP&gt;The Market Surveillance Authority must consult with the Commission in cases of objections to authorization.&lt;SEP&gt;The Market Surveillance Authority consults with the Commission regarding national measures taken in relation to AI systems.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,compliance enforcement,inter-agency communication,regulatory oversight,regulatory process</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-13bd6c41d609ae7976a7b3ac4ab8e3fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4c7e75432b8ffa8e0b96687dc4dd380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07ee6b3452d764ccd9733dceadb1ac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee6d94a5f64203f09d02387acbdb39c5</data>
