    <edge source="Market Surveillance Authority" target="Member State">
      <data key="d6">55.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Member States designate market surveillance authorities to monitor and regulate AI systems accordingly.".&lt;SEP&gt;The Market Surveillance Authority plays a crucial role in overseeing the compliance of AI systems within the framework established by each Member State. Each Member State has its own designated Market Surveillance Authority, which is responsible for regulating high-risk AI systems and ensuring that they adhere to applicable regulations. These authorities collaborate closely with Member States to enforce compliance and implement corrective actions when necessary. Operating within their respective jurisdictions, the Market Surveillance Authorities are tasked with the comprehensive oversight of AI regulations and testing compliance, ensuring that AI systems used within their territory meet the required standards and guidelines.</data>
