    <edge source="High-Risk AI System" target="Provider">
      <data key="d6">99.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The High-Risk AI System refers to advanced artificial intelligence solutions classified under regulatory frameworks due to their significant potential impact on health, safety, and rights. The Provider, which includes distributors and importers of such systems, carries a crucial responsibility to ensure compliance with all pertinent regulatory requirements and safety standards associated with high-risk AI systems.

The Provider must diligently oversee the compliance process, which includes registering the high-risk AI system in the EU database prior to market entry. This registration is vital for maintaining transparency and accountability in the regulatory landscape. Furthermore, the Provider is obligated to assist in compliance efforts for any AI systems that may transition into high-risk categories in the future.

To ensure the safe deployment of these systems, the Provider must implement appropriate risk mitigation measures and conduct thorough impact assessments. They are tasked with supplying necessary instructions that inform the impact assessment process regarding these high-risk AI systems. Moreover, the Provider is responsible for assessing any changes to the AI systems and ensuring continued compliance through regular evaluations.

Overall, the Provider must adhere to all obligations set forth for high-risk AI systems within the relevant regulations, thus safeguarding the functionality and legal compliance of these critical technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;The Provider is the entity that places the high-risk AI system on the market and ensures its compliance with regulations.</data>
      <data key="d8">compliance,compliance assessment,cooperation,information sharing,market introduction,provider obligations,registration requirement,regulatory compliance,regulatory responsibility,responsibility,risk management,stakeholder role,supply chain,supply chain responsibility</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-c3ee1fc3ca38d0fe1cd19861a325e159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4329be6d4972c392a3a71593d402998&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fc356102e8bbeed5152b8bb0cda2ff6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b5e606b14946a1b388f008868e8e155&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f13d730755b7535c59eb130d6f7ac62e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be61089eed18cfaf2703713378c589a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8af2de29a8b78dd2b512b6eb64d912a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21678b36bef336bf18e091bdfdb68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f116a95954c59b63ce3149e6283ed8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee04f6104a24650416810ede28f3790b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73fd7e801c2d8d41361f6b16b45c6ed0</data>
      <data key="d10">./cached_docs/article_23.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_86.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_25.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_128.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_96.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/recital_65.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_47.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_docs/article_49.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1750863630</data>
    </edge>
